window.AKK_TRANSMIGRATED_INTO_A_SISTER_FORTUNE_ON_THE_FARM_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_TRANSMIGRATED_INTO_A_SISTER_FORTUNE_ON_THE_FARM_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":501,"title":"Chapter 501: Yang Cenan left, and Gu Baozhu and Gu Jinghong also departed.","paragraphs":["Watching Huo Chong leave Suining City, the Shadow Guard returned to the government office to report to Song Jinzhao.","“Around half past seven this morning, Huo Chong left Suining City. These are the words the three of them spoke last night, and the rest is what Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan said alone after leaving the inn.”","The two sheets of paper were written clearly, not a single word omitted.","Song Jinzhao stared at the line that said not to tell him, and smiled.","“He’s probably pleased, thinking that when the time comes to attack Suining City, he’ll have someone to pass him information.”","The Shadow Guard remarked with meaning, “Qu Ya might, but Guan Nianshan still needs to be watched.”","Song Jinzhao removed the lamp shade and burned both pieces of paper.","“Time can change a person’s mind, and besides, they have weaknesses.”","“Withdraw the people from the inn, but keep watching Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan.”","The Shadow Guard nodded in acknowledgment. “Your subordinate obeys.”","Soon after the Shadow Guard left, Qingshuang entered from outside.","“County Princess, news has come from the capital. Prince Qi has died of illness in Jinzhou.”","Song Jinzhao’s hand holding the brush paused, and she looked up in surprise.","“It shouldn’t have happened this soon.”","Qingshuang said, “Officially, it’s being declared as death from illness, but actually Prince Qi went mad and accidentally fell into a pond and drowned. The emperor felt it would damage the royal family’s dignity, so he falsely claimed illness as the cause.”","“The emperor also decreed that aside from the Princess of Qi and the two commanderies’ ladies, everyone else in the prince’s household shall be buried alive with him—three hundred and twenty-one people in total.”","The ink smudged. Song Jinzhao set down her brush and fell silent for a long time.","“None of the court officials objected?”","Qingshuang clenched her teeth and let out a sigh.","“Lord Ye took another beating at court, and after that, no one dared to object.”","He truly spared no old feelings.","Song Jinzhao breathed deeply and let out a sigh.","“Inform Eldest Young Master about this. If Ye Liangyu stays in the capital any longer, he’ll eventually lose his life.”","Upon learning that his Teacher had been beaten again, Song Qiming’s face turned darker than the bottom of a pot.","He slammed his fist onto the table, barely containing his rage.","“In the history of the Eastern Zhao Kingdom, no emperor has ever made the living die with him. Has the emperor lost his mind?”","“Even if it’s grief over losing a son, I never saw the emperor treat Prince Qi well when he was alive.”","Thinking of her own son, Qingshuang said, “Perhaps regret only comes after death.”","Song Qiming shut his mouth, too furious to speak.","Summoned at will, dismissed at will; fickle in favor and harsh in gratitude.","And his Teacher was stubborn by nature. If this continued, it wouldn’t be impossible for the emperor to order his execution.","After calming down, Song Qiming began writing a letter.","He scribbled rapidly, the strokes revealing his inner fury.","“Deliver this letter to Teacher as quickly as possible.”","Qingshuang accepted the envelope with both hands and assured him, “It will be sent out today.”","Once the door was closed, Song Qiming grew restless, stood up, and paced the room, his thoughts churning with agitation.","As soon as the five-day period was up, Yang Cenan could hardly wait to return to Panzhou. The government physician stood before Song Jinzhao with full respect, bowing in gratitude.","“These past days, I am deeply grateful for the County Princess’s guidance. I have learned a great deal.”","Song Jinzhao replied calmly, “It’s because you are eager to learn. Remember to stay alive until we meet again.”","The physician’s face stiffened. Remembering Yang Cenan’s frequent outbursts of rage in recent days, he felt uncertain himself.","“I hope so. County Princess, I take my leave.”","On the city wall, the carriage convoy gradually disappeared from everyone’s sight.","Gu Jinghong lowered his head and whispered into Gu Baozhu’s ear, “Shouldn’t we be heading back?”","Having eaten and lived at the government office for a full month, even he felt a bit embarrassed.","Her pink lips were chapped from biting. Gu Baozhu sighed softly and said, “Let’s go back. We’ll leave this afternoon.”","Staying any longer would be pointless, and besides, she was starting to miss home a little.","After coming down from the city wall, Gu Baozhu went to bid Song Jinzhao farewell.","Seeing the cheerfulness in Gu Jinghong’s eyes, Song Jinzhao attempted to persuade them to stay but failed, so she stopped insisting.","After lunch, the two mounted their horses and left.","Yang Cenan’s departure lifted a heavy weight off the minds of all the officials in Suining City. The stone pressing on their hearts was finally removed."]},{"number":502,"title":"Chapter 502: Gu Baozhu Rejects a Marriage Arrangement","paragraphs":["After the autumn harvest, the most important task was collecting the grain tax.","In previous years, the entire collection process would last nearly a month.","To improve efficiency, Song Qiming summoned all the officials and clerks of Suining City for a brief meeting.","\"Every year, the common folks have to laboriously transport their grain tax to the county office. If the grain fails inspection, they must take it back to dry and sort again. This year, we’ll change the approach.\"","\"Every county office has enough manpower. They’ll all be dispatched to the towns for unified collection, bringing in the grain tax all at once. Those who haven’t paid, or whose grain is rejected, will have a second chance three days after the first collection.\"","\"There’s still much to do after the autumn harvest. The entire collection process must be completed within ten days.\"","At his command, the room fell silent.","The household clerk pushed the ledger for spring seed purchases in front of Song Qiming.","\"Sir, this lists the amount of rice seed borrowed from the prefectural office by the people this spring. It can be collected together with the grain tax.\"","The three thousand taels used to buy the rice seed had originally been borrowed from the merchants by the prefectural office.","Song Qiming pressed his right hand on the ledger. \"Issue all the tax notices tomorrow.\"","\"The standards for grain tax collection, the method, and the location must all be clearly stated. Not a single extra grain of rice should be taken from the people.\"","The next day, along with the tax notices, sixteen officials from the prefectural office were dispatched.","They were divided into four groups, heading to Qingxia County, Yunzhu County, Songhe County, and Yanshan County.","Their tasks were twofold: first, to escort all collected grain taxes back; second, to conduct inspections and supervision, ensuring that no lower-level officials embezzled the grain or oppressed the people during collection.","...","Gu Baozhu and Gu Jinghong had barely stepped into their residence in Songzhou City when the entire Gu family gathered.","Madam Gu, seeing Gu Jinghong, who had turned a shade darker, screamed in shock.","\"How did you get so dark?\"","Then she cupped Gu Baozhu’s face and scrutinized her closely.","\"At least you’re only a little dark. A few days of rest should bring back your complexion.\"","After the evening meal, Madam Gu came alone to Gu Baozhu’s room.","\"The Xue family sent word that their eldest son passed the imperial examination. Once he returns, your father will summon him to the residence for you to meet.\"","Frustrated, Gu Baozhu walked over to the bed and lay down.","\"Mother, I’ve only just returned. Could you not talk about this right now?\"","Madam Gu pulled back the thin quilt and tugged her daughter upright.","\"In Songzhou City, the number of talented young men of your age can be counted on two hands. Those whose family background barely matches ours number only two or three. If you don’t secure one early, someone else will snatch them away.\"","Gu Baozhu slumped weakly on the bed. \"If they can be snatched away, it means there was no fate between us.\"","She grasped Madam Gu’s hand and looked at her with pleading eyes.","\"Mother, I don’t want to marry too early. During my visit to Suining City, County Princess Linghui told me that a woman’s optimal childbearing age is between twenty-four and twenty-nine. Marrying too young harms the body and increases the risk of difficult labor.\"","\"In the entire Southwest Province, Father holds the highest official rank. Since I’d be marrying beneath my station anyway, waiting a few years won’t matter.\"","Madam Gu’s eyes widened. \"By twenty-four, a child would already be attending school! Did County Princess Linghui truly tell you this?\"","Gu Baozhu nodded emphatically. \"Of course. Otherwise, why haven’t the County Princess and Shixue married yet? They’re several years older than me.\"","Madam Gu thought for a moment, then shook her head frantically.","\"I was only eighteen when I gave birth to your elder brother, and my health was fine. As long as you take good care of yourself, everything will be fine.\"","\"A man usually marries at twenty. If you don’t marry early, you won’t find a suitable match.\"","Seeing this approach fail, Gu Baozhu took another tack. \"At home, I’m the precious pearl cradled in my parents’ and elder brother’s hands. If I marry out, who knows whether my husband’s family will treat me well?\"","\"If you want me to marry, I’m fine with it—but only if my husband marries into our family.\"","A thunderbolt seemed to strike Madam Gu, leaving her mind blank. She was so shocked it took her a moment to recover.","\"Having a husband move in won’t do. Our family isn’t short of sons. If we bring in a live-in son-in-law, chaos would ensue.\"","Gu Baozhu had completely lost patience. She pulled the thin quilt over her head.","\"Then let me wait two years. At least wait until I’m twenty to marry.\"","For the next two quarters of an hour, Madam Gu pleaded earnestly, but Gu Baozhu refused to respond. Finally, she had no choice but to leave in frustration.","In the main room, Madam Gu sat on a stool, sighing three times.","\"My lord, what are we going to do?\"","Gu Zhongxun, who had just finished his bath, slipped on his inner robe.","\"Since Baozhu is unwilling, let her wait. My daughter, Gu Zhongxun's daughter, will have no shortage of suitors.\"","Madam Gu glared at him fiercely. \"Then name a few suitable matches for Baozhu three or four years from now.\"","Gu Zhongxun fell silent.","The only ones who could match her were the current candidates. There truly were none who were younger.","\"Actually, even a slightly lower family background would be fine, as long as he treats Baozhu well.\"","Madam Gu flung her handkerchief at his face and snarled, \"It’s already a step down for her. Any lower, and he won’t be worthy of my daughter.\"","\"Marriages are decided by parents and matchmakers. All this trouble is because you spoiled her.\"","Watching his wife storm off in anger, Gu Zhongxun looked utterly bewildered.","He muttered to himself in grievance, \"What do you mean I spoiled her?\"Don’t you spoil her too?\""]},{"number":503,"title":"Chapter 503: After Song Qiming finished his work, he found that no one was home.","paragraphs":["After receiving the conscription notice from the government, the Village Head immediately summoned the leaders of each village.","He waved the notice in his hand, his smile brighter than a sunflower.","\"This year, the government will collect grain in the town directly. We no longer need to transport it to the county office.\"","\"The official in charge of collecting grain will arrive the day after tomorrow. After you return, you must inform every household. Don't miss the deadline.\"","The village leaders exchanged glances and practically flew out the door as they left.","With thirty people per town, plus six clerks responsible for recording and accounting, and in the absence of bandit raids, all grain collected that day could be transported to the county granary before nightfall.","With Song Qiming closely monitoring the progress, the entire Suining Prefecture’s grain tax was fully collected and transported to the Suining granary within half a month.","Staring at the single granary that was only half full, Song Qiming let out a deep sigh.","\"This is barely enough. If a famine or war breaks out, it won't even last a year.\"","Shi Simian, standing nearby with his head slightly bowed, looked delighted.","\"This is already quite a lot. In previous years, half the grain would be lost by the time it reached Suining City. This year, thanks to the harvest from the newly reclaimed land, having one granary full is truly a blessing.\"","Song Qiming took a deep breath and let it out slowly.","\"Sell the grain that was collected as soon as possible. Exchange all the grain from the reclaimed land for coarse grains, so we don’t run short.\"","Thousands of laborers had to eat every day. Just the cost of the Prefectural Office buying grain from outside in the first half of the year had been exorbitant. Now, at least they no longer had to purchase it.","After more than ten consecutive days of leaving early and returning late, Song Qiming finally had an afternoon free.","He returned to the rear courtyard to have lunch with his family, only to find that no one was home. The kitchen had only prepared meals meant for him.","\"Where are the Eldest Miss, the Second Miss, and the Young Master? Aren’t they eating lunch at home today?\"","Chunxing, the head steward, looked puzzled.","\"The County Princess had business to attend to today and went out.\"","\"The Second Miss hasn’t been coming home for lunch these past few days because of the heat—many commoners are suffering from heatstroke.\"","\"As for the Young Master, he hasn’t been home during the day for about seven or eight days, so he’s not eating here either.\"","Song Qiming raised an eyebrow in surprise. \"What has he been busy with? Has he been going to the academy?\"","Chunxing shook her head. \"It seems he’s been going to the bookshop. Every time he comes back, he’s filthy.\"","Losing his appetite for lunch, Song Qiming headed straight to the bookshop.","The plaque that once read “Xue’s Bookshop” had been replaced with “Song’s Bookshop.” As he walked in, he saw the clerks sitting in the courtyard eating lunch.","The small yard held eight dining tables, each with four people seated on two long benches.","Scanning the group, Song Qiming spotted Song Anhao sitting at the front.","He was sitting on a stool, holding a bowl and eating heartily, chewing with more gusto than he ever did at home.","\"Elder Brother, why are you here?\" Seeing Song Qiming, Song Anhao immediately put down his bowl and finished chewing.","Song Qiming walked over and noticed that the food was the same at every table.","One meat dish, one vegetable dish, and a bowl of soup—but the meat dish only had a few shreds of meat.","\"Why aren’t you eating at home?\"","After all, compared to his two older sisters, the youngest Song Anhao had lived a comfortable life ever since he could remember.","Compared to what he usually ate, this meal was very simple.","Song Anhao said, \"Going back and forth wastes time. It’s more convenient to eat here. Elder Brother, have you had lunch yet?\"","Upon hearing the boss call Song Qiming “Elder Brother,” Manager Lou and the clerks, who had been sitting, immediately stood up to bow.","\"We humble subjects pay our respects to the Lord Prefect.\"","Song Qiming turned to them. \"No need for such formalities. Continue eating.\"","With that, he walked over and sat across from Song Anhao.","\"Not yet. Go get me a bowl of rice.\"","Yao Ying quickly ran to the kitchen and brought out a bowl of rice.","Song Anhao, trying to curry favor, pushed the leftover stir-fried celery with shredded pork and greens in front of Song Qiming.","\"The bookshop’s meals are made per person, so Elder Brother, you’ll have to make do.\"","Song Qiming picked up the bowl without complaining, even though there was barely anything left on the plate.","\"Before you were born, our family ate wild vegetables every meal. A bit of minced meat was something we only had during the New Year. These meals are already quite good.\"","The clerks, who had been eating with their heads down, glanced at the shreds of meat in their bowls.","Before the change of ownership, there had been no meat in their meals. Compared to before, things were now much better."]},{"number":504,"title":"Chapter 504: Development of Movable Type Printing Technology Succeeds","paragraphs":["Song Qiming used the soup left in the bowl to mix with his rice, barely filling his stomach before setting down his chopsticks to ask,","\"What have you been busy with these past few days? You don't come home during the day. Have you finished the assignments I gave you?\"","Song Anhao grabbed Song Qiming by the sleeve and pulled him into the room.","\"I've been working on movable-type printing these past few days, and I've made great progress.\"","The room was lined with boxes on both sides. Song Anhao picked up a bronze block from the table and handed it to Song Qiming.","\"Elder Brother, look—this is a bronze type mold. Doesn't it look just as good as handwriting?\"","Just making these type molds had cost Song Anhao a great deal of effort. The craftsmen he had brought from Songzhou City had failed dozens of times before finally producing a set that worked.","The process of filing and polishing alone had taken seven days.","Song Anhao continued showing off. \"I originally planned to make ceramic ones, but they turned out all different shapes after firing. The craftsmen said they couldn't control it, so I had to give up.\"","\"Once the type molds were done, people said I should use pine resin or wax to fix them together, and heat them up to take them apart when not in use. But I thought that was too troublesome, so I came up with the idea of carving a groove at the bottom of each type.\"","\"When they're arranged together, I insert bamboo strips into the grooves to lock them in place. When not in use, I just pull the strips out.\"","\"This is the improved version. You've come just in time—we're testing it this afternoon.\"","Song Qiming touched the type mold with his fingers. It was square and solid, with smooth edges—no small amount of effort had gone into polishing it.","He picked up another piece and compared them. The blocks were exactly the same size; the naked eye could barely tell them apart.","\"How did you come up with this?\"","Movable-type printing—he had never heard of it before.","Song Anhao looked at the type molds on the table, stars in his eyes.","\"I thought of it last time when I went to the bookshop with our sister. I just felt that since there would be so many novels to sell in the future, carving a new block for every single one would be far too inefficient.\"","He let out a wry laugh and scratched his head sheepishly.","\"But the cost of trial and error has been huge. I've spent a lot of money these days, and I have no idea when I'll break even.\"","Song Qiming didn't think it was a problem. His eyes and heart were full of pride.","He reached out and put his hand on his younger brother's shoulder.","\"The fact that you could think of inventing a new printing method—and actually make it work—is already amazing.\"","\"The cost has been high for now, but the impact will be huge. Like our sister once said, a new invention can drive an entire industry forward. What you're driving here is the printing industry.\"","Song Anhao blinked, half-understanding.","That sounded like a really big deal.","The first page of The Cry for Justice was soon assembled by the workers.","Foreman Lou picked up a brush, dipped it lightly into the ink bucket, and then brushed it evenly over the type molds.","How much ink he picked up, and how heavily or lightly he brushed—these things had a big effect on the quality of the print.","After laying a sheet of paper over the molds, he used a palm brush to press evenly and firmly across the back. When he carefully lifted the paper, the text was clearly printed on it.","After it dried, he picked it up. The quality was almost identical to the fixed carved blocks they had used before.","Song Anhao proudly handed it to Song Qiming, grinning as wide as could be.","\"It works! Next, I'll have the workers make more sets of type molds—especially for frequently used characters. At least twenty copies of each.\"","Song Qiming lifted his chin, his neck feeling sore and stiff.","\"You're in charge of the bookshop you bought, so you make the decisions. But when the government office needs to print something in the future, you'd better give your Elder Brother a discount.\"","Song Anhao shook his head generously. \"No discount needed—I'll give it to you for free.\"","Seeing his brother putting on such an adult air, Song Qiming reached out and pinched his cheek.","\"If you give everything away for free, you're going to lose a lot of money.\""]},{"number":505,"title":"Chapter 505: Purchase All Coal Mines in Suining Prefecture","paragraphs":["Outside the city, at the foot of a certain mining mountain, Song Jinzhao emerged from the mine shaft covered in grime.","Qingsuang bent down to brush the coal dust off Song Jinzhao’s skirt, but only smeared it worse. She finally straightened up with a resigned sigh and wiped her hands clean.","She shouldn’t have gone down there earlier—the stench was so thick she almost couldn’t breathe.","Seeing that Song Jinzhao’s complexion had returned to normal, the coal mine owner hastily put on a flattering expression. “My mine is the biggest in the entire Suining Prefecture. If you, miss, want to buy it, I can knock off another twenty percent.”","A sucker had finally shown up—he had to unload this burden fast.","Song Jinzhao took a couple of deep breaths to clear the coal smell from her nostrils.","If she bought it, she’d have to renovate it. Digging coal in a shaft like this was far too dangerous. Even if the tunnel didn’t collapse, over time, the workers would develop black lung disease, rheumatoid arthritis, chronic poisoning, and eye problems. They were literally risking their lives for money.","Worse, the wages were low, so in the end, they couldn’t afford treatment and would be slowly tortured to death by illness.","“Twenty percent off is still too high. The fact is, my pottery factory doesn’t need that much coal—buying more would just be wasteful.”","Master Li’s face twisted in distress. “These two mines are connected underground—I can’t sell just half. If your kiln doesn’t need it all, you can sell the rest to the locals or to blacksmiths.”","“Now that the Prefect and County Princess Linghui have wiped out the bandits on the road to Songzhou City, shipping it out would only take a few days.”","Qingshuang deliberately pinched her nose to sound disdainful. “Master Li, you’re not trying to fool us, are you? Coal of this quality, when used for forging iron, makes it brittle and prone to cracking. Few people want to buy it.”","“Even if you ship it far away, the price is low, and with transport and labor costs, you’d barely make anything.”","Seeing him hesitate, Lanxi deliberately leaned close to Song Jinzhao.","He lowered his voice, but just loud enough for Master Li to overhear.","“Miss, there’s another coal mine to the west. It’s smaller, but the quality is higher than this one. Maybe we should check it out first?”","At that, Master Li panicked.","He knew about that western mine—it was his biggest competitor. Its output was only a third of his, but the quality was slightly better.","If they went over there, they’d never come back.","“I can lower it by another ten percent at most. I’m practically selling at a loss.”","Song Jinzhao replied coolly, “You bought this mine for a thousand silver taels. After digging for three years, you’re still trying to sell it to me for fourteen hundred? Do you take me for a fool? Five hundred taels is the max. Any more, and I’ll walk.”","Master Li’s heart jolted. He hadn’t expected his lie to be so easily exposed.","He glanced at Song Jinzhao’s face and saw impatience creeping into her expression. His gut twisted.","Taking a step back, his tone softened. “I spent a lot of silver digging the shafts in the first year—those are all costs. You’ve got to let me make a little profit.”","Song Jinzhao said bluntly, “The shafts are too narrow, ventilation is terrible, and there’s no reinforcement inside. They’re completely substandard.”","“Even if I buy it, I’ll have to rebuild from scratch. If five hundred doesn’t work for you, I’ll find another seller.”","With that, she turned as if to leave.","Master Li hurried after her, looking like he was carving flesh from his own heart. “Five hundred it is. If the profits weren’t so slow, I really wouldn’t want to sell.”","He’d made just over seven hundred taels in three years. Now that the bandits were gone, good-quality coal from outside Suining City would start flooding in.","He couldn’t compete at those prices and would only have to keep lowering them. Better to take the cash and start a business inside the city—with all the traveling merchants coming through now, that would surely bring in more money.","Once he agreed, Lanxi immediately ordered someone to take him to the government office to finalize the paperwork.","The clerk at the office was polite and efficient. They were in and out in less than half the time it takes to finish a cup of tea.","Master Li smiled and asked, “Does your miss know people in the office?”","The guard folded the deed and tucked it into his chest. “Let’s just say she has connections. The mine will be taken over today. You’d better head back.”","By the time all thirty-two coal mines around Suining City had changed hands, Master Li, curious, started making inquiries and realized the buyer might be just one group.","This wasn’t about having too much coal—it was clearly being too little.","Amazed, his curiosity grew even stronger.","Why buy so many coal mines? They wouldn’t sell out in ten years."]},{"number":506,"title":"Chapter 506: Burning Cement to Build Cement Roads","paragraphs":["That evening, no sooner had Song Jinzhao stepped into the back courtyard than Song Anhao rushed over like a firecracker, shouting loudly.","“Elder Sister, I’ve invented movable-type printing!”","Song Jinzhao’s eyes lit up.","“Really?”","Song Anhao nodded vigorously, her pupils shining like gems.","“Really. I tested it this afternoon, and the printed words are even neater than before.”","“Liu Ziyuan’s ‘Record of Grievances’ is already finished. I plan to start printing tomorrow, and I can have it on sale within ten days.”","Song Anhao prattled on nonstop until she walked into the room and noticed the black stains covering the lower half of Song Jinzhao’s dress.","She blurted out, “Elder Sister, did you fall into a ditch?”","Song Jinzhao laughed helplessly. “No, I got dirty at the coal mine.”","The round table in the center of the room was laden with dishes. Even though Song Jinzhao had returned late, the three siblings hadn’t eaten ahead of time.","A maidservant brought a basin for Song Jinzhao to wash her hands. As she sat down and picked up her bowl, Song Qiming asked curiously, “I heard Ah Jie bought dozens of coal mines today. Are you planning to go into the coal business?”","Song Jinzhao took a big bite out of a chicken drumstick.","“In a few days, I’ll show you two things.”","At this, Song Qiming’s curiosity grew even stronger.","He pressed on, “What things?”","Song Jinzhao replied with a smile, “You’ll find out when the time comes.”","Song Jinzhao had purchased all two hundred mu of mountain land next to the Li family’s coal mine. When she arrived the next day, twenty pits one meter deep had already been dug on the flat terrain.","A layer of coal and a layer of limestone were poured in, burned for a full day and night, and then left to cool for two days.","The limestone hadn’t broken, but its surface was covered with a dense network of cracks.","......","Song Qiming waited impatiently for several days, until the afternoon of the fourth day, when Song Jinzhao had two carts of cement transported and parked at the entrance of the government office.","When he was called out, Song Jinzhao had already directed people to fence off the open space in front of the office with wooden boards, dividing it into dozens of sections.","“Ah Jie, what are you doing?”","Song Jinzhao turned back and smiled. “One of the things I mentioned earlier has been made.”","“Watch carefully. We’ll need it later for paving roads.”","She instructed the guards: “First, dump one bag of cement, two bags of sand, and three bags of gravel on the ground, then mix them.”","Song Qiming obediently watched in silence. Paving roads in his spare time was something he and his sister had agreed on long ago, and now it seemed Ah Jie had invented something new.","When the mixture was about right, Song Jinzhao continued directing, “Dig a pit in the middle and pour in the water.”","“Don’t add too much at once. When stirring with the shovel, be careful not to get any on yourself. This stuff heats up and can burn you.”","A quarter of an hour later, looking at the formed concrete, Song Jinzhao wore a satisfied smile.","“Pour it all into one section, and use a wooden board to smooth the surface.”","Thinking about how in the coming months the streets and alleys of Suining City could be paved with cement roads, Song Jinzhao felt a swell of pride.","The sun was harsh on the eyes. Song Jinzhao looked up at the sky.","“Water it every two hours. Don’t let it dry out too quickly.”","Lanxi said, “Rest assured, County Princess. I’ll personally watch over it.”","During the two days while they waited for the cement to dry, officials, yamen runners, and commoners alike stopped to take a look whenever they passed by. Anyone trying to get close was stopped by Lanxi. “It hasn’t dried yet; you can’t step on it.”","Shi Simian, dressed in his official robe, crouched down to examine it closely. “Manager Lan, will using this for roads be reliable?”","Lanxi replied firmly, “Whatever the County Princess sets her mind to, she never fails at.”"]},{"number":507,"title":"Chapter 507: Construction of the First Main Street Begins","paragraphs":["Three days later, Song Jinzhao stepped onto the pale gray concrete ground. Seeing her go up, Song Qiming decisively followed.","It was flat, hard, and didn't crack even after a couple of jumps.","Song Qiming looked at Song Jinzhao with surprise in his eyes.","\"If the main streets of Suining City are all paved with concrete, we'll never have to worry about rainy days again.\"","A dozen officials from the prefectural office cautiously walked back and forth on the concrete road, like Granny Liu visiting the Grand View Garden.","Song Jinzhao didn't dare to exert too much force. She scraped the ground with the sole of her shoe to make sure it wouldn't flake.","\"Concrete isn't just for paving roads; it can also be used to build houses, dams, and more. It's an excellent construction material.\"","Song Qiming nodded rapidly, his mind already imagining what the city would look like with all the concrete roads finished.","\"Ah Jie is really clever, but how much silver does one bag of concrete cost?\"","Sand could be found in the river, and pebbles were everywhere in the mountains—those were free. He was only worried that the concrete itself might be too expensive.","Shi Simian and the others all turned their eyes to Song Jinzhao. It was a good product, but if it cost too much, they simply couldn't afford it.","Song Jinzhao said, \"The concrete for the eight main streets we planned earlier—I'll provide it for free. You just supply the labor from the prefectural office. We can start work tomorrow.\"","As soon as she said this, everyone erupted in excitement.","It was free? That was incredible.","Song Qiming's heart sank. He was afraid Song Jinzhao would lose too much.","\"The prefectural treasury still has sufficient funds, so Ah Jie doesn't need to do this. I can pay for it.\"","Song Jinzhao smiled gently. \"The cost of making concrete is very low. I'll explain more when we get back.\"","The product was meant to make money eventually, but the profits would have to come from other avenues. These eight main streets were her way of winning people over.","Song Qiming followed Song Jinzhao to the back courtyard. A route map that had already been drawn lay before them.","\"The main costs of making concrete are labor and fuel. All told, one bag of concrete costs about fifty wen to produce.\"","\"Paving these eight main streets will cost no more than five thousand taels of silver, but it will leave a lasting impression on everyone. That's quite a bargain.\"","Song Qiming suddenly understood—Ah Jie was after the people's hearts.","The next morning, after a half-month rest, the laborers were back to heavy work.","Cartload after cartload of sand and stone were transported to the inner city. Wooden boards for fixing the forms also had to be cut from the mountain. By the end of the day, the work was even harder than the farm labor before.","The busiest street in the inner city, Tongbao Street, was the first to be renovated. Not only was the concrete road laid, but drainage ditches were also dug on both sides.","At first, the shop owners on both sides were reluctant, worried that the road closure would hurt their business. But once the first section of concrete hardened, all the rumors and complaints vanished.","Anyone with eyes could see how good the road was. What did it matter if the street was closed for ten or fifteen days? It would be so much more convenient to travel afterward.","Tongbao Street ran all the way from the south gate of the inner city to the north gate, with only a detour around the prefectural office.","By the time the second half was finished, the first half had already been in use for half a month, with astonishingly good results.","People were all asking: Which street would be renovated next? Would it reach their doorways?","Meanwhile, Song Jinzhao handed over the newly built concrete factory to Lanxi and went to buy two brick kilns.","She hadn't bought the coal mine just to fuel the concrete kilns—she planned to use it for another purpose.","Charcoal was expensive, and ordinary people couldn't afford it. Every bitter winter, some froze to death.","If a snowstorm hit and their stored firewood ran out, the death toll in the Eastern Zhao Kingdom would climb by the thousands each year. Every winter, reports of disasters filled the emperor's desk—which showed just how huge the market was.","Low-quality coal produced heavy smoke, and breathing it in could cause poisoning, so many people dared not use it.","But if Song Jinzhao could turn that coal into smokeless briquettes, the profit would reach millions."]},{"number":508,"title":"Chapter 508: Buying Up All Coal Mines in the Southwest, the New County Magistrate Is an Acquaintance","paragraphs":["Songzhou City.","“What did you say? County Princess Linghui bought all the coal mines in Songzhou?” Gu Zhongxun gripped the memorial in his hand, his face full of disbelief.","Although the imperial court did not concern itself with who owned the coal mines, the main fuel for smelting iron was coal. Given the unique geographic position of the Southwest Province, Gu Zhongxun had specifically instructed that large-scale transactions be monitored.","Gu Huaiyuan, the Prefect of Songzhou, nodded.","“The person who came was a guard of County Princess Linghui, whom I’d seen before at home. I heard they also bought coal mines in other places.”","Gu Zhongxun’s anxious heart eased, but he frowned in confusion.","“Why is she buying so many coal mines? This thing doesn’t make much silver.”","Aside from doing business, Gu Zhongxun could think of no other reason.","Gu Huaiyuan stood on tiptoe. “Should we send someone to check?”","Gu Zhongxun shook his head and handed the memorial back to him.","“Wait a few more days. Zhao Jinmin, the Magistrate of Qingxia County, is on his way to Songzhou. We’ll go together once he arrives.”","Gu Huaiyuan opened the memorial, surprise flickering in his eyes.","“It’s a scholar from Anyang Prefecture.” The Song family had originally come from Anyang Prefecture.","Gu Zhongxun nodded slightly, a hint of emotion in his expression.","“A new jinshi this year, with a rather high rank. What a pity.”","Gu Huaiyuan silently closed the memorial.","This person must have offended someone; otherwise, he wouldn’t be so unlucky.","Without family connections or backing, officials sent to the Southwest were almost never transferred away. His own father was the most typical example.","Even though Gu Zhongxun now held a high position, with no one in the Southwest outranking him, he still harbored a lingering resentment over failing to be transferred to the capital when he was younger.","Zhao Jinmin arrived quickly. Ten days later, he was in Songzhou.","Gu Zhongxun saw the anticipation in his eyes, took a deep breath, and patted Zhao Jinmin on the shoulder.","“Do your best in Qingxia County. It’s far better there than it was half a year ago.”","“Lord Song is a man of action, and since you’re both from the same hometown, he will certainly look after you.”","Zhao Jinmin smiled and bowed with clasped hands.","“Not just from the same hometown—when Lord Song achieved top scholar in Anyang Prefecture, I was in the same exam session. Later, we were even classmates.”","Gu Zhongxun raised an eyebrow in surprise.","He hadn’t expected their relationship to be so close. He had thought they were merely fellow townsmen who didn’t know each other.","“What a coincidence. After all these years, you’ve come together again.”","Though the gap between them was wide—one a prefect of the fifth rank, the other merely a magistrate of the seventh rank.","...","The people sent to purchase coal mines across the Southwest soon returned to Suining City.","In total, there were one hundred and seventy-two coal mines, large and small. The transfer documents, when stacked, stood taller than a table.","Song Jinzhao said, “Dig while repairing. Mine as much as possible while ensuring safety. This winter, I plan to make a big push.”","Although the shops opened in the capital, Anyang Prefecture, and Suining City made money every day, Song Jinzhao was also spending a great deal.","To accomplish great things, one needed tens of millions of taels of silver. Recruiting soldiers and buying horses—none of it came cheap.","Song Qiming walked in excitedly, holding a transfer order.","“Ah Jie, the new magistrate of Qingxia County is finally coming. It’s Zhao Jinmin. He passed the imperial exam and became a jinshi.”","Song Jinzhao looked up, trying to recall.","“Is that the classmate who left to observe mourning after only a few days of study?”","Song Qiming nodded slightly.","“For four generations, his ancestors were all artisans. Back then, he wanted to visit Ah Jie, but a sudden tragedy struck his family. Not only did he miss the visit, but it also delayed him for three years.”","Song Jinzhao raised an eyebrow. “Assigned to Qingxia County? Did he do poorly on the exam?”","Song Qiming shook his head meaningfully.","“He ranked thirteenth among the second-tier jinshi. With that ranking, even if he couldn’t stay in the capital, places like the Jiangnan water towns were his for the asking. Something must have gone wrong along the way.”"]},{"number":509,"title":"Chapter 509: Startled by the Cement Road","paragraphs":["Zhao Jinmin not only came himself, but brought his entire family along.","When the carriage arrived at the South Gate and they saw the straight, wide main road, everyone was stunned.","The trusted subordinate sent by Gu Zhongxun sat dumbfounded in the carriage.","He scrambled down from the carriage, feeling the hardness and smoothness beneath his feet, then looked up at the straight, broad road stretching ahead, unable to move for a long time.","The bluestone-paved streets of the capital were unparalleled, yet this road was far superior to even bluestone.","His lips trembling, he muttered to himself, \"What kind of road is this? It wasn't like this the last time I came here.\"","The constable in charge of guarding the city gate, upon hearing this, said with a face full of pride, \"This is a cement road. It was only opened for traffic a few days ago.\"","\"County Princess put up the money, and Lord Prefect led us in building it.\"","Zhao Jinmin's eyes lit up, and he pressed excitedly, \"Is that County Princess Linghui and Song Qiming?\"","The constable's brows furrowed, and he looked Zhao Jinmin up and down with displeasure.","\"Who are you people? How dare you speak the Lord Prefect's personal name?\"","Zhao Jinmin puffed out his chest, \"This official is the newly appointed magistrate of Qingxia County. I was once a classmate of your Lord Prefect.\"","The displeasure on the constable's face vanished in an instant, replaced by a burst of joy.","\"You must be Magistrate Zhao?\"","Zhao Jinmin froze, \"You know me?\"","The constables quickly cupped their fists and bowed in salute.","\"The day before yesterday, Lord Prefect specifically instructed us that you were coming and told us to keep an eye out for you.\"","Upon hearing this, Zhao Jinmin felt utterly delighted—Song Qiming hadn't forgotten him.","He gestured toward the man beside him and said to the constable, \"This is Magistrate Li of Songzhou City.\"","The constable cupped his fists and bowed his head, \"Greetings, Magistrate Li.\"","Li Zhidao pointed at the ground and asked, \"What is this 'cement' you mentioned? Who invented it?\"","The constable replied with a smile, \"County Princess Linghui did.\"","Li Zhidao lowered his hands.","The constable gestured for them to board the carriage, \"Allow me to lead the way for you two gentlemen.\"","Li Zhidao shook his head, looking dazed.","\"It's not far from here to the government office—we'll walk.\"","The smile on the constable's face stiffened for a moment.","Walking from the South Gate to the government office would take half an hour—they certainly didn't mind the fatigue.","Zhao Jinmin and Li Zhidao walked side by side in front, while the constable followed half a step behind Zhao Jinmin.","As he walked, looking at the surroundings, Li Zhidao asked, \"The side streets haven't been paved yet?\"","The constable, slightly hunched, replied, \"We need to pave eight main streets before winter. We've only just finished the first one. The side streets probably won't be done until next year.\"","Zhao Jinmin walked to the roadside and examined the drainage ditch beneath it, which was plastered with cement and very clean.","\"How much does this cement road cost?\"","The constable scratched his head, \"We dug the sand and stones ourselves. The cement was donated by County Princess. I hear it's not expensive, but I don't know the exact amount in silver.\"","After about two ke of walking, they saw people working on a road near an intersection.","Li Zhidao and Zhao Jinmin stopped and went over to take a look.","As far as the eye could see, everyone was busy.","There were people mixing, paving, and nailing boards, with constables and corvée laborers each making up half the workforce.","The two men stood there watching for a long time before leaving.","It didn't look difficult—it was all about the materials.","Halfway there, Li Zhidao could no longer walk. At the constable's suggestion, they climbed back into the carriage, and the pace picked up again.","The group stopped at the entrance of the government office. By the time Song Qiming learned of their arrival, they were already in the second hall.","\"Brother Zhao.\" Song Qiming stepped over the threshold and paused, his voice rising loudly.","Zhao Jinmin turned his head, and the moment he clearly saw the other's face, the teacup in his hand nearly tipped over.","He quickly stood up and called out, \"Brother Song.\"","Seeing the two of them acting like reunited old friends, Li Zhidao couldn't help but envy Zhao Jinmin's good fortune.","With such a superior, if Zhao Jinmin ever encountered any difficulties in Qingxia County, Song Qiming would surely help out.","And when Song Qiming was later promoted back to the capital, he might even recommend Zhao Jinmin, possibly getting him transferred out of the Southwest."]},{"number":510,"title":"Chapter 510: It Was Because of Refusing Marriage","paragraphs":["As they were about to sit face to face, Song Qiming finally shifted his gaze to the woman seated beside him.","Zhao Jinmin was the only son in his family... Could it be that—","Noticing his look, Zhao Jinmin walked over to the woman.","With a face full of tenderness, he introduced her to Song Qiming: “This is my humble wife, Madam Wang. We just married after the imperial examinations.”","Song Qiming raised his brows in surprise. “So this is my sister-in-law. What a pity I missed your wedding feast.”","After a few pleasantries, Song Qiming arranged for everyone except Zhao Jinmin to rest at the official inn.","Alone in the room with just the two of them, Song Qiming asked bluntly, “Brother Zhao, why have you come to the southwest?”","The expression on Zhao Jinmin’s face instantly fell, and he lowered his head with a sigh.","“I was just unlucky. After the palace examination, Prime Minister Gu Qishan wanted me to marry his granddaughter, but I had a fiancée at the time, so I refused.”","“Who would have thought he’d later take revenge and send me to Qingxia County as magistrate.”","Song Qiming suddenly understood. “So that’s how it is.”","There was a look of regret in his eyes as he gazed at Zhao Jinmin.","What a pity he hadn’t been in the capital back then, or he could have helped.","Zhao Jinmin forced a smile and perked up. “But it’s fine now. Knowing you’re in Suining City puts my mind at ease.”","Having his direct superior be an old schoolmate would save him so much trouble in the future.","Thinking of the concrete road he had seen upon entering the city, Zhao Jinmin straightened his back and scooted his chair back slightly.","“I saw the concrete road just now. Can Qingxia County build one too?”","Song Qiming replied, “Once the inner city is finished, we’ll pave the outer city, then the official road from Suining Prefecture to Songzhou City, and after that, the roads connecting the four counties. What happens within the county will be up to you to figure out.”","Zhao Jinmin understood—this meant the county government would have to foot the bill.","“Can we buy cement? How much does it cost per li of road?”","Song Qiming shook his head. “Not yet. The cement factory was just built, so production is still limited. Ah Jie is planning to recruit more workers. In about two months, there should be extra to sell.”","Zhao Jinmin chuckled. “Magistrate Li brought it up twice earlier, and you shut him down both times. He’s probably not going to give up.”","Song Qiming leaned back in his chair, fearless.","“I didn’t invent cement, and the factory isn’t mine either. Everything depends on Ah Jie’s arrangements.”","Zhao Jinmin’s expression turned sorrowful again.","“I had wanted my father to meet the County Princess before, but I never expected he’d pass so soon.”","Song Qiming wasn’t sure how to comfort him.","“Come over for dinner tonight. You’ll get to see my sister then.”","No sooner had Zhao Jinmin set foot in the inn than Li Zhidao came over to pry for information.","“I never expected Magistrate Zhao and Prefect Song to be so close. From now on, this humble official will have to rely on your guidance.”","Zhao Jinmin quickly stepped back to avoid the flattery.","“Magistrate Li is a trusted man of the Provincial Administration Commissioner. Someone like me, a mere county magistrate, hardly needs your reliance. It’s just that we haven’t seen each other in many years, and it stirred up some emotions.”","Li Zhidao pressed on as they walked, “You spoke for quite a while. Did you mention cement at all?”","Wanting to discourage Li Zhidao from troubling Song Qiming further, Zhao Jinmin revealed the limited production truth.","“Lord Song said cement output is limited. County Princess Linghui plans to recruit more people. There won’t be extra to sell until next year.”","“Next year? That’s way too slow!” Li Zhidao exclaimed.","Everyone wanted good things. Songzhou City outranked Suining City, so its roads should be paved first.","Zhao Jinmin shrugged.","“There’s nothing to be done about the high demand. We’ll just have to wait.”","Li Zhidao asked, “Did he mention how much a bag of cement will sell for?”","Zhao Jinmin shook his head. “They haven’t set a price yet since they haven’t started selling. The cement factory is the County Princess Linghui’s personal property, so everything depends on her decision.”","Li Zhidao deflated. He still hadn’t asked about the coal mine, and now cement had cropped up. He needed to report back to the Provincial Administration Commissioner as soon as possible."]},{"number":511,"title":"Chapter 511: Only Twenty-Three Copies Sold in Three Days","paragraphs":["In the evening, Zhao Jinmin and his wife were invited to dine in the back courtyard of the government office, and Li Zhidao accompanied them as well.","Seeing Song Jinzhao standing beneath the eaves, Zhao Jinmin couldn’t help but pause.","She stood like a solitary figure detached from the world, her gaze calm yet exuding a cool aloofness, as if nothing in this mortal realm was worth her time—a presence that inspired awe.","Madam Wang noticed he had stopped and nudged his arm gently, asking in a low voice, “What’s wrong?”","Zhao Jinmin shook his head quickly but subtly. “Nothing. Just suddenly felt a bit nervous.”","Following her husband’s gaze, Madam Wang’s heart tightened.","That was the County Princess Linghui, personally enfeoffed by the emperor.","At that very moment, Song Jinzhao turned her head and looked in their direction. Her gaze met Madam Wang’s, and a faint smile curled at the corners of her mouth.","Zhao Jinmin and Li Zhidao: “Your humble officials, Zhao Jinmin and Li Zhidao, pay respects to the County Princess.”","Madam Wang curtsied. “May the County Princess Linghui be at peace.”","Song Jinzhao extended her hand. “No need for formalities.”","At the dinner table, Song Anhao ate while quietly observing.","Sitting at a table with strangers, he felt a bit restrained.","Amid the clinking of glasses, Li Zhidao casually inquired, “Recently, the County Princess has been sending people to purchase coal mines on a large scale in the southwestern region. May I ask what purpose this serves?”","Song Qiming replied, “The vegetation around Suining City is relatively sparse, with little firewood. The coal is for burning to make cement.”","Li Zhidao’s eyes lit up with understanding, and the worry that had been weighing on his chest instantly dissipated.","His brows curved into a smile, revealing six teeth. “So that’s it. With so much coal, you’ll certainly be able to produce plenty of cement.”","“This trip has truly opened my eyes. When I return and report to the Provincial Administrator, perhaps Songzhou City will also want to buy cement.”","Song Jinzhao curled her lips. “Once production ramps up, we’ll sell it externally. If you want any, just have Lord Gu send a letter.”","Freebies were out of the question. After the eight main streets were finished next year, anyone else wanting cement would have to pay for it.","Zhao Jinmin left Suining City the next morning. No sooner had he departed than Li Zhidao rushed back to Songzhou City at full speed on horseback.","...","After ten thousand copies of The Cry for Justice were printed, Song Anhao’s heart felt like it had sprouted wings, beating with anticipation.","He was both excited and nervous, dreaming of the book becoming a bestseller, with lines of customers clamoring to buy it and prompting another print run.","But reality dealt him a heavy blow.","From excitement to numbness, then to doubt, and finally to squatting on the ground in silence—it took only three days.","He couldn’t figure it out. The book was clearly good, so why was no one buying it?","Watching the eight-year-old Young Master, the bookshop owner’s heart softened involuntarily.","He spoke gently to console him. “Liu Ziyuan is a newcomer without a reputation. Good books take time to spread. Once feedback circulates over a few days, sales will naturally pick up.”","Song Anhao looked up. “Really? But only twenty-three copies have been sold so far.”","The bookshop owner coughed out a laugh. “There aren’t many scholars in Suining City to begin with. Why not ship some to Songzhou City to sell?”","Song Anhao pressed his lips together without a word. He had considered selling elsewhere, but only after the book had passed the test of Suining City’s locals.","Now, with such poor results, he had no confidence.","Song Anhao trudged home with a heavy heart, hoping to find Song Jinzhao. But when he realized she wasn’t around, his spirits sank even further.","The brick kiln had been repurposed by Song Jinzhao to burn smokeless coal.","Staring at the whitened coal briquettes in the furnace, Song Jinzhao turned to Qingshuang and said, “Tomorrow the cement factory will start recruiting workers. Based on the output I mentioned, calculate how many more people we need. Discuss it with Lanxi and handle the hiring together.”","Qingshuang pulled a piece of paper from her bosom and handed it over.","“I’ve already calculated. I plan to hire five hundred people first.”","Song Jinzhao glanced at the paper.","“If there’s a crowd of applicants, add another two hundred. Have them work day and night shifts in rotation. Doubling the output will ensure we don’t struggle to sell in winter.”","Qingshuang: “Understood.”"]},{"number":512,"title":"Chapter 512: Advertising Requires Strategy Too","paragraphs":["Song Anhao crouched at the doorway, practically straining his eyes with anticipation. Yao Ying urged him several times to go back inside and sit down, but he refused.","“Even if I sat, I wouldn’t be at ease. I’ll wait right here for Elder Sister to return.”","Earlier, to create the movable-type printing press, he had spent two thousand taels of silver. Now that the books were printed but couldn’t be sold, Song Anhao was frantic with worry.","After leaving the coal factory, Song Jinzhao had gone on to inspect eight shops in the city. By the time she returned to the government office, the sun was nearly setting.","Hearing the sound of hooves approaching, Song Anhao snapped his head up.","When he saw that it was Song Jinzhao, he immediately stood up from the ground—but having crouched for so long, his legs were numb from the knees down the moment he took a step.","Fortunately, Yao Ying was quick to steady him, or he would have tumbled down the steps.","“Elder Sister~” he called, his voice drawing out the last syllable as he shot toward her like a firecracker.","Song Jinzhao dismounted and caught him. “What’s wrong?”","His eyelids drooped; clearly, he was upset.","Song Anhao tilted his chin up, turning his face toward her.","“I printed ten thousand copies of The Cry of Injustice, but in three days on the shelves, I’ve only sold twenty-three. It’s a huge loss.”","Song Jinzhao raised an eyebrow in surprise.","She had read the book herself and expected it to sell well.","Taking his hand, she led him into the study.","“How many bookshops in the city did you approach to sell it?”","Song Anhao’s eyelids sagged like a balloon pricked by a needle.","“I reached out to three bookshops, and I even printed flyers to hand out on the streets, but no one bought it.”","Song Jinzhao asked, “What about the flyers? Let me see them.”","Yao Ying, standing nearby, immediately produced a flyer and placed it in front of Song Jinzhao.","The entire sheet was covered in neat, tiny script. It was dizzying to look at and gave no desire to read.","“How many copies of the flyer did you print, and who did you give them to?”","Song Anhao blinked.","“I printed five thousand copies and distributed them only in the inner city. Manager Lou said plenty of people fought to take them.”","Song Jinzhao slapped the flyer down onto the desk.","“In Suining City, fewer than one in ten people are literate. You handed out five thousand flyers randomly on the streets—were they supposed to grab them for use in the latrine?”","Song Anhao was taken aback. “But before, you always handed them out on the streets.”","Song Jinzhao replied, “Food and clothing are necessities, regardless of literacy. But someone who can’t read will never buy a book.”","“You need to distribute these flyers where scholars gather. Otherwise, it’s all wasted effort.”","She held the flyer up, facing Song Anhao. “And this flyer of yours lacks any novelty—there’s no desire to keep reading it.”","“Advertising needs to highlight a key point and leave a lasting impression. You have to first draw readers in, leaving them restless for the ending, so they have no choice but to buy the book.”","Song Anhao fell into thought.","“Elder Sister means I should print part of the book on the flyer?”","Song Jinzhao nodded. “You could print the first half of the first story from The Cry of Injustice on the bottom half of the flyer. Anyone who wants to know the ending will have to buy the book.”","“In Suining City, sales will top out at a few thousand copies at most. You need to expand to Songzhou City and even south of the Yangtze River. Once Liu Ziyuan’s reputation is established, his next book will have no trouble selling.”","Song Anhao leaned back in his chair, staring at the ceiling beams in deep thought for a long time.","What Elder Sister said made sense, but...","He bit his lip and looked at Song Jinzhao sheepishly.","“Doing all that costs money, and the bookshop’s accounts are already empty.”","Since buying the bookshop, he had asked Elder Sister for three thousand taels of silver in installments. He could barely bring himself to ask again.","Song Jinzhao calmly took out a key.","She opened the small cabinet under the desk, pulled out a five-hundred-tael banknote, and handed it to Song Anhao.","“Keep it as a loan. Pay me back when you make a profit.”","Compared to restaurants and taverns, a bookshop was a long-term investment and would serve a bigger purpose later.","Song Anhao hesitantly took the banknote, worried he might not be able to repay it.","“Elder Sister, you mentioned earlier you wanted to meet Liu Ziyuan. The second volume of The Cry of Injustice is due for submission the day after tomorrow. Want to come along?”","Remembering her earlier suspicions about Liu Ziyuan’s identity, Song Jinzhao nodded.","“Morning or afternoon?”","Song Anhao’s mood lifted slightly. “Noon. We’re meeting for a meal at a restaurant.”","Song Jinzhao said, “Alright. We’ll go together.”"]},{"number":513,"title":"Chapter 513: Job Recruitment: A Massive Crowd of People Lining Up","paragraphs":["After Tongbao Street's concrete road was built, half of the city's vendors rushed to set up stalls there, and in the morning, folks from outside the city also came.","Straw mats were spread out, piles of fresh vegetables still glistening with dew were stacked one after another, and loud cries of hawking rose and fell in waves.","Captain Liu Hucheng, with a sabre slung over his shoulder, walked from one end of the street to the other, counting three to four hundred people.","\"These past few days, quite a few folks have been squabbling over stalls, and some have even come to blows. You must keep your eyes peeled and step in the moment you spot trouble.\"","The yamen runners he'd cautioned nodded quickly. \"Rest assured, Boss. We're patrolling non-stop now, afraid someone might start a fight.\"","Another yamen runner nearby couldn't help but grumble.","\"If you ask me, the prefect should start charging stall fees. That would thin out the crowd and bring in some extra revenue for the yamen.\"","Liu Hucheng stopped in his tracks and glared at him.","\"Since when does the prefect need you to tell him how to do his job?\"","\"Half of these people are from outside the city. They earn just a few coppers selling vegetables all morning. You want to charge them what?\"","The runner was left speechless.","Liu Hucheng rolled his eyes and scolded, \"Once the concrete roads at the East and West Gates are finished, they'll spread out there. It'll only take a few days.\"","As the sun crept higher, many who hadn't managed to sell their goods began packing up and heading out.","\"Recruiting workers at the cement plant and coal plant outside the city.\"","\"Coal miners, porters, stokers—men and women welcome, ages eighteen to fifty-five, strong and healthy preferred...\"","The moment they heard the word \"recruiting,\" young and old, men and women with bamboo baskets on their backs or carrying shoulder poles, rushed forward like mad.","By the time they spotted the recruits, two tables already had queues stretching over ten meters.","People stood on tiptoe, craning their necks forward, desperate for their turn.","Many dashed over and grabbed passersby at random, asking, \"Hey lad, what kind of work is this?\"","\"Where's the job? How much is the pay? Do they provide meals?\"","Others squeezed to the front to read the notice pasted on the wall, but they couldn't understand it—only noticed the numbers thirty and twenty.","The bolder ones turned to the supervisor sitting behind the table and asked, \"Sir overseer, is the daily wage thirty coppers?\"","The supervisor glanced up quickly.","\"For the day shift, men earn thirty coppers a day, women twenty coppers. Work starts at the beginning of the chen hour and ends at the end of the shen hour, with one meal provided at noon.\"","\"For the night shift, men earn thirty-five coppers a day, women twenty-five coppers. Work starts at the beginning of the xu hour and ends at the end of the yin hour, also with one meal provided.\"","The man's eyes lit up. \"Is it permanent or temporary work?\"","The supervisor: \"Permanent. Wages are paid monthly.\"","Word spread like wildfire. Soon, the South Gate was packed with people queuing up, some registering for their elders and brothers.","The line grew longer and longer until, by midday, it nearly reached the outer city gate.","Song Jinzhao stood on the city wall with a telescope, watching as more people kept streaming in at the end of the line.","\"Bring twenty more tables, or we'll be stuck here till dark and still not finish.\"","Lanxi turned and hurried downstairs.","The sea of people was so dense it seemed the whole of Suining City had showed up. Qingshuang hesitated before speaking.","\"County Princess, we can't hire this many people.\"","According to the original plan, the cement plant and coal plant were to recruit 1,500 workers in total. It seemed they'd already filled that up in just one morning.","But Song Jinzhao had already made up her mind.","\"Double the size of both plants, and assign twice as many people to keep watch.\"","Qingshuang nodded in acknowledgment. \"I'll see to it right away, Miss.\"","After finishing his official duties, Song Qiming came over to watch the excitement.","As he looked at the common people lining up one by one to register for jobs, his eyes were filled with joy, and his heart was overjoyed.","During the slack farming season, it wasn't that the people didn't want to work; they simply couldn't find any work.","Now that the cement factory and the coal factory were hiring, the people would have income and their lives would improve.","No one was more eager than Song Qiming to see the people of Suining City become prosperous."]},{"number":514,"title":"Chapter 514: Meeting Liu Ziyuan","paragraphs":["On the first day, the number of applicants exceeded two thousand. After excluding those who did not meet the age or physical condition requirements, there were still one thousand five hundred people left.","Afraid they might not be able to register the next day, many would rather spend the night there than leave.","Lanxi and Qingshuang returned to the government office and handed the roster to Song Jinzhao for review.","\"Today, a total of one thousand five hundred and thirty-one people registered, including three hundred and twenty-one women.\"","Song Jinzhao roughly flipped through the household registrations of these people. They came from both the inner and outer city, and about half were from nearby villages.","\"Arrange the women for the day shift. If there are parents, brothers, or husbands signing up together, try to assign them to the same factory whenever possible.\"","Understanding the deeper intent, Qingshuang immediately nodded in agreement. \"I understand, ma'am.\"","Working in a place mostly occupied by men, staying with family would help avoid a lot of gossip and rumors.","The next day, Song Anhao dragged Song Jinzhao to the restaurant to meet Liu Ziyuan.","Only a day had passed, and his mood was noticeably better than before.","In the carriage, Song Anhao smiled as she shared an update with Song Jinzhao.","\"I asked Manager Lou to reprint the flyers and hand them out in front of academies and private schools. Yesterday combined with this morning, we sold seventy-one copies. The situation is much better than before.\"","Song Jinzhao nodded in satisfaction.","\"If it's effective, keep it up. Are you planning to ship the books to Songzhou City for sale anytime soon? Do you need your elder sister's help?\"","Song Anhao shook her head in refusal.","\"No need for now. Manager Lou knows quite a few bookstore owners in Songzhou City, so he'll go there in person tomorrow.\"","The carriage stopped at the entrance of the restaurant. The waiter, wearing a white cloth towel, lit up the moment he saw Song Anhao step off the carriage.","He hurried over to greet her, grinning so wide his mouth nearly reached his ears.","\"We just got a few pounds of live shrimp in the back kitchen today. We've been waiting for you, Second Young Master Song!\"","Song Anhao asked him, \"Has Young Master Liu arrived yet?\"","But when his gaze swept over Song Jinzhao emerging from the carriage, the waiter began to stammer.","\"He arrived a quarter of an hour ago. He's in the private room on the second floor.\"","\"Greetings to County Princess Linghui.\"","\"No need for formalities.\" Song Jinzhao smoothed down her skirt and glanced at him lightly.","Led up to the second floor, the waiter pushed open the door to the private room. Inside, Liu Ziyuan quickly stood up and greeted Song Anhao.","\"Second Young Master Song.\"","Song Anhao stepped aside with a smile and said, \"My elder sister wants to meet you.\"","Realizing who the newcomer was, Liu Ziyuan's heartbeat began to race.","\"Your humble servant Liu Ziyuan greets County Princess Linghui.\"","Song Jinzhao said, \"No need for formalities. Let's all sit down.\"","The three of them took their seats. Song Anhao looked up and ordered the waiter, \"Bring a serving of that fresh shrimp you mentioned, plus a few of the signature dishes.\"","Liu Ziyuan, feeling uneasy under Song Jinzhao's steady gaze, found it hard to sit still. Even the pain in his right foot, where he was missing some toes, began to throb faintly.","Sensing the awkward silence, Song Anhao gestured toward Liu Ziyuan.","\"Quick, show my elder sister your copy of The Cry for Justice II. She said your writing is excellent.\"","Knowing that County Princess Linghui was pleased with him, Liu Ziyuan's anxious heart settled slightly.","He fumbled for the book on the stool beside him and gently placed it in front of Song Jinzhao.","The pages were bound together with rough white thread, a very crude method.","\"My humble work, written in my spare time. It is my honor that the County Princess would deign to look upon it.\"","Song Jinzhao picked up the book, turning over the first page with a light smile as she praised Liu Ziyuan.","\"Young Master Liu, you need not be overly modest. A work so logically rigorous and captivating can hardly be called a humble effort.\"","Unable to wait any longer for Song Jinzhao to finish, Song Anhao slid her seat closer to the neighboring chair and craned her neck to read along with her.","The second installment retained the style of the first, but the narrative had become more polished, showing that Liu Ziyuan's storytelling skills had improved."]},{"number":515,"title":"Chapter 515: Definitely Not a Time Traveler, the Girl Who Stopped the Carriage","paragraphs":["After finishing the first story, Song Jinzhao handed the manuscript to Song Anhao.","\"Master Liu has a unique narrative style—many parts feel as if they were experienced firsthand.\"","Liu Ziyuan replied respectfully, \"To be honest with you, County Princess, the elder next door was once a coroner. When I was young, I often heard him tell stories.\"","Song Jinzhao nodded knowingly. \"I see.\"","She probed lightly, \"I recall that in government records, there was a coroner surnamed Holmes. I found it strange at the time—I wonder if it’s the same person?\"","Liu Ziyuan stared blankly, his eyes wide with confusion.","\"Holmes? That surname doesn’t seem to be from our Eastern Zhao Kingdom.\"","\"Our entire village is surnamed Liu. The elder next door is named Liu Zhaoxian—definitely not the same person.\"","Seeing that his reaction didn’t seem like a lie, Song Jinzhao had her answer in mind.","Liu Ziyuan probably wasn’t a time traveler; the similarity in his writing style was just a coincidence.","\"Perhaps he was surnamed Fu, and previous records got it wrong.\"","She casually brushed off the topic and turned to look at Song Anhao, who had just closed the book.","\"The plot was full of twists and turns, and the reversal was simply brilliant—Master Liu’s writing has truly improved.\"","\"Not at all, it’s merely practice making perfect.\" Liu Ziyuan spoke modestly, but his eyes betrayed a hint of confidence and pride.","Having confirmed that Liu Ziyuan wasn’t a time traveler, Song Jinzhao lost interest in staying longer and planned to leave after the meal.","As she descended to the first floor, a gaze fell upon her, catching her attention.","With a slight sweep of her eyes, Qingshuang immediately lowered her head to scan the surroundings.","A young girl, simply dressed and no more than a teenager, was hiding behind a pillar, secretly watching Song Jinzhao.","Returning to the carriage as if nothing was wrong, after driving a short distance, the girl was still following them.","\"County Princess, she’s the only one around, and she runs very slowly.\"","Song Jinzhao stopped Song Anhao, who was trying to look outside.","\"Keep going. I want to know what she’s up to.\"","Song Anhao looked up. \"Elder Sister, is someone following us?\"","Song Jinzhao tapped his temple to scold him.","\"Don’t think that just because we have guards, you can let your guard down. Stay alert in everything you do.\"","The carriage turned twice, and the figure behind them vanished.","Qingshuang reported, \"County Princess, she didn’t keep up.\"","The carriage wasn’t going fast on the street, yet she still couldn’t keep pace—clearly, the girl knew no martial arts and had poor stamina.","On the other side, realizing she couldn’t catch the carriage, Liu Ruoxi gasped for breath and darted into a nearby alley. After winding through several turns, she dashed out in front of the carriage on another street.","Seeing someone suddenly rush out, Yao Ying yanked hard on the reins, causing the horse to rear up with a sharp neigh, its front hooves lifting into the air.","Song Jinzhao grabbed the window frame with her left hand and stopped Song Anhao, who was stumbling toward her, with her right.","Recognizing the girl’s face, Qingshuang’s brows furrowed in irritation, almost pinching a fly.","\"What do you think you’re doing?\"","The sharp interrogation made Liu Ruoxi’s face turn pale.","Trembling, she spoke, \"My name is Liu Ruoxi. I’m Liu Ziyuan’s younger sister. I need to speak with County Princess Linghui.\"","Hearing that she was Liu Ziyuan’s sister, Qingshuang froze.","Looking closely, there was indeed a slight resemblance between their features.","She softened her tone slightly. \"What business do you have with the County Princess?\"","Liu Ruoxi pulled a stack of bound papers from her chest, the cover bright red.","\"I’ve written a story manuscript, and I’d like the County Princess to take a look.\"","Hearing it was another story manuscript, Song Anhao was the first to lift the carriage curtain and step out.","\"Since it’s a story, let me have a look.\"","Liu Ruoxi stepped back, pressing the manuscript against her chest.","\"You can’t read it. It has to be for the County Princess.\""]},{"number":516,"title":"Chapter 516: Ten Thousand Times More Profitable Than \"The Cry of Injustice\"","paragraphs":["The girl's eyes, full of rejection, puzzled Song Anhao.","He planted his hands on his hips and demanded righteous indignation: \"Your brother always shows me his manuscripts first. Why not you?\"","Liu Ruoxi bit her lip, her eyes shimmering with unshed tears.","\"You're too young. This book isn't for you.\"","Her gaze darted nervously toward the carriage. Seeing that the curtain showed no sign of being drawn back, Liu Ruoxi's heart sank.","She swallowed hard, her fists clenching and unclenching, her palms drenched in sweat.","Unwilling to let this chance slip away, she mustered her courage and dropped to her knees, shouting toward Song Jinzhao inside the carriage.","\"I wrote this manuscript more suited for female readers. Please, County Princess Linghui, give me a chance!\"","Her knees hit the ground with a thud that sounded painful.","Song Jinzhao lifted the carriage curtain and instructed Yao Ying, \"Pull over to the side of the road.\"","\"Qingshuang, bring me her manuscript.\"","Liu Ruoxi looked at Song Jinzhao with delight.","After Qingshuang took the manuscript, the group walked to the roadside and stopped.","Song Anhao crossed his arms, pouting unhappily.","\"I may be young, but I've grown up.\"","Liu Ruoxi stayed silent, her eyes fixed unblinkingly on Song Jinzhao's face, her heart tight with both hope and anxiety.","The bright red book cover looked as if it had been dyed with blood.","When the cover was opened, it described the rear courtyard of some official's household in Jiangnan, the protagonist being the legitimate eldest daughter—a typical internal family strife novel.","Song Jinzhao grew intrigued and leaned against the carriage to turn to the next page.","Time ticked by. Song Anhao couldn't contain his curiosity and climbed up to peek.","The moment his head leaned over, Song Jinzhao suddenly snapped the manuscript shut, her cheeks flushing.","Startled by her abrupt movement, Song Anhao exclaimed in confusion, \"Sister?\"","Song Jinzhao pressed her lips together, her lashes fluttering rapidly.","\"You're still too young. This book isn't suitable for you.\"","She cast a curious glance at Liu Ruoxi and asked, \"Are you married?\"","As if she knew why Song Jinzhao was asking, Liu Ruoxi looked down at the ground, embarrassed, and shook her head.","\"Not yet.\"","Song Jinzhao raised an eyebrow. She must have seen quite a few erotic paintings to describe a wedding night in such detail.","\"Have you shown this book to your brother?\"","The embarrassment on her face faded, replaced by sorrow flooding her heart.","Her voice choked as she said, \"He read a bit, scolded me, and tore it up. This is the version I rewrote.\"","\"He said a woman should follow the Three Obediences and Four Virtues, should not be jealous or do evil, and that my writing was nonsense, disgraceful, and worse than waste paper.\"","Every day I hid while writing, afraid of being discovered. For a month, I've been constantly on edge, often having nightmares of being scolded and waking up in terror.","If not for that stubborn fire in my gut, I would have quit long ago.\"","The more he heard, the more suspicious Song Anhao became. His eyes fell on the bright red book cover.","What the hell was in it?","Song Jinzhao instructed Qingshuang: \"Find a nearby teahouse to sit down. I want to finish reading this book.\"","Page by page, Song Jinzhao sat in the teahouse for an entire afternoon.","It wasn't until the sun slanted westward that she closed the last page.","It was a classic fast-paced female-oriented palace rivalry revenge novel—sweet with a touch of bitterness, depressed yet cathartic, utterly unputdownable.","\"Did you come up with all the content in this book yourself?\"","Liu Ziyuan's family was poor; Liu Ruoxi definitely hadn't experienced life in wealthy households, let alone official ones.","Liu Ruoxi replied sheepishly, \"A few plots came from gossip about rich families in Suining City that I spruced up a bit. The rest I imagined myself.\"","Song Jinzhao's eyes sparkled, as if she were looking at a long-buried young genius, a gleaming gold nugget.","Stories come from life, but being able to write them down is a gift—and she did it brilliantly. This book was ten thousand times more addictive than The Cry for Justice.","Song Jinzhao could guarantee that once this book hit the shelves, it would sell out entirely. Its readership would range from thirty-something housewives to teenage girls experiencing their first stirrings of love—a massive market."]},{"number":517,"title":"Chapter 517: Song Anhao's Questioning","paragraphs":["Liu Ruoxi's limbs trembled as she clutched the contract and the banknotes.","She never expected Song Jinzhao to agree to sell her book so quickly—and to look so excited about it.","Back at the teahouse, Song Anhao asked with a pitiful look, \"Elder sister, is this storybook really that good?\"","Song Jinzhao replied, \"It just appeals to a different audience. Maybe Liu Ruoxi will stir up a whirlwind in the world of storybooks.\"","She handed the manuscript to Song Anhao. \"Have someone proofread it, then print it. Preferably ship it to Songzhou City along with The Cry for Justice.\"","Hearing this, Song Anhao felt even more aggrieved. When he had recommended The Cry for Justice earlier, his elder sister hadn't valued it this much.","Not long after returning to the government office, a message arrived from the hidden guards stationed in Panzhou.","The day before Yang Cenan returned to Panzhou, the twin infants of his elder brother Yang Cedong—barely a month old—had suddenly died.","Song Jinzhao tapped the table meaningfully. \"A month old and they die suddenly? That must have been some nasty cold.\"","Qingshuang lowered her gaze and spoke in a solemn voice.","\"Yang Cenan is taking revenge. He hadn't even reached Panzhou when the incident occurred, and he was badly injured himself. No one would suspect him.\"","Song Jinzhao said, \"In any case, the Yang family is bound to fall into chaos. Have the hidden guards keep a close watch.\"","Qingshuang nodded. \"Rest assured, County Princess. We already have one of our men stationed inside the Yang residence.\"","Bringing the manuscript to the bookshop, Song Anhao couldn't hold back his curiosity any longer.","He leaned against the wall, pulled up a stool, and sat down.","He opened to the first page. The descriptions were dull.","After finishing the first page—really not impressive.","By the end of the first chapter, he couldn't bear to read on.","Closing the book, he stared at the cover with a skeptical look.","The writing was mediocre. The immersion was mediocre. Why did his elder sister think it was any good?","Unable to figure it out, Song Anhao decided to ask someone else.","He summoned Manager Lou and handed him the manuscript. \"Tell me what you think of this book.\"","Seeing that it wasn't the sequel to The Cry for Justice, Manager Lou grew suspicious.","Hadn't she said she'd bring back the second part today? Why was this a different book?","Opening the cover, he found it belonged to a completely different category.","After reading the first page, Manager Lou couldn't help but settle down seriously.","Unlike Song Anhao, he had been in this trade for years. He had read plenty of storybooks enjoyed by women.","Whether a book was good or not—you could tell from the first page.","After finishing the first three chapters, Manager Lou slowly closed the book.","\"The storybooks women usually read in the market are about immortals and mortals, immortals and demons, or noble ladies and poor scholars—the bigger the class gap, the better. This book is different from all of them.\"","Song Anhao pressed, \"I just want to know—will people buy it?\"","Manager Lou thought long and hard, struggling to make a decision.","\"There's never been a book like this on the market. It's hard for me to say. Maybe print a thousand copies to test the waters?\"","Song Anhao frowned, deeply dissatisfied with this answer.","\"My elder sister said this book should be shipped to Songzhou City along with The Cry for Justice. We need to print at least ten thousand copies.\"","Manager Lou raised the manuscript in surprise.","\"Is this a recommendation from County Princess Linghui?\"","Song Anhao nodded.","\"My elder sister said this book will become a hit—even bigger than The Cry for Justice.\"","Manager Lou blinked. \"Since County Princess Linghui favors it, let's print it.\"","Song Anhao turned to him in exasperation.","\"Can't you have an opinion of your own?\"","Manager Lou gave an awkward, flattering smile.","\"The County Princess is wise. How could I dare to say a single 'no'?\"","Having an opinion depended on who it was about. Besides the County Princess Linghui's noble status, purely on the grounds of business, Manager Lou felt he had no right to refuse.","Song Anhao's irritation faded somewhat, and instead he started lecturing Manager Lou.","\"I expect you wouldn't dare.\"","He snatched the book back and began reading it again.","His elder sister was brilliant and always knew how to make money. If the story seemed boring, it must be because he hadn't understood it correctly.","To his disappointment, he still couldn't get through the first three chapters.","And when he reached the chapter about the male and female lead's wedding, his brows furrowed even tighter.","He tilted his head, pondered for a moment, then finally tossed the book aside in disgust.","\"What kind of nonsense is this? Making such a big deal out of taking off clothes and going to bed is just gross.\"","Manager Lou stared at him, opening his mouth as if to say something, but decided against explaining.","The child was only eight—still too young to understand. Better that he stayed clueless for now.","Picking up the book, Manager Lou asked quietly, \"So how many copies should we print?\"","Song Anhao thought for only a second. \"Since my elder sister said so, print ten thousand copies first. Get the promotional flyers made as soon as possible.\"","\"Leave five hundred copies in the bookstore. Ship the rest to Songzhou City.\""]},{"number":518,"title":"Chapter 518: Gifts from Panzhou","paragraphs":["Li Zhidao, a trusted subordinate of Gu Zhongxun, promptly reported everything he had seen and heard upon returning to Songzhou City.","“My lord need not worry. County Princess Linghui purchased the coal mine to burn materials for making a substance called cement, which is used for road construction.”","“When I arrived at Suining Prefecture, the main road leading to the government office was already completed. The road was both smooth and hard, even surpassing the stone-paved streets of the capital in quality.”","He clasped his hands in a salute and proposed: “In my humble opinion, we should have Song Qiming transport all the cement to Songzhou City. If roads are to be built, we should build ours first.”","Gu Zhongxun asked skeptically, “Is the cement road really that good?”","Li Zhidao patted his chest in assurance: “It’s only slightly inferior to the white marble roads of the imperial palace.”","Gu Zhongxun’s curiosity was thoroughly piqued.","“The grain tax reported by Song Qiming is half a percent higher than last year, and commercial taxes these past few months have also seen noticeable growth. Perhaps I should visit Suining City by the end of the year.”","Li Zhidao’s eyes lit up like two sparks of candle flame.","“They plan to complete eight main streets before winter sets in. If you go then, the changes will surely be even more significant.”","“County Princess Linghui said that cement production is insufficient this year; surpluses won’t be available for sale until next year. My lord could ask for it when you visit.”","Gu Zhongxun shook his head with a laugh.","“Since the County Princess Linghui intends to sell it, she won’t give it away for free. By then, we’ll certainly have to pay silver for it.”","Li Zhidao’s lips moved hesitantly, but he swallowed his words after a long pause.","Some things were better left unsaid. If the County Princess Linghui found out and grew angry, even Lord Gu might not be able to protect him.","Gu Zhongxun finally decided to leave for Suining City in early November. Any later, and the snow would make travel difficult.","...","Gazing at the courtyard filled with red lacquered chests, Song Qiming opened one at random and found a pair of exquisitely crafted famille rose vases with double ears.","The contents of the other chests were all equally valuable.","“What are all these things?” he asked the maidservant.","His elder sister never bought so many impractical decorative items at once; these must have been gifts.","Could the wealthy merchants of Suining City have come bearing gifts?","The maidservant curtsied slightly and replied: “They were brought by someone from Panzhou. The County Princess is receiving the guests in the main hall.”","“Why wasn’t I informed?” Song Qiming asked, his eyes full of surprise.","Someone from Panzhou had arrived, and he, as the prefect, knew nothing about it.","The maidservant replied: “The visitor requested to see the County Princess and Second Miss Song. The gifts were brought in through the side gate, and you were not at the government office at the time.”","Song Qiming walked into the main hall with a serious expression and found the visitor dressed in the attire of a steward, neither a civil nor military official.","Upon seeing Song Qiming enter, the steward guessed his identity and bowed.","“Your humble subject, Yang Mo, pays respects to the Prefect.”","Song Jinzhao gestured for Song Qiming to sit down.","The man was dressed as an ordinary commoner and carried household registration documents from Suining Prefecture, which had prevented the city gate guards from immediately identifying his status.","“What official position do you hold in Panzhou? Did Third Young Master Yang send you, or was it the Pacification Commissioner?”","Yang Mo maintained a faint smile, displaying three parts respect, but mostly calm composure.","“I hold no official post; I am merely the steward of the Yang estate.”","“I was sent by the Pacification Commissioner to thank County Princess Linghui and Second Miss Song for saving our Third Young Master’s life.”","A steward was a trusted confidant, and the gifts were substantial, showing genuine sincerity.","Song Jinzhao asked, “How is Third Young Master Yang’s recovery?”","Yang Mo replied: “His body seems largely healed, but his face often remains cold, and he’s frequently downcast.”","“Before I came, the Pacification Commissioner specifically instructed me to ask the County Princess: Can Third Young Master’s face truly not be restored to its original state? Also, his stutter and slowed reactions—are they normal compared to before?”","His voice dropped even lower, and his expression became slightly cautious.","“Is there anything else wrong with his health, such as his ability to produce heirs?”","Song Jinzhao shook her head helplessly. “The chances of his facial reactions fully recovering are slim. At most, his expression will be somewhat muted.”","“As for the stutter and slower responses, there is a strong possibility of recovery through rehabilitation therapy.”","“Third Young Master Yang is physically robust, with no other issues. His ability regarding heirs is completely unimpaired.”","It seemed Yang Ruiping still valued Yang Cenan most as a son, or he wouldn’t have sent someone specifically to inquire about heirs.","Yang Mo felt both disappointed and relieved.","A few fewer expressions was tolerable; as long as he could produce heirs, that was what truly mattered."]},{"number":519,"title":"Chapter 519: Initial Sales Mini-Boom","paragraphs":["After asking, Yang Mo went straight back to the inn.","Watching his swift and decisive figure, Song Qiming sighed with emotion.","\"Yang Ruiping values Yang Cenan the most among his sons.\"","Song Jinzhao ordered people to carry the chests into the warehouse.","\"The more he values him, the more urgent his other two sons will become. They're bound to stir up trouble again.\"","There were undercover guards watching outside the inn. Yang Mo left Suining City early the next morning with his men, and the guards returned to report to Song Jinzhao.","\"After the noon meal, Yang Mo took his men and spent nearly an hour strolling along Tongbao Street, where the three streets had already been paved with cement roads.\"","\"He also went to the cement factory outside the city. After being chased away by the guards, he wandered around outside for most of the day before leaving.\"","Song Qiming slammed his palm on the ground, pacing anxiously in place.","\"He's definitely trying to steal the formula!\"","Song Jinzhao sat steadily, calmly setting down his teacup.","\"What's the rush? In the short term, they won't be able to replicate it. Once we start selling cement after the new year at a low price, no one will be fixated on the factory anymore.\"","Thinking of Li Zhidao, who had left a few days earlier, Song Qiming stopped in his tracks.","\"By then, Songzhou City and other places will all want to buy. Will the production be enough?\"","Song Jinzhao: \"We're already working overtime. I plan to expand the factory and hire another batch of workers in a month.\"","Until spring arrived, the common folk were idle at home, so there'd be no shortage of applicants.","Seven days later, at the door of the bookshop, Manager Lou set off for Songzhou City with ten thousand copies of \"The Complaint Record\" and ten thousand copies of \"The Tale of Qin Niang.\"","After watching him leave, Song Anhao instructed the workers to send a hundred copies each to three bookstores in the city for sale.","Three days later, flipping through the order forms from the three bookstores, Song Anhao's pupils dilated as he turned to the temporary manager.","\"The hundred copies we sent last time are all sold out?\"","The manager beamed, nodding with a flushed face.","\"They were all sold out by yesterday afternoon. The newly ordered six hundred copies were delivered this morning.\"","\"The managers of all three bookstores said that when female customers came in with the flyers, not one left empty-handed. I wonder how things are going in Songzhou City?\"","Looking up at the copy of \"The Tale of Qin Niang\" placed on the corner of his desk, Song Anhao's expression was dazed.","\"It really turned out just as my eldest sister predicted. This book is even more popular than 'The Complaint Record.'\"","Selling more in three days than half a month’s worth of \"The Complaint Record\" left Song Anhao utterly astonished.","\"The County Princess has excellent taste. This time, we're sure to make a profit.\"","At this moment, the manager’s admiration for Song Jinzhao had soared to the skies. After years of losses at the bookshop, hope had finally arrived.","Hearing the words \"make a profit,\" Song Anhao's mind gradually cleared.","He paced back and forth with his hands clasped behind his back, imitating the demeanor of an adult. Finally, he clenched his fist as if he had made a decision.","\"Tell the workers to stop all current printing tasks and focus entirely on printing twenty thousand more copies of 'The Tale of Qin Niang.' Also print another five thousand copies of 'The Complaint Record.'\"","\"Yes, sir. I'll see to it right away.\"","The temporary manager practically floated out the door, moving with a lightness never seen before.","Song Anhao returned to his seat behind the desk.","He picked up the copy of \"The Tale of Qin Niang\" again, opened it, and began reading while taking notes.","He had to figure out what made this book so captivating. Otherwise, how could he avoid missing the mark if he encountered another like it?","Meanwhile, a hundred li away, Manager Lou was visiting the proprietors of bookstores he knew, carrying the novels with him.","After reading both books, each bookstore owner placed orders for one or two hundred copies.","But even so, the twenty thousand copies he had brought still left a large surplus.","With a command, he began distributing flyers outside academies and private schools, following Song Anhao’s instructions.","Since \"The Tale of Qin Niang\" targeted female readers, Song Anhao had also tailored the outreach accordingly.","At shops selling clothes and jewelry, whenever they saw women, they handed out flyers, accompanied by highly enticing pitches that easily piqued people's curiosity."]},{"number":520,"title":"Chapter 520: Big Explosion, the Book Merchant from Jiangnan","paragraphs":["A day passed, and the first bookstore owner came to request more stock.","His forehead was sweating, his face flushed red, and he looked thoroughly thrilled.","\"Old Lou, give me another five hundred copies of 'The Qinniang Conspiracy'—this book is a hit! And 'The Cry for Justice,' give me two hundred of that too.\"","Manager Lou ordered someone to arrange the delivery while asking his friend about the situation.","\"Have you sold out everything in your shop?\"","The bookstore owner’s eyes fixed on the large cart in the inn’s courtyard.","He lifted the canvas covering it; inside were all books.","\"Only a dozen or so left. Customers have been coming in and out nonstop.\"","\"Some even asked how old the author is, where she’s from, and tried to buy more of her other stories. Your scriptorium has struck gold this time.\"","Steward Lou’s shoulders trembled. He turned away, wiping the corners of his eyes with his sleeve.","After all these years, he could finally see hope.","Half an hour after the first owner left, another bookstore owner showed up.","Their shops were all on the busiest streets of Songzhou City.","Once he learned about the remaining stock, the new owner directly took a thousand copies and left.","Three days passed like this. Out of the ten thousand copies brought in, nine thousand had been sold.","Manager Lou stood by the window on the second floor. In the courtyard below, seventeen of the twenty horse-drawn carts were now empty, and the tarps on the remaining three had also been pulled back.","\"Damn it, I have to send someone back to get more stock.\"","A servant beside him said, \"The sales pace in the bookshops has clearly slowed down today. Those who wanted to buy probably already have. If we ship more, what if we can't sell it?\"","Manager Lou replied, \"If we can't sell here, we’ll sell elsewhere. Songzhou City’s demand is filled, but the other county towns are still empty. We won’t have trouble moving them.\"","No sooner had he spoken than rapid footsteps thudded to a stop outside the room door.","Urgent knocking followed. \"Manager, there’s an out-of-town book merchant downstairs who wants to see you.\"","Those words hit like a thunderbolt over both their heads. They’d just talked about selling elsewhere, and a book merchant had appeared!","Manager Lou ran to open the door, his voice stammering as he demanded, \"Where are they?\"","The attendant said, \"On the first floor. He said he’s heading south to Jiangnan in a few days.\"","Manager Lou’s knees went weak, nearly sending him stumbling over the threshold.","\"Come on, let’s go see.\"","As he walked down the stairs and reached the landing, he started scanning the ground floor.","\"Which one is it?\" Several tables were occupied, and he couldn’t tell who the merchant was.","The attendant pointed to a man and a woman drinking tea by the window. \"That’s them.\"","Following the direction of the finger, he saw a man and a woman sitting side by side, both appearing to be in their twenties.","The man wore a bright, moon-white long robe with subtle patterns, and the woman a lotus-patterned mandarin jacket in lotus root purple—clearly fabrics from Jiangnan.","Seeing the attendant leading Manager Lou over, the two tea-drinkers set down their cups.","\"Are you both book merchants from Jiangnan?\" Manager Lou asked.","The man, wearing an emerald hairpin, nodded slightly.","\"My father’s surname is Lin. We moved to Jiangnan years ago and have come back to pay respects at the ancestral graves.\"","He picked up two books from the table. \"We were supposed to leave tomorrow, but we stumbled upon these two excellent works in a bookshop.\"","Manager Lou raised his eyebrows in surprise. \"Could it be the Lin family of Willow Leaf Lane?\"","The man replied, \"You know of us?\"","Suppressing the excitement inside him, Manager Lou sat down across from the two.","\"When the Lin family moved out more than a decade ago, it was quite a grand spectacle. I was fortunate enough to witness it in person.\"","\"So, how many copies were you thinking of ordering?\"","The woman, who hadn’t spoken until now, said, \"A hundred thousand copies of 'The Tale of Qinniang' first, and fifty thousand of 'The Cry for Justice.'\"","\"Cough, cough, cough.\" The hot tea he’d just sipped caught in his throat. Manager Lou quickly set down his cup and covered his mouth with his sleeve.","It felt like a hole had been punched in his throat, and a long time passed before the coughing fit subsided.","\"Are you sure about a hundred thousand copies?\" he asked, eyes wide with disbelief, staring at the woman who had spoken.","\"Yes, I’m sure.\" Those two decisive, unwavering words left Manager Lou unable to calm down for a long time."]},{"number":521,"title":"Chapter 521: Shameless profiteer, haven't you bothered to ask who our boss is","paragraphs":["The noise outside the window buzzed in Manager Lou’s ears, yet his mind felt as still and blank as if it had been sealed shut.","Fifteen thousand copies, at a profit of one tael each, that would be fifteen thousand taels — enough to buy several hundred bookshops.","He clenched his fists, pressing his nails into his palms to force himself to calm down quickly.","“I’ve only brought fewer than a thousand copies from my stock. Many bookshops have already placed orders. If you want this many, you’ll have to wait a while.”","The woman’s expression remained calm as she pressed, “How many days?”","Manager Lou thought for a moment and replied, “Fifteen days.”","The woman glanced at the man beside her, who immediately shook his head.","“That’s too long. My sister and I are returning to Jiangnan in a few days. Can’t it be shorter?”","Seeing how composed they both were, Manager Lou’s heart began to waver.","Could it be that their determination to order wasn’t strong? If this deal fell through, he would lose a fortune.","With that thought, he slowed his speech and put on a reluctant tone. “How many days would suit you?”","The man raised his hand and made a gesture. “Seven days. If you don’t have enough time, you can find other bookshops to share the printing.”","Manager Lou frowned. The timeframe was even shorter than he had anticipated.","“We only have a few printing blocks. It won’t work to bring in other bookshops. Even shipping the books from Suining City will take at least two days. Seven days simply aren’t enough.”","“Why not take half now and have the other half escorted by a local armed escort?”","The man gave a surprised laugh, and the woman seated beside him subtly curled her lips.","“Suining City seems a bit remote. It looks like your bookshop isn’t very large, Manager Lou.”","A small bookshop in a small town — without strong backing, there were more ways to handle things.","The man slowly picked up his teacup, taking a patient sip.","“Hiring an armed escort would cost a substantial amount of silver. You’d have to lower the wholesale price on the storybooks, or we won’t make any profit.”","Manager Lou said, “I assume you’ve checked the prices at other bookshops before coming. If you order fifteen thousand copies, I can lower the price by a hundred wen per book. That makes it one thousand five hundred wen per book.”","The man shook his head. “You’re not being sincere, Manager Lou.”","“Suining City is over a thousand li from Jiangnan. The transport costs are too high. At the very least, you’ll have to cut the price in half — seven hundred wen per book.”","Manager Lou’s temper flared immediately. His eyes bulged like a cow’s.","“Impossible! Seven hundred wen won’t even cover production costs.”","The man countered, “But shipping really is a huge expense.”","As the two reached an impasse, the woman in the gold hairpin spoke up. “What if you sell us a set of the printing blocks for those two books? We’ll print them ourselves in Jiangnan. That saves you the trouble and us the freight.”","A tense string snapped in Manager Lou’s mind. “How much are you willing to pay for them?”","The man held up two fingers. “Two thousand taels.”","For an instant, the air went still.","He looked at the man and woman sitting before him and felt as though he had been blind.","Two thousand taels? What was the difference between this and outright robbery?","“Impossible. Even ordinary storybooks aren’t that cheap, let alone The Tale of Qin Niang and The Cry for Justice, which sell so well.”","“Selling you the printing blocks means letting you print freely in Jiangnan. The printing and distribution rights alone should be worth at least one hundred thousand taels.”","At that price, the two of them let out a light laugh and leaned back in their seats.","The woman said, “One hundred thousand taels? Manager Lou, you really do have a lion’s mouth.”","The man added, “Storybooks that sell well always see pirated copies on the market soon enough. That’ll hurt sales anyway. All we’re after is a timing advantage.”","“If you think the price is too low, then four thousand taels. If you’re not willing, then let’s forget the whole deal.”","Seeing the scornful smiles on their faces, Manager Lou suddenly understood the meaning behind their words.","If he didn’t sell, they would just buy the books and have them copied. Anyone could carve printing blocks.","Jiangnan was over a thousand li from Suining Prefecture. There was nothing he could do.","He gritted his teeth and said, “Anyone who dares to pirate our books, our boss will take them to court. They’ll pay for every copy sold until they’re bankrupt.”","The warning didn’t frighten them. They remained calm, looking at Manager Lou as if he were some kind of clown.","“There are plenty of pirate printers everywhere. At best, you can sue them in Suining Prefecture. Any farther than that, and everyone has their own backing.”","“To be honest with you, the Lin family has some standing in Jiangnan. We even have marriage ties with the yamen.”","As he spoke, he pulled a one-hundred-tael banknote from his chest and pushed it across the table to Manager Lou.","“Take the deposit and deliver the printing blocks as soon as possible. Or sign a contract so we can carve them ourselves when we get back. Don’t end up losing both the books and the money.”","“A small workshop making a few thousand taels — that’s already a fortune.”","“Creak—”","Manager Lou shoved his chair back and stood up abruptly. His cheeks were tight, his eyes blazing with fury.","“You two shameless scoundrels, daring to bully the Song family bookshop!”","He picked up his teacup and threw the liquid into the young man’s face, then slammed the cup’s base onto the table so hard it shattered.","“Before you came, you should have asked around. Our boss is the younger brother of Prefect Song of Suining, a fifth-rank official.”","“And the young lady of the family is County Princess Linghui, personally conferred by the current emperor — her status is noble as a relative of the imperial family. Even if you wanted to file a complaint at the Golden Throne, it would only take one word. If you dare to pirate our books and sell bootlegs, be careful you don’t lose your heads.”","After delivering that threat, he turned and left without looking back.","As soon as he reached the second floor, he immediately asked the servant, “What kind of faces did they make?”","The servant replied, “Pale as ghosts. They’re probably scared out of their wits.”","Manager Lou took a deep breath, his heart trembling with rage.","“If I’d known such scum would come knocking, I should have revealed our boss’s identity from the start. How dare these vile creatures bully us.”","The servant smiled flatteringly, “You handled it brilliantly, sir. In such a public place, lots of people must have heard.”","“The Lin family may have moved to Jiangnan, but they still have some influence left in Songzhou City. Once word gets out, no one will dare pirate our books anymore.”"]},{"number":522,"title":"Chapter 522: Want to Give a Gift to Apologize After Panic","paragraphs":["The man blankly wiped the tea off his face with his hand, not even noticing the handkerchief handed over by the servant beside him.","Luckily, it was cold tea; if it had been hot, his face would have been scalded.","“County Princess Linghui... that name sounds familiar, like I’ve heard it somewhere,” he murmured to himself, his chest like the sea before a storm, filled with suffocation and panic.","The woman’s voice trembled as she said, “That’s the divine physician, the one who invented the waterwheel and is a martial arts master—the commoner princess.”","She had envied how the other woman had stumbled into such luck. She herself was by no means inferior, but she never expected to run into the Song family in Songzhou City.","The man couldn’t accept the outcome. He slammed his fist against the table.","“Why aren’t they staying in the capital? What are they doing in the southwest, running a bookshop selling storybooks? Why didn’t anyone inform us?”","Silence was the only response.","Unable to vent his rage, the man turned to scold his servant.","“Why didn’t you find out who they were? How could you be so stupid!”","The servant couldn’t argue back, so he simply lowered his head with a look of grievance.","You never told me to investigate. It was you and Second Miss who went ahead on your own, doing everything yourselves. What does this have to do with me?","The commotion drew murmurs from others nearby, who had witnessed the entire scene.","Trying to bully someone soft, only to run into an iron wall—how ridiculous.","Surrounded by so many staring and gossiping, the woman felt as if she were sitting on a bed of nails.","She whispered, “Brother, there are too many people here. Let’s just go back first.”","The man straightened his neck and looked around, seeing many people watching and mocking them. He swept the teacups off the table with a swift motion and got up to leave.","Seeing the broken teacups and teapot scattered on the floor, the inn’s waiter, who had been watching, immediately stepped forward to demand compensation.","The servant quickly took silver from his pocket, placed it on the table as a sign, and only then did the waiter slow down.","The group hurried out of the inn, and the main hall instantly erupted in chatter.","“The bookshop run by County Princess Linghui—the Lin family’s people really kicked an iron plate this time.”","“What’s a bookshop? I heard that Suining Prefecture recently recruited thousands of workers and built a cement workshop.”","Someone asked in confusion, “Cement? What is that? I’ve never heard of it.”","“I heard it’s used for building roads, and the wages are pretty good. My father-in-law’s neighbor wanted to join, but unfortunately, they filled the positions in just two days—he couldn’t even make it in time to sign up.”","The discussion continued endlessly.","Back at the mansion, the two Lin family members immediately ordered someone to investigate the background of the Song family’s bookshop. They had to find out if what the other party said was true.","Half a day later, the servant who had been sent to inquire returned.","“The Song family’s bookshop was originally called the Xue Family Bookstore. It was owned by Gu Zhongxun, the Southwest Administrative Commissioner’s wife, and changed hands just over a month ago.”","“I asked around at the Gu family’s other shops, and they said Miss Gu sold it to the Song family during a trip to Suining City. The shop manager also said that Gu Baozhu and Second Miss Song are close friends—like sisters.”","Eldest Young Master Lin slumped into his chair.","“How did the Gu family have a bookstore in Suining City? Why did no one ever tell me—”","His words seemed to question both himself and the servant.","The reason he had dared to threaten them was that he knew the bookshop came from Suining City—a small place with no one worth fearing.","Even if he hadn’t known about the change of ownership, if he had known the previous owner was the wife of the Southwest Administrative Commissioner, he would never have done what he did.","The servant kept his eyes on the ground, his forehead nearly touching the floor.","“Over a decade ago, the mansion stopped dealing in the bookshop trade, so we never looked into it.”","Second Miss Lin tugged at her handkerchief, pulling out several threads. She thought for a moment and then suggested,","“We can bribe that Manager Lou. As long as he doesn’t report today’s incident, the Song family will never find out.”"]},{"number":523,"title":"Chapter 523: When the Path Dims, a Village Appears Beyond the Willows and Flowers","paragraphs":["A full hour had passed, and Manager Lou still couldn't catch his breath, the anger lodged in his chest like a stone.","\"What a piece of work—coming in here, thinking they can just scoop up the spoils. Who gave them the nerve!\"","Watching the old manager pace back and forth across the room, the shop hand couldn't help but try to soothe him.","\"Getting angry only wears you out. We simply won't do business with them. The Qin Niang and The Grievance are selling like hotcakes—we won't be short of customers.\"","Manager Lou stopped pacing, pressed his right hand to his chest, took a long, deep breath, and let it out slowly.","\"You're right. If not them, there'll be another. What matters now is our stock.\"","\"You go back right away and tell the young master we need to print more copies of both books—a hundred thousand of Qin Niang and fifty thousand of The Grievance. If we can't strike a deal with booksellers from outside the region, I'll take them south to Jiangnan and sell them myself.\"","This golden opportunity that had finally come his way—he had to seize it with both hands.","If he let it slip, who knew if the next book would sell half as well.","That afternoon, no sooner had Manager Lou dozed off than the shop hand came knocking with news.","\"Manager, the two young masters and misses from the Lin family are back. They say they want to apologize and brought gifts with them.\"","Manager Lou, who could barely keep his eyes open when hauled awake, snapped fully alert at once.","He sprang out of bed, threw the door open in a rush, and spat his words straight into the shop hand's face.","\"Not seeing them. I wouldn't do business with such scheming folk even if my life depended on it. Tell them to get as far away as possible.\"","Watching the door slam shut with a bang, the shop hand leaned his neck back and swallowed nervously.","In all his years working at the bookshop, this was the first time he'd seen Manager Lou this furious.","The shop hand went downstairs, where the two Lins standing in the main hall wore grim expressions.","The shouting from upstairs had carried clearly—they had heard every word.","A manager might sound all high and mighty, but at the end of the day, he was still just a hired servant.","For them to show up with gifts and apologize in person, only to be refused an audience and scolded into the bargain—it was enough to make anyone's blood boil.","Second Miss Lin asked anxiously, \"Brother, what do we do now?\"","Eldest Young Master Lin frowned in agitation, his gaze drifting to the gifts in the servants' hands, which only made him more irritated.","He snapped at his sister in a harsh tone.","\"What else can we do? We're heading back to Jiangnan at once. The matter's dead in the water—surely the Song family won't chase us all the way there to make trouble.\"","The two stepped out the door, and just then a man in his forties brushed past them.","He paused, turned his head, and cast a glance their way.","After being roused from sleep, Manager Lou found he couldn't drift off again. He had just gotten up when the door was knocked on once more.","Thinking it was the two Lins who refused to leave, he lifted his chin and roared.","\"I said I won't see them! Throw them out this instant!\"","The shop hand lowered his knocking hand. \"They're already gone. The head of the Yue Long Escort Agency has come to see you—he's already downstairs.\"","Manager Lou's knitted brows slowly relaxed, and he opened the door, a flicker of uncertainty in his eyes.","\"Yue Dongqun?\"","The shop hand nodded.","At the prospect of meeting an old acquaintance, Manager Lou's mood brightened somewhat.","He walked over with a smile and sat down across from Yue Dongqun.","\"I came by your place a few days ago and you weren't home—when did you get back?\"","Yue Dongqun set a full cup of tea in front of the other man.","\"Came back yesterday around noon. The reason I've come today is that I want to transport a batch of books down to Jiangnan to sell.\"","Manager Lou paused, the teacup hovering in his hand. \"What gave you that idea? You don't have a bookshop in Jiangnan.\"","Yue Dongqun chuckled. \"I heard the Lins were going to order books from you and ship them south. Our escort agency has a job heading to Jiangnan next month, so I figured I might as well try to grab that business along the way—but it turns out they backed out.\"","\"The fact that the Lins were interested means there's money to be made. Since it's on the way, I thought I'd give it a shot. Once I get to Jiangnan, I can sell directly or pitch to the local bookshops. Worst case, I stick around a little longer.\"","Manager Lou's amiable expression gave way to a serious one.","\"Let me be clear—we don't take back any books we sell to you. If you can't move them and take a loss, we won't buy them back.\"","The man had absolutely no experience selling books, and Manager Lou worried he'd fail simply for not knowing the trade.","Yue Dongqun replied, \"Before I came, I already checked out a few bookshops and read the books. They're quite good.\"","\"Once I'm in Jiangnan, I'll just copy your promotional methods. Even if I can't sell everything, I certainly won't come back asking for refunds.\"","Hearing that put Manager Lou at ease.","They'd been friends for years, and he didn't want this deal to sour things between them."]},{"number":524,"title":"Chapter 524: Song Anhao Is Furious","paragraphs":["“How many copies would you like to order?”","Yue Dongqun: “One hundred thousand copies of The Tale of the Qinniang, and fifty thousand copies of The Cry for Justice.”","Manager Lou gave a slight nod—it was the same quantity the Lin family had wanted to order before.","“We’re old friends, so I’ll give you the lowest price I can: one guan and four qian per book. Delivery in Songzhou City in twenty-five days.”","Yue Dongqun had checked the bookstore’s wholesale prices before coming, and he knew that one guan and four qian was already rock bottom, so he accepted without haggling.","“No problem, but the timeline has to be solid—I must set out next month.”","Manager Lou smiled and nodded.","“Absolutely no problem. Sales have been brisk these past few days, so I’ve already sent word back to Suining City to increase the print run. I was originally planning to go to Jiangnan myself, but then you showed up.”","Yue Dongqun raised his teacup in a toast.","“Better to come early than to come late—saves you the trouble of traveling all the way to Jiangnan.”","“I can see you’ve got more spring in your step ever since the bookstore changed owners.”","Manager Lou took a hearty gulp of tea, full of confidence.","“The new owner is young and doesn’t put on airs, so most of the day-to-day running is still in my hands.”","“More importantly, with County Princess Linghui and Prefect Song backing us, we’ve got the clout—no one dares to bully us.”","The two members of the Lin family left Songzhou City early the next morning, as if a tiger were snapping at their heels.","When the servant rushed from Songzhou City to Suining City and delivered the news that another one hundred thousand copies needed to be printed, Song Anhao stood frozen in place for a long while.","“Excluding travel time, we sold out ten thousand copies in just a few days?”","The servant, face glowing with excitement and sweat still dripping, replied:","“Manager Lou said that if we can’t find out-of-town booksellers to partner with, we’ll just haul the books to Jiangnan and sell them ourselves.”","He then told Song Anhao about how the Lin family had tried to force the price down and then threatened to sell pirated copies.","“Luckily, Manager Lou invoked County Princess Linghui and Prefect Song to put them in their place—otherwise, with pirated books flooding the market, we’d have lost a fortune.”","Song Anhao, only eight years old and at the height of his idealism, flew into a rage at the thought of someone copying his books and selling pirated editions.","He immediately ran back to find his elder sister Song Jinzhao and tattle.","“Big sister~ We’ve barely started selling and already someone wants to copy us. I’m going to lose so much money. Can you give the Lin family a warning?”","Song Jinzhao paused her hand as she flipped through the ledger. “Didn’t Manager Lou already warn them?”","“The world is big, and there are so many people—no matter how you manage it, you can’t stop everyone from selling pirated books.”","“What you need to do right now is race against time: keep the printing presses running, get the books out to every corner of the country as fast as you can, and once everyone has a copy, who’s going to buy a pirated one?”","Song Anhao grumbled, “I just can’t stand the injustice.”","Song Jinzhao said: “A mouse gnawing on a rice sack—you can’t guard against everything. Don’t let a little thing ruin a big plan.”","“Your little bookshop isn’t that big—isn’t it time to hire more people? What happens when Manager Lou isn’t around? Can you handle it?”","Song Anhao’s voice came out muffled.","“There’s a deputy manager. I’ve already told him to start hiring.”","Song Jinzhao raised an eyebrow at him. “A single book takes only a few days to read. If you want to keep making money, you need new books.”","At that, his eyelids lifted, and his hazy eyes gradually sharpened.","A glint flashed in his gaze, and Song Anhao shot up from his chair, spun around, and bolted out the door.","“I’ve got it—I’m going to find Liu Ruoxi right now.”","Seeing Song Anhao run off, Qingshang stepped up to the table and asked in a low voice:","“County Princess, the bookstore’s profits are only going to grow. Should we assign someone to keep an eye on things?”","“The young master is only eight after all—it wouldn’t do for someone to take advantage of him.”","Song Jinzhao tapped her finger on the table, lost in thought. Yao Ying was in charge of protection, but the other aspects were inevitably weaker.","After a moment’s consideration, she gave her orders.","“Pick a sharp, clever girl who’s good with numbers and send her to Anhao’s side. Preferably someone a bit older, who can keep the two managers in line.”","Qingshuang said respectfully, “I think we could pick a reserve shopkeeper from one of our stores—they see all kinds of people and handle matters smoothly. That would fill the gap by the young master’s side nicely.”","Song Jinzhao nodded in approval.","“That’s the way. Pick a few candidates and let Anhao choose.”"]},{"number":525,"title":"Chapter 525: The Liu Siblings' Quarrel","paragraphs":["Liu Ziyuan stormed home in a rage, his teeth grinding audibly with fury.","Hearing his footsteps, Liu Ruoxi, who was in her room, quickly stuffed the draft she had just written into a drawer and picked up a broom, pretending to sweep the floor.","The door was shoved open from outside with brute force, slamming against the wall with a loud bang, sending dust flying and making her cough.","The moment she noticed the storybook in his hand, Liu Ruoxi’s heart skipped a beat.","She put on a puzzled expression and asked, “Brother, what’s wrong with you?”","Liu Ziyuan slammed The Tale of the Qin Maiden hard onto the table.","His face was colder than ice, and the anger radiating from him had almost taken physical form.","“Did you write this storybook?”","Liu Ruoxi glanced at it nervously and immediately shook her head in denial.","“No, didn’t you already tear up the one I wrote before?”","His neck bulged with rage as he slapped the table over and over, the surface threatening to collapse under the force.","“Do you think I’m blind and easy to fool? The name’s changed, but everything else is exactly the same. If you say it wasn’t you, you’d have better luck lying to a ghost!”","Seeing that she couldn’t talk her way out of it, Liu Ruoxi clenched her fists and raised her voice to bolster herself, though her tone was full of grievance.","“So what if I wrote it? Even County Princess Linghui said I write well, so why can’t I sell it?”","“And I’m not just writing this one—I’m going to write many more in the future.”","Seeing his sister dare to talk back, Liu Ziyuan’s anger only flared higher.","He grabbed The Tale of the Qin Maiden from the table and waved it in front of Liu Ruoxi’s face.","“Is this the kind of thing a respectable girl should write? And if people find out, who would still want to marry you? How am I supposed to explain this to Mom and Dad?”","Liu Ruoxi gritted her teeth. “It’s not even porn, so why can’t I write it?”","“Besides, I’m using a fake name, so no one will know. And honestly, if it weren’t for you getting upset, I would’ve used my real name.”","Liu Ziyuan widened his eyes in disbelief. “You knew I’d be angry, and you still wrote it?”","His voice turned bitter and choked.","“Have I ever starved you or denied you anything? Do you have any idea what the neighbors will say if this gets out?”","Seeing her brother so upset, Liu Ruoxi felt bad too.","Her voice softened, but there was not a shred of regret in it.","“I haven’t murdered anyone or started a fire. Who cares what people say? Nothing matters more than money. I don’t want you to work yourself to the bone—I want our family to live a better life. Is that wrong?”","With that, she began to cry, tears streaming from her eyes in big drops, splashing onto the floor and soaking into the ground.","Liu Ziyuan put down the storybook and tried desperately to reason with her.","“But your brother can support the family now. The debts are all paid off. Can you just stop writing from now on, please?”","Liu Ruoxi sobbed. “What’s wrong with me making money? Turning down silver is what fools do.”","Seeing that his sister was dead set in her ways, Liu Ziyuan said, “I’ll let you manage all the household money from now on. Young Master Song said I have talent, so I’ll only be earning more in the future.”","Liu Ruoxi stared at him with burning intensity. “But County Princess Linghui also said I have talent. I earn even more than you do.”","The two of them stood facing each other—one with tears glistening in his eyes, the other crying without stop—but neither was willing to back down.","After a long silence, Liu Ziyuan spoke in a low voice. “But what if your future husband’s family looks down on you for writing these shameless storybooks, and you end up unable to marry? What then?”","Liu Ruoxi roughly wiped the tears from her face, her eye corners rubbed raw.","Her voice was full of stubborn resolve.","“If he looks down on me for that, then he’s not the right one. On their wedding night, people still read erotic picture books to get the deed done. I only wrote a few lines about intimate moments between husband and wife—what’s so shameless about that?”"]},{"number":526,"title":"Chapter 526: The storybook written by your younger sister earns more money than yours.","paragraphs":["Song Anhao arrived at the Liu family home by carriage and, stepping into the courtyard, found the main gate tightly shut.","\"Could they be out?\" he murmured to himself, about to turn and leave when he suddenly heard voices and the sound of crying coming from inside the house.","After a moment's thought, he called out loudly, \"Young Master Liu, are you home?\"","Instantly, the expressions on the two people inside the room froze.","Liu Ruoxi hastily wiped the tears from her face, pretending nothing had happened.","Liu Ziyuan took a deep breath, pushing the emotions in his mind down.","\"Stay in your room and think about it some more. I'll go out and greet our guest.\"","The door was closed behind him, and Liu Ruoxi sat silently on the stool, biting her lip relentlessly.","When the gate swung open, Song Anhao immediately walked over.","Noticing that Liu Ziyuan's eyes were slightly red at the corners, he paused mid-step.","\"I thought I heard someone crying in there earlier. Have you run into some trouble?\"","Liu Ziyuan turned his head away and invited the man inside.","\"No trouble at all, just a small family matter.\"","Unwilling to continue that topic, he quickly asked Song Anhao after sitting down.","\"Second Young Master Song, what brings you here today? I haven't started writing The Cry for Justice III yet.\"","The second volume of The Cry for Justice had already been put on the shelves at the bookshop, and he assumed Song Anhao had come to press him for the next manuscript.","Glancing around and not spotting Liu Ruoxi, Song Anhao explained, \"I'm not here to see you today. I'm here to see your sister.\"","In the room, upon hearing his words clearly, Liu Ruoxi flung the door open and rushed out.","\"I'm right here.\" Those four words left Song Anhao completely baffled.","Her hair was slightly disheveled, her eyes rimmed with red, and tear streaks still half-dried on her face—it was plain to see she had just been crying.","Song Anhao's eyes darted uncertainly between the siblings' faces, and he spoke softly, \"Did I pick a bad time to come today?\"","Both siblings waved their hands frantically at once. \"No, no, Second Young Master Song, you've come at just the right time.\"","They depended on this man for their living; no matter what, they couldn't afford to turn him away.","Song Anhao let out a sigh of relief, and the excitement surging inside him rose again.","His eyes lit up as he stepped up to Liu Ruoxi.","\"The Tale of the Qin Maiden has been selling incredibly well. We're about to print another hundred thousand copies to sell down south to Jiangnan. I came today to ask if you still intend to write another book—and will it be on the same subject?\"","At the mention of a hundred thousand copies and selling to Jiangnan, Liu Ruoxi was completely stunned.","Liu Ziyuan, standing in front of his stool, stared blankly. He walked over to Song Anhao in disbelief.","\"You're really going to print a hundred thousand copies and sell them to Jiangnan?\"","Song Anhao nodded with a smile. \"After The Tale of the Qin Maiden sold nearly ten thousand copies in Songzhou City, someone took notice. Not only do they want to order a hundred thousand copies, they also want to order fifty thousand copies of your The Cry for Justice.\"","Liu Ziyuan swayed on his feet—fifty thousand versus a hundred thousand, half the amount, which meant his own storybook wasn't nearly as popular as The Tale of the Qin Maiden.","How could that be?","Snapping back to herself, Liu Ruoxi beamed, her eyes curving more than a crescent moon.","\"Are there really that many people who like the stories I write?\"","Song Anhao nodded vigorously.","\"Of course there are. Just in Suining City alone, over three thousand copies have sold. It won't be long before it's sold all across the Eastern Zhao Kingdom.\"","\"So that's why I rushed over to press you for the next book—when will the next one be done?\"","Liu Ruoxi clenched her jaw. The moment she remembered her brother's scolding just now, tears poured out uncontrollably again, leaving Song Anhao at a loss.","He took a step back. Was this crying for joy?","Liu Ruoxi lifted her chin and choked the tears back.","With a tearful voice, she glanced at Liu Ziyuan and complained to Song Anhao, \"I want to write, but my brother won't let me.\"","\"Huh?\" Song Anhao looked at Liu Ziyuan, confused.","\"Why?\"","Before Liu Ziyuan could speak, Liu Ruoxi cut in: \"He says what I write is shameless and embarrassing.\"","Song Anhao's brows knitted further, his bewilderment deepening.","He asked Liu Ziyuan, \"Why is it shameless? You write storybooks yourself—how is that embarrassing?\"","Staring at Song Anhao, who was still just a child, Liu Ziyuan opened and closed his mouth, but he simply couldn't find the words to explain."]},{"number":527,"title":"Chapter 527: Using Song Jinzhao as a Shield","paragraphs":["After shaking his head and agonizing for quite a while, Liu Ziyuan gritted his teeth and shut his eyes.","“No can do, no matter what. I have to think about her future.”","Song Anhao stared at him in confusion. “If you’re thinking about the future, then you should write even more. Without silver, there’s no future to speak of.”","The house they lived in was a mud-brick hut in the village, roofed with thatch, and looking around, the place was bare as bare could be.","If they didn’t earn money and kept living this hard life, that would be even dumber than Snowball.","From the look on Song Anhao’s face, Liu Ziyuan could tell what he was thinking, and blushing, he said, “I can already earn money now. The days ahead will only get better and better.”","Song Anhao blurted out, “But your sister’s storybooks are far more popular. She earns more than you do.”","Liu Ziyuan’s lips opened and closed, but the words got stuck in his throat.","Seeing him like that, Song Anhao simply turned his gaze to Liu Ruoxi.","“Do you want to write? For your next book, I’ll raise your payment tenfold, and on top of that, I’ll give you an extra five coppers per copy sold. If we sell another hundred-plus thousand copies, that’s several thousand taels of silver. Even ten thousand isn’t impossible.”","Just thinking about earning tens of thousands of taels sent a thrill through Liu Ruoxi’s heart.","She clenched her fists and nodded firmly, answering without hesitation, “I’ll write. I’ll keep writing.”","Seeing the determination in his sister’s eyes, Liu Ziyuan grew angry and frustrated, panting heavily as he lifted his head to stare at the roof beam.","Seeing how displeased he was, Song Anhao tried to soothe him. “To be honest, I actually prefer your “Cry for Redress.” Compared to other storybooks on the market, it’s already very well received.”","“Your sister’s writing is different from yours — hers are bought by ladies of wealthy households and young misses from inner chambers. You two each have your own strengths — a pair of blades in one scabbard.”","This only made Liu Ziyuan feel even more speechless. He had no energy left to argue with Song Anhao, and just wished he would leave quickly so he could talk some sense into his sister.","Worried that Liu Ziyuan might stop his sister from writing after he left, Song Anhao smiled at Liu Ruoxi before departing and left her with one remark.","“My elder sister is still waiting for your new storybook. Write quickly.”","Liu Ruoxi’s face was practically glowing with joy, the corners of her mouth upturned to reveal a few teeth.","“I’ll write quickly for sure. I’ll come find you at the bookshop then.”","Song Anhao left, looking thoroughly content, as though he had settled some major matter.","After watching the carriage go until it disappeared, Liu Ziyuan whirled around.","He stared at Liu Ruoxi with a thunderous face.","Seeing this, Liu Ruoxi took a deep breath and forced a light tone as she turned away.","“County Princess Linghui is waiting on my next storybook. I’d better write quickly now.”","Liu Ziyuan’s head was buzzing. He stood there staring at the closed door for a long time without moving.","After who knows how long, Liu Ruoxi suddenly opened the door again.","“If the wives and daughters of rich households can read it, then there’s no problem with me writing it either.”","“Once we’ve earned enough silver, don’t talk about people looking down on us — the doorstep will be worn down by matchmakers lining up.”","Liu Ziyuan’s temples throbbed, a dull ache spreading around his entire head.","“If Father and Mother were still alive, they would blame me.”","Liu Ruoxi replied, “If Father and Mother were still alive, the first thing they’d worry about would be your marriage. At your age and still unmarried — the Liu family line is about to come to an end.”","With a bang, she slammed the door shut, leaving Liu Ziyuan outside stomping his feet in frustration.","Meanwhile, the bookshop’s workers had been putting in overtime for two weeks straight, delivering two hundred thousand copies of the book to Songzhou City ahead of schedule.","Of those, one hundred fifty thousand were to be handed to Yue Dongqun. The remaining fifty thousand were orders from other bookstores around the southwest province, with three or four urgent requests on record. Manager Lou had nearly gone back to Suining City himself to keep a close eye on the printing presses."]},{"number":528,"title":"Chapter 528: Song Qiming's Worry","paragraphs":["During the busy period at the bookstore, Song Anhao walked briskly, as if he had wind - fire wheels under his feet.","Seeing him in a hurry, even having to eat breakfast on the go, Song Qiming couldn't help asking, \"Is the bookstore very busy recently?\"","Song Shixue smiled with a wonton in her mouth.","\"He calculates how much silver he has earned from the new orders in front of me every night. He's having so much fun that he doesn't want to leave.\"","Song Qiming put down his chopsticks.","Although he had no objections to Song Jinzhao's decision to train Song Anhao in business, he couldn't help but worry.","\"He liked shiny gemstones and beads when he was a child. Later, he liked anything valuable and wouldn't let go of them.\"","\"Is he a bit too obsessed with making money?\"","Song Jinzhao looked at Song Qiming with a smile. \"Who in the world doesn't like gold and silver treasures? When the government yamen was short of money, you couldn't eat or sleep well. Now do you think merchants have a strong smell of money?\"","The distressed look on Song Qiming's face disappeared in an instant, and he shook his head like a rattle.","\"Of course not. I just think Anhao is young and his mind is not yet settled. If he values money too much and incurs a loss one day, he will be extremely sad.\"","His eldest sister did small business to support herself and her two younger siblings, and even the money for his own schooling was earned from setting up a stall. How could he say that doing business was bad?","Swallowing the wonton in her mouth, Song Shixue guessed, \"Brother, are you worried because Anhao hasn't gone to the academy for half a month?\"","Caught out, Song Qiming averted their gazes and blinked.","\"I just think that even if he doesn't take the imperial examinations, he should read more books.\"","\"He has spent too little time on reading these days.\"","Song Jinzhao said, \"Don't you assign him homework every day and check it on time?\"","Song Qiming shook his head dejectedly and sighed.","\"Although he has completed the homework on time and made progress, it's not as significant as before.\"","Song Shixue complained, \"It's because you have too high requirements. I think his work is quite good. The academy has a monthly small exam. How about waiting for the results of this exam to come out and then seeing?\"","\"He finally managed to build up the bookstore. If you ask him to focus on his studies now, he will definitely be reluctant.\"","Song Jinzhao nodded in agreement. \"Let's do it like this.\" She had confidence in Song Anhao.","Seeing that both of them said so, Song Qiming had no choice but to give up.","When he picked up his official hat and went out, Song Shixue lowered her voice and tilted her head towards Song Jinzhao.","\"Brother really wants Anhao to take the imperial examinations in his heart, so he has such high requirements for him.\"","The maid handed over a warm handkerchief.","While wiping her hands, Song Jinzhao said, \"It doesn't matter what he wants. This child is naturally fond of doing business and making money.\"","\"However, knowledge is never enough. It's okay for Qiming to be strict.\"","Song Shixue blinked and happily went out to the medical clinic.","Half an hour later, Song Jinzhao rode a horse and appeared at the entrance of the coal mine. Qingshuang rushed over to greet her.","As Song Jinzhao walked towards the workshop, she asked, \"How many warehouses have been filled?\"","Qingshuang replied, \"The second warehouse will be filled today.\"","As she walked into the workshop, the temperature suddenly rose.","It had started to blow the autumn wind outside, but inside, with hundreds of earthen kilns burning together, the temperature was so high that people would sweat. Any strong man pulled out at random was sweating profusely.","After randomly inspecting an earthen kiln, Song Jinzhao came to the warehouse where the smokeless coal was stored.","The guard at the door opened the iron gate with a key. Looking up, the coal inside was piled up higher than a mountain.","\"With two warehouses of coal, the people in Suining Prefecture can use it for one winter. How long will it take for the newly dug earthen kilns to be completed?\"","\"Two hundred have already been dug, and the rest will be all completed in three days.\" Qingshuang said in an unhurried tone.","With the tight schedule, she personally inquired about the progress of all the work at the coal mine twice a day and knew everything clearly.","Song Jinzhao stopped and looked at her. \"Issue the recruitment notice for the second round in advance so that the people in the surrounding counties of Suining City will also know about it.\""]},{"number":529,"title":"Chapter 529: Second Recruitment Drive: Seeking Opportunities in Suining City","paragraphs":["After receiving the order from the coal yard, Song Anhao, amid her busy schedule, found time to have two hundred recruitment notices printed overnight.","In just three days by fast horse, recruitment notices were plastered across the main streets of four county towns, including Songhe County and Yanshan County.","Two people were dispatched to each of the four cities to spread the word in crowded areas, ensuring that even villagers who couldn’t read would get the news.","“The Suining City coal yard is hiring three hundred workers—men and women alike. Daily wages range from fifteen to twenty-five coppers, spots are limited, first come first served. Anyone interested, sign up here with me.” A newly appointed junior supervisor, just a month on the job, waved the recruitment notice vigorously at the city gate.","This recruitment trip came with a bonus—not only a daily allowance of fifty coppers, but an extra five coppers for every person recruited.","With three hundred slots split between two people, each stood to earn over seven hundred coppers.","A burly man carrying a shoulder pole heard the commotion and rushed over excitedly, asking, “Is this the same coal yard that County Princess Linghui recruited for a while back—the one that hired thousands at once?”","Hearing this, the junior supervisor’s chest swelled with pride.","He smiled and nodded at the man.","“This is our second round of hiring. The coal yard provides room and board for those who live far away, so the wages are a bit lower than before, but the food is excellent—meat at every meal.”","At the mention of room and board, the locals who had been worried about that very thing surged forward to confirm.","“You really provide room and board, plus over twenty coppers a day in wages?”","The junior supervisor quickly explained, “Female workers earn fifteen coppers a day, male workers earn twenty to twenty-five coppers, minimum twenty.”","The burly man who had asked first wasted no time, jabbing his finger at the registration book.","“My name is Gou Dali. I want to sign up—write my name down now!”","The crowd swarmed in, nearly toppling the table.","Another supervisor cupped his hands around his mouth and shouted, “Don’t push—one at a time!”","Standing off in the distance, Zhao Jinmin, the magistrate of Qingxia County, watched the scene unfold. Beside him, his deputy, Hai Wenzhang, felt nothing but envy.","“They’re recruiting all the way out here in Qingxia County. The County Princess’s coal yard must be raking in money hand over fist.”","Zhao Jinmin shook his head.","“They’re using the coal to fire cement, so they won’t see real profits until they sell the cement after the New Year. Where would they get silver now?”","The mention of selling cement made Hai Wenzhang anxious.","“Your Honor, given your ties to Prefect Song, could Qingxia County get our cement for free?”","Zhao Jinmin rolled his eyes at him. “Not a single coin for free? Impossible. At most we’ll get a discount.”","Hai Wenzhang: “How much of a discount?”","Zhao Jinmin turned and walked away.","“The price hasn’t even been set yet, so how would I know? Earliest will still be after the New Year.”","Hai Wenzhang chased after him. “Can’t it be sooner?”","Zhao Jinmin: “...”","The three hundred slots filled up within a single day. The next day, watching those who had signed up follow behind the carts, those who had missed out were filled with regret.","“If I’d come to the county town yesterday, I might have gotten in.”","Amid the waves of lament, a man quietly slipped out of the crowd and sprinted home.","He burst through the door shouting, “Wife, steam me a few corn buns—I’m heading to Suining City!”","The woman on the kang, mending clothes, was startled by the door slam. Seeing it was her husband, her relief turned to worry.","She set aside the half-mended garment and walked into the room, only to find him grabbing clothes from the chest and stuffing them into a cloth bundle.","Bewildered and uneasy, she asked, “What are you going to Suining City for?”","The man kept packing as he looked up. “The county princess’s coal yard only hired three hundred people here in Qingxia County. I’m going to Suining City—they’re hiring a lot more there. I want to sign up in Suining City.”","The woman grabbed his arm to stop him. “Once the slots are full, they’ll stop taking people. Going to Suining City won’t do you any good.”","The man said with certainty, “Even if they’re full this time, there’ll be another round. Sticking around Qingxia County means I’ll always be late to the news.”","The woman saw his logic, but the thought of her husband leaving Qingxia County weighed on her heart.","“Maybe I’ll come with you?”","The man glanced toward the child asleep on the kang in the main room.","“If you come, what about the child? While I’m away, take the kid and move to my parents’ place. I’ll go tell them now.”","With that, he headed out the door, leaving the woman hesitating for a long while before retreating to the kitchen to steam the corn buns."]},{"number":530,"title":"Chapter 530: The official road leading to Suining City stretches grandly and majestically.","paragraphs":["After arranging everything at home, the man shouldered his pack and set out along the main road toward Suining City.","But to his surprise, the farther he went, the more travelers he encountered instead of fewer. People kept joining the road from the paths on either side.","At a glance, their coarse gray-black clothes were covered in patches. Their fingers were cracked, and their faces and necks were a deep bronze—a clear sign that they spent all year under the blazing sun.","Suppressing his excitement, the man stepped forward and asked, “Brother, where are you headed?”","The brawny man carrying a bamboo basket glanced at him without slowing down.","“I’m going to Suining City to find work.”","The man immediately broke into a smile and quickened his pace to walk beside him. “I’m headed to Suining City too. Why don’t we travel together, brother?”","It was several hundred li away, and having someone for company made the journey less daunting.","The brawny man nodded. “All right. Let’s walk faster, or someone else will get there ahead of us.”","The man looked at the travelers going both ahead and behind them. Most of them were probably heading to Suining City in search of work. His decision had clearly been the right one.","In the Gu residence in Songzhou City, Gu Baozhu stared at the name of the publishing house printed on the back of The Story of the Qin Maiden, feeling a little regretful.","“If only I’d known book publishing could make so much money, I wouldn’t have sold it back then.”","These past few days, The Story of the Qin Maiden had been selling like hotcakes in Songzhou City. Nearly every literate woman from a well-off family owned a copy. The Record of Injustice was also popular with the students at the academies—even Gu Jinghong had bought two copies.","Madam Gu took the storybook and flipped to the page she had reached.","“It’s making money because the story is well written. If you hadn’t sold it, you wouldn’t have made any money at all.”","Gu Baozhu leaned her head back against the soft cushion and gestured with one hand.","“I wonder whether Song Anhao found these two stories himself or whether County Princess Linghui found them for him. When that child came to me back then, I thought he was only fooling around.”","Madam Gu set down the book and sighed with emotion.","“All three of the Song children are so outstanding. Ultimately, it all comes down to County Princess Linghui’s excellent guidance.”","“People say an eldest sister is like a mother, but there are very few people in the world who could do as much as she has. In just a few years, the Song family rose from commoners to an official household.”","Before long, Gu Jinghong came rushing in, his head drenched in sweat. He picked up the teapot from the table and drained it in one gulp. Water dripped down his chin, and he roughly wiped it away with his hand.","Seeing how desperately he was drinking, Madam Gu walked over in concern and wiped his sweat with a handkerchief.","“Slow down. Don’t choke.”","After finishing the last drop, Gu Jinghong set the teapot heavily on the table.","“Lunch was way too salty, and I dropped my water pouch on the road. I was dying of thirst.”","Gu Baozhu gave him a disdainful look. “Couldn’t you buy some water on the way? It’s not as if there aren’t tea stalls along the road.”","Gu Jinghong said, “I wanted to, but my father wouldn’t let me.”","Madam Gu felt sorry for her grandson and immediately began blaming her son.","“Your father really is something. He wouldn’t even let you have a drink of water. Just wait until he comes back—I’ll give him a piece of my mind.”","“I knew Grandmother was the one who truly cared about me.” Gu Jinghong nodded repeatedly in agreement, his words as sweet as honey.","After sitting down, he suddenly remembered something and said to Gu Baozhu with a grin, “Guess what I saw on my way back?”","Gu Baozhu asked indifferently, “What did you see?”","Gu Jinghong leaned his neck forward, raising his brows with an expression that said he alone knew a great secret.","“I saw a lot of commoners carrying bundles on their backs and heading toward Songhe County. When I asked around, I learned they were going to Suining City to look for work. I counted about twenty of them.”","Madam Gu looked at him in surprise. “Why are they going to Suining City to find work? Is there no work here in Songzhou City?”","Gu Jinghong shrugged. “I heard County Princess Linghui’s coal mine is hiring again.”","Gu Baozhu straightened her back.","“If even people from Songzhou City are going there, just how many workers is she hiring?”","Gu Jinghong pressed his lips together and hazarded a guess. “At least a thousand.”"]},{"number":531,"title":"Chapter 531: Begging: Can You Recruit Us Too","paragraphs":["Nearly all of the 1,200 recruits drawn from the four county towns were able-bodied men. Upon arriving in Suining City, they were taken straight to the coal plant for training.","Seeing the coal plant’s gates about to close, some of the townsfolk who had followed behind immediately ran over and asked, “Sir, is your coal plant still hiring?”","The guard on duty looked at him, his gaze sweeping over the several dozen people standing behind him.","Their eyes were filled with urgency, as though every one of them wanted to ask the same question.","“The second round of hiring is already full,” the guard said.","That single sentence sent everyone’s hearts plunging to the bottom of an abyss.","After two consecutive days of travel, they were already starving. The breath they had been holding finally left them, and quite a few slumped down to sit or squat, disappointment plain on their faces.","“We shouldn’t have come.”","The first man to speak refused to give up. He grabbed the guard and pressed on, “When will you be hiring again?”","“Is it easier to apply for work in Suining City?”","The guard did not know how to answer. Just then, Qingshuang was drawn over by the commotion.","“What is going on?” she demanded sternly.","Her gaze passed over the crowd, her heart full of questions. They looked like ordinary commoners—what were they doing here?","As though he had spotted a savior, the guard hurriedly turned to explain.","“Steward Qing, they followed the recruitment party from Qingxia County. They want to know when we’ll be hiring again.”","Seeing that the guard treated the woman with great respect, the man hesitated briefly before stepping forward and pleading humbly.","“We’ve walked for two days. We thought Suining City would surely be hiring more people. Could you take us on? We’ll work for less pay if necessary.”","“Yes, yes! We’ll work for lower wages too. Please, Madam Steward, take us in.”","Hearing the guard address the woman as a steward, and guessing that she had the authority to decide, the others gathered around as well, clinging to hope.","After thinking for a moment, Qingshuang said, “Wait here for a while. I’ll go ask the cement plant whether they still need workers.”","Meanwhile, the cement plant had run into trouble as well.","The junior steward in charge of managing production materials hurried over to report to Lanxi.","“Manager Lan, the sand and limestone arrived two shichen late today. The foreman over there says that the deeper they dig into the riverbed, the longer it takes, and output has fallen. He wants to know whether we can hire more people.”","Lanxi’s brows drew together. The more workers they hired, the more silver they would have to spend. The cement plant had not earned a single coin yet.","Seeing that he remained silent, the junior steward said indignantly, “I heard the coal plant hired another thousand-odd laborers. They’re digging coal to fuel our cement plant—why do they need so many hands?”","“In this humble servant’s opinion, the cement plant is more important. Why not speak to the County Princess and have those people transferred here for us to use first?”","Before he had even finished, Lanxi shot him a glare.","“How dare you question the County Princess’s decision? Do your job properly. Say another word, and you needn’t work here anymore.”","Others might not know what the coal plant was doing, but Lanxi understood perfectly well.","It was Song Jinzhao’s money-maker. Once winter arrived, it would bring in a fortune. It was no less important than the cement plant.","The junior steward’s face went stiff with fright. He stood rooted to the spot, not daring to move.","Why was this different from what he had expected?","County Princess Linghui valued the coal plant more highly and had allowed it to recruit so many workers. Manager Lan should have been deeply dissatisfied—so why was he scolding him instead?","The sound of approaching hoofbeats rang out. When the cement plant’s guards saw that it was Qingshuang, they immediately opened the barred gate.","Recognizing the figure on horseback, the junior steward quietly turned and slipped away.","Speak of the devil. If he had known she was coming, he never should have brought it up just now."]},{"number":532,"title":"Chapter 532: Recruited into the Cement Factory, Living in the Guanyin Temple","paragraphs":["When Lanxi came into view, Qingshuang swung down from her horse.","“What was that person doing? He looked rather flustered,” she asked casually.","Lanxi glanced in that direction, already understanding the situation perfectly.","“He saw you coming and got guilty in a hurry. I can handle it. How are things at the coal plant?”","Qingshuang replied, “The newly recruited workers will be arriving one after another. After two days of training, they’ll be ready to start work.”","“I came to ask whether the cement plant still needs more people.”","“There are quite a few Qingxia County locals at the coal plant entrance who didn’t manage to register. If you’re short-handed, you can take them all.”","Lanxi’s eyes lit up. She immediately asked, “How many are there? Are they all men?”","“We’re badly short of workers at the riverbed and the stone quarry. I’ve been worrying about it.”","The corners of Qingshuang’s lips lifted slightly, and her expression softened.","“They’re all men, probably in their thirties or forties. They look exhausted after traveling for two days.”","Lanxi immediately called for someone to bring them over. “I’ll go take a look. If they meet the requirements, I’ll hire them all.”","The same scene unfolded when the recruitment teams from Yuzhu County, Songhe County, and Yanshan County returned.","In all, Lanxi recruited 132 able-bodied men who met the requirements.","At the same time, the number of people from outside Sui’ning City continued to grow.","Even after learning that recruitment had ended, they chose not to leave Sui’ning City. Instead, they tried to find other work in the city. If they couldn’t find any, they slept in abandoned temples or on the streets, waiting for the next round of hiring.","Beside the seventh main road outside the western gate, where cement was being laid, Song Qiming looked up at the sky and pulled his collar closed.","“The weather is getting colder. The final two streets must be finished this month.”","“Once it snows and the ground freezes, the cement will freeze as well, and construction will have to stop.”","Shi Simian immediately pledged, “Rest assured, my lord. We’ll definitely finish within seven days.”","Only a short section remained on the seventh main road, and it would be completed today. Preparations for the final road were already proceeding at the same time. Seven days would be more than enough—they might even finish ahead of schedule.","The gate inspector in charge of patrolling the city gates had already been waiting nearby for quite some time.","When he saw that Song Qiming had finished his business and was about to leave, he seized the opportunity and hurried forward, forcing his voice to sound as calm as possible.","“My lord, this subordinate has an important matter to report.”","Song Qiming looked at him. “What is it?”","The gate inspector said, “Many people from the subordinate counties have poured into the city over the past few days. Unable to find work, they’ve been sleeping in the corners of the inner city and along the streets. Some are dressed almost like beggars, which has prompted much discussion among the townspeople. This subordinate truly doesn’t know how the matter should be handled.”","Song Qiming’s eyes widened. “They came from the four counties?”","The gate inspector nodded, still astonished that so many people had voluntarily come to Sui’ning City to seek work.","“There are also a few from the villages under Songzhou City, though there aren’t many—only seven or eight.”","Song Qiming asked solemnly, “Where are they staying? Take me there at once.”","The gate inspector led Song Qiming to a small corner near the eastern side of the southern gate. There stood a Guanyin Temple.","The tiles on the roof were dilapidated, as though the temple had not been repaired in many years. Yet the ground was relatively clean, giving the impression that someone came by regularly.","After dismounting, the gate inspector pointed inside the temple and said, “This temple had been deserted for a long time. It was occupied only by beggars.”","“Recently, life has improved a little for the common people, and some gradually began coming here to offer incense. Yesterday, they discovered that many people were staying here and panicked. They spread the news everywhere and even told the constables patrolling the streets. That was how this subordinate learned that these people hadn’t stayed at inns or sought refuge with relatives—they had been sleeping here at night.”","“There are several other places in even worse condition than this one. The earthen walls on all sides can barely keep out the wind, and they don’t even stop the rain.”"]},{"number":533,"title":"Chapter 533: Surviving on Wild Vegetables","paragraphs":["Hearing footsteps, the beggars sleeping on the dry grass instinctively lowered their heads after taking a glance. The moment they saw that the newcomer wore an official’s uniform, they froze.","The two men scrambled to their feet and dropped to their knees, pressing their foreheads to the ground as they cried out in panic, “Greetings, Your Excellency! Greetings, Your Excellency!”","At the same time, countless possibilities flashed through their minds. They went over everything they had ever done in their lives.","They hadn’t done anything. Why had the authorities come for them?","The prison official pointed to the row of depressions in the straw mats and said, “The others are probably out looking for work during the day. These two are the beggars.”","Song Qiming frowned as he studied the two beggars, who appeared perfectly healthy.","“Some time ago, the coal plant and cement plant were hiring. Why didn’t you go apply?”","While everyone else went out looking for work during the day, these two able-bodied men slept here instead. Would they rather remain beggars than work?","The two beggars paused. Their backs stiffened, and a chill of fear spread through them.","At last, they stammered out an explanation. “This humble one’s clothes barely cover our bodies, and our hair is a mess. The people recruiting workers would only drive us away. We couldn’t apply.”","Song Qiming questioned them, “Couldn’t apply, or didn’t dare to?”","“As far as I know, the coal plant and cement plant only consider whether one is physically fit enough to work.”","The two heads pressed to the ground cautiously stole a glance upward.","One of them said, “We’re used to being driven away, so we didn’t dare go.”","Song Qiming’s face darkened in speechless frustration.","Just then, footsteps approached. Several people carrying bundles appeared at the entrance to the Guanyin Temple. The sight of officials and soldiers inside frightened them into stopping where they stood.","Song Qiming turned around. Once he saw the four people’s clothes and appearance, his expression softened slightly.","Their clothing was somewhat dirty, but their hair was reasonably neat and their faces clean. They were not beggars.","Song Qiming walked over, and the four hurriedly knelt to pay their respects.","“This commoner pays respects to Your Excellency.”","Song Jinzhao raised a hand slightly. “Rise. There is no need for so much ceremony.”","After they stood, he continued, “Where are you from?”","The eldest-looking of the four stepped forward and answered, “The four of us are villagers from Longjing Village in Yunzhou County. We heard that the coal plant and cement plant here were hiring, so we came to try our luck and find work.”","Seeing wild vegetable leaves sticking out of one of their bundles, Song Qiming pointed at them and asked, “These are...?”","The man shifted the bundle behind him with an embarrassed expression and said awkwardly, “We haven’t been able to find work for some time, and food costs silver. So we thought we’d dig up some wild greens to stave off hunger.”","There were no wild greens in the inner city. Even families in the outer city dug them up, so these greens had most likely been gathered outside the city, a considerable distance away.","When Song Qiming looked back at the straw mats, each bearing the hollow left by someone sleeping there, it was quite possible that the others were doing the same.","How long could wild greens sustain them? When the weather turned colder, life would be even harder.","The thought that these people were all citizens under his administration weighed heavily on Song Qiming’s heart.","Ah Jie had hoped to attract more people to settle in Suining City by creating jobs. Now the people had come, but there was not enough work to go around.","Heavy-hearted, he returned to the government office. As he entered the rear courtyard, he happened to run into Lanxi, who was striding out in haste.","They both stopped at once.","Lanxi took a step back and cupped his hands in salute. “Young Master.”","Song Qiming glanced in the direction from which he had come. “Have you just come from Ah Jie’s study?”","Lanxi nodded slightly. Seeing the curiosity in Song Qiming’s eyes, he explained, “I heard that quite a few people from other places have recently come to Suining City looking for work. The County Princess intends to expand the cement plant and has ordered me to prepare to recruit more workers.”","Song Qiming’s eyes widened instantly, the light in them nearly dazzling Lanxi.","“Really?”","Lanxi nodded slowly and firmly.","“It’s true. I was just about to make arrangements. This afternoon, notices will be posted at all four gates of the inner city.”","The great weight in Song Qiming’s heart finally lifted. He gestured for Lanxi to go. “That’s good. Go on, then.”","He had just turned to leave when he suddenly stopped, turned back, and called Lanxi to a halt.","“There are quite a few able-bodied beggars in the city. If they want to apply, they may be hired as well. Mention it in the announcement.”"]},{"number":534,"title":"Chapter 534: Earned Two Hundred Sixty Thousand Taels","paragraphs":["By the study window, Song Jinzhao looked up at the sky. For the first time, she found herself hoping it would snow soon.","The initial investment was enormous. The profits from the several shops in Suining Prefecture were limited each month, while the bulk of the earnings had to come from the essential-oil and perfume factory in the capital.","Song Qiming pushed open the door and walked in.","“Elder Sister, government officials from below have been sending letters these past few days, asking to buy cement. Lord Gu also wants to come take a look and, while he’s here, review this year’s administration and tax records for Suining Prefecture.”","“The cement shops need to open as soon as possible. Otherwise, once Gu Zhongxun starts asking for it free of charge, refusing him will be troublesome.”","Song Jinzhao turned and sat down beside the chair.","“The shops will open as soon as the final two roads are finished. Gu Zhongxun is your superior. Not only can we not offend him, we also need to cultivate a good relationship with him.”","“It’s for a public road, so sell it to him at half the original price when the time comes. At the very least, we can’t take a loss.”","Song Qiming nodded in agreement.","“That was my thought as well. The news hasn’t fully spread yet, but once the other prefectures and provinces hear about it, demand will likely grow even more. The capital will want some too.”","Song Jinzhao walked to the map of the empire hanging on the wall and ran her finger along the official roads, which radiated outward in every direction.","“Once the coal and cement plants open, the transport and sales teams will set out immediately. We’ll establish a temporary sales point in every county. This winter is crucial. We can take cement orders first, but even if construction is approved, the work won’t begin until spring.”","“Government runners won’t be working in winter. They’ll be idle anyway—should we have them help with deliveries?”","Song Qiming had been keeping track of the hiring numbers for the two plants, and he knew how to do the math.","Money was flowing out like water every day. If they didn’t start earning soon, he was afraid Song Jinzhao’s purse wouldn’t be able to hold out.","Song Jinzhao shook her head.","“Government runners can’t be used for private work. If anyone investigates, it’ll cause trouble. If the prefecture’s guards aren’t enough, hire people from an escort agency when the time comes.”","“Elder Sister—”","With Song Anhao’s thunderous shout, the study door was flung open from the outside.","Saying that his face was glowing with excitement would have been an understatement. He was practically hopping up and down, grinning so widely that his upper and lower teeth barely came together.","“Brother—” He called out again when he saw Song Qiming, then stopped in front of the desk and looked around at the two of them.","Seeing how delighted he was, Song Jinzhao had already guessed what it was about.","The corners of her lips lifted as she teased, “Did you make a fortune?”","He hadn’t even had the chance to speak before she guessed correctly. Song Anhao’s eagerness to show off instantly dimmed by half.","He puffed out his cheeks and pursed his lips, then pulled a stack of banknotes from his robes and displayed them before the two of them. He spread the notes out in a fan on the desk in front of Song Jinzhao.","“After the Yuelong Escort Agency ordered one hundred thousand copies of The Ballad of Qin Niang and fifty thousand copies of The Wronged Cry Out, several more booksellers ordered four hundred thousand copies. We’ve collected all the remaining payment, for a total of five hundred thousand taels of silver.”","Song Qiming, standing nearby, suddenly widened his eyes. “That much?”","Song Anhao nodded proudly and began counting on his fingers as he explained.","“We’d already sold several tens of thousands of copies before this. After deducting the costs, we made two hundred and eighty thousand taels this time. I gave the workers and managers at the publishing house twenty thousand taels in bonuses, leaving two hundred and sixty thousand taels. It’s all here.”","Only after examining the banknotes did Song Qiming realize that every one of them was worth ten thousand taels.","To earn more than two hundred thousand taels in such a short time was honestly a little frightening.","“I never imagined selling storybooks could be this profitable. If I’d known, I would have written one myself.”","Song Jinzhao smiled and shook her head. “Only a storybook that becomes a runaway success can make this much money. It’s completely different from the essays written for the imperial examinations.”"]},{"number":535,"title":"Chapter 535: Song Qiming: I Shouldn’t Be the Poorest in the Family, Right","paragraphs":["Song Anhao nodded vigorously, completely agreeing with her.","“That’s right, that’s right. I never expected The Qin Lady’s Tale to become so popular either. Even now, I still think it’s not as good as The Wronged Man’s Record. Watching women scheme against one another is honestly a little boring.”","“The things described in the book are nothing like our family at all. It makes my head feel a little strange.”","Song Jinzhao smiled calmly.","“There’s still a big difference between what men and women like. It’s perfectly normal that you can’t appreciate it.”","Besides, he was only eight years old and had no yearning for complicated romantic feelings between men and women.","Song Anhao reached out, picked up the banknotes on the table, and quickly counted out half of them before handing them to Song Jinzhao.","“The money spent by the bookstore before this was all provided by Eldest Sister. Consider these your share of the profits.”","Then he took away the top three notes and handed the remaining ten to Song Jinzhao.","“Eldest Sister, keep these one hundred thousand taels for me. I’m honestly a little scared carrying so many banknotes around.”","Song Jinzhao smiled and teased him, “Looks like my investment this time was quite successful.”","A return of twelve hundred percent, and in such a short time.","Song Anhao scratched his head shyly.","“If Eldest Sister hadn’t said The Qin Lady’s Tale would sell so well, I might not even have thought much of it. In truth, you deserve the most credit.”","Song Qiming, who had been left sitting to one side, couldn’t help feeling puzzled when he heard that the two of them had each earned one hundred and thirty thousand taels.","Which was higher—his salary or Shixue’s consultation fees?","Could he actually be the poorest person in the family?","He got his answer at the dinner table that evening.","Song Shixue held her chopsticks and said, “Including consultation fees and the cost of medicine, I make around twenty taels of silver a month.”","Her medical skills had already earned her some renown in Suining City. However, she kept her fees low so ordinary people could afford to see her, so her income was only average.","Hearing that she earned just twenty taels, Song Qiming couldn’t help letting out a relieved breath and nodding twice. He said aloud, “That’s not too bad.”","Song Anhao, a chicken wing stuffed in his mouth, glanced at Song Shixue before lowering his head, his eyes shifting thoughtfully.","Song Jinzhao noticed this and smiled faintly to herself, secretly shaking her head.","If they were really comparing private savings, Song Qiming might not necessarily have more than Shixue.","She hadn’t earned much in Suining City, but she had made quite a lot while she was in the capital.","Relying solely on his salary and refusing to touch any illicit income, Song Jinzhao was certain that Song Qiming had no more than a thousand taels on him.","After dinner, Song Anhao quietly slipped back into his room.","He took out the box hidden beneath his pillow, opened it, and tucked a ten-thousand-tael banknote into his clothes.","Then he walked out of the room as though nothing had happened. Just as he was about to head next door, he saw Song Qiming.","Song Qiming demanded sternly, “There’s a quiz at the academy tomorrow. Why aren’t you reviewing your lessons?”","“I’m going to see Second Sister first, and then I’ll go study.”","The door to Song Shixue’s room was open, so he went straight inside after speaking.","Heye heard the commotion. Just as she came out from the inner room, she saw Song Anhao close the door behind him.","She blinked in confusion.","Why close the door?","Outside, Yao Ying and Song Qiming exchanged a glance. They forced stiff smiles, then lowered their heads and looked away.","The Young Master seemed to be guarding against the Eldest Young Master.","Song Shixue was sitting before her dressing table, undoing her hair, when she turned and saw a banknote held out in front of her.","“What’s this for?”","Song Anhao smiled ingratiatingly as he stuffed the banknote into Song Shixue’s hand.","“Keep it as private spending money. You earn too little running your clinic—you can’t even buy yourself a decent piece of jewelry.”","Song Shixue stared at the banknote, both surprised and delighted, yet also unsure whether to laugh or cry.","She took Song Anhao’s hand and returned the banknote to him.","“What kind of jewelry costs so much that even twenty taels of silver wouldn’t be enough?”","“Your Second Sister has money. I don’t need you to give me any.”","Song Anhao refused to take it back. Pounding his chest, he said, “Pretty jewelry is expensive. I just want to give it to you.”","With that, he opened the door to the inner room and left, nearly colliding with Song Qiming, who was standing outside."]},{"number":536,"title":"Chapter 536: The Urgency Brought by Ranking in Minor Examinations","paragraphs":["Song Qiming hadn’t heard the words clearly—the voice had been too soft—but he had still caught a few of them.","In particular, he had heard Song Shixue say, “I have money. I don’t need you to give me any.”","As if acting on instinct, he immediately stretched his hand out in front of Song Anhao.","“Both your sisters got some. You’re not going to give me a little too?”","Song Anhao bit his lip, looking somewhat reluctant.","With an innocent expression, he said, “You’re the biggest man in our family. How could you compare yourself to women?”","“Eldest Sister and Second Sister are women. Once we earn money, we have to spend it on them.”","Then he widened his eyes and deliberately tilted his head as he asked, “Unless you didn’t give them any?”","Song Qiming’s pupils narrowed at once. “Of course I did! I hand over seventy percent of my monthly salary to the household accounts office.”","Song Anhao gave an acknowledging “Oh” and nodded.","That reaction left Song Qiming so annoyed that his chest began to ache—entirely because he had worked himself up.","The frustration bounced around in his mind twice before he instinctively puffed out his chest and urged sternly, “Why are you still standing there? Go study. If you can’t keep first place this time, I’ll double your usual workload.”","Song Anhao shrugged and left.","Song Qiming clutched his chest, tears nearly welling in his eyes.","“How could he treat me like this...”","After muttering to himself, he suddenly thought of something and went into Song Shixue’s room to ask, “How much money did Anhao give you?”","Song Shixue held up one finger.","Song Qiming: “Ten thousand taels?”","Song Shixue nodded.","This time, his heart truly ached.","He let out a howl and strode out, his face caught between exasperation and amusement.","“What a little ingrate. I’ve loved him for nothing!”","Yao Ye, walking half a step behind him, clenched his teeth to keep from laughing. The maids and guards nearby who had heard the cry either lowered their heads or turned away, struggling to hide their smiles.","In the study, Song Anhao heard the howling and pressed his lips tightly together. Unable to stop himself, he reflected on his actions. A moment later, as if he had made some sort of decision, he let out a heavy sigh.","That night, when Song Qiming lay down to sleep, he saw a five-thousand-tael banknote sitting beside his pillow. The corners of his mouth instantly stretched nearly to the back of his head.","He held the banknote and examined it from every angle for a full quarter of an hour before finally placing it beside his pillow with great care, as though it were a precious treasure.","When he closed his eyes and went to sleep, the smile never left his face.","The rankings for the academy’s small examination were posted on the wall early the next morning.","Seeing that he had still placed first, Song Anhao breathed a sigh of relief.","But when he walked over to read the essays of the students ranked second and third, his brows slowly furrowed.","The student in second place had improved tremendously since before, to the point that he was nearly Song Anhao’s equal. Even the student in third place was close behind, and the gap between them was gradually shrinking.","Song Anhao silently withdrew from the crowd gathered around the notice board. Seeing that his expression was troubled, Yao Ying, who was accompanying him, couldn’t help feeling a jolt of anxiety.","He plastered on a smile. “To think you could stay at the bookshop for so many days and still come in first. That’s truly impressive.”","The compliment did nothing to improve Song Anhao’s mood. After walking several dozen paces, he slowly came to a stop.","“Big Brother is right. I’ve been too relaxed lately and let my guard down. From now on, I really should spend more time at the academy.”","When Song Anhao appeared in class the next day, the academy tutor secretly nodded in approval.","At least he felt some pressure and knew he needed to work harder.","Manager Lou returned from Songzhou City. With one of the clever maids Song Jinzhao had sent over managing the bookshop’s accounts, Song Anhao felt reassured and divided half of his attention back toward his studies.","It wasn’t until Liu Ruoxi came looking for him to say that the new story had been written that he brought Song Jinzhao along to a restaurant to treat the two of them to a meal.","Inside the private room, Liu Ziyuan cast a deeply aggrieved glance at Song Jinzhao from time to time, while Liu Ruoxi beamed happily beside him.","With the utmost respect, she presented the newly written story to Song Jinzhao. Her lips curved upward, and her eyes were filled with springlike warmth.","“County Princess, this is the story I’ve just written. Please take a look.”"]},{"number":537,"title":"Chapter 537: New Storybook: The Melancholy Brother, the Excited Sister","paragraphs":["Liu Ziyuan’s resentment deepened. His chest felt so tight that he simply turned his head away—only to meet Song Anhao’s fixed, watchful gaze.","“Have you finished The Chronicle of Grievances, Volume Three?”","Liu Ziyuan choked up and shook his head wearily.","These past few days, every time he saw Ruoxi writing those tales full of schemes, intrigues, and lingering romance, he had felt irritated. How could he possibly be in the mood to write his own storybooks?","“Not much of it. The Chronicle of Grievances, Volume Two is still selling, isn’t it?”","Song Anhao glared at him in disappointment.","“How can you be less diligent than your own sister? A proper man must take responsibility. This simply won’t do.”","Being rebuked for lacking responsibility by a child more than ten years his junior made Liu Ziyuan’s expression stiffen. Somewhat embarrassed, he lowered his head to avoid Song Anhao’s gaze.","“I’ve been feeling a little troubled these past few days. I’ll get back to writing when I return.”","Remembering Liu Ziyuan’s attitude toward Liu Ruoxi writing storybooks, Song Anhao simply shut his mouth.","He still did not understand why Liu Ziyuan objected so strongly to his sister writing fiction.","He could write himself, yet would not allow his sister to do the same. It was not as though writing storybooks was anything shameful.","Watching Liu Ziyuan suffer this setback, Liu Ruoxi pressed her lips together to hide a smile.","Whenever he saw her writing, her brother always had to lecture her. It was only fair to tease him a little.","She withdrew her gaze and looked once more at Song Jinzhao, her heart beginning to pound.","She wondered whether this storybook would meet the County Princess’s standards.","Cup after cup of tea was replaced on the table. The dishes had gone cold by the time Song Jinzhao finally looked up.","Liu Ruoxi clasped her hands into fists, her eyes filled with nervousness, afraid of hearing anything unfavorable.","Song Jinzhao set down the manuscript.","Turning toward Liu Ruoxi, she smiled and praised her. “It’s as good as your previous book. I especially like the ending.”","Liu Ruoxi’s eyes widened in disbelief. “Really?”","She had been afraid that her ideas were too unconventional and that people would condemn her for putting them into writing.","Song Jinzhao nodded. “Your readers are women. Writing it this way is what will make it memorable.”","A woman killing her husband and then taking power in the name of her young son—such a course of action would certainly strike many women of this era as shocking and unbelievable.","Yet after the shock came reflection. Perhaps it might even change something.","Hearing that Song Jinzhao’s praise was sincere, Song Anhao eagerly picked up the manuscript and began to read.","After a few pages, it was much the same as before.","He quickly flipped to the final chapter. After finishing it, his brows furrowed.","He understood what had happened, but not why.","There was something rather strange about this storybook. He would have to examine it again when it was being printed.","“I’ll take it to the bookshop today and have someone proofread it. If there are no problems, it will be typeset soon.”","The storybook his elder sister liked could not possibly be wrong. Would this one make another fortune?","Seeing that both Song Jinzhao and Song Anhao were pleased, Liu Ziyuan let out a long, deep sigh.","Since he could not stop her, he could only minimize the consequences.","Gathering his courage, he said to Song Jinzhao, “County Princess, my sister is not yet married. If people learn that she writes such things, it would harm her reputation. I ask that the County Princess and Second Young Master Song please keep this secret and not let others know that my sister is the author of these storybooks.”","Song Jinzhao’s gaze paused before she looked at Liu Ruoxi, as if asking: What do you think?","Liu Ruoxi took a deep breath. The heavy stone in her heart finally fell away.","As long as she could continue writing, this condition was entirely acceptable.","“Let’s do as my brother says. Staying mysterious is rather nice, too.”","The stories she wrote were set either in the inner households of official families or within the grand estates of immensely wealthy clans.","If people learned that the author was merely an unmarried young woman with neither wealth nor status, they would inevitably feel disappointed.","Someone who had intended to buy the books might change their mind after finding out.","Since the person concerned agreed, Song Jinzhao had no objection.","“It is better if no one knows. Otherwise, people might come knocking every day, asking endless questions. That would only be a nuisance.”","Liu Ruoxi immediately nodded. “If people came to visit every day, I would never be able to settle down and write.”","It was as though a switch had been flipped in Liu Ziyuan’s mind; he instantly lifted his head.","Now that the family had money to prepare his sister’s dowry, it was time to find a matchmaker and make some proper inquiries."]},{"number":538,"title":"Chapter 538: Mid-Late Grain Rain Season Arrives in Suining City","paragraphs":["Liu Ruoxi skipped away happily with the banknotes in hand, while Liu Ziyuan trailed behind her, looking as though a dark cloud hung over his head.","Song Anhao planted her hands on her hips and shook her head with a sigh. “What’s wrong with making money? Why can’t Young Master Liu understand that?”","A faint smile curved Song Jinzhao’s lips as she reached out and stroked Song Anhao’s soft, fluffy hair.","“Beliefs ingrained since childhood are difficult to change, especially when most people think the same way.”","Song Anhao lifted her chin, gazing at her beautiful and clever elder sister with admiration.","“Just because most people believe something doesn’t mean it’s right. Other people’s opinions deprive women of the opportunities they deserve to display their talents. That is a form of restraint and suppression.”","“Take Eldest Sister and Second Sister, for instance. You are more capable than many men. If you had cared about what others thought, how could you ever have come this far?”","Song Jinzhao’s lashes trembled slightly, and the hand resting on Song Anhao’s head gradually grew warm.","Though this child had been raised by her own hands, Song Jinzhao had never expected an eight-year-old to say such things.","Softly, she said, “Ideas that have endured for thousands of years cannot be changed in a day. We must take it slowly.”","She believed that day would not be too far away.","...","The cement factory recruited another two thousand workers in its second round of hiring.","Seeing the now-empty Guanyin Temple, Song Qiming could not help but smile in relief.","“At least they didn’t come all this way for nothing. If they earn a little more silver, they’ll be able to enjoy a prosperous New Year.”","The eight main streets had been completed a day ahead of schedule. Looking at the cement that had not yet fully dried, Song Qiming smiled with quiet satisfaction.","“It seems like snow is coming soon.”","The late-autumn wind felt faintly rough against his face.","Once winter arrived in the southwest, the first snowfall would not be far behind.","In the middle of winter, Gu Zhongxun’s carriage arrived in Suining City after a light rain.","After receiving word from the gate official, Song Qiming hurriedly led the officials of Suining City to the South Gate of the inner city to welcome him.","“My lord, we have arrived.”","A soldier lifted the carriage curtain, and Gu Zhongxun, dressed in a purple brocade robe with a round collar, stepped out.","“This subordinate, Song Qiming, Prefect of Suining Prefecture, pays his respects to Your Excellency, the Provincial Administration Commissioner.”","More than a dozen people dropped to their knees in a dark mass. Shi Simian’s calves were trembling.","The last time Gu Zhongxun had come to Suining City to inspect official affairs was ten years ago. At the time, Shi Simian had been nothing more than a low-ranking minor official. He could only kneel at the very back of the crowd and had not even had a chance to speak.","Standing atop the carriage, Gu Zhongxun looked down at the kneeling officials. His gaze paused briefly on Song Qiming’s head before moving on.","“Rise.”","He stepped down from the carriage onto the remarkably hard cement road. Before him stretched a broad, straight avenue.","Wide, clean, and orderly—it was truly thousands of times better than even the Imperial Street along the capital’s central axis.","“Prefect Song, you have truly impressed me. With you overseeing Suining Prefecture, I can rest assured.”","Song Qiming gave a small nod.","“You flatter me, my lord. It is all thanks to my elder sister’s brilliance. I have merely fulfilled my duty.”","Seeing that Gu Zhongxun had no intention of returning to his carriage, Song Qiming and the other officials could only follow slowly at his side, keeping half a step behind.","“Prefect Song, is the prefectural yamen ahead along this road?”","Song Qiming nodded. “After passing through the next three intersections, we will arrive.”","Noticing that there was no standing water on the road, Gu Zhongxun looked around, then walked past a vendor’s cart to the roadside.","Long rectangular bricks covered the mouth of the drainage channel, with finger-width gaps between them. Bending down, he could still see rainwater inside that had not yet dried up.","“Where does all this water flow?”","Song Qiming replied, “Into the Yongning River.”","The large contingent of officials and soldiers behind them had blocked Tongbao Street completely. The commoners who had come to set up their stalls after the rain hurriedly moved their carts and baskets back, afraid that offending such important figures might bring disaster upon them."]},{"number":539,"title":"Chapter 539: Gu Baozhu: Sometimes I Really Envy You","paragraphs":["“The prefect has to personally accompany them and show them the way. Just how high-ranking is this official...?”","The people’s whispers could not contain their curiosity.","They had seen plenty of soldiers and officials, but for so many officials to escort someone, that person had to be an extraordinary figure.","Seeing how slowly the procession was moving, the impatient Gu Baozhu nudged her horse forward and veered to the side. “I’m going to find Shixue. If my father asks, tell him where I went.”","Sitting on horseback, Gu Jinghong instinctively tried to stop her, but Gu Baozhu had already ridden away.","Gu Jinghong sighed and shook her head. Just how long were they going to keep walking?","Disappointingly, when they passed the second intersection and saw a cement road to the left, Gu Zhongxun turned onto it without hesitation.","“It’s still early. I’ll look around a little longer.”","With that, he turned and instructed Li Zhidao, “You take them to the post station to rest first.”","Seeing the determination in Gu Zhongxun’s eyes, Li Zhidao nodded in response. Only after Gu Zhongxun had gone some distance did he turn around and lead the others away.","Following behind them, Gu Jinghong quickly dismounted and tossed her reins to the young servant beside her. “Take my horse to the post station.”","Then she turned and ran after Gu Zhongxun. Song Qiming happened to glance back and met her eyes.","His brows rose in surprise, and he mouthed silently, “You came too?”","Gu Jinghong covered her mouth and replied in a low voice, “Grandfather doesn’t want to attract too much attention, so he had my aunt and me ride behind the others.”","Song Qiming asked, “Where’s Miss Gu?”","Gu Jinghong raised a hand and pointed toward Sophora Blossom Alley to the south. “She went to find Shixue.”","Song Qiming nodded.","Hearing the voices, Gu Zhongxun suddenly turned around.","The two of them instantly scattered like mice caught by a cat, ducking away and daring not to say another word.","Dressed in men’s clothing, Gu Baozhu dismounted and tossed aside the reins before running into the clinic. Her maid, dressed the same way, nearly failed to keep up.","“Miss, slow down!”","“Shixue—” Her voice arrived before she did.","When Song Shixue saw Gu Baozhu dressed as a young man, a trace of amazement flashed through her eyes.","What a handsome young man.","“Your face is so pale. Are you too cold?”","She hurriedly took Gu Baozhu’s hand and led her inside to sit down. Her hand was cold.","Gu Baozhu shook her head. “I’m not cold. I’m wearing plenty of clothes.”","Song Shixue asked, “Did you come with your father?”","Her brother had mentioned before that Gu Zhongxun would be coming to Suining City on an inspection tour before the New Year. At the time, she had guessed that Gu Baozhu might come along as well.","Heye lifted the curtain and entered, carrying a freshly brewed cup of milk tea. She placed it in front of Song Shixue.","Song Shixue pushed it toward Gu Baozhu. “Have some milk tea to warm yourself up.”","Gu Baozhu nodded and lifted the lid. The fragrance of milk mingled with the scent of red dates and wafted toward her, warming her face.","“My father thought the cement roads were fascinating and insisted on walking down each one. Your brother is here too, but I was bored, so I came to find you.”","She took a small sip. It tasted even better than the milk tea sold at the shop in Songzhou City. Apart from red dates, it seemed to contain osmanthus flowers as well.","When she chewed carefully, she found actual osmanthus petals inside.","Song Shixue asked, “Are your parents still in a hurry to find you a husband?”","Gu Baozhu smiled and shook her head. “After I went home, I told my mother that having children too early would harm my health, and that I wanted to bring a husband into the family. She never mentioned it again after that. My father also said I could wait another two years.”","Perhaps she had thought of something, because the smile on her face gradually faded.","“Sometimes, I’m actually rather envious of you. County Princess Linghui not only taught you medicine, but also allowed you to open your own clinic.”","“Unlike my parents. Although they don’t place too many restrictions on me, it would be impossible for me to enter military camps with Jinghong or lead troops into battle.”","Song Shixue placed a hand on her shoulder and comforted her. “My family comes from humble beginnings. We used to struggle even to have enough food to eat, so naturally we don’t have as many rules.”","“Your Gu family is different. Compared with the unmarried daughters of ordinary officials, you already have far more freedom.”","“Ladies in the capital aren’t even allowed to leave their homes whenever they please. At least you can go out whenever you want.”","Gu Baozhu leaned her neck back against the chair and complained, “What freedom? Jinghong has to come with me every single time.”"]},{"number":540,"title":"Chapter 540: Yanaka Shun Wants Cement, and the Cement Factory Is His Eldest Sister's Private Property","paragraphs":["Meanwhile, on the broad cement road, the officials of Suining City, great and small, had already accompanied Gu Zhongxun on foot for nearly an hour.","Song Qiming had practiced martial arts since childhood, so he did not feel tired in the slightest. The other officials, however, were clearly reaching their limits.","In late autumn, they did not sweat much, but the soles of their feet were already aching and sore. Every step felt as though their feet were breaking apart, and the blisters rubbed raw by their shoes made it even more unbearable.","Again and again, they looked toward Gu Zhongxun at the front. Seeing that he still appeared eager and full of energy, they could only sigh inwardly.","Wasn’t he tired?","They had circled from the South Gate to the West Gate, reached the North Gate, and only then entered the government office. It had taken a full two hours. By the end, even Song Qiming had to admire Gu Zhongxun’s stamina.","The moment he sat down, Gu Zhongxun began praising Song Qiming.","“This road has been built exceptionally well. It must have cost a considerable sum.”","Song Qiming replied, “The cement was supplied free of charge by my eldest sister, County Princess Linghui. The road was built by clerks from the government office and prisoners held in the jail, so the expenses were relatively low.”","“The eight streets cost a total of five thousand taels of silver. Thirty percent went toward meals, while the remaining seventy percent was used to make the sewer covers.”","Gu Zhongxun silently calculated the distance they had just covered and the cost involved. Songzhou City was three times the size of Suining City. To pave several main streets properly would likely require tens of thousands of taels of silver.","And then there was the cement. It had been free in Suining City—but would it be free for Songzhou City as well?","“How much cement is needed for one li of road? And roughly how much would it cost?”","Song Qiming deliberately furrowed his brow in apparent confusion. After a long pause, he cupped his hands and apologized to Gu Zhongxun.","“The cement factory is the private property of my eldest sister. I have been occupied with official duties and rarely involve myself in its affairs, so I would need to ask her about the exact price.”","“All I know is that each bag of cement weighs one hundred jin. A single li of cement road requires approximately two thousand five hundred bags.”","Gu Zhongxun looked away, a dark gleam flashing through his eyes.","It was obvious that the Song family had no intention of providing cement for free. Otherwise, Song Qiming would not have stressed that it was Song Jinzhao’s private property.","“That will be all for today. Starting tomorrow, we will inspect the various affairs of Suining Prefecture.”","Only after respectfully seeing him back to the post station did Song Qiming depart.","When he went to the rear courtyard to find Song Jinzhao, he discovered that Song Shixue was at home, with Gu Baozhu beside her, still dressed in men’s clothing.","After pausing briefly, he nodded in greeting. “Miss Gu.”","Gu Baozhu rose and gave him a formal salute. “Lord Song.”","Dressed in men’s clothes while performing a woman’s courtesy—it looked awkward no matter how one viewed it.","The room was full of women, so Song Qiming greeted them briefly and left.","Gu Baozhu stood, preparing to depart as well.","“It seems my father has already returned to the post station, so I should head back too.”","Song Shixue said, “I’ll have He Ye escort you.”","Gu Baozhu waved her hand. “There’s no need. I know the way to the post station.”","Only after she had left did Song Qiming return.","“The moment he sat down, Gu Zhongxun began asking about the cement. I managed to deflect him.”","“But I doubt he’ll give up. He’ll certainly bring it up again in a few days.”","Song Jinzhao said, “The cement shop will open tomorrow. Gu Zhongxun will definitely send someone to inquire about the prices. After that, we’ll take things one step at a time. Remember to play up how difficult things are—the voice of the common people is important too.”","She gave him a meaningful look. “The cement factory and the coal mine have hired more than ten thousand workers. If they cannot make a profit, won’t we have to dismiss them all?”","Immediately understanding her meaning, Song Qiming stroked his chin in thought.","“There are indeed some things that ought to reach Gu Zhongxun’s ears, so that he can ponder them carefully.”","If the people lost their livelihoods, they would cause unrest. Suining Prefecture had never been particularly stable, so Gu Zhongxun would certainly have his concerns.","Song Jinzhao cautioned, “Do it discreetly. Gu Zhongxun must come to the conclusion himself.”","Song Qiming nodded. “Understood.”"]},{"number":541,"title":"Chapter 541: Day One of the Inspection: Exceeding the Mid-Valley Expectations","paragraphs":["Gu Baozhu had just come out through the side gate when she happened to run into Song Anhao, who was returning from the academy. Without hesitation, she stepped in front of him.","“Anhao—”","Song Anhao, who had been hurrying inside, nearly collided with her. He came to an abrupt stop and looked up.","At first, he was merely confused. Then, recognizing her, he asked in surprise, “Sister Baozhu, why are you wearing men’s clothes? And you haven’t even done your hair.”","“Men’s clothes are more convenient when I’m out.”","In truth, she simply didn’t want to attract too much attention. If people found out that Gu Zhongxun had brought his daughter along while inspecting the local administration, there would inevitably be gossip.","Song Anhao frowned in puzzlement. “Then why weren’t you wearing them last time?”","Irritated by all the questions, Gu Baozhu planted her hands on her hips. “I’ll wear what I want. Why are you asking so many questions?”","“I heard the bookshop has been doing quite well recently. You look so pleased with yourself—must have made quite a bit of money, huh?”","Song Anhao took a step back and composed himself.","Could she be regretting that she had sold it too cheaply before and now wanted it back?","“Pleased? My schoolwork was so poor that my brother and my teacher both scolded me. I’ve been studying at the academy these past few days and haven’t gone to the bookshop in ages.”","Seeing the wariness on his face, Gu Baozhu couldn’t help finding it amusing.","“What are you afraid of? It’s not as if I’m going to take the bookshop back.”","“I’ve read The Tale of Qin Niang and The Wronged Man’s Record. They’re both very well written. When will that Peach Blossom Hermit release another story?”","Only after hearing that she had come to ask about a new manuscript did the wariness fade from Song Anhao’s face.","“It’s already being printed. In a few days, the new story will be on sale in Songzhou City.”","He had already discussed it with his elder sister. When they shipped the smokeless coal to the city, they would send the new books along with it, saving the cost of hiring a separate escort.","The next day, Gu Zhongxun inspected all the administrative records from the past year at the prefectural government office, with Song Qiming accompanying him throughout the entire process and answering any questions on the spot.","From official documents and public infrastructure to grain and commercial taxes, from the grain stores to the treasury, every item left Gu Zhongxun astonished.","After the more than seven hundred bandits had been captured shortly after his arrival in Suining Prefecture, the number of thefts, robberies, brawls, and other cases in Suining City and the four counties under its jurisdiction had dropped sharply compared with previous years. Most of the remaining incidents were minor squabbles between neighbors over trivial matters.","The river channel, which had been dry for many years, was flowing again. Although the harvest along both banks had not changed much this year, the amount of wasteland registered by the prefectural government had increased by a full twenty thousand mu. It was easy to imagine that, barring droughts or floods, the harvest next year would certainly be excellent.","This year, Suining Prefecture had been the first to collect and deliver its grain taxes to Songzhou City.","On the road to Suining Prefecture, Gu Zhongxun had also noticed that, beginning at the prefecture’s boundary, watch posts had been established every ten li along the main road, with constables patrolling day and night.","Caravans of merchants and escorted transport teams traveled constantly along the road.","Though everyone seemed to be hurrying, their faces were all bright with smiles. They looked nothing like the merchants of previous years, who had turned pale at the mere mention of Suining Prefecture.","The steadily increasing commercial tax revenue also showed that more and more merchants were coming to Suining City to do business.","When he reached the section on newly registered residents, he found that the population on the household rolls had increased over the year. Apart from newborn infants, most of the increase consisted of temporary residents—fully five hundred people.","“Bring me the household register,” said Gu Zhongxun.","At the desk by the window, the clerk responsible for managing the household registers felt his heart jolt. He cautiously glanced up at Song Qiming’s expression.","Only after seeing him nod did the clerk quickly retrieve the register from the shelf behind him and bring it over.","Gu Zhongxun began flipping through it from the back, scanning the information on the temporary residents registered over the past year.","One-third of them came from Qingxia County and Yunzhu County, while many others had previously moved away and now returned.","After a while, he rose and said to Song Qiming, “Let’s inspect the grain stores first.”","No matter how much had been written on paper, Gu Zhongxun still had his doubts about whether it was true.","He knew that Suining Prefecture had improved over the course of a single year—but could it really have become this much better?"]},{"number":542,"title":"Chapter 542: Inspecting the Granaries: Pre-War Reserve Grain","paragraphs":["When they arrived at the granary, they saw the yamen runners stationed at the entrance.","They held weapons in their hands, standing ramrod straight with their eyes fixed ahead. They looked like sharp blades, constantly on guard and ready to cut down any villain who might appear.","It seemed they had not been like this ten years ago.","Gu Zhongxun hesitated before speaking. “These yamen runners appear to have even stricter discipline than the soldiers in the military camp.”","Song Qiming’s expression remained utterly calm as he replied, as though he were mentioning something completely insignificant.","“When suppressing the bandits, I discovered that the yamen runners of Suining Prefecture were rather lax. So afterward, I specifically trained them for a period of time.”","Gu Zhongxun stopped and stared at him. “As far as I know, you learned martial arts personally from County Princess Linghui.”","Song Qiming smiled and nodded. “My elder sister has always set high standards for the household guards, so I merely imitated what I saw and learned a little of the basics.”","When the granary doors opened, Gu Zhongxun discovered that there were even more yamen runners inside than outside.","After passing through the heavily guarded courtyard, the warehouse clerk calmly used a key to unlock the inner doors.","Inside, they saw heaps of burlap sacks piled in the middle of the room like a small mountain.","Gu Zhongxun walked over with barely concealed excitement. A perceptive servant immediately hurried forward and untied the hemp cord around one of the sacks.","The reddish-brown sorghum grains had a hard, coarse surface and were slightly smaller than soybeans.","Gu Zhongxun personally opened another sack.","It was sorghum again.","“You planted rice. Why is all of this sorghum?” he asked Song Qiming in confusion, turning his head.","Song Qiming stepped forward to explain. “There are five hundred yamen runners in Suining City and more than seven hundred convicts in the labor camp. Digging rivers, farming, and repairing roads all require a great deal of food every day.”","“Furthermore, silver only flows out of the prefectural government treasury and never comes in. So after the rice from the wasteland was harvested, I ordered half of it sold and exchanged all the rest for sorghum and millet, thinking that they would keep longer.”","Gu Zhongxun suddenly understood and nodded approvingly. “I see. Coarse grains are indeed more practical. Eating rice at every meal would be far too extravagant.”","After leaving the granary, they headed next to the cellar beside it.","Thirteen baskets of potatoes sat on wooden boards raised above the damp ground. Gu Zhongxun calculated the amount of potatoes harvested in Songzhou City this year.","“I didn’t give you many potato seeds. How did you manage to harvest so many potatoes?”","The yield was more than double that of Songzhou City. Could there be some method of cultivation that increased production?","Song Qiming naturally could not tell him the truth.","The potatoes Gu Zhongxun had provided would only have produced half this amount. The other half had been added by Song Jinzhao within the bounds of what would not seem too outrageous.","Song Qiming answered with a smile, “There really were this many when they were harvested. Even my elder sister said the potatoes grew exceptionally well this year. It was probably because they received plenty of sunlight and just the right amount of rain.”","“The soil in Suining City is shallow, so my elder sister instructed us to fertilize it more heavily. That may also have contributed.”","Gu Zhongxun drew a deep breath, his chest feeling tight and heavy.","Potatoes had been discovered by County Princess Linghui, so she was certainly the most familiar with them. “Are there any records of the planting process and their growth? I’d like to take them back so the people in Songzhou City can study them as well. If we can increase the yield, that would naturally be ideal.”","The soil in Songzhou City was better than that in Suining City, yet its yield was lower. In Gu Zhongxun’s eyes, that meant they had not done well enough.","Song Qiming readily agreed.","“The agricultural officials have kept daily records. I’ll have someone make a copy for Your Excellency to take with you later.”","Gu Zhongxun fell into thought for a moment before speaking again. “The grain in the granary is not only meant to supply the yamen runners and laborers. Suining Prefecture occupies a strategically important position. In the past, the people were poor and the government was struggling as well, leaving the granaries empty for years.”","“Now that circumstances have improved, you must stockpile more grain in preparation for unforeseen events. I’m sure you understand what I mean.”","The darkness and significance in his eyes made the meaning behind his words obvious to Song Qiming.","“This subordinate understands.” If the southwestern foreign tribes ever raised an army and marched east, grain and provisions would be essential once the two sides went to war.","Song Qiming lowered his eyes to the ground, his thoughts churning.","But who would ultimately use those supplies was another matter entirely..."]},{"number":543,"title":"Chapter 543: Its Current Name Is the Immortal River","paragraphs":["The next day, Gu Zhongxun arrived at the bank of the river that had recently begun flowing again.","The azure river churned with white-capped waves, beautiful and pure, like snowmelt flowing down from the Tianshan Mountains.","Gu Zhongxun walked over to the stone stele standing on the riverbank.","“Shenxian River. What was it called before?”","Song Qiming smiled and shook his head.","“Before there was any water, the common people all called it a dry ditch. The name Shenxian River was given later, to represent Heaven’s blessing.”","Song Qiming had already reported the incident of lightning splitting the mountain to Gu Zhongxun in the name of an auspicious sign, and Gu Zhongxun had used it to report the good news to the emperor as well. The imperial court, however, had shown little response.","“Which fields were reclaimed by the government, and which belong to the people?” Gu Zhongxun gazed at the vast stretches of wasteland in the distance. In the plot before them, they could still see rice stalks that had not yet been cleared away.","Song Qiming pointed toward the bare trees in the distance. “Everything from that tree to the one over there belongs to the government.”","“Beyond that row of trees, all the reclaimed wasteland belongs to the people. There are at least fifty households in that area alone. Downstream, both banks of the river are covered with fields as well.”","The twenty thousand mu of newly added farmland all lay along both banks of the Shenxian River. The government had dug the ditches beside the roads and built waterwheels in the river, making irrigation much more convenient.","If Sui’ning City had not been so sparsely populated, the common people would have fought over this wasteland when it was first made available.","As they continued downstream along the riverbank, more and more farmland came into view, leaving Gu Zhongxun deeply shaken.","The impact of seeing the figures written on paper with his own eyes was several times greater than he had expected.","As they walked, Song Qiming said, “The soil in Sui’ning Prefecture is shallow and cannot retain water. Before spring arrives next year, I plan to use cement to pave the irrigation channels, as well as build embankments along both banks of the Shenxian River.”","“Of course, the prefectural office will have to pay for all that itself.” He smiled.","Gu Zhongxun’s footsteps paused for a moment. “I heard that County Princess Linghui’s cement factory has hired several thousand laborers since the autumn harvest?”","Song Qiming replied, “There were 4,600 people hired across two recruitment drives. The coal mine also recruited twice, bringing the total to nearly ten thousand.”","“The wages and daily meals for all those people are a considerable expense. My elder sister originally hadn’t planned to hire so many people the second time, but the common people came rushing to Sui’ning City as soon as they heard there was work available. In the end, she had no choice but to take them all on.”","Song Qiming seized the opportunity to suggest, “The cement shop is opening today. Would you like to take a look, my lord?”","She actually hired ten thousand people. County Princess Linghui certainly had nerve.","That was not only Gu Zhongxun’s thought, but also the thought of the other officials from Songzhou City who had accompanied him.","A workshop capable of employing five thousand people at once was beyond anything they had ever dared imagine, yet Song Jinzhao had two of them.","The cement shop was located on the busiest street in the outer city.","By the time Song Qiming and the others arrived, the entrance was already crowded with commoners. Some stood outside watching the excitement, while others sat inside discussing business. A price board was displayed on the wall facing the street, its prices clearly marked.","The characters were larger than a fist, making them easy to read even from outside.","The moment Gu Zhongxun saw the prices, he murmured, “Twenty copper coins a bag. That isn’t expensive.”","For something so useful, he had assumed it would cost at least several silver taels.","Song Qiming said with a smile, “My elder sister says cement can be used not only to build roads, but also to construct houses. It’s both sturdy and durable.”","“She wants ordinary people to be able to afford it, so she’s only adding a small markup to the production cost.”","Li Zhida scoffed from the side.","A small markup? Who would believe that?","The stuff was made from stone, so its production cost had to be very low. Song Jinzhao was definitely making a fortune.","What Li Zhida understood, Gu Zhongxun could naturally figure out as well.","After all, no one would openly announce their profits in business. Anyone who did would simply be a fool."]},{"number":544,"title":"Chapter 544: Doing Business in a Cement Shop, Inflated Cost Prices","paragraphs":["Once they entered the shop, the conversations between the shop assistants and customers became clear.","“I heard this cement can be used to build houses. Our master wants to build a three-room structure in the backyard. How many bags will we need?”","“How many bags would it take to pave a road half a li long and two chi wide in our courtyard?”","“Do you sell sand and gravel here as well? We’d rather not dig them up ourselves.”","“Can you give us a discount if we buy fifty bags...”","All ten tables inside the shop were occupied. The assistants, who had undergone three days of training beforehand, were able to answer most of the questions.","Before long, the first order—twenty bags—was completed. A servant from the Wang household at the north gate arrived with an ox cart to haul away the cement.","When the shop assistant saw a man in official robes enter, his gaze swept over Song Qiming’s face. One free assistant hurried to the counter and called out,","“Shopkeeper, someone from the government is here, along with the Eldest Young Master!”","The shopkeeper, who had been copying information from an order slip, abruptly raised his head. The moment he saw Song Qiming, he immediately set down the paper and brush.","He rushed out from behind the counter and knelt.","“Your humble subject, Xie Zhi, pays his respects to the Southwestern Provincial Administration Commissioner and Prefect Song.”","His loud voice instantly silenced the shop. Many people turned around.","They had heard that the Southwestern Provincial Administration Commissioner had arrived in Suining City a few days earlier to inspect official affairs. Since Prefect Song himself was accompanying him, this had to be the man.","In an instant, everyone dropped to their knees in a scattered chorus, and the sounds of people bowing and paying their respects rose one after another.","“Greetings, my lords...”","Gu Zhongxun’s hearty voice told them to rise.","Xie Zhi looked at Song Qiming questioningly. The other man gave him a discreet signal and shook his head slightly.","It was fine.","Seeing that Gu Zhongxun’s expression remained calm and showed no sign of displeasure, Xie Zhi finally relaxed.","With a smile on his face, he bent at the waist and respectfully said to Gu Zhongxun, “My lord, there is a place inside where you can rest.”","Gu Zhongxun shook his head without hesitation. “This official will stand for a while and then leave.”","Xie Zhi looked toward Song Qiming.","Song Qiming silently shook his head.","After who knew how long, Xie Zhi began to feel as though his legs had gone numb.","Then a red figure suddenly appeared at the entrance, as if a divine soldier had descended from heaven.","“Greetings to County Princess Linghui,” Xie Zhi was the first to speak. His eyes shone when he looked at Song Jinzhao.","Gu Zhongxun had lingered for so long that, even with Song Qiming present, Xie Zhi still could not fully relax.","Song Jinzhao smiled and nodded. “Lord Gu.”","Gu Zhongxun took a step back and clasped his hands in greeting. “Good health to County Princess Linghui.”","After exchanging pleasantries, Song Jinzhao took the initiative to bring up the matter.","“I heard from Qiming that Lord Gu intends to build cement roads within Songzhou City?”","Gu Zhongxun replied, “That is indeed my intention.”","“However, the streets of Songzhou City run in every direction, and the city has no distinction between an inner and outer district. It is more than five times the size of Suining City. The silver required to build the roads will surely be considerable.”","Song Jinzhao entered the sitting room and took a seat. Gu Zhongxun had no choice but to follow her inside.","“Songzhou City has not only government runners but also garrison troops, so there is no need to spend money on labor. The sand and gravel can be dug up ourselves as well. The only expense will be the silver needed to purchase cement.”","“Although the cement factory has been operating at a loss so far, and I have constantly been covering the shortfall myself, as long as it is for the good of the country and its people, I am willing to sell the cement to Lord Gu at cost.”","Gu Zhongxun did not look particularly pleased. He asked in an even tone, “And how much is the cost price?”","“Fifteen wen per bag.”","Li Zhidao, who was standing nearby, looked at Song Jinzhao as if she were a heartless merchant.","Gu Zhongxun struggled to contain his anger, and the temples on both sides of his head throbbed.","Fifteen wen per bag was absolutely not the cost price.","“The retail price is twenty wen per bag. Could the cost really be that high?” he challenged.","Song Jinzhao calmly explained, “This princess developed cement for the sake of benefiting the common people. Earning enough to cover my meals is sufficient. What matters most is that ordinary people can afford it.”","With a single sentence, she placed herself on the moral high ground, leaving Gu Zhongxun at a loss for how to refute her.","Just as the slightest trace of self-doubt began to arise in his heart, Song Jinzhao instructed Xie Zhi to bring over the account book for Gu Zhongxun to examine.","It clearly recorded how many bags of cement the factory could produce each day.","How many people worked there? How much was spent on food and other living costs? What were the operating expenses for the shop and its assistants?","Every single item was calculated down to a few wen, ultimately arriving at a cost of fifteen wen per bag.","Gu Zhongxun could find no problem with the account book. Every expense fell within a reasonable range for market prices.","After pondering for a moment, Gu Zhongxun calmly set the account book down.","“To be honest, this official is extremely curious about the cement factory. I have also grown somewhat tired from inspecting official matters these past two days. Could I visit the cement factory? It would be a good opportunity to relax and rest.”","He wanted to see whether there truly were so many workers there, but he was also genuinely curious about how cement was made.","Song Jinzhao had anticipated this. She smiled sweetly.","“Of course. However, the cement factory is extremely hot, and there is a great deal of dust...”","“This official does not mind.” Gu Zhongxun cut her off before she could finish, afraid that Song Jinzhao might use the conditions as an excuse to refuse him.","Song Jinzhao deliberately paused, pretending to be at a loss after her objection had been rejected.","“Then let us depart from the courier station tomorrow at the hour of the Snake. We can have the midday meal at the cement factory. Sharing a meal with the common people will be an interesting experience.”","Gu Zhongxun readily agreed. Li Zhidao, sitting beside him, was so furious that he felt as though his blood had boiled dry."]},{"number":545,"title":"Chapter 545: If You Can't Defeat the Competitor, Find a Way to Transfer Him Away","paragraphs":["“Eating the same food as the common people? Just how bad must the meals be? County Princess Linghui is clearly making things difficult for you on purpose!”","The moment they returned to their room at the courier station, Li Zhidao shut the door and began complaining.","Gu Zhongxun glanced at him. “Since you know she did it deliberately, why let yourself be troubled by it?”","“There are thousands of commoners at the cement factory. What do they eat and drink? How are they living? Those are precisely the things I care about.”","Li Zhidao’s brows were knitted tightly, and his entire face seemed to droop with worry.","“A bag for fifteen wen? I certainly don’t believe it.”","As Gu Zhongxun’s trusted aide, Li Zhidao had always spoken frankly with him, never bothering to hide his thoughts.","That was also why Gu Zhongxun liked him.","Gu Zhongxun said, “There’s nothing wrong with the accounts. We’ll know once we take a look tomorrow.”","“Grandfather~”","A knock sounded at the door, and both men looked up at once.","“Come in.” Gu Zhongxun gestured for Li Zhidao to leave.","The door opened, and Gu Baozhu ran inside, with Gu Jinghong following a step behind.","Li Zhidao bent at the waist in greeting before leaving the room.","“Father, I want to go to the cement factory too.”","His stomach feeling a little empty, Gu Zhongxun picked up a peach pastry from the plate and took a bite. “Remember to wear men’s clothing.”","Gu Baozhu’s face lit up with delight, and she nodded vigorously. “All right.”","Gu Jinghong took the opportunity to speak, successfully earning himself a roll of the eyes from Gu Baozhu.","“Grandfather, don’t worry. I’ll stay by my aunt’s side the entire time.”","That night, Song Qiming could not settle his mind in the study.","When he opened the window and saw that the lamp in Song Jinzhao’s room was still lit, he hesitated for a moment before walking to her door and knocking.","“Elder Sister, are you asleep?”","“No. Come in.” Song Jinzhao paused in turning the pages of the account book and raised her head slightly.","Seeing the worry written all over Song Qiming’s face, she guessed what was troubling him.","“Everything for tomorrow has already been arranged. You don’t need to worry. Gu Zhongxun definitely won’t spot any problems.”","Song Qiming took a deep breath, but the worry on his face did not lessen.","“That isn’t what I’m worried about. After dealing with Gu Zhongxun for a year, I know that he’s deep-minded and has a powerful desire to control the Southwest.”","“Before coming to Suining City, he handed all his official duties over to his eldest son, Gu Huaiyuan, who serves as the prefect of Songzhou. We’re both prefects, and our official ranks are technically comparable, but he is a senior fifth-rank official while I am junior fifth-rank. In three years, when Gu Zhongxun retires, I’m afraid I won’t be able to secure the position of Southwest Regional Administration Commissioner.”","Song Qiming’s concerns were entirely justified. Gu Zhongxun had spent decades in the Southwest. There was no way the emperor would feel at ease appointing just anyone.","Gu Huaiyuan had remained in the Southwest ever since entering government service. Whenever a problem arose, Gu Zhongxun would guide and advise his own son. Gu Huaiyuan was undoubtedly the best candidate for the position of Southwest Regional Administration Commissioner.","The atmosphere in the room gradually fell silent.","Song Jinzhao slowly rose, bracing her fingers against the tabletop.","“What is suitable now may not be suitable later. What the emperor wants is peace in the Southwest. The Gu family can give him stability, but if it comes to resisting invasions by the Southwest’s ethnic tribes, Gu Zhongxun can’t do it, and Gu Huaiyuan can’t do it either. If the son simply succeeds the father, there will certainly be officials who oppose it.”","“The Southwest has always been a burden on the imperial court, and Suining Prefecture is the first line of defense against invasions from the region’s ethnic tribes. But if we can turn that burden into an unbreakable cornerstone, the emperor may decide to keep you here so that his throne can rest more securely.”","Song Qiming’s brows drew tightly together. “Gu Zhongxun has deep-rooted influence in the Southwest. If he wants to put obstacles in our way, we’ll have no way to guard against him.”","An outsider and his own son— even a fool would know whom he would protect.","The corners of Song Jinzhao’s lips lifted as she said meaningfully, “But what if Gu Huaiyuan weren’t in the Southwest?”","Song Qiming froze. His mind went blank for an instant before he quickly began to think.","The candlelight swayed, and his pupils gradually brightened.","Rubbing his chin, he paced back and forth across the room.","“Gu Huaiyuan has held the position of prefect of Songzhou City for five years. It isn’t impossible to transfer him elsewhere.”","Song Jinzhao blinked.","“The three members of the Gu family have been left in the Southwest for so many years. It’s time they were promoted to positions in the capital.”","With a direction to pursue, Song Qiming’s spirits soared. He clenched both fists and struck one palm with the other.","“Exactly. Transfer him away. Becoming a capital official has far better prospects than serving in the provinces. As long as he has no ulterior motives, anyone would know which option to choose.”"]},{"number":546,"title":"Chapter 546: Patrol Inspection of the Cement Plant","paragraphs":["Before the first quarter of the Si hour the next day, Song Jinzhao and the others arrived at the entrance to the courier station.","Gu Baozhu, who had been waiting there in advance, spotted them and ran down the steps excitedly.","“County Princess~” Her cheerful voice made anyone who heard it think the two had a close relationship.","A yamen runner hurried inside to report their arrival. Not long afterward, Gu Zhongxun came out.","The grand procession headed toward the outskirts of the city, and the common people along the road hastily stepped aside.","Throughout the journey, Gu Baozhu’s curiosity got the better of her. She kept edging closer to Song Jinzhao, asking question after question, as though she were treating the cement factory like a tourist attraction.","Lanxi had been waiting outside the factory building. As soon as she saw the procession-clearing flags, she immediately led several junior managers forward to greet them.","“Greetings to County Princess Linghui. Greetings to Lord Gu, Lord Song, and the others...”","The factory gates stood wide open, and the carriages drove straight inside before coming to a stop.","Song Qiming took the masks Lanxi handed over and gave one to Gu Zhongxun. “There’s a lot of dust inside. My lord, please put this on.”","Gu Zhongxun took the mask and examined it. Seeing that Song Jinzhao and the others had all put theirs on, he understood that it served the same purpose as a face covering.","The moment they entered the factory building, a wave of heat struck them. Before long, their faces had been baked red, and their entire bodies felt hot.","“Is it this hot here every day? It feels like being inside a furnace.”","Lanxi glanced at Song Jinzhao before answering Gu Zhongxun with a smile.","“Calcining cement produces tremendous heat. The windows can’t be opened too wide, either. Autumn and winter are still fairly comfortable, but once summer arrives, it’s truly hot enough to kill.”","Nearby, workers pushed carts loaded with stone. In the distance, muscular men with bare arms were wielding heavy hammers.","Farther away, the heat had turned into smoke that lingered over the factory building.","There were many people, but no disorder. Everything proceeded in an orderly fashion, as though everyone had long since grown accustomed to it.","After two quarters of an hour, Gu Zhongxun was drenched in sweat. Beads of perspiration covered his forehead and chin, and his undershirt clung to his body so tightly that no amount of tugging could pull it free.","Gu Baozhu and Gu Jinghong were still in fairly good spirits, though the sparkle in their eyes had dimmed somewhat.","Only Li Zhidao, who was following beside them, kept wiping his forehead with his sleeve. He looked as though he were on the verge of fainting.","The difference between those who exercised regularly or practiced martial arts and those who did not was immediately apparent.","It took another half hour to finish touring the entire factory. The moment they stepped outside, Li Zhidao tore off his mask with a thump, dropped to his knees, and began vomiting.","Song Qiming said, “Quick, bring some water.”","A junior manager following behind Lanxi promptly ran over with a waterskin.","At lunchtime, three large wooden barrels held pork offal stewed with pickled vegetables, boiled spinach, and sorghum rice.","The workers from the factory came out in shifts to collect their meals, and barrel after barrel was replaced.","Sitting on an unsteady wooden bench, Gu Zhongxun stared at the pork offal floating in oil in his bowl, unable to find much appetite.","Li Zhidao, who had only just finished vomiting, wrinkled his brows in disgust and turned his head away. “How can anyone eat this with so much grease?”","Song Jinzhao paused just as she was about to eat a piece of pork intestine. Her tone was mild as she said, “The workers do hard physical labor. If their food doesn’t contain enough oil, they won’t have the strength to work.”","“I failed to consider that,” Li Zhidao said awkwardly, lowering his head. He did not dare say another word.","Gu Baozhu picked up a slice of pork lung and put it into her mouth.","It had been boiled until tender, crumbling at the slightest bite. Together with the pickled vegetables, it made every mouthful of coarse grain rice much easier to swallow.","She sincerely praised it. “It actually tastes pretty good. Most importantly, it goes very well with rice.”","At that, Li Zhidao became even quieter, especially when he saw that Gu Zhongxun was eating with obvious enjoyment as well.","After finishing a bowl of rice, Gu Zhongxun remained seated on the bench, watching the men and women line up to collect their meals one after another.","As they waited in line, they chatted among themselves, craning their necks to see what dishes were being served that day. When they squatted on the ground to eat, their faces shone with happiness—something Gu Zhongxun had never seen before.","He had seen farmers with hollow, sallow faces working in the fields beneath the blazing sun. They ate a watery gruel made by boiling wild vegetables together with coarse grain. After working all year, they still earned only a few coins and could barely keep themselves fed."]},{"number":547,"title":"Chapter 547: Moved by Yana, she gives 20% of the profits to the Higashikata family.","paragraphs":["After watching for who knew how long, Gu Zhongxun suddenly rose and walked over to a man who looked to be around thirty.","The man was startled by Gu Zhongxun, who was dressed in an official’s robes.","Just as he was about to kneel, Gu Zhongxun stopped him with a hand on his shoulder. Then he crouched down so they were at eye level.","“Do you get enough to eat?”","The man looked completely bewildered, then hurriedly nodded. “There’s plenty of food here. You can even go back for more after you finish.”","Gu Zhongxun asked again, “Where are you from?”","The man replied, “Qingxia County.”","Gu Zhongxun’s eyes widened in surprise. “That far?”","“What made you come all the way to Suining City for work? Who do you have at home?”","Seeing that Gu Zhongxun remained gentle and amiable throughout, the man’s tense nerves gradually relaxed.","“I heard they were hiring here, so I came. I’ve got an elderly mother, a wife, and children at home. They’re all waiting for me to bring my wages home for the New Year so we can have a prosperous one.”","Gu Zhongxun asked, “How long have you been working here? Have you received your wages?”","The man nodded. “I came half a month ago, and they paid me yesterday—more than three hundred copper coins.”","Then he added with a broad smile, “They provide food and lodging, so by New Year’s I’ll be able to earn a whole tael of silver. It’s all thanks to County Princess Linghui. Now there’s hope for better days ahead. I’ll come again next year.”","Gu Zhongxun’s eyes flickered, and for a moment he seemed lost in thought.","No one knew how long they continued talking. He only returned to himself after the man finished eating and left.","Gu Zhongxun sat on a stool without saying a word, staring blankly ahead. He looked as though he were lost in thought—or perhaps deep in contemplation.","After a long while, he suddenly stood up and said, “All right, let’s go back.”","It was the court’s money, after all. If it could bring smiles to the faces of so many common people and give them hope for the future, then it did not matter if Song Jinzhao made a little money from it.","As they departed, cries of “We respectfully see off County Princess Linghui!” and “We respectfully see off the Provincial Administration Commissioner!” rang out across the heavens and earth. Song Jinzhao had arranged it in advance.","Those in positions of power generally enjoyed being flattered to some degree. The higher the hat placed on their heads, the harder it was to take it off.","The day after returning to the post station, Song Qiming came to see Song Jinzhao in high spirits.","“Gu Zhongxun said that each bag of cement will cost fourteen copper coins. After the New Year, he wants the first one hundred thousand bags delivered to Songzhou City, with payment made in full upon delivery.”","Their bottom price was twelve copper coins. They had expected a lengthy round of haggling, but the final price had exceeded their expectations.","Song Jinzhao said, “Tell Gu Zhongxun that we already have one hundred thousand bags in stock. We can give them to him first, and he can take them with him when he leaves. I’ll arrange for people to escort the shipment.”","Song Qiming’s mind raced.","“Is Elder Sister worried that Gu Zhongxun will lower the price once the smokeless coal is produced?”","“Taking precautions is always wise,” Song Jinzhao replied. “If he tries to force the price down, we can use the same method again.”","“Still, based on what we observed yesterday, Gu Zhongxun does care about the common people. He has compassion for those suffering among the populace. You can play up their hardships a little more when you negotiate with him in the future.”","Song Qiming nodded. “I already sent a letter to Yukun yesterday and had someone deliver it. We’ll see whether he can find a way to have Gu Huaiyuan transferred to the capital.”","“With the Dongfang family’s help, it shouldn’t be a problem.”","Song Jinzhao lowered her eyes and thought for a moment before returning to the desk and picking up her brush.","“When you ask someone for help, you have to offer them something in return. The Dongfang family is extremely influential in the imperial court, and your relationship with Dongfang Yukun alone won’t hold forever. We need to tie them to our ship.”","Curious, Song Qiming walked over to see what Song Jinzhao was writing.","When he saw that she intended to give the other party twenty percent of the coal factory’s profits, he was utterly stunned.","“Isn’t twenty percent too much?”","Elder Sister had said that the smokeless coal’s profits would amount to at least several million taels of silver. Twenty percent would be hundreds of thousands of taels, or even more.","Song Jinzhao’s expression remained calm, but her tone was firm.","“The Dongfang family has served in government for three generations. Dongfang Yuanbin’s former students and protégés are spread throughout the six ministries of the imperial court and all across the realm. Ordinary favors mean little to the Dongfang family. We have to offer them substantial benefits. If we keep asking for things without giving anything in return, even the best relationship will eventually develop cracks.”","Song Qiming nodded slowly. Gritting his teeth, he said, “Then we’ll wait until next spring. At that time, we’ll send them the coal factory’s profits together with the contract.”","Song Jinzhao gave a slight nod. “Very well. Have Lanxi deliver them personally.”"]},{"number":548,"title":"Chapter 548: The Advent of Honeycomb Briquettes","paragraphs":["After everything had finally come to an end, Gu Zhongxun inspected the superior rice seeds saved from this year’s autumn harvest before setting off.","“They look a little plumper than ordinary rice seeds. When can they be made widely available?”","Song Qiming answered with a smile, “If everything goes smoothly, in two or three years.”","Gu Zhongxun’s expression softened slightly. He nodded. “Take it slowly. If you encounter any difficulties, send someone to inform me at any time.”","Under the gloomy sky, Gu Baozhu reluctantly let go of Song Shixue’s hand.","“I don’t know when we’ll be able to meet again. If only your brother could be transferred to Songzhou City.”","Song Shixue smiled brightly. “He’s only in the first year of his three-year term as prefect. Once I have some free time after the New Year, I’ll go to Songzhou City to visit you.”","Gu Baozhu pouted and muttered, “Three years from now, you won’t still be here either. The capital is too far away.”","Song Shixue looked at her without saying a word.","Seven days after Gu Zhongxun and the others left Suining City, the city’s first snow of the year arrived right on schedule.","The temperature dropped sharply. By the next morning, there were far fewer people on the streets, and only a handful of vendors remained at their stalls.","When a few brave townspeople ventured out into the biting wind and entered the shops, restaurants, and inns owned by Song Jinzhao, a wave of warmth greeted them, making them reluctant to leave.","One customer looked enviously at the shop assistant who came forward to greet him.","“You’ve already started burning charcoal even though winter has just begun. Your employer really is generous.”","The assistant pointed toward the brazier in the middle of the room.","“Charcoal is too expensive to burn. This is smokeless coal. It costs three copper coins per pound—only thirty percent of the price of charcoal.”","The customer froze. He stepped closer and stared at the smokeless coal burning inside the brazier.","The pieces were shaped like lotus-root segments, with holes through their centers—the same form as modern honeycomb briquettes.","“How is there no smoke?”","Some people did use coal for heating, but most burned it in heated brick beds. Even with chimneys, the smell would still seep through the cracks in the bed’s surface. Unless the cold was truly unbearable, half the population would rather not burn coal at all.","Following the shopkeeper’s instructions, the assistant continued enthusiastically praising the product.","“This is specially made smokeless coal from the coal factory. When burned, it gives off no irritating or choking smell, and it lasts a long time. A single piece can burn for three or four shichen.”","The customer bent down in disbelief.","He circled the brazier, turning his head as though he wanted to inspect it from every possible angle, practically wishing he could uncover some hidden secret.","After a long while, he had detected only the faintest trace of an odor. The piece of coal remained almost completely intact, barely burned at all, and delight spread plainly across his face.","“Shop assistant, where can I buy this smokeless coal?”","The same scene played out at several other shops. Even patients at Song Shixue’s medical clinic were asking about it.","The shop selling smokeless coal stood right next to the shop selling cement, separated by only a single wall. The assistants, who had been prepared in advance, opened the doors wide as soon as they saw people hurrying over.","“Do you have smokeless coal?”","“Is this where smokeless coal is sold?”","“...”","As customers rushed in, their questions rose one after another.","The assistant greeted them warmly, nodding as he ushered them inside. “Yes, yes, we have it. This way, honored guest.”","Customers came in an endless stream. Once those who had made their purchases left, they immediately told their neighbors.","Before long, a huge crowd came rushing over. When they saw the brazier displayed at the entrance, their eyes filled with delight.","In previous years, the price of charcoal rose steadily from the beginning of winter. Before winter set in, it cost nine copper coins per pound; by the depths of winter, it would rise by at least thirty percent.","In years when disasters struck, even charcoal costing twenty or thirty copper coins per pound was in short supply.","Now that smokeless coal cost only three copper coins per pound, everyone had to buy as much as possible and stockpile it. Otherwise, they might not be able to buy any later—or might have to pay a higher price and end up losing out.","At the same time, four transport teams, each consisting of fifty men, set out directly from the coal factory.","With Suining City as their center, they headed east, south, west, and north. The carts, loaded with smokeless coal, left trail after trail of wheel tracks in the snow."]},{"number":549,"title":"Chapter 549: With Honeycomb Briquettes, Half as Many People Will Die This Winter","paragraphs":["Within Suining Prefecture, the temporary shops in Qingxia County, Songhe County, Yunzhu County, and Yanshan County were the first to receive the goods.","The well-trained shop assistants immediately took samples to inns and restaurants throughout the area, promoting the smokeless coal as quickly as possible. They made sure everyone knew that it cost only thirty percent as much as charcoal, produced little odor, and burned for a long time—making it especially suitable for heating in winter.","Once the first step was completed, there was hardly any need for further promotion. Everyone who had bought it praised the product, so there was no need to worry about sales. The only concern was whether there would be enough to meet demand.","Songzhou City.","Staring at the glowing honeycomb briquettes burning in the brazier, Gu Zhongxun felt so weak in the chest that he could barely speak.","So the coal plant had not been built solely to supply fuel to the cement factory. It had also been established to produce this.","Li Zhidao pointed indignantly at the smokeless coal. “My lord, it’s only been a few days since we left Suining City, yet County Princess Linghui and Song Qiming haven’t let a word slip. They deliberately kept this from you.”","Gu Zhongxun glared at him. “As if I needed you to point that out.”","The Gu brothers walked in together.","They untied the cloaks draped over their shoulders and went over to the brazier.","Gu Huaiyuan said with a smile, “I heard about it on the way back. I didn’t expect it to be true.”","Gu Huaiyuan complained in distress, “If I’d known this would happen, I wouldn’t have stockpiled so much charcoal before winter. We’re going to take a huge loss.”","There were many soldiers in the military camp, and they needed a great deal of charcoal every winter.","Worried that the price of charcoal would rise during the coldest months, Gu Huaiyuan usually had people purchase enough to last the entire winter before the season began.","Gu Huaiyuan dropped into a chair, his face filled with admiration for Song Jinzhao.","“County Princess Linghui really is extraordinary. I have no idea how her mind works—she can actually create all these miraculous things. Perhaps she’ll come up with something even more impressive in the future.”","Gu Zhongxun fell silent, and Li Zhidao wisely kept his mouth shut.","Who could say otherwise? Ever since they had first heard the name Song Jinzhao, one astonishing thing after another had emerged in just a few short years: the waterwheel, potatoes, the treadle-powered threshing machine, cement, smokeless coal, and the perfumes and essential oils sold in the capital. She was also highly skilled in martial arts and exceptionally gifted in medicine. The list of her merits seemed endless. Who knew what other wonders she might create in the future?","As he thought about all this, the pent-up frustration in Gu Zhongxun’s chest slowly dissipated.","Someone this capable was not worth offending for no reason.","Whether cement or smokeless coal, both were beneficial to the country and its people.","They were in Suining City, within the jurisdiction of the southwestern provincial administration. If he reported these achievements to the imperial court, he would receive part of the credit as well. Besides, they would leave sooner or later. Once they had finished developing Suining Prefecture, who would ultimately benefit if not his own family?","After thinking it through, Gu Zhongxun waved for Li Zhidao to leave.","“With these honeycomb briquettes, at least half as many people in the southwestern province will die this winter.”","Gu Huaiyuan shrugged. “More than just the southwestern province. Before long, people from other provinces will probably flock to Suining City to buy smokeless coal. I wonder whether County Princess Linghui’s coal plant can keep up with demand.”","His words plunged Gu Zhongxun and Gu Huaiyuan into thought.","Gu Huaiyuan said, “If the supply can’t keep up, will they have to recruit more workers?”","Father and son exchanged a glance. They were thinking exactly the same thing.","What they did not know was that the coal plant had been stockpiling supplies ever since it began operations. There would certainly be enough to last through the entire winter’s sales.","The snow fell harder and harder. A single step into the snow could sink a person all the way to the knees.","On the twenty-sixth day of the twelfth lunar month, workers at the cement and coal plants who lived far from home collected their wages and prepared to leave.","Looking at the vast expanse of white, they complained about the terrible roads. Some who did not want to spend money put on straw rain capes and prepared to walk home, while many others formed groups of three or five and went into the city to hire carriages.","After these workers left, only half of the original workforce remained at the cement and coal plants.","From the twenty-seventh day of the twelfth lunar month through the third day of the New Year, those who stayed behind to work overtime would receive an extra five wen in wages each day. Quite a few workers whose homes were near Suining City decided to stay and earn more money. They would simply return home for the New Year’s Eve reunion dinner before coming back."]},{"number":550,"title":"Chapter 550: In the Depths of Bitter Winter: The Hardships of Ordinary People","paragraphs":["Three days before New Year’s Eve, the snow in Suining City had already piled up to thigh height.","The bitter wind cut across people’s faces like knives. Unless absolutely necessary, no one ventured out onto the streets.","The farther west one went, the heavier the snowfall became. In Qingxia County, at the westernmost edge of the region, the snow had already reached waist height, while the icicles hanging from the eaves stretched seven feet long.","On the main street, Zhao Jinmin, magistrate of Qingxia County, was still freezing despite wearing more than a dozen layers of clothing.","His pale-yellow skin had been chilled white. Bright-red chilblains stood out on both earlobes, and even the sweat breaking out on his back was cold.","Pointing at a mound of snow jutting out ahead, Zhao Jinmin shouted at the yamen runners, “You lot, get over there! All this snow must be cleared before dark!”","More than a hundred yamen runners were spread across the two main streets. Wooden shovels, iron spades—nearly every tool in the storeroom had been brought out.","To keep their roofs from collapsing under the weight, the shopkeepers on either side of the street had to climb ladders twice a day to sweep off the snow.","Every thirty paces or so, a small mountain of snow had been piled up along the street. The slush underneath had frozen into solid ice, so hard that even a knife could not chop through it.","As for which shop still had customers, the only one was the coal store opened by Song Jinzhao.","“I’d like ten jin of smokeless coal.” The man had his face and neck buried deep inside his clothes. Even his hands trembled as he took out his copper coins and household register.","After giving the register a quick glance, the shop assistant efficiently grabbed a sack and went to fill it with coal.","The shopkeeper standing behind the counter looked up. Seeing that the man’s padded coat was thick and free of even a single patch, he assumed the man’s family was reasonably well-off and casually remarked, “It’s going to keep snowing for several more days. You’d better buy a little more to take home, so you won’t have to come back again in a few days.”","Several threads of blood appeared on the man’s cracked lips as he spoke.","“Ten jin is enough. If we use it sparingly, it’ll last a month.”","Realizing he had misjudged the man, the shopkeeper immediately fell silent.","After the man shouldered the sack and left, the shop assistant, a local, walked over to the shopkeeper, who was from out of town.","“His family used to run a shop across the street. Later, both his parents came down with tuberculosis. Over the past six months, they’ve sold everything they could. That padded coat he’s wearing is probably the last thing they have left.”","The shopkeeper’s pupils widened, and the corners of his mouth slowly drooped.","When the man carried the sack home, the door was opened by a boy barely as tall as the door latch.","“Big brother, you’re back~”","The man smiled and nodded. Once inside, he quickly shut the door.","The fire in the stove had not yet gone out. He carefully picked up a piece of honeycomb coal and placed it inside. Once it caught, he put it into the brazier and covered it with the hood.","The boy grasped the two small handles on the brazier and carried it into the room on the left.","Two elderly people were propped up in bed. Their hair was white, and their mouths hung open, revealing a few jagged, yellow-stained teeth.","When the old woman saw the boy enter, her lips moved faintly. Her voice was hoarse, as though it had been rubbed raw with sandpaper.","“Shuanzi, your brother’s back?”","The boy set the brazier beside the bed and held his hands over it, rubbing them until they were warm.","“He’s back.”","Before the words had even faded, the man entered carrying a clay kettle and set it on top of the brazier’s hood.","After finishing, he sat down beside the bed and clasped his mother’s hand, his gaze fixed on both of his parents’ faces.","“Father, Mother, your son has failed you. After the New Year, I plan to go to Suining City to find work.”","The words brought tears to the eyes of all three people in the room.","The boy bit his lip, gripping the hem of his clothes tightly in both hands.","After a moment’s thought, he put on a brave front and said through a choked voice, “Big brother, don’t worry. I’m here. I’ll take good care of Father and Mother.”","The man lovingly stroked his younger brother’s head. Shuanzi was only ten years old, yet he would have to look after two elderly people on his own. He could not bear it and could not feel at ease, but there was no other choice.","There was no work to be found in Qingxia County. He had to go somewhere he could find a job; otherwise, before long, they would not even have enough money to buy medicine.","“I know Shuanzi has always been capable. Once your brother has established himself in Suining City, I’ll bring all of you there.”","The boy nodded through tear-filled eyes. He clenched his teeth, barely managing not to cry aloud."]},{"number":551,"title":"Chapter 551: Blue Creek Returns to the Capital with a Mission","paragraphs":["The day after New Year’s Eve.","“This letter is for Dongfang Yukun, and this one is for Dongfang Yuanbin. You must deliver them personally and make our position clear.” Song Qiming handed the two letters to Lanxi.","Song Jinzhao gave Lanxi the properly registered contract.","“If the Dongfang family wants to buy a share, you may accept a small amount. The businesses and connections in the capital are all being handled by Fushun, so go with him.”","The word “small” was heavily emphasized. After thinking for two seconds, Lanxi understood what Song Jinzhao meant.","“This subordinate understands.” They could accept something—but absolutely not too much. It was only meant as a gesture.","Knowing that Lanxi was returning to the capital, Song Anhao came running over with a wooden box almost as long as his arm.","“Please help me take this to Dongfang You. There are gifts and a letter for him inside. Tell him I miss him very much.”","As he spoke, Song Anhao’s eyes began to glisten. It had been nearly a year since he had seen his good friend.","Lanxi bent down and accepted the wooden box with both hands, smiling as he said, “Young Master, rest assured. I will personally deliver the box into Young Master Dongfang’s hands.”","On the day he left, Song Shixue stood where she was for a while, watching the carriage gradually disappear into the distance before finally turning away.","Standing beside her, Heye secretly sighed.","Although Manager Lan was handsome enough and very capable, he was still a servant. No matter how highly the County Princess regarded him, Heye still felt that he was unworthy of her young mistress.","Yet Song Shixue had taken a liking to him. This left Heye troubled every time she saw them together, though there was nothing she could do about it.","Two months later, Lanxi’s carriage passed a relay station five hundred li from the capital just as the Ministry of Rites officials sent from the capital were leaving.","Long-missed sunlight shone upon the gates of the County Princess’s residence. Since Song Jinzhao and the others were rarely home, the main gates were usually kept closed, and all the servants entered through the side door.","Hearing a knock, the gatekeeper called, “Who is it?” and pulled the door open a crack.","The moment he recognized Lanxi’s face, the gatekeeper’s eyes lit up, and he instantly broke into a smile as bright as two crescent moons.","“Manager Lan, you’re back!”","Seeing the carriage and the three guards behind him, the gatekeeper hurriedly opened the side gate as wide as it would go. He then brought out a ramp from inside and placed it over the steps.","After the carriage was pushed into the courtyard and handed over to the other servants, Lanxi asked the gatekeeper, “Is Steward Fu at the residence?”","The gatekeeper shook his head. “The steward has been out checking the accounts at the end of the month. He should be at the perfume shop today.”","Lanxi gave a slight nod. “We’ll go rest first. Tell Steward Fu that I’m back when he returns.”","“Yes, sir.” The gatekeeper nodded eagerly.","Winter days were short, and by the time Fushun returned to the residence, the sunlight had already faded almost completely.","The gatekeeper opened the door and immediately reported, “Steward, Manager Lan is back.”","Fushun’s footsteps paused, and his eyes suddenly lit up.","“Has the County Princess returned?”","The gatekeeper shook his head. “No, only Manager Lan and three guards came back. They went to rest right after dinner.”","Lanxi woke to find that night had already fallen.","The two men discussed matters in the room for a full hour and a half before deciding to seek out Dongfang Yukun first thing the next day.","Dongfang Yukun had just finished court when he received the calling card. He accepted it with a puzzled look.","“Wasn’t one sent just last month?”","Bringing Gu Huaiyuan to the capital would not be difficult, but they needed to wait for the right opportunity.","Qiming was not an impatient man. He should not have come pressing for an answer so soon.","Lanxi bowed deeply, his eyes fixed unwaveringly on Dongfang Yukun.","“I have returned from the southwest at the County Princess’s command. She has a business matter she wishes to discuss with your family. This letter was specifically given to me by the Eldest Young Master before I left. He hopes you will help mediate.”","A business matter?","The gentle expression on Dongfang Yukun’s face slowly faded as he reached out and opened the letter.","The farther he read, the more solemn his expression became.","What kind of coal could possibly be better than charcoal?","After pondering for a moment, he said, “I still have official business to attend to today. You may return first.”","Lanxi then took two more letters from inside his robe.","“This one was written by the Eldest Young Master for your family’s Old Master.”","“This one was entrusted to me by the County Princess for the Dongfang family. You will understand once you open it.”","Dongfang Yukun hesitated slightly before accepting the two envelopes. The thicker one on the left sent a chill through him.","Fushun picked up the wooden box from the table and opened it for Dongfang Yukun to see.","“These are gifts from my young master for Young Master Dongfang You. There is also a letter inside. Please see that it is delivered to him.”","Dongfang Yukun gave a slight nod, and the attendant waiting nearby immediately stepped forward to take the box."]},{"number":552,"title":"Chapter 552: An Overwhelming Fortune Shocks Three Generations","paragraphs":["After Lanxi and Fushun left, Dongfang Yukun did not immediately attend to official business. Instead, he opened the thicker of the two letters.","The thick stack of banknotes inside confirmed Dongfang Yukun’s suspicions. At that moment, he appeared unusually calm.","He picked up the contract written on white paper and read it from beginning to end. Then, without hesitation, he took the letter and banknotes to find Dongfang Yuanbin, who was staying at home.","The grandfather and grandson spent a long while examining the letter and contract. When they finished counting the banknotes and confirmed that they amounted to one hundred thousand taels, the shock in their hearts lingered.","“One hundred thousand taels in a single winter?” Dongfang Yukun’s pupils contracted, and he could not help drawing in a sharp breath.","“Not one hundred thousand taels—several hundred thousand, perhaps even over a million taels!”","Dongfang Yuanbin tapped the banknotes beside him with one finger.","“This is only twenty percent. When Song Jinzhao’s people sent them back, winter was barely halfway over.”","Dongfang Yukun unconsciously clenched his fists. One shock after another made his chest pound like a drum, as though his heart might burst through it at any moment.","“It’s even more astonishing than a money tree. I truly want to see this smokeless coal for myself.”","Dongfang Yuanbin slowly lowered himself into a chair, steadying himself against the edge of the table. “They haven’t sold it in the capital yet. We’ll have to investigate the matter thoroughly.”","“And the coal mines around the capital.”","At that thought, Dongfang Yuanbin immediately stood and called for someone.","“As I recall, there are several small coal mines around the capital. Find out who owns them and how much they produce. Do it quietly, without alerting anyone. Come back and report to me as soon as you have the answers.”","Seeing the seriousness on his master’s face, the servant hurriedly acknowledged the order, then turned and strode away without looking back.","After a moment of silence, Dongfang Yukun could not help asking, “Grandfather, if the profits from smokeless coal really are as County Princess Linghui claims, should our family get involved?”","“Such astonishing wealth, all in exchange for having Gu Huaiyuan transferred away—I can’t help feeling uneasy.”","Dongfang Yuanbin let out a soft laugh. “It’s not merely a matter of having Gu Huaiyuan transferred away. Three years from now, if Song Qiming wants to become the Provincial Administration Commissioner of the Southwest, he’ll need our help. His Majesty no longer trusts Ye Liangyu. If the Song family wants to rise, they must find allies.”","When he finished, he sighed. “To be honest, County Princess Linghui is quite clever.”","Dongfang Yukun exhaled slowly and sat down.","“She’s more than clever. If she were a man, there would be no place in the civil service for men of your grandson’s generation.”","By the time the servant hurried back that evening, Dongfang Shaoting had already returned from the Secretariat.","Three generations of the Dongfang family sat in the study and listened to the servant’s report.","“There are seven coal mines in total around the capital. Their output isn’t particularly high. Five of them changed hands at the end of last year. On the surface, the new owners are innkeepers from neighboring counties, but in reality, they’re servants sent out from County Princess Linghui’s residence. If I hadn’t recognized one of them, I never would have noticed.”","“That innkeeper once came to our residence when Young Master Song was studying here.”","Dongfang Yuanbin pressed him, “What about the other two coal mines?”","The servant’s tone grew solemn.","“The hidden owner of the remaining two coal mines is Chancellor Gu. I also heard that the two mines are apparently about to be sold.”","Dongfang Yuanbin asked, “Have the county princess’s people been in contact with them?”","The servant shook his head. “Probably not. When they bought the coal mines last year, they deliberately avoided those two.”","After serving as Chief Secretary for a year, Dongfang Shaoting had already taken on the bearing his father had possessed in his prime.","Even so, faced with the prospect of receiving a share worth more than a million taels, his heart still raced slightly.","He took a deep breath and calmed himself.","“Since Gu Qishan wants to sell, we’ll buy them and join the venture. We can’t take too much advantage of the Song family.”","Dongfang Yuanbin cautioned him, “Send someone unfamiliar to make the purchase. For now, don’t let Gu Qishan know that we’re the buyers. Before news of the smokeless coal reaches the capital, get it done within the next two days.”","When Prince Qi was still around, the Dongfang family had kept its distance from both sides, so its relationship with Gu Qishan could not be considered particularly close.","Gu Qishan was suspicious by nature. If the Dongfang family suddenly bought coal mines, they feared he might become suspicious.","Seeing how his grandfather and father had settled the matter in just a few sentences, Dongfang Yukun felt conflicted.","Compared with the twenty percent profit offered by the Song family, two coal mines seemed like too little.","The contribution and the returns were out of balance. Whenever he thought about taking advantage of the Song family, he felt uneasy."]},{"number":553,"title":"Chapter 553: Cooperation Achieved, Song Qiming Promoted to Fifth Rank Official","paragraphs":["It took less than two days, and by the next day, the property deeds of the two coal mines were delivered to Dongfang Yuanbin's hands.","\"Ask the people from the Song family to come tomorrow.\"","Dongfang Yukun nodded slightly.","Shortly after 10 a.m. the next day, Lanxi and Fushun arrived.","In the front hall, apart from Dongfang Yuanbin, who was idle at home, and Dongfang Yukun, who had specially taken time off to stay at home, all the other servants were sent away.","Dongfang Yuanbin placed the property deeds and the profit - sharing contract that Lanxi had brought before on the edge of the table, motioning for Lanxi and Fushun to take them.","\"These are the property deeds of two coal mines in the capital. They are the Dongfang family's capital for investing in the anthracite coal business. When you return to Suining City, tell County Princess Linghui that our Dongfang family is willing to participate in this business, and the profit - sharing will be as you proposed.\"","Seeing the red fingerprints and signatures on the deeds, Lanxi suppressed the excitement in his heart and stepped forward to fold the three deeds and put them into his sleeve.","\"Thank you, Lord Dongfang. The county princess will be very happy if she knows this.\"","Dongfang Yuanbin asked, \"How does Gu Zhongxun, the Southwest Chief Secretary, treat your eldest young master in Suining City?\"","The smile on Lanxi's lips faded a bit.","\"Before, they were a bit estranged, but it's better now before I came to the capital.\"","Dongfang Yuanbin nodded slightly.","\"That's good. If there are any difficulties in the future, ask your county princess to write to us. We will definitely help if we can.\"","When Lanxi and Fushun were sent out of the Dongfang family, Dongfang Yukun chased after them from behind.","Knowing that Lanxi was highly regarded by the Song family, he asked, \"Compared with being the Southwest Chief Secretary, does your eldest young master really not plan to return to the capital?\"","Lanxi pretended to be in a difficult position and lowered his head, his tone full of helplessness.","\"I've heard that in the past six months, the emperor has begun to rely on Prince Ying again, and Lord Ye and Lord Fei have been repeatedly demoted. Our county princess and eldest young master are afraid of getting into trouble, so they think it's better to stay in the southwest. It's really a last - resort thing.\"","Dongfang Yukun's mood also became heavy.","Since the marriage alliance between the two countries, the Kingdom of Shuobei has stopped causing trouble, and even Prince Ying's reputation has been somewhat restored.","The common people all praised him for bearing the humiliation for the peace between the two countries, marrying a princess who grew up in a brothel since childhood and still having to dote on her.","After a long silence, Dongfang Yukun said to Lanxi, \"Go back and tell your eldest young master that Gu Huaiyuan will definitely be transferred away at the latest next year.\"","\"You came back early and may not know that the emperor has issued an imperial edict to promote Qiming one more rank. The edict was sent out two months ago, and it should be arriving soon.\"","As a fifth - rank prefect, only the prefect of Songzhou in the entire Southwest Province could be on an equal footing with Song Qiming.","Hearing this news suddenly, Lanxi was stunned for a moment and then became excited.","\"Thank you, Lord Dongfang, for telling me. I'm going to set off for Suining early the day after tomorrow. If you have any letters to send, you can just send someone to the county princess's mansion.\"","Dongfang Yukun thought for a moment.","\"Okay, I'll send someone there tomorrow.\"","It was time to write a letter to Qiming. He still wanted to ask more about the anthracite coal business.","At the same time, the official from the Ministry of Rites in charge of delivering the imperial edict had arrived in Songzhou City and was arranged by Gu Zhongxun to stay at the posthouse overnight.","\"A nineteen - year - old fifth - rank prefect. The emperor really values him.\"","Thinking that his eldest son was thirty - nine years old when he was promoted to the fifth rank and had not been promoted for five years, Gu Zhongxun couldn't help but feel disappointed.","He was the one who submitted the memorial, but only Song Qiming was rewarded.","Hearing this, Gu Huaiyuan sitting on the chair pursed his lips.","If he were like Song Qiming, their family would have moved to the capital long ago.","Although he felt envious and resentful in his heart, Gu Huaiyuan still calmed down to comfort his father.","\"Suining Prefecture's achievements have been greatly improved last year, and the pedal - type thresher was invented by County Princess Linghui. The emperor just loves the one he loves and extends his love to the related things.\"","\"The officials in charge of delivering the edict didn't mention cement and anthracite coal. Didn't you mention them, Father?\"","Gu Zhongxun leaned back in his chair and shifted his eyes guiltily.","\"Those are for County Princess Linghui to make money, not to be presented to the court. Why should I mention them? The emperor will naturally know when they are sold to the capital.\"","He had thought at that time that he wouldn't tell the court first and take advantage of the time difference to let the Southwest Province develop first. Otherwise, if other provincial officials knew, he would have no advantage.","Now it seems that it was right not to mention it. If he had really told the court, all the credit would have gone to the Song siblings, and he wouldn't have gotten any benefits."]},{"number":554,"title":"Chapter 554: Investigating the Demographic Information of Ethnic Minorities in Southwest China Using Anthracite Coal","paragraphs":["When the imperial edict arrived, Song Qiming was discussing with Song Jinzhao the people of the Wumeng and Shimen tribes who had gone to Qingxia County and Yanshan County respectively to buy smokeless coal.","A faint smile played at the corners of Song Jinzhao’s lips.","“From the first month of the year until now, a total of 1,232 people from the two tribes have gone to the coal shops in Qingxia County and Yanshan County to buy smokeless coal. Their family information has all been recorded as well.”","Three ledgers, each an inch thick, lay on the table. Song Qiming flipped through them with a smile.","“Sister, your method really is the best. By requiring people to show their household registration documents when buying smokeless coal, we learned everything about the two tribes without lifting a finger.”","Although the various southwestern tribes submitted annual reports to the imperial court detailing the populations within their jurisdictions, the court had always had doubts about whether those figures were accurate.","Song Jinzhao wanted the true numbers. Thus, when residents of Qingxia County and Yanshan County went to the shops to buy smokeless coal, they were required to present their household registers.","Whenever a register showed that the buyer belonged to one of the southwestern tribes, the shopkeepers would discreetly record the information.","Officially, this was to prevent people from hoarding coal and reselling it at inflated prices. In reality, it was a means of gathering information on the southwestern tribes.","Their native places, names, ages, occupations, and even the amount of farmland owned by their families could all be found out.","Song Jinzhao tapped her fingers against the tabletop at irregular intervals as she said, “Those 1,232 people represent 1,232 households, with a total of 7,462 people. The Wumeng and Shimen tribes reported a combined population of more than 23,000. Fewer than one-third of them have bought smokeless coal.”","Song Qiming lifted one of the ledgers.","“They’re all ordinary commoners. There isn’t a single official or merchant among them.”","Song Jinzhao curled her lips into a smile. “There’s no need to hurry. A wall has to be dismantled brick by brick.”","“Tap, tap, tap—”","A burst of hurried footsteps rang out.","Yao Ye, who was standing guard at the door, lowered his hands and gripped the sword hanging from his waist.","“What is it?”","His cold voice forced the guard to calm down at once.","The guard caught his breath and pointed outside. “Someone from the front office says an imperial edict has arrived. The Young Master is to receive it immediately.”","The moment he finished speaking, the door before him opened from inside.","The guard quickly stepped back and bowed. “County Princess, Young Master.”","Song Qiming asked, “How many people came?”","“Three. One of them claims to be a Langzhong from the Ministry of Rites.”","Song Qiming turned around.","Song Jinzhao nodded. “Go on.”","By the time they reached the front office, a crowd of runners and minor clerks had already gathered outside the main hall.","When Song Qiming entered, the Langzhong from the Ministry of Rites responsible for delivering the edict immediately smiled and unrolled it to read aloud.","“By the Mandate of Heaven, the Emperor decrees: Where territories adjoin one another, only those who are loyal and diligent can preserve peace. Since taking office, Song Qiming, Prefect of Suining, has trained troops, suppressed bandits, promoted agriculture, and opened wasteland for cultivation. As a result, Suining has become peaceful and its people have enough food and clothing, which greatly pleases Us. We now bestow special favor and promote you to the rank of Senior Fifth Grade. Your official post shall remain unchanged, as recognition of your achievements. Thus We decree!”","Behind him, the entire crowd fell to its knees. Song Qiming raised both hands high to receive the imperial edict.","“Your subject thanks His Majesty for his grace. Long live the Emperor! Long live the Emperor! Long, long live the Emperor!”","After handing over the edict, the Langzhong from the Ministry of Rites hurriedly helped Song Qiming to his feet.","With a smile, he flattered him, “Lord Song, you have attained Senior Fifth Grade before even reaching the age of twenty. You truly are a remarkable young hero. Your future is limitless.”","Strictly speaking, the other man’s official rank was one grade lower than Song Qiming’s current rank. If not for the fact that Suining was so far away that no one wanted the post, Minister of Revenue Kang Zhibo would never have sent him here.","Once they were standing, the Langzhong from the Ministry of Rites asked, somewhat puzzled, “When I entered the city, I noticed that the roads in Suining were exceptionally smooth and hard. Were they newly built?”","Song Qiming handed the imperial edict to Yao Ye. “They were built last year. It was a little invention my elder sister came up with. I merely benefited from her work.”","The man’s expression tightened slightly. He moved closer to Song Qiming and lowered his voice.","“Why didn’t you report such a remarkable thing to His Majesty? It might have earned you an even higher position.”","Song Qiming covered his mouth and drew the Langzhong from the Ministry of Revenue to one side.","“The material used to build the roads is called cement. There are already shops selling it in the city.”","The single sentence made the Langzhong from the Ministry of Revenue understand immediately. He nodded with a smile.","“I see. Since Commissioner Gu didn’t mention it, I naturally won’t say anything either.”","Song Qiming gave a slight nod.","He dared to speak so frankly because the Langzhong from the Ministry of Rites was a disciple of Fei Yanzhang. They had met before at Fei’s residence."]},{"number":555,"title":"Chapter 555: Spring Agenda: Discussions for the New Season","paragraphs":["As the snow melted, sales of anthracite declined, while cement sales began to soar.","More and more households started using cement to build their homes. Even the garden paths outside and inside their houses were being paved with cement.","Not only did it make them look respectable, but it was also sturdier, cheaper, and easier to maintain than bluestone bricks.","“The year’s plans begin in spring.” On the first day of the third month, the prefects of the various prefectures across the Southwestern Province gathered at the Southwestern Administration Commissioner's Office, awaiting Gu Zhongxun’s instructions.","The eleven men stood in two rows, with Gu Huaiyuan and Song Qiming at the front of their respective lines.","Gu Zhongxun sat upright in the main hall. His gaze swept over everyone unhurriedly. He was not fierce, yet his presence made them lower their heads instinctively as their chests grew tight with anxiety.","“The first major matter after the New Year is spring plowing. Last year, aside from Songzhou Prefecture and Suining Prefecture, most of you fell behind on the grain taxes submitted to the imperial court. This year, I hope every one of you will collect the full amount. Jia Ding Prefecture in particular.”","Zou Shoushan, the Prefect of Jia Ding, immediately stiffened, and his palms began to sweat.","In previous years, Suining Prefecture had always ranked last, with Jia Ding Prefecture second from the bottom. But last year, these two unfortunate prefectures had suddenly risen to the top, leaving him in last place.","Gu Zhongxun continued, “You should also learn from Prefect Song. If you collect only half again this year, even I won’t be able to protect you.”","A bead of cold sweat dripped onto his shoe. Zou Shoushan clasped his hands and knelt to admit his mistake.","“This subordinate will certainly learn from Prefect Song and follow his methods.”","Only after applying both persuasion and pressure for a full hour did Gu Zhongxun finally dismiss them. When they left the office, many of the men’s legs were trembling, and their feet had gone numb.","“Lord Song!” Zou Shoushan called out, and three or four prefects immediately crowded around him.","On their way into the city, they had seen constables repairing the roads. After asking around, they learned that the new roads were made of cement—and that the cement came from Suining City.","“Lord Song, I’d like to buy some of the cement used to repair Songzhou City’s roads as well. I heard it costs fourteen wen per sack. Could you make it any cheaper?”","“Lord Song, how could you keep such a wonderful thing to yourself instead of telling us sooner? Hiding it away isn’t the conduct of a gentleman.”","“Lord Song, I’ll take ten thousand sacks to start. We need to repair our roads in Yueyang Prefecture too.”","“...”","They chattered on without pause, making Song Qiming’s ears ring. The other prefects had also stopped to watch.","Song Qiming raised a hand and called out loudly, “Gentlemen, gentlemen.”","Once they quieted down, Song Qiming smiled faintly. “It’s not that I wanted to keep it from you. The truth is, there simply wasn’t any stock to sell.”","“Most of the cement produced before the New Year was bought by the Administration Commissioner. What remained was only enough to sell within Suining Prefecture. But rest assured—the cement factory has been working overtime during the New Year holiday and has produced quite a lot. If you want to buy some, send someone to place an order at the shops that sell anthracite in each prefecture. Your goods should arrive within a few days.”","Then he deliberately lowered his voice. “The cement factory is my elder sister’s private business. She already sold most of it to the Administration Commissioner at a loss. It definitely can’t be any cheaper; in fact, the price will probably have to be higher.”","The Prefect of Yueyang exploded the moment he heard that.","He grabbed Song Qiming by the arm, slipped an arm around his shoulders, and whispered, “Brother Song, the people of Yueyang Prefecture are poor, and so is the government office. Fourteen wen is already an astronomical price for me. It absolutely can’t go any higher. I’ll place an order as soon as I return. You have to make sure County Princess Linghui sends someone to deliver our shipment first.”","Looking at the Yueyang Prefect’s three wisps of beard and the wrinkles at the corners of his eyes—there were so many that he could have been Song Qiming’s father—Song Qiming had no idea how the man could bring himself to call him “Brother Song.”","“To my knowledge, Yueyang Prefecture’s annual tax revenue is second only to Songzhou Prefecture’s, ranking second among the eleven prefectures.”","The Yueyang Prefect’s eyes widened. “What good does ranking second do? Which of the eleven prefectures in the Southwest isn’t poor?”","That one sentence left Song Qiming speechless.","It was true. They were all poor. At best, some were merely better off compared with the other prefectural cities in the Southwestern Province.","Bring in any prefectural city from another province, and it could crush them in every respect.","Zou Shoushan’s eyes grew slightly moist as he said to Song Qiming from the bottom of his heart, “This old man is not as fortunate as Lord Song. A sister as clever as County Princess Linghui is a rarity seen only once in a thousand years. When I have the opportunity, I shall personally pay her a visit and behold County Princess Linghui’s incomparable beauty.”","Several contemptuous gazes fell upon Zou Shoushan.","What a bootlicker. He just had to show off!"]},{"number":556,"title":"Chapter 556: Mrs. Gu: Mistakenly Believing Song Qiming and Gu Baozhu Had a Spark","paragraphs":["After leaving the government office, Song Qiming went to the Gu residence.","When Madam Gu heard that he had arrived, she raised her brows in surprise.","“What has he come here for? Isn’t Master at the government office?”","Gu Zhongxun had left early that morning for the early-spring council meeting.","The servant boy replied, “He said he has something to give to the eldest young lady.”","“Baozhu?” Madam Gu’s voice rose at the end. She lowered her eyes, pondering.","What could the two of them possibly have to give each other?","A sudden thought flashed through her mind, and Madam Gu’s eyes widened.","“Could it be...”","She drew in a breath and rose to her feet, the fist clutching her handkerchief pressing against the tabletop.","Baozhu had been spending so much time with the Song family. Could it be that she and Song Qiming had taken a liking to each other?","Just then, she saw Gu Baozhu pass by the doorway in a pale green dress with a ruffled hem. She was walking hurriedly, as though in a great rush.","Madam Gu quickly led her people after her.","“Lord Song.”","At the call, Song Qiming set down his teacup and rose. “Miss Gu.”","Once she had entered, Song Qiming picked up the wooden box on the table and held it out to her.","“These are things Shixue asked me to bring you,” he said. “With the change from winter to spring, more and more people have caught colds. She won’t be able to come to Songzhou City for the time being.”","The corners of Gu Baozhu’s lips, which had just lifted, immediately drooped.","“I knew she wouldn’t have the time to come.”","They had agreed it would be after the New Year. She had thought that Shixue would come with Song Qiming this time, but it seemed that plan had fallen through again.","After a few moments of disappointment, Gu Baozhu reached out and hugged the wooden box.","“I’m sorry to trouble Lord Song, but please tell Shixue that the crabapple blossoms in Songzhou City will be blooming in another month. She must come and enjoy them.”","Song Qiming nodded. “I’ll be sure to pass that along.”","Madam Gu, who had been hiding outside the door, had heard that the entire conversation was about Song Shixue. Seeing the respectful, composed expressions on their faces, the curiosity in her heart instantly faded.","It seemed there was nothing romantic between them after all.","Having understood the situation, Madam Gu turned and left. The nanny beside her noticed the lack of a smile on her face and hesitated before asking, “Madam, you don’t seem very happy.”","Madam Gu stopped and sighed. “I’m worried about Baozhu’s marriage. Why is that child in no hurry at all?”","The nanny smiled. “In this old servant’s opinion, it’s a good thing that Miss didn’t take a liking to Prefect Song. The Song family will be transferred back to the capital sooner or later. With you and Master so far away and unable to stay by her side, what will she do if someone bullies her?”","Madam Gu sighed and shook her head.","“I never intended for Baozhu to marry far from home. It’s just that when I suddenly thought of Song Qiming, setting aside the fact that he’ll eventually return to the capital, he is absolutely the finest match in the entire southwestern province.”","After returning to her room, the two continued chatting.","The nanny said, “Come to think of it, Prefect Song’s parents are both deceased. If Miss married him, she wouldn’t have to suffer mistreatment from her parents-in-law. Her life would certainly be comfortable.”","Madam Gu shook her head. “Not necessarily. Baozhu said that County Princess Linghui intends to take a husband into her household. If that really happens, then even if Baozhu married into the Song family, she would have no way to take charge of the household.”","“Now that I think about it, he isn’t such a good candidate after all.”","Hearing this, the nanny wisely fell silent.","Back in Suining City, Song Qiming passed on the message.","“Miss Gu invited you to Songzhou City to admire the crabapple blossoms a month from now. Try to keep your schedule open. She seemed rather disappointed this time.”","Song Shixue had just finished writing a prescription.","“I know. I’ll go then.”","If there hadn’t been so many patients suffering from colds lately, she would already have gone to Songzhou City yesterday.","Before dinner, Song Anhao lounged on the couch in the study, rolling a banknote between her fingers.","“Once you have too much money and nowhere to spend it, it starts to feel meaningless.”","Song Qiming happened to step through the door with one foot just as he heard this. A feeling of being blocked in the chest came over him.","“You’re not out of places to spend money. You’re just too stingy to spend it. Even when you go out to buy roast chicken, you have to haggle with the shopkeeper.”","Song Anhao immediately sat up straight and puffed out her cheeks as she defended herself.","“He charges more than everyone else. Of course I have to bargain! Otherwise, wouldn’t I be making a fool of myself?”","Sitting behind the writing desk, Song Jinzhao pressed her lips together to hide a smile.","Song Qiming waved his hand. “You may leave. I have something to discuss with Elder Sister.”","Song Anhao puffed out both cheeks, climbed down from the couch, and went out, closing the door behind her."]},{"number":557,"title":"Chapter 557: Selling Houses in Laocheng Camp","paragraphs":["Song Qiming sat down across from Song Jinzhao.","“Elder Sister, now that half of Laocheng Camp is empty, shouldn’t we sell it?”","At the end of last year, all the prisoners whose crimes were minor and whose hands were free of blood were released and sent home. With fewer prisoners, half of Laocheng Camp now stood vacant.","When the camp was first built, they had said it would eventually be sold. Song Qiming felt that the time had now come.","Song Jinzhao said, “We can sell it, but we’ll need to build a ten-foot-high wall through the middle first. The remaining bandits all have blood on their hands.”","Song Qiming nodded firmly. “Don’t worry, Elder Sister. They all have their hands and feet shackled, and three hundred constables are keeping watch over Laocheng Camp day and night. It’s absolutely safe.”","They worked themselves to exhaustion during the day, then spent every night snoring. Not a single fight had broken out there in the past year.","Once word spread that the government was selling the houses, people crowded around the public notice boards.","“What’s so good about buying a house outside the city? There isn’t another person around.”","“People have died in those cells before. Has the government gone mad?”","“What kind of houses are they, and how much do they cost?”","“...”","Questions sprang up like bamboo shoots after a spring rain. The constable standing in front of the notice board raised his hand and shouted, “Quiet, everyone!”","“First, no one has died in the cells. Those whose crimes were minor were released and sent home at the end of last year.","“Second, the houses are just outside the city. There are homes with one main room and one inner room, as well as homes with one main room and two inner rooms. You can go and take a look for yourselves. Someone will be there to show you around.","“Third, a one-room house costs around three taels of silver, while a two-room house costs about six taels. Prices may vary depending on the location. Anyone who wants to see them can go now.","“Fourth, people without household registration in Suining City can have their registration transferred on the spot after purchasing a house. Those who came to Suining City from elsewhere to work within the past six months and signed a labor contract lasting more than three months may purchase a house at eighty percent of the original price. Supplies are limited, so it’s first come, first served. Does anyone have any other questions? Raise your hands, one at a time.”","The same scene unfolded in front of every public notice board throughout the city.","Before long, the temporary inquiry office set up at the entrance to Laocheng Camp outside the city welcomed its first group of prospective buyers.","A constable led one interested customer around the vast campgrounds in the west.","“The row of houses closest to the river costs an extra three hundred copper coins. All the others are the same price.”","The curious townsman looked around before pointing at the constables mixing cement in the distance.","“Officer, what are they doing?”","The constable smiled. “The prefect ordered a ten-foot-high wall to be built through the middle. There are also several hundred constables patrolling the other side day and night, all to ensure everyone’s safety.”","Hearing that the wall would be ten feet high and that several hundred constables would stand guard, many people felt somewhat reassured.","At the same time, the cement factory and the coal mine passed along a message to their workers.","“Workers who wish to purchase a house in Laocheng Camp may, after completing one month of work, draw up to three months’ wages in advance to pay for it. Anyone interested should register with their team leader.”","The moment those words were spoken, many workers’ heads began to buzz.","After a brief silence, the uproar nearly lifted the roof off the factory, especially among the migrant workers.","Beside a clay kiln in a corner of the yard, a man who had arrived less than two months earlier stared blankly at the departing overseer.","A one-main-room, one-inner-room house cost three taels of silver. A few days ago, he had sent five hundred copper coins home, leaving himself with four hundred. Even after adding three months’ wages, he would still be short by two hundred copper coins—and he would need money for the following three months as well.","Thinking of his parents, who were suffering from tuberculosis, and his younger brother, who was still a child, the man clenched his teeth. After a moment’s thought, he quietly set down the shovel in his hand.","He went to find the junior overseer who had just made the announcement.","“Manager Li, about what you said just now about buying a house... Could I draw four months’ wages in advance?”","Manager Li looked at the man.","He remembered him. The man was from Qingxia County. When he had arrived, he had said that both his parents were suffering from tuberculosis and that he had a younger brother who was not yet ten years old. With no money to buy medicine, he had been forced to come to Suining City to find work.","Manager Li sympathized with him, but there were rules at the factory to consider as well.","After hesitating for a moment, he eventually shook his head.","“Three months is the rule set by the people above. If I make an exception for you, what will I do when everyone else comes asking?”","The longing in the man’s eyes immediately faded.","Unwilling to give up, he fell to his knees and raised a hand in oath. “Manager Li, I swear I won’t tell anyone.”","Manager Li hurriedly helped him to his feet and patiently explained, “Everyone who leaves home to make a living has it hard. If you truly want to buy a house at Laocheng Camp, why not go home and sell your old house?”","The man froze. Sell the house back home? He had never considered it.","Manager Li continued, “If you bring your whole family here, you won’t have any use for the house in your old village anyway. You might as well sell it.”","“You’ve seen what Suining City is like. It’s bound to keep improving. Take advantage of this opportunity to transfer your household registration here. From now on, this can be your home.”","The man blinked as he thought, his mind in turmoil.","Manager Li reached out and patted him on the shoulder.","“Make your decision quickly. There aren’t many houses left at Laocheng Camp. If you wait too long, you may not be able to buy one even if you want to.”","With that, he turned and walked away, giving the man plenty of time to think."]},{"number":558,"title":"Chapter 558: It'll Be Gone If You Wait Any Longer","paragraphs":["For the first two days, most people were still hesitating over whether to buy. While they compared locations and prices and tried to scrape together the money, several houses in Laocheng Camp were quietly sold.","When the townspeople came for a second viewing and saw that more than half the houses on the signboard had been crossed out, their eyes widened with alarm.","One man grabbed an attendant and asked, his beard trembling.","“Sir, have all the houses marked with red crosses been sold?”","The attendant nodded. “Yes, they’ve all been sold.”","The news struck him like a bolt from the blue, and the question slipped out before he could stop himself.","“How did they sell so quickly?”","The attendant smiled. “They were bought by laborers from out of town who work at the cement and coal factories. County Princess Linghui took pity on them for having left their homes behind, so anyone who wanted to buy a house in Laocheng Camp could draw three months of wages in advance.”","The townsman’s eyes filled with envy. “If only I’d known, I would’ve gone to work at the coal factory too.”","As the two men spoke, another attendant approached from behind. He was holding a red brush, and he drew a cross over the house at the far right of the third row.","At this point, only three of the single-entry houses remained, all of them near the outer wall.","Seeing this, the attendant asked, “Do you want a one-hall, one-room house, or a one-hall, two-room house?”","The townsman opened and closed his mouth. “I want a one-hall, one-room house.”","The attendant raised an eyebrow. “Then you’d better hurry. There are only three left. They’ll be gone if you wait any longer.”","“If you really want one, you can pay a deposit to reserve it. But remember, if you change your mind after paying, the deposit won’t be refunded.”","When they had come to look the day before, no one had been willing to pay a deposit.","First, they had thought there were plenty of houses and that they wouldn’t have trouble buying one.","Second, they had been worried that the deposit was nonrefundable and might go to waste.","Even now, they were still wavering. After agonizing over it for a long while, they finally hurried home.","Meanwhile, the man who had applied the day before for four months’ wages in advance clutched a stamped deposit receipt as he ran back to the dormitory.","He had already requested leave from the supervisor and planned to return to Qingxia County immediately to sell his house, then bring his parents and younger brother over to live with him.","After lunch, Qingshuang carried a thick stack of official cement orders to Song Jinzhao.","“County Princess, these are orders sent in by various prefectures and counties. Altogether, they amount to three hundred and sixty-eight thousand bags of cement.”","Lanxi had gone to the capital to deliver a letter, so Qingshuang was temporarily overseeing the cement factory.","Song Jinzhao flipped through the orders one by one. Yueyang Prefecture had placed the largest order.","“Do we have enough in stock?”","Qingshuang replied, “We’re short by sixty thousand bags, but we can finish producing them within half a month.”","Song Jinzhao calmly placed the orders back on the desk.","“Send the cement ordered by the counties under Sुईning Prefecture first. For the other prefectures and counties, plan the delivery routes carefully and save as much time and expense as possible. All these orders must be delivered within a month.”","“Yes.” Qingshuang’s reply was loud and resolute.","Seven days later, the smokeless-coal shop in Qingxia County was selling both cement and smokeless coal.","Dozens of carts were parked outside the shop, while the shopkeeper led his assistants in checking the shipment.","The guard in charge of escorting the cement handed him the delivery receipt. “Sign it if everything is in order.”","The shopkeeper accepted it with a smile. After inspecting the goods and confirming that everything was correct, he wrote his name in the signature column and pressed his thumbprint onto the page.","He sighed with emotion. “The county office has urged us several times. It’s finally arrived.”","The guard kept a duplicate in his pocket. “Qingxia County was the first delivery. We’ve already gotten it here as quickly as we could.”","Zhao Jinmin and Song Qiming were both friends and classmates, so Qingshuang knew without needing to ask which order should be delivered first.","After delivering the goods ordered by the county office, more than three hundred bags of cement remained in the rear courtyard.","The shopkeeper directed the assistants, “Move all of these to the front hall and put them up for sale.”"]},{"number":559,"title":"Chapter 559: The Wumeng Clan Secretly Buying Cement Was Discovered","paragraphs":["As soon as the cement was moved into the front hall, a customer came in to buy smokeless coal and began asking questions.","“Is this the cement being used to build the roads in Suining City? How much is a bag?”","The shop assistant replied, “Twenty wen a bag.”","The assistant who had just been loading coal for the man stopped what he was doing and looked over from behind the counter.","Remembering the man’s identity as recorded in the household register, he casually walked behind the counter, picked up the ledger, and headed toward the rear courtyard.","“Shopkeeper, there’s someone from the Wumeng tribe outside who wants to buy cement.”","The shopkeeper took the open ledger. The man’s identity was written there in clear detail.","A traveling peddler.","“How many bags does he want?”","The assistant shook his head. “I’m not sure. He’s still outside.”","The two of them went behind the curtain and stopped there. The conversation outside could be heard clearly.","“You want all three hundred bags?”","The man laughed and patted his chest. “I make my living transporting goods. I thought I’d buy more and earn a little profit by selling them back home.”","“Since I’m buying so much, can you give me a discount?”","The assistant refused. “This price is already very low. County Princess Linghui barely makes any profit on it so that ordinary people can afford to use cement.”","The man refused to give up. “How can you do business without making money? I heard you sell cement to the government offices for only fourteen wen a bag. I’m not asking for the same price—eighteen wen a bag will do.”","The shopkeeper, standing behind the curtain, narrowed his eyes.","The price for cement sold to government offices in other prefectures and counties was fifteen wen a bag. Only the cement sold to Songzhou City was priced at fourteen wen.","The assistant shook his head firmly. “Government offices buy tens of thousands of bags at a time, and they’re using it to build public roads. Naturally, the price is different.”","The man waved his hand up and down, arguing his case. “If this deal goes through, I’ll definitely buy more next time. Give me a little discount.”","The assistant opened and closed his lips several times, then steadied himself and put on a troubled expression.","“How about this? I’ll ask the shopkeeper, though I can’t promise he’ll agree. After all, our cement isn’t in short supply.”","The shopkeeper and the other assistant standing behind the curtain hurried back into the courtyard.","Once the assistant had come in, the shopkeeper said calmly, “Give him a discount of one wen. He’ll have to arrange transportation himself.”","The assistant nodded. After standing there for a moment, he went back outside.","As soon as he saw the man pay, the shopkeeper rushed back to his room and changed into another outfit. He even stuck on a beard and added a mole to his face.","Before long, the man found several strong laborers to load all the cement onto a cart. They headed out of the city.","After leaving the city, they traveled toward Yinma Town, which lay across a mountain from the Wumeng tribal lands.","The shopkeeper followed them the entire way, passing through forests and crossing gorges. When he saw them enter a residence in the center of a Wumeng settlement, his suspicions were confirmed.","It was the residence of the Wumeng tribe’s successive chieftains.","A homing pigeon delivered the news to Song Jinzhao the following day at noon.","“Let them buy it, just as we did with the smokeless coal.”","Once cement was produced, it was bound to become the best choice for every household building homes and repairing roads. Song Jinzhao had never considered stopping the southwestern tribes from using it.","As long as she had explosives in hand, even if they truly came to blows one day, Song Jinzhao was not worried about losing.","...","In just four days, all three hundred houses in Laocheng Camp had been sold. The speed was astonishing.","Two hundred of them had been bought by the commoners working at the cement and coal factories.","Whenever those people, finally getting a single day off, came out to shop in their identical work clothes, many passersby looked at them enviously.","The outsiders who had found other work in Suining City after missing the factory recruitment were especially envious.","A villager delivering vegetables to a restaurant saw an acquaintance squatting on the ground and asked curiously, “Yu Gui, did you buy a house?”","The man called Yu Gui raised his head. His pupils were dull, devoid of any light.","“My employer refused to sign a three-month labor contract with me. I could only buy one at the full price, so I didn’t.”","The villager froze.","For a house with one hall and one inner room, the eighty-percent price and the full price differed by six hundred wen. Without a labor contract, that was a huge loss.","“Didn’t you plead with him?”","Yu Gui shook his head. “I did, but he refused.”","As he spoke, a bitter smile appeared on his face. “There are several people on this street who want to buy one, just like me. They’re all held back by the labor contract.”","The villager sighed. “The cement and coal factories really are better. Not only do they sign contracts for half a year at a time, they’ll even advance three months’ wages.”","Yu Gui gazed enviously at the assistant serving customers in the braised-meat shop across the street.","“It isn’t just the cement and coal factories. The shops owned by County Princess Linghui all pay higher wages than other places. They even give out gifts during festivals. It’s just too difficult to get in.”","Apart from the cement and coal factories, most of the assistants in Song Jinzhao’s shops had signed lifetime contracts. Some of them were covert guards planted there as well, so the shops rarely recruited from outside.","Even when they did recruit, the wages and benefits were so good that countless applicants competed for each position.","Only one person was chosen from dozens of candidates. The difficulty was practically the same as ascending to the heavens.","The villagers had heard about this too. “You should wait for the cement and coal factories to recruit again and try then. I heard that government offices in all the prefectures have been buying cement recently. It probably won’t be long before they start hiring again.”","Yu Gui pressed his lips together and sighed. “I hope so. Half the houses in Laocheng Camp are still unsold. Maybe I’ll make it in time.”","The villager shook his head in disagreement.","“The remaining bandits have all killed people. Unless they die of old age or exhaustion, they’ll never get out.”"]},{"number":560,"title":"Chapter 560: The Three Yang Brothers: As Incompatible as Water and Fire","paragraphs":["No one knew whether they would be able to get out, but one thing was certain: the bandits were going to be put to work again.","After lying fallow through the winter, the fields were hard as stone.","They had to break open the gray-black soil inch by inch with plows and hoes, releasing the rich, earthy scent of freshly turned ground.","In addition to the wasteland reclaimed last year, Song Qiming had ordered another thousand mu to be cultivated this year.","It was not just him. Along both banks of the Immortal River, stretching two li in either direction, the wasteland that the common people had once scorned as too far away was now being claimed by eager farmers—all because they had heard that the government intended to extend the irrigation channels.","Seven hundred li from Suining City, in Panzhou.","Pacification Commissioner Yang Ruiping stared at the cement ground after it had hardened, his eyes filled with astonishment.","“Song Jinzhao is selling it openly. He isn’t guarding against us at all.”","When he had previously sent his steward Yang Mo to deliver a gift of thanks, he had learned that Suining City had built cement roads.","But hearing about them was different from seeing them with his own eyes. And since they had been unable to obtain any cement at the time, Yang Ruiping had not taken the matter too seriously.","This time, it was only because Yang Cenan had insisted on buying some that the Wumeng tribe had sent people over.","Standing to one side, Yang Cenan slowly spoke. “The Song family made its fortune through commerce. Merchants value profit above all else. As long as they can make money, they’ll sell to anyone.”","A smile tugged at the corners of Yang Ruiping’s mouth, but his eyes remained cold.","“That’s good. A man without weaknesses would be frightening indeed.”","“Since they’re willing to sell, send people to buy from them. Whatever Dongzhao has, Panzhou must have as well.”","Yang Cenan took a step back and bowed his head. “Your son understands.”","Yang Ruiping’s eldest son, Yang Cedong, saw his third brother emerge from the council hall. The hatred in his eyes raked across the other man like a knife.","When Yang Cenan spotted Yang Cedong, he stopped. Their eyes met, sharp as blades, clashing in the air hundreds of times.","Yang Cedong sneered. “Don’t think Father favors you. That doesn’t mean the position of heir is yours for the taking.”","“Our Yang clan has never had a leader who stammers and wears a face as stiff as a corpse.”","Although Yang Cenan’s body had recovered, the paralysis in his face had never improved. He either stammered when he spoke or spoke with a slight, sluggish drawl.","His sore spot having been struck, the corner of Yang Cenan’s mouth twitched faintly as he replied, “Even if I can’t speak clearly or make expressions, I’m still better than a useless good-for-nothing like you.”","Yang Cedong’s face flushed with anger. “Did you kill my son?”","Yang Cenan curved his lips. “Brother, you jest. I wasn’t even in Panzhou at the time, so how could I have killed your son?”","“I’d say it’s because you’ve done too many evil deeds. This is simply retribution.”","Watching his brother walk away with a furious wave of his sleeve, Yang Cedong clenched his fists, wishing he could charge over and kill him on the spot.","Behind a pillar not far away, Yang Cexi watched the two men walk off in opposite directions, a satisfied smile curling across his lips.","When the snipe and the clam fight, the fisherman profits. Ideally, the two of them would kill each other. Then the position of heir would naturally fall into his hands.","The crabapple blossoms opened in late March. In early April, as promised, Song Shixue arrived in Songzhou City. Song Anhao came with her.","Madam Gu could not help sighing when she saw the two girls enter the room arm in arm, looking as close as sisters.","“There’s only Baozhu in the family, and she really does get bored sometimes.”","The older maid smiled. “How could she be bored? Young Master Jinghong is always by her side.”","Madam Gu shook her head. “Jinghong spends more and more time at the military camp. Baozhu hasn’t even left the house for several days.”","In the martial arts yard behind the residence, Gu Jinghong crouched in front of Song Anhao, his eyes shining.","“Can I touch it?”","Hearing that Gu Jinghong wanted to touch the tiger, his personal attendant Laixi hurried over to stop him. Several guards standing beneath the wall also quickly came forward.","Song Anhao tightened her grip on the rope and hugged Xuetuan around the neck as she shook her head.","“Xuetuan is a little wary of strangers. It might bite you.”","Gu Jinghong stared greedily at Xuetuan. His pale blue eyes gleamed as he tilted his head to one side. With Song Anhao shielding it beneath her, he looked like a gigantic cat.","After being stared at for too long, the impatient Xuetuan opened its jaws and let out an “Awooo~”","Its sharp teeth made everyone’s scalp prickle, and fear rose in their hearts.","Gu Jinghong stood up and muttered to himself, “You really do have to raise one from the time it’s a cub. If only I could raise one too.”","Laixi pressed his lips into a thin line, feeling helpless.","Even raising one from childhood wouldn’t work. Hadn’t they noticed that this white tiger’s brain was wired wrong? If he raised an ordinary one, it would be capable of biting a person to death by the time it was a year old if it didn’t obey."]},{"number":561,"title":"Chapter 561: Enjoying Flowers at Songzhou City","paragraphs":["On his way back from the academy, Gu Congwen heard the commotion and turned toward the martial arts yard.","Passing through the arched gate, he saw an enormous white tiger tied to a training post. He froze where he stood.","His trembling gaze swept across the yard, where seven or eight people had formed a circle. At the center stood Gu Jinghong and Song Anhao, facing each other with swords in hand. Their movements crossed in a manner that looked extremely dangerous.","Xuetuan’s forelegs were off the ground as it strained against the rope, roaring furiously at Gu Jinghong. Its growls were fierce and urgent.","“Jinghong!”","After taking a wide detour around Xuetuan, Gu Congwen shouted angrily, his face dark with displeasure.","Gu Jinghong’s sword halted. Song Anhao had no time to pull his own blade back, and it struck Gu Jinghong’s arm, slicing open a tear in his sleeve.","Gu Congwen was startled at first, but when he saw that the wound was not bleeding, his anger returned.","“How could you spar with a child? He’s more than ten years younger than you!”","Song Anhao had never met Gu Congwen before, and he looked at Gu Jinghong in confusion.","“Who is this older brother?”","Gu Jinghong hurriedly introduced him with a smile. “He’s my elder cousin, Gu Congwen, the son of my father’s elder brother.”","Then he explained to Gu Congwen, “I knew what I was doing. I was holding back.”","Song Anhao lifted his chin. “He isn’t more than ten years older. I’ll be nine after the New Year, so there’s only a ten-year difference.”","He tightened his grip on the sword and raised it. “I’ve practiced martial arts since I was little. Sparring is an everyday occurrence for me, and I agreed to this just now.”","Gu Congwen stared at Song Anhao, as though he were looking at Gu Jinghong when he was young.","They had the same natural courage.","Like a newborn calf unafraid of a tiger, they were all the more eager to try something the more challenging it was.","After taking a breath, he said, “Shixue praised you for being good at your studies as well. You’ve always ranked near the top in the academy’s examinations. Why don’t you come with me to Songzhou Academy tomorrow? By observing how the various schools of thought converge, you’ll be able to broaden your own learning.”","Song Anhao’s eyes widened. His chest rose and fell like waves surging in a storm.","“Tomorrow I’m going to admire the begonias with everyone else, so I’m afraid I won’t have time to go to the academy.”","“Then the day after tomorrow will do.”","Song Anhao shook his head furiously. “The day after that, I’m going into the city to visit all the bookstores. I won’t have time then either.”","Gu Congwen knitted his brows. Remembering that they would be leaving the day after next, he could only give up with a helpless sigh.","“Then come the next time you visit. I hear you study under Lord Dongfang, the former Grand Secretary. I’d truly like to see what you’ve learned.”","Song Anhao gave two fake laughs and tugged at his collar to fan himself.","“We worked up quite a sweat during that spar. I’m going back to change clothes.”","With that, he hurried over to the training post, untied Xuetuan, and ran off leading the tiger.","Gu Jinghong cast a helpless glance at Gu Congwen.","“Not everyone likes studying as much as you do. Look—you scared him away.”","Gu Congwen paid no heed. “He’s still young and hasn’t outgrown his playful nature. That’s precisely why he needs someone to guide him.”","“Song Qiming placed third in the palace examination. If his younger brother can still rank near the top at the academy after going to Suining City, then he must be guiding him at home every day.”","Gu Jinghong shook his head in disagreement.","“I don’t think so. County Princess Linghui has already begun having Song Anhao learn about trade. That child is studying all sorts of things. In the future, he may not necessarily enter government service.”","Gu Congwen remained firm in his opinion.","“Although Song Jinzhao is a county princess, strictly speaking, Song Qiming is the only official in the Song family. If they want the family to flourish, they’ll need more men in office—just like our family.”","Gu Jinghong fell silent in thought. It did seem to make some sense.","He looked up at Gu Congwen and smiled. “Song Anhao could also take up the martial path, like my father and your father—or you and me.”","Gu Congwen pressed his lips into a smile. Everything was understood without needing to be said."]},{"number":562,"title":"Chapter 562: Discovered that a large number of similar derivative script copies have been listed","paragraphs":["In Gu Baozhu’s room, the two of them sat on round stools, discussing their flower-viewing plans for the next day.","“There won’t just be a vast sea of flowering crabapple trees. There’s also a strange and spectacular forest of cloud-wreathed stone pillars, many of which are engraved with poems—all written by scholars who have earned the juren degree.”","“The flowers are at their peak these days, so plenty of people go there every day for spring outings and picnics in the open. But I know a beautiful spot where hardly anyone goes. I’ll take you there tomorrow.”","“Before we set out, we’ll stop by Ruyi Study to buy some food. Then we can spread out a mat and sit right there. We can even fly kites over the lake.”","Song Shixue listened, nodding from time to time and giving a soft “Mm.”","By the time Song Anhao led Xuetuan over, the teapot on their table had already been replaced once.","“How did the sparring go?” Song Shixue asked with a smile, turning her head toward him.","After patting Xuetuan on the head and letting it lie down on the floor, Song Anhao sat down and said, “We had only just started when Sister Baozhu’s eldest nephew arrived. He gave Brother Jinghong a good scolding and even wanted to take me to observe classes and exchange ideas at Songzhou Academy, so I hurried back.”","At that, Gu Baozhu pulled the corners of her mouth into a smile. “Congwen has loved reading since he was little. Apart from eating, washing, and sleeping, he spends every hour of the day immersed in poetry and books. Whenever he meets someone talented, he wants to strike up a conversation with them.”","Noticing the many books arranged on the shelf beside the folding screen, Song Anhao immediately spotted a new storybook written by Liu Ruoxi.","“Sister Baozhu, may I look at those?” Many of the titles were ones Song Anhao had never seen in the bookstores of Suining City.","Song Shixue glanced at the storybooks on the shelf and gave him a knowing smile.","“Ever since the Peach Blossom Hermit published the second volume of her story, many books with similar plots have appeared in Songzhou City. Those are the ones I bought recently.”","Song Anhao walked over and casually pulled out a book. The cover bore the title The Story of Yun Niang, differing from The Story of Qin Niang by only one character.","He sat down and opened to the first page. It was another tale of household intrigue. The writing was relatively rough, but the plot moved quickly, making it the same sort of book as The Story of Qin Niang.","After reading the first third, Song Anhao had a general idea of what it was about. He returned the book to its place, picked up another, and opened it.","They were all exactly the same type—nothing more than imitations.","The more Song Anhao read, the heavier his heart became. He closed the book and sat there in a daze.","“Why haven’t I seen these kinds of books in the bookstores of Suining City?”","Gu Baozhu shook her head with a smile.","“Everyone knows that the author who pioneered The Story of Qin Niang may be from Suining City. Your Song family is the most powerful family in Suining Prefecture, so who would dare sell imitations there?”","“But don’t worry. These books aren’t as well written as the Peach Blossom Hermit’s. They’re merely substitutes for passing the time. Some of them are so dull that they make people want to doze off while reading.”","Song Shixue took the dark-blue book from Song Anhao’s hands and opened it.","After a moment, she looked up and said, “There’s a bit too much pointless chatter, but it’s readable enough. I just don’t know how well it sells.”","Song Anhao bit his lips tightly, his thoughts in complete disarray.","“I’ll visit the bookstores in the city tomorrow morning, then come find you two around noon.”","When he had more money than he knew how to spend, Song Anhao had found life rather dull. Now that he knew someone was trying to take a share of his business, he was anxious again.","As they chatted, nearly an hour passed. A maid from Gu Baozhu’s courtyard entered and said, “Miss, lunch has been served.”","Gu Baozhu rose with a smile. “Come on, let’s eat in the reception hall.”","Afraid things might become awkward—and because Song Anhao was still young—she had already spoken with Madam Gu. Whenever Song Shixue visited, they would dine separately in her courtyard."]},{"number":563,"title":"Chapter 563: Departing for the Stone Forest Flower Sea","paragraphs":["The next morning, Song Anhao set out first with Yao Ying and two guards. An hour later, Gu Baozhu and Song Shixue departed together for the Stone Forest Flower Sea.","This time, Gu Baozhu did not allow Gu Jinghong to accompany them. She brought only two maids and four guards.","It took the carriage half an hour to reach their destination. Along the way, one of the guards stopped at Ruyi House to buy some pastries.","When Song Shixue lifted the carriage curtain, she saw a row of carriages at the foot of a small hill, along with a few scattered vendors setting up their stalls.","The vendors caught sight of Gu Baozhu and Song Shixue getting down from the carriage. Their eyes immediately lit up, and they began hawking their wares with renewed vigor.","“Crispy honey cakes, fresh from the oven!”","“Freshly made glutinous rice dumplings, still steaming! We have red-bean paste, sesame and nut, and osmanthus honey fillings!”","The cries drew Song Shixue’s attention. She had just started to slow down for a closer look when Gu Baozhu took her arm and led her away.","“I’ve tried all of these before. They’re only so-so—not even a tenth as good as the ones from Ruyi House.”","Hearing this, Song Shixue secretly chuckled.","As the two women proceeded up the hill surrounded by maids and guards, the vendors who had been shouting moments ago could not help showing their disappointment.","The owner of the wonton stall on the right collected the bowls and chopsticks left by his customers and placed them in a basin. As he washed them, he said to the vendor beside him, “They’re carrying food boxes. They definitely won’t buy anything from us.”","The vendor selling crispy honey cakes lowered his head and grumbled, “That young lady in yellow was just about to come over, but the one in green stopped her.”","The vendor on the left, who sold glutinous rice dumplings, immediately put on a solemn expression and scolded him, “Keep your voice down. That’s the daughter of Lord Gu, the provincial administration commissioner.”","The crispy-honey-cake vendor’s face changed, and his gaze shot toward the figures disappearing behind the hill.","When he saw no reaction from them, his rapidly pounding heart finally began to settle.","Thankfully, they hadn’t heard him. Otherwise, he would have been finished.","After descending the slope, they could see from a distance the cloud-mist stones of various sizes and bizarre shapes. Their surfaces were a blue-gray, with natural white markings like snow-covered mountains spiraling upward along their layered formations.","The white areas were as clear as fresh snow, while the dark portions gleamed with a moist luster. Layer upon layer, they resembled a naturally formed ink-wash painting.","The largest cloud-mist stone bore the inscription:","“Strange peaks and wondrous rocks—could clouds have fallen from the sky?","Or did an immortal cast down a jade hairpin?”","Gu Baozhu’s eyes curved with a smile, and the corners of her lips rose uncontrollably.","“My father wrote that when he took office as the provincial administration commissioner of the southwest fifteen years ago. After all these years, the carved marks have faded considerably.”","Song Shixue stared at the lines, polished until they gleamed. Judging by the inscriptions on the cloud-mist stone behind them to the right, these two verses must have been touched by countless hands.","“His brushwork could startle the wind and rain. Your father must have carried great ambitions in his heart back then.”","The smile in Gu Baozhu’s eyes faded, and a trace of melancholy appeared on her face.","“It’s a pity that things did not turn out as he wished. After all these years, there are hopes that one is destined never to attain in a lifetime.”","Remembering what her elder sister and brother had discussed at home, Song Shixue pressed her lips together and said nothing.","About fifteen minutes later, a vast sea of begonias came into view. An endless sweep of pink and white linked the green grass with the deep blue sky. As the spring breeze stirred the blossoms, the air carried a quiet, distant fragrance, as though it had drifted across a stream.","Voices floated over from the distance. Looking ahead, Song Shixue saw a riot of color. The brightly dressed visitors made the begonia grove itself seem almost like a mere backdrop.","Covering her mouth, Gu Baozhu whispered, “It’s like this every year. The moment there are too many people, it becomes noisy. Quite a few even treat this place as a romantic destination, like the peach-blossom groves where couples pledge themselves to one another. Every time the begonias wither, there’s always a sudden increase in weddings throughout Songzhou.”","Song Shixue’s lips twitched.","When they drew closer, they saw quite a few scholars in round-collared scholar’s robes gathered in the pavilion to the west.","Although the two groups were separated by a wide stretch of open ground, people from either side kept stealing glances at one another, their eyes shy yet filled with smiles.","Gu Baozhu led Song Shixue around the edge, following a narrow path."]},{"number":564,"title":"Chapter 564: Forced Coincidence Encounter","paragraphs":["Qiu Wangzhi, who had been chatting with his fellow classmates in the pavilion from time to time, sprang to his feet as if stung by a needle the moment he caught sight of Gu Baozhu.","The ink-stained writing brush slipped from his hand and fell to the ground. A scholar beside him frowned unhappily at the ink spots splashed across his clothes.","“Brother Qiu, what has you so flustered?”","Qiu Wangzhi hurriedly cupped his hands. “My apologies. I have suddenly remembered an urgent matter. I must be going.”","The others watched his anxious departure, their faces filled with confusion.","“He was the one most eager to come this morning. Why is he leaving already?”","Gu Baozhu led Song Shixue onward for quite some time before finally stopping. The path ahead was blocked by clouds of mist and rocks of all sizes.","Gathering up her skirts, Gu Baozhu stepped onto the stones. “Once we cross this rocky slope, we’ll reach the place I wanted to show you.”","The rocks were jumbled together, all sharp edges and uneven surfaces. Song Shixue’s embroidered shoes slipped and caught painfully against them.","Fortunately, Song Shixue, Gu Baozhu’s maid, and the guards who had accompanied them were all nimble enough to cross steadily and safely.","At the highest point of the rocky slope stood several flowering crabapple trees, with a few cloud-mist stones beneath them that reached about knee height.","Looking down from there, an entire forest of rocks and sea of flowers unfolded before their eyes. In an instant, their hearts and bodies seemed to open up with the view.","Seeing the look of enjoyment on Song Shixue’s face, Gu Baozhu smiled.","“I told you this was the most beautiful view here.”","A falling petal landed in Song Shixue’s hand, and she nodded in agreement.","“The best part is that there are so few people. It’s peaceful.”","Flowers bloomed overhead, while the scenery below was even more magnificent. In the distance, they could see the tiled roofs of houses, and the river shimmered with bright, sparkling waves.","By the time the two turned around, the maid had already spread two layers of pale green cotton cloth over the stones and placed two soft cushions on top.","The food from the chest had been set out between them, and even the milk tea was still hot.","Sitting on the cushions, the two gazed at the distant scenery and chatted, as though they would never run out of things to say.","Heye peeled a mandarin and handed it to Song Shixue. When she turned back, she happened to glimpse someone in white hiding behind a tree.","Her expression changed, and she shouted coldly, “Who’s there?”","She raised her right hand and took aim, the concealed sleeve arrow ready to fire at any moment.","The sudden shout made Song Shixue and Gu Baozhu turn around, and it startled Qiu Wangzhi as well.","He drew a deep breath, stepped out from behind the tree, and bowed toward Gu Baozhu with cupped hands.","“Miss Gu, it’s been a long time.”","Gu Baozhu frowned in confusion. “You are?”","She was fairly certain they had never met. His face looked especially unfamiliar.","Qiu Wangzhi inclined his head, the corners of his mouth curving into what he believed was a refined and gracious smile.","“My surname is Qiu, and my given name is Wangzhi. My father is the Yueyang Prefect. We met briefly at Lord Gu’s birthday banquet three years ago.”","Gu Baozhu’s brows drew together even more tightly. She studied his face carefully, certain that she had no impression of him whatsoever.","“It was too long ago. I don’t quite remember.”","The Yueyang Prefect did have a son, but the portrait her mother had shown her did not seem to look anything like this.","A flicker of disappointment crossed Qiu Wangzhi’s eyes before quickly turning into another faint smile.","He looked down at the forest of rocks and sea of flowers beneath his feet, puffed out his chest, and put on an expression of rapture.","“Silken clouds drape the emerald peaks, while jade blossoms tailor robes for ten thousand valleys.","“Standing high amid the azure void, I watch my sleeves stir the stars and scatter their radiant glow.","“I never expected that taking a wrong turn by chance would allow me to witness such scenery. Truly, this is the most breathtaking view in the entire Stone Forest Flower Sea.”","Song Shixue glanced at the black scuff marks on his shoes and the gray dew staining the hem of his robe. Her eyes filled with speechless disbelief.","He had clearly gone to great lengths to cross the rocky slope and arrange this chance encounter. Could he not have come up with a more convincing lie?","She stole a glance at Gu Baozhu’s expression. Gu Baozhu looked awkward, plainly having seen through him as well. Moreover, she clearly had no interest in the man before her; otherwise, she would not look as though she wanted to escape.","When Qiu Wangzhi saw that no one was responding, he was briefly at a loss.","He had spent three whole months polishing that poem, all for today. How could it have received no reaction whatsoever?","After taking a breath, he continued, “The scenery here is so delightful that it is truly difficult to leave. Would Miss Gu mind sparing a single stone so that I might sit for a while?”","Glancing at the three unoccupied stones around them, Gu Baozhu pointed to the one farthest away.","“Young Master Qiu, you may sit over there. The view is even better from that spot.”","Qiu Wangzhi clenched his teeth. The foot he had been about to place beside the stone where Gu Baozhu and Song Shixue were sitting was forced to withdraw.","With his back rigid, he walked over to the stone Gu Baozhu had indicated and sat down. The anger in his chest continued to rise.","She had no sense of romance at all. Even the girls at Spring Breeze Pavilion were more obedient and knew how to play along.","If not for her prominent family background, he would not have bothered with her at all."]},{"number":565,"title":"Chapter 565: An Annoying Fly","paragraphs":["In that exact same spot, Gu Baozhu and Song Shixue were no longer as relaxed as they had been while chatting.","The two of them nibbled at their pastries for ages, managing only a single bite each.","After a while, their eyes met. Gu Baozhu frowned. Why hadn’t he left yet?","Song Shixue shook her head lightly. He probably wasn’t going to leave.","“I hear Miss Gu enjoys traveling through the mountains and visiting scenic places. Yueyang City is countless times wealthier than Suining City. You should visit Yueyang someday. When you do, I’ll play host.”","The maidservants and guards Song Shixue had brought all turned their eyes toward him.","The corner of Gu Baozhu’s mouth twitched faintly. “Young Master Qiu, have you ever been to Suining City?”","Qiu Wangzhi gave a soft laugh.","“Of course I have. It’s the poorest and most chaotic place in the southwest. I nearly got robbed by bandits on the road, but fortunately, I had guards with me at the time.”","Song Shixue asked, “When did you go?”","Only then did Qiu Wangzhi turn his head and cast a glance at her. Until now, he had never paid her any attention.","Over the past two months, he had met all the daughters of wealthy merchants and officials in Songzhou City, but he had never seen this one.","Her pale, plain-silk skirt was decorated with very little embroidery. She wore no bracelets, and the pearl flowers and other ornaments in her hair were relatively modest as well. Her family background was probably nothing special, though she was rather pretty and delicate-looking.","“Two years ago. I happened to be passing through. This young lady looks unfamiliar. Have you come to Songzhou City for sightseeing?”","Song Shixue gave a slight nod and said no more.","At least the part about two years ago was probably true.","Gu Baozhu said, “Since the new prefect took office last year, Suining City has changed greatly from how it used to be. Young Master Qiu, you should go take a look when you have the chance.”","“It’s getting late, and it’s time for lunch. Shixue, let’s go.”","As she spoke, she motioned for Song Shixue to stand. This man was far too annoying. They needed to leave quickly.","Song Shixue had no desire to stay either, and rose at once.","The maid efficiently packed the food into the box.","Seeing Gu Baozhu about to leave, Qiu Wangzhi grew anxious.","He took a long stride and blocked the two women’s path. “As it happens, I’ve reserved a private room at Ruyi House. Why don’t we dine together?”","Gu Baozhu forced down the impatience surging to her chest and replied stiffly, “No, thank you.”","The maid beside her used her body to block Qiu Wangzhi’s prying gaze. The group hurried away.","Once their figures disappeared from sight, Qiu Wangzhi kicked a loose stone on the ground away. His eyes darkened, sinister as a demon’s.","When she saw that he had not followed them, Gu Baozhu couldn’t help but breathe a sigh of relief.","Her expression fell as she complained, “Our perfectly good outing is ruined. What rotten luck.”","Song Shixue placed a hand on her arm and smiled. “He clearly knew you were coming here. Even if it hadn’t happened today, it would have happened tomorrow. You can’t avoid him forever.”","Gu Baozhu pursed her lips, her entire body radiating helplessness.","“Scenes like this have happened dozens of times over the past two years. They’re all telling me that I’ve reached the age when I’m supposed to get married.”","Song Shixue cupped her chin, raising her brows.","“Were they all as eager and persistent as Qiu Wangzhi?”","Gu Baozhu shook her head. “Most of them were more tactful. Once I turned them down, they let it go. He’s the most shameless of the lot.”","When they reached the small hillside, the people in the begonia grove had yet to disperse.","Song Anhao’s usually expressionless face finally broke into a smile when he saw Song Shixue.","He hurried over to them and called out, “Second Sister, Sister Baozhu.”","Song Shixue stopped and noticed the weariness in his eyes.","“Did you visit the bookshops? How did it go?”","Song Anhao sighed. “The bookshelves are packed with stories of the same type. Every bookshop has them. They aren’t selling in huge numbers, but they aren’t selling poorly either.”","“Once we get back, I’ll have to find more people to write them. We need to keep up in both quantity and quality.”","The trend they had started had been completely taken advantage of by others. Not a single one of those books had secretly made its way to Suining City. He should have come to Songzhou City sooner.","“You two are heading back? So early?”","Song Shixue glanced at Gu Baozhu. “Your Sister Baozhu ran into an annoying fly, so we had no choice but to leave.”","“Huh?” Song Anhao frowned in confusion.","“Let’s go.” Song Shixue pressed a hand to his shoulder and spun him around one hundred and eighty degrees."]},{"number":566,"title":"Chapter 566: Qiu Wangzhi booked the wing room for half a month in a row.","paragraphs":["By the time Qiu Wangzhi stumbled out from the slope of loose stones, Gu Baozhu and the others had long since disappeared.","He turned his head toward the pavilion, where his classmates were still chatting, shut his eyes in simmering anger, and strode away.","On the carriage, Gu Baozhu was so worried about running into Qiu Wangzhi that she no longer even wanted to dine at Ruyi House.","“If only we’d booked a private room earlier. There definitely won’t be one available now.”","Song Shixue lowered her eyes with a gentle smile. “Perhaps there will be. Heye can ask when we pass by.”","Gu Baozhu leaned her head against the carriage wall, pouting as she sighed.","“You don’t know since you haven’t been in Songzhou City. You have to book a private room at Ruyi House three days in advance, or you won’t be able to get one at all.”","Song Shixue’s lips curved in a faint smile. “We can at least ask.”","When the carriage stopped outside Ruyi House, Heye lifted the curtain and hopped down.","Gu Baozhu rested her head against the window, replaying Qiu Wangzhi’s every move in her mind. She was so frustrated she could hardly bear it.","Heye entered the restaurant just as the manager, Feng Yi, who was tallying the accounts, happened to look up and meet her gaze.","“Manager Feng, Miss Gu booked a private room for lunch today. Please change the reservation to this evening.”","Feng Yi opened the ledger of reservations.","“The Tianzi Number One Room on the third floor has unexpectedly become available tonight. It can be reserved.”","Knowing that Song Shixue and Song Anhao had come to Songzhou City these past few days, he had kept the Tianzi Number One Room from being rented out.","Heye smiled and nodded. “Good. We’ll take the Tianzi Number One Room.”","Just before leaving, she suddenly remembered something and turned back to ask, “Did someone named Qiu Wangzhi reserve a private room here for lunch?”","Feng Yi paused, then nodded without even checking the ledger.","“Yes. He reserved the Yuzi Number Five Room. He’s kept it booked for half a month, but has only shown up once. He’s already lost quite a bit just on the deposits.”","Heye nodded and returned to the carriage.","“I’ve asked the manager. He said we were lucky—the Tianzi Number One Room happened to become available this evening.”","Gu Baozhu’s eyes lit up. “Really?”","Heye nodded. “And that young man, Qiu, really did reserve a private room at Ruyi House. He’s kept it booked for half a month, but has only come once. He stood us up every other time.”","The brightness faded from Gu Baozhu’s eyes. Her shoulders slumped as she leaned back.","“I knew it. He’s only doing this because of me.”","She closed her eyes, pressing at her aching temples. “How annoying!”","The sun rose higher in the sky. Half an hour later, the people stationed on either side of the crabapple grove finally began to disperse.","“I think I just saw Miss Gu with another young woman. Why didn’t she come over?” one of the women accompanying the person at the center asked curiously.","The woman she addressed was the legitimate daughter of the circuit intendant of the southwestern province. Her father was certain to be transferred to the capital next year.","Jiang Roulan looked toward her and replied gently, “The woman beside her was Song Shixue, the younger sister of County Princess Linghui. I heard she’s been sightseeing in Songzhou City these past two days.”","“The younger sister of County Princess Linghui?” The woman’s eyes widened in surprise. She had not expected that to be the case.","The news quickly spread as people exchanged glances and began whispering among themselves.","“The Song family’s Second Miss—did County Princess Linghui come as well?”","“I heard she didn’t. Only Second Miss Song came.”","“But I heard there was also a younger brother...”","When Qiu Wangzhi’s classmates returned to the academy, they found him lying on his bed without moving.","“You said you had something important to take care of, and this is what you came back for—to sleep?”","Qiu Wangzhi opened his eyes, a trace of impatience flashing through them.","“It’s already taken care of. I’ve been rather tired these past few days. I won’t be going to the Stone Forest Sea of Flowers tomorrow.”","One of his classmates plopped down on the bed opposite him and pulled off his boots.","“I don’t know why you kept going there day after day. I’d have been exhausted long ago.”","“You left early today, so you missed her. County Princess Linghui’s younger sister also came to admire the flowers. Too bad you didn’t see her.”","Qiu Wangzhi’s brows shot up, and his voice instantly rose.","“County Princess Linghui’s younger sister?”","His classmate nodded. “She came with the daughter of the provincial administration commissioner. I heard she’s been sightseeing in Songzhou City these past two days.”","Qiu Wangzhi’s mind descended into chaos. All he could think about was the face of the woman beside Gu Baozhu.","Could she really have been County Princess Linghui’s younger sister?","“You spoke to her?”","His classmate let out a mocking laugh and looked up.","“She didn’t go anywhere crowded at all. Miss Jiang only caught a distant glimpse of her figure from over there. She’d seen Song Shixue before.”","Qiu Wangzhi collapsed onto the bed, his face expressionless. His chest was filled with nothing but frustration and regret.","Her family background was so distinguished, yet she had dressed so plainly. Why?","The more he thought about it, the angrier he became. He buried his head in the bedding and kicked his feet.","The scholar sitting on the opposite bed stared at him in bewilderment.","What was wrong with him? He usually wasn’t like this."]},{"number":567,"title":"Chapter 567: The Furious Lady Gu","paragraphs":["After returning to the Gu residence, Gu Baozhu instructed the servants to take Song Shixue and Song Anhao to rest, then hurried straight to Madam Gu’s courtyard.","“Mother, didn’t you show me a portrait of the Yueyang Prefect’s son before?”","Madam Gu abruptly raised her head, her face lighting up with delight.","“You’ve changed your mind and decided to get married?”","Gu Baozhu brought both feet to an abrupt stop and lowered her eyes with a silent sigh.","“No. Today, I met someone at the Stone Forest Flower Sea. He claimed to be the Yueyang Prefect’s son. His name is Qiu Wangzhi, and he said he’d attended the birthday banquet before.”","Madam Gu’s expression changed drastically. Her face darkened as she explained coldly, “He’s the Yueyang Prefect’s younger son, not the one in the portrait.”","“Did Qiu Wangzhi approach you first? Stay away from him.”","Seeing how angry she was, Gu Baozhu sensed there had to be some juicy gossip behind this.","She walked over and sat beside Madam Gu, then recounted the entire incident without leaving out a single detail.","“Bang!”","The pearwood tabletop shook three times, splashing water from the teacups.","Madam Gu glared with an expression that looked ready to devour someone.","“That toad actually wants to eat swan meat without even considering what kind of person he is. How dare he set his sights on my daughter!”","“I’m telling your father right now. I’ll have him drive Qiu Wangzhi out of Songzhou.”","Gu Baozhu’s lips parted slightly. It had been many years since she had last seen her mother like this.","“Mother, don’t get so worked up. I didn’t pay him any attention at all.”","Madam Gu leaned forward and took Gu Baozhu’s hand.","“You must never pay him any attention. Back when I took a liking to Young Master Qiu, his family hadn’t committed any such disgraceful acts. His first wife had been dead for barely half a month when he took his concubine and made her his legal wife. You absolutely cannot marry into a family like that.”","Gu Baozhu raised a brow. “Qiu Wangzhi is a son born to a concubine?”","Madam Gu sat back down with a grim expression. “He used to be, but now he’s the legitimate son.”","“If his father weren’t the Yueyang Prefect, Qiu Wangzhi wouldn’t even have been able to enter Songzhou Academy. He’s worlds apart from his older brother.”","Gu Baozhu’s expression shifted. She rose and leaned against the couch.","She said meaningfully to Madam Gu, “Fortunately, I went to Suining City back then. Otherwise, if I had become betrothed to the Qiu family, it would have been too late to regret it.”","Madam Gu stalked over and pinched her ear.","“What do you mean, too late? With your father backing you, I could make you return home after a divorce even if you were already married, let alone merely betrothed.”","“If the Qiu family’s eldest son knows right from wrong, we can lure him over to our side as well. Then even the Yueyang Prefect wouldn’t dare say a word.”","Gu Baozhu wisely fell silent, her eyes darting from side to side.","Had her maternal grandfather thought the same thing back when he chose her father as a son-in-law?","That evening, the three members of the Gu family, along with the Song siblings, went to Ruyi Pavilion for dinner. This left the Gu couple and their two sons at the dining table.","Madam Gu gripped her chopsticks so tightly that her knuckles turned white as she glared at the three men.","“That concubine-born son of the Yueyang Prefect’s family pretended to run into Baozhu at the Stone Forest Flower Sea today. He’s been keeping an eye on her for half a month—delusional and shamelessly trying to climb the social ladder. Find a way to drive him out of Songzhou.”","Gu Huaiyuan paused with his chopsticks in hand. “The Qiu Wangzhi who came to Songzhou to study last month?”","Madam Gu nodded. “They sent away a legitimate son and brought in a concubine-born one. I’d say the Yueyang Prefect is both incapable of recognizing talent and willing to violate proper moral conduct.”","She shot Gu Zhongxun a sidelong glare. “People like that should be used sparingly. He’ll become a source of trouble sooner or later.”","Gu Zhongxun spoke in a deep voice. “We’ll ask Congwen when he returns. If Qiu Wangzhi’s grades at the academy are poor, we’ll find an opportunity to send him away. The Yueyang Prefect may still be of some use.”","With a sharp crack, the chopsticks slammed against the edge of the bowl.","The room instantly fell as quiet as a flock of startled chickens."]},{"number":568,"title":"Chapter 568: The Target Changed to Song Shixue Was Ignored","paragraphs":["“Miss Song, what a coincidence. We meet again.”","At the sound of that familiar voice, Gu Baozhu grabbed Song Shixue by the arm and hurriedly pulled her up the stairs.","Song Anhao stopped. The instant he saw Qiu Wangzhi, his sharp gaze swept over him from head to toe.","Average looks, average height, an ordinary face—at a glance, he clearly wasn’t a good person.","Gu Congwen and Gu Jinghong stared expressionlessly at Qiu Wangzhi. Three encounters in a row—he really was like a piece of dog-skin plaster, impossible to shake off.","Being watched by three pairs of eyes as though he were an enemy, every hair on Qiu Wangzhi’s body stood on end. He froze rigidly in place.","Watching the five of them leave with cold, indifferent backs turned toward him, Qiu Wangzhi braced himself against the wall and slowly crouched down.","In the private room upstairs, Gu Baozhu sat by the window, her gaze following the despondent figure disappearing below.","“Looks like he’s found a new target.”","Song Shixue calmly picked up a bright-red cherry from the table and popped it into her mouth.","“It doesn’t matter. I’m leaving tomorrow anyway.”","The door opened as Song Anhao pushed it inward, with Gu Congwen and Gu Jinghong following behind him.","Not long after everyone had taken their seats, the dishes were served. They were all the restaurant’s best-selling signature specialties.","Gu Congwen said, “Qiu Wangzhi is very good at making friends with his fellow students at the academy. I never expected him to harbor ambitions of currying favor with the powerful.”","Gu Jinghong said, “You can know a person’s face but not their heart. Over the years, have we not encountered enough people who act one way to your face and another behind your back?”","As the grandsons of the Southwestern Provincial Administration Commissioner, both Gu Congwen and Gu Jinghong were treated with flattery wherever they went.","The number of people who were sincere toward them could be counted on one hand.","The next day, Gu Baozhu brought Song Shixue to the stone forest and flower sea once more. This time, the Gu brothers came along as well.","Song Anhao led Xuetuan, whose enormous body drew everyone’s attention wherever it went.","“Oh my goodness, that looks like a tiger!”","Everyone wanted to keep their distance while also wanting to get closer. In the end, they could only watch from afar as Gu Baozhu and the others walked away.","The sunlight was gentle, and a spring breeze stirred the air. Lying on a blanket spread over waterproof paper and cotton cloth, gazing up at the sky, made all their worries seem to disappear.","“It’s a pity you’re leaving tomorrow. Otherwise, I would have to take you sightseeing and show you the mountains and rivers.”","A satisfied smile curved Song Shixue’s lips.","“There are many patients at the clinic. I’ll come visit the next time I have some free time.”","Gu Baozhu propped herself up on her right elbow and turned her face to the side.","“When you have time next time, send someone to deliver a message to me. I’ll go to Suining City to find you.”","As she spoke, she leaned close to Song Shixue’s ear and whispered, “When the time comes, let’s travel west. I really want to see how the people of the southwestern ethnic tribes live.”","Song Shixue’s pupils widened slightly. “You’re incredibly bold. If your uncle and aunt find out, they’ll lock you up for another two months.”","Gu Baozhu raised an eyebrow. “Then they just can’t find out.”","Song Shixue shook her head. When that time truly came, she absolutely would not agree.","If anything happened, she could not bear the responsibility. The Gu family’s wrath was no joke.","“Awooo~”","Xuetuan leaped high into the air, bit down on the kite string, and ran back.","The tourists below the mountain all looked up. It was the cry of the white tiger from earlier.","“Xuetuan—”","Song Anhao rushed over and pried open its mouth. By the time he managed to rescue the string, it had already snapped.","The kite fell onto a crabapple tree. Gu Jinghong climbed up to retrieve it, only to discover that the branches had torn it to pieces.","Seeing this, Song Anhao grabbed Xuetuan by the ear and scolded it. “Look at what you’ve done! Now we don’t have a kite anymore.”","Xuetuan wrinkled its nose and shook its head. Then its huge body curved around and leaned into Song Anhao’s embrace, knocking him onto the ground and leaving his backside covered in dew.","“Xuetuan, get up right now!”"]},{"number":569,"title":"Chapter 569: Acquiring the Escort Agency","paragraphs":["They had arrived in a single carriage, but when they left, they had an extra one—half of it filled with the storybooks Song Anhao had bought at the bookshop, and the other half with gifts from the Song family.","After the spring planting, Suining City entered a period of rapid development.","Cement roads were being built from the inner city to the outer city. The government would take responsibility for repairing any road wide enough for a carriage to pass through, while for the narrow alleys leading to individual homes, residents who wished to pave them could purchase cement from the cement shop at a thirty-percent discount.","The roads in both the inner and outer cities were being repaired, and the river embankments reinforced.","Considering that Suining City’s population would continue to grow, Song Qiming planned to build a new outer-city wall. In the future, Suining City would no longer be divided into an inner and outer city.","“All dilapidated or abandoned houses and vacant lots in the city are to be registered with the government office once it has been confirmed that they have no owner. Then, when the time is right, we’ll sell them.”","Song Qiming had drawn hundreds of circles on a detailed map marking every alley, some in red and others in black.","The weariness in Shi Simian’s eyes instantly transformed into delight.","Every day, he worried about how much money the government treasury had spent and how much remained. It had taken them so much effort to go from poverty to prosperity, and he never wanted to return to those days.","Yet Song Qiming did one thing after another every day, spending money as if it were water. This tormented him endlessly. He had even hoped that one day they might stumble upon another unexpected fortune, just as they had when they wiped out the bandits’ den.","And now, that fortune had arrived!","Since the beginning of the year, more and more people had been coming to Suining City for work. In addition to the coal and cement factories outside the city, 202 new shops had opened in the inner city, hiring a total of 478 workers. Quite a few inns in the city had already raised their prices, and even the rent for private residences had gone up by ten copper coins a month.","Selling land now would definitely bring in a huge profit.","“This subordinate will make the arrangements immediately. I won’t let a single plot of sellable land slip through our fingers!” Shi Simian’s voice was so loud that he practically roared.","He staggered out of the room. Before long, two-thirds of the minor officials in the front hall were busy at work.","In the study in the rear courtyard, Lanxi and Qingshuang stood on either side of Song Jinzhao.","Lanxi said, “During this period of transporting cement and smokeless coal, we made contact with 321 escort agencies across the southwestern province, involving a total of 3,645 people.”","Qingshuang continued, “Of them, 208 are willing to sell their escort agencies, representing a total of 1,836 people. Of the remaining 113, thirty-five are still negotiating, while the other seventy-eight have clearly refused.”","Of the twenty agencies near the top of the list, only three had received a red check mark. Only one had been circled. All the others had been crossed out.","“Those who refuse to sell are the leaders of the industry. They didn’t even name a price?”","Lanxi shook her head. “No. Every time we approached them, they rejected us outright.”","Song Jinzhao closed the list.","“Then there’s no need to contact them again. When the time is right, they’ll come to us themselves.”","“I’m planning to build houses near the coal and cement factories. When the time comes, I’ll bring all of these people and their families here.”","Lanxi pondered for a moment before nodding.","“Suining City is completely different now. As long as there’s a place for them to live, it shouldn’t be difficult to persuade them to move here. Should we charge rent?”","Building all those houses would cost money. For 1,836 people, they would need quite a few.","Song Jinzhao tilted her head slightly and shook it. “No rent. Anyone who works for me can live there for free. That way, they’ll be tied to us.”","The two people standing before her exchanged a glance. When they thought of all the strong, able-bodied workers at the factories, they realized that perhaps those workers could also serve as reserve soldiers.","“Eldest Sister—”","The voice came before the person did.","Song Anhao burst into the study with a huge stack of storybooks in her arms. With a bang, she set them on the desk, and the pile began sliding off. Qingshuang hurriedly reached out to catch them.","Lanxi turned toward the study door. The moment she saw Song Anhao, her pale-blue eyes lifted sharply.","After wandering outside for seven days, she had finally returned.","“Why did Second Miss come back a day late?”","Heye pushed her way to the front and answered first. “She ran into some clingy pest who was trying to marry above his station, so she came back a day late.”","“Heye.” Song Shixue stopped her.","Heye puffed out her cheeks and retreated.","Lanxi remained where she was, doubts stirring in her heart as an alarm began ringing in her mind.","A clingy pest trying to marry above his station... So another man had taken an interest in Shixue.","The more Lanxi dwelled on the possibility, the more worried she became. Sitting alone in the corner of a dim room, she remembered that she, too, had married above her station. Her mood sank even further."]},{"number":570,"title":"Chapter 570: Land Auction, Hosting a Picture-Writing Storybook Competition","paragraphs":["At a single command, every piece of abandoned, ownerless land in Suining City was surveyed, measured, and registered within seven days.","The townspeople stared in confusion at the dilapidated houses sealed off with official notices.","What could the government want with houses this rundown? Were they planning to rebuild them?","The answer soon became clear.","The government office posted an announcement declaring that all ownerless land within the city would be auctioned off. The notice was posted not only throughout Suining City—even many merchants in Songzhou City had heard about it.","The auction would be held a month later, giving them plenty of time to make up their minds and come.","At the first watch of the night, every room in a row at the back of the government office was brightly lit.","Song Jinzhao stood staring at a map covering an entire wall, occasionally marking it with her brush.","Song Anhao sat facing a wall of storybooks, pondering hard enough to make his head ache. One idea after another was crossed out on the sheet of paper before him.","Meanwhile, Song Qiming had already begun planning how to drive the land prices as high as possible at the auction a month later—especially how to make merchants from out of town see Suining City’s enormous potential.","The only one thinking about getting to the clinic early the next day was Song Shixue, who had gone to bed long ago.","Over breakfast the next morning, Song Anhao excitedly shared the idea he had come up with.","“I’m planning to hold a competition. We’ll invite anyone who wants to write storybooks—or already knows how—to write on a randomly assigned theme. Then we’ll sign contracts with everyone whose work is good.”","Song Jinzhao paused with her fingers and asked with a smile, “How did you come up with that?”","Song Anhao propped his chin on one hand. “At first, I had no idea what to do. Then I thought about how Big Brother could hold an auction to sell the land, and I realized I could hold a competition to find writers.”","“Elder Sister, will you be one of the judges? When it comes to good taste, no one can compare with you.”","The chicken soup wontons in the bowl were still steaming. Song Jinzhao set down her spoon.","“Only a small portion of the population can read and write fluently. People who can write storybooks—or even want to write them—are rarer still. How do you plan to organize this competition?”","A printing house was no government office. It could not simply issue an order and expect people to comply on the strength of official authority and credibility. Getting proud scholars to submit their work voluntarily would be difficult enough, especially with transportation being inconvenient and there being no internet.","Song Anhao raised one finger toward the ceiling, his eyes shining with confidence.","“There’s nothing silver can’t solve. As long as the reward is generous enough, people will come. I’m planning to offer prizes to twenty winners. The first-place winner will receive three thousand taels of silver, the second place one thousand five hundred, and the third place one thousand.”","“Fourth through tenth place will each receive five hundred taels, and eleventh through twentieth place will each receive three hundred. Great rewards inspire great courage.”","After calculating the total, Song Qiming’s eyes widened. “The prize money alone comes to twelve thousand taels!”","Song Anhao nodded vigorously. “And that’s not all. I’m also going to print one hundred thousand flyers and put them up as far away as possible, so that as many people as possible hear about it.”","Song Qiming fell silent.","Was this what it felt like to have money to burn?","Still, if that many people really came to Suining City, perhaps they could make good use of the opportunity.","Song Jinzhao said, “I’ll agree to be a judge as long as the number of applicants exceeds one thousand.”","“No problem. If we can’t even get a thousand applicants, then there’s no point in holding the competition.” Song Anhao spoke with complete confidence.","He took a huge bite out of a steamed bun, as though he were chewing his way through all the storybook writers who would soon be added to his money-making roster.","Song Qiming posted two notices in every county, while Song Anhao scattered a thousand flyers across each one.","The deliberately emphasized prize amounts successfully caught the attention of everyone who could read.","“Three thousand taels? The Song Family Bookshop is being awfully generous.”","“Even second place gets fifteen hundred taels. I’ve studied the classics all these years—writing a storybook should be a piece of cake.”","Quite a few people thought the same way.","Even if they couldn’t win three thousand taels, surely they could manage to win three hundred.","The auction and the storybook competition would both be held a month later. For a time, the official roads leading to Suining City grew increasingly crowded.","One carriage after another carried four or five people. Some travelers sat with their eyes closed, searching for inspiration. Others were engrossed in reading storybooks, while still others gazed out at the scenery, wondering what sights might be worth including in a story.","The merchants traveling alone in their carriages stood in stark contrast to them. Some even had goods loaded aboard.","As they watched the carriages ahead and behind them, along with the hurried pedestrians on the road, their anticipation for the auction grew stronger.","More people meant more business and more money to be made. No one wanted to miss an opportunity they could already see coming."]},{"number":571,"title":"Chapter 571: The auction begins","paragraphs":["From Yunzhu County to Suining City, ten li outside the city and high above the road, unsuspecting commoners pointed in confusion at the thick smoke rising in the distance.","“What’s going on over there? Has something caught fire?”","A merchant who knew the reason lifted the carriage curtain. “Those are the chimneys of the coal plant and the cement plant.”","The scholar stared straight ahead, his face filled with astonishment.","“So that’s where the coal plant and cement plant are. Is Suining City just ahead?”","The merchant nodded, but just as he was about to answer, his expression turned uncertain.","“Why has the outer city wall grown so much taller?”","A farmer carrying a load to sell in the city passed by and replied, “The prefectural government is rebuilding the outer wall. It isn’t finished yet.”","The merchant and the scholar turned toward him in unison. “Rebuilding the city wall?”","The farmer nodded with a grin. “I heard they’re making it thirty feet high, using nothing but cement and steel.”","When they reached the city gate, they saw people everywhere, both above and below the wall.","Some were carrying cement and sand. Others were mixing it with iron shovels, while still more strained at ropes to hoist the cement upward. Every person was busy at work.","Once they passed through the wall, they found a broad thoroughfare stretching straight ahead.","It was flat and spacious, extending so far that the end could not be seen. It looked as though it had been built with every inch measured by a ruler.","The carriage traveled smoothly along the cement road. Those who had never visited Suining City before all pulled aside the curtains and looked out, their eyes filled with amazement.","“I heard long ago that Suining City had changed, but I never imagined it would be this different!”","“Is this really the same Suining City as before—the place overrun with bandits and thieves, wedged between the western southern tribes?”","As they approached the inner city wall, the liveliness increased dramatically. Even before entering the city, they could hear peddlers hawking their wares, while the enticing aroma of food drifted into their noses and made them swallow involuntarily.","Unlike the outer city, where only the main road had been paved with cement, every street and intersection in the inner city was paved with cement.","The roads ran in all directions, far surpassing even Songzhou City, which the people of the southwest regarded as their provincial capital.","“Honored guests, would you like a room at our inn?”","“Gentlemen, we’ve just received some fine Dragon Well tea. Would you care to come in and rest awhile?”","Over the past few days, merchants from other parts of the country and young gentlemen dressed in long robes had been arriving in Suining City one after another. Everyone guessed that they had come for the land auction and the story-writing competition.","After setting down their belongings and taking a brief rest, the merchants would go downstairs for a meal. Then, following the requirements listed in the announcement, they would head to the prefectural government office to collect the information on all the plots of land soon to be auctioned.","With maps in hand, they ran from one plot to another, judging which location was best and where they could make the most money in the future. Once they returned to the inn, they still had to calculate which plots offered the best value.","The writers participating in the story competition, meanwhile, shut themselves away in their rooms and racked their brains. When registering, they were required to submit the first hundred thousand characters of their story, along with a basic outline of the entire work.","And in corners no one noticed, several young ladies of respectable families, accompanied by maids and servants, quietly checked into inns near the Song Family Bookshop.","“I wonder whether the story I wrote can win a prize.”","The maid making the bed turned her head. “Miss is exceptionally talented, and you’ve loved reading stories since you were little. You’re sure to win.”","The woman wearing a silver hairpin reclined against the couch. Beside her lay a stack of manuscripts—some written recently, others from long ago. Their only common feature was that, aside from her maid, no one had ever seen them.","Behind the counter of a silk shop, a young girl doing the accounts waited until the store was empty before secretly pulling a draft sheet from beneath the ledger and writing a few lines. The moment someone entered, she immediately covered it again with the account book.","On the day of the auction, more than three hundred merchants interested in the proceedings sat in the open space before the prefectural government office.","When the appointed hour arrived, the minor official in charge of warming up the crowd stepped onto the platform.","“Honored merchants and gentlemen who have traveled here from afar, today we have gathered together to contribute to the future development of Suining City...”","The awkward introductory speech had been read and memorized by the minor official hundreds of times, yet he still stumbled over it. The main reason was that he had never said such things before. When had the prefectural government ever treated merchants with such respect and praise? This was unquestionably the first time.","The opening remarks stirred everyone’s spirits, drawing them into a single camp to speak of ideals and shared purpose.","Their eyes widened. Their hearts pounded long after the words had ended. Their hands tightened around the auction booklets, and they wished they could turn every page until it fell apart in their hands."]},{"number":572,"title":"Chapter 572: No One Is Willing to Buy the Guanyin Temple","paragraphs":["Once the opening remarks came to an end, two yamen runners from Tianya pushed in a huge notice board. Pasted across it was a map three chi high and six chi long, clearly marking every parcel of land.","The notice board was pushed to the left. Another yamen runner then wheeled in a second one, displaying the first plot to be auctioned. Its area and location were listed, along with all its advantages.","The clerk who had delivered the opening remarks stepped down. Dressed in formal official robes, Song Qiming slowly walked to the center of the platform. A tall table stood before him, bearing a brass loudhailer.","“It is this official’s honor to invite all esteemed merchants to Suining City today to discuss our grand plans.”","“Without further ado, the first plot to be auctioned is located at the end of Sophora Blossom Lane. It covers approximately forty square bu, equivalent to one mu and five fen. It lies directly beside the South Gate of the inner city—a quiet spot amid the bustle, with a moderate flow of people. The starting price is fifty taels of silver, with each bid increasing by at least one tael.”","As soon as he finished speaking, a local merchant seated in the middle raised his hand.","“Fifty-five taels.”","“Fifty-six.”","“Fifty-seven.”","A merchant from out of town leaned toward the man beside him. “Brother, the place is small and the location only so-so. Why are so many people bidding it up?”","The local merchant who had just called out fifty-seven glanced at him, then turned back to the front, ready to raise his bid again at any moment.","“That just shows you don’t understand the business. Sophora Blossom Lane may be in an ordinary location, but the Song Family Medical Hall is only three streets away. County Princess Linghui’s younger sister practices there, under the tutelage of a divine physician, and patients come streaming in every day. This price isn’t expensive at all.”","What he did not mention was that once the outer city gates were completed, the inner city gates would no longer need to be guarded by yamen runners.","According to rumors, several smaller gates would be opened in the inner city walls to the east, south, west, and north. The foot traffic around Sophora Blossom Lane was bound to increase.","“Seventy taels.”","As they spoke, the price had already climbed to seventy taels.","In the end, the plot was sold for seventy-two taels to a local merchant in the cloth trade.","In the household office not far away, Song Jinzhao sat in a chair by the open window, watching the proceedings.","“This income should be quite substantial.”","The clerk across from her continued writing furiously, hurriedly nodding with an ingratiating smile.","“It’s thirty percent higher than the usual price. His Excellency’s idea of holding an auction is truly unprecedented.”","Song Jinzhao glanced at him, the corners of her lips curling into a smile.","Of course it was novel—it had been brought over from the modern world. Merchants bidding against one another was nothing unusual there.","But here, this was the first time the authorities had ever auctioned off land.","As one plot after another was sold, the atmosphere of the auction gradually reached a fever pitch. Quite a few people had already become completely caught up in the bidding, with nothing left in their minds but calling out higher prices.","The final property to be auctioned was the Guanyin Temple, which Song Qiming had visited before. Its location was not the best, but it was the largest plot by far.","More importantly, once the main roads of the outer city were completed, the official road outside the Guanyin Temple would lead directly to the coal plant and the cement plant. The area was slated to become one of Suining City’s key districts for future development.","Before the auction began, a worried merchant stood up and raised his hand.","“Lord Song, this land originally belonged to the Guanyin Temple. It doesn’t feel quite right to tear it down and rebuild.”","The others nodded one after another. They had the same concern. Whether the Bodhisattva would punish them was one matter; they were even more afraid that the surrounding commoners would gossip about them. If that happened, customers might avoid their businesses altogether.","Song Qiming raised a hand to quiet them.","“I understand everyone’s concerns, which is why the auction for this plot will be somewhat different.”","“After purchasing this land, the buyer must preserve the Guanyin Hall at its center and assume responsibility for its restoration and day-to-day maintenance.”","The announcement left the merchants silent, though none of them were pleased.","Keeping the Guanyin Hall intact meant losing nearly one-fifth of the usable area. On top of that, restoring the building and maintaining it year-round would certainly cost a great deal.","The merchants who had initially been interested in the property began to back away. They had assumed the authorities would demolish the temple, sparing them the blame from the common people. Who could have guessed that Song Qiming would come up with this condition?","Seeing that no one was speaking, Song Qiming remained completely calm.","“The starting price for this plot is five hundred taels of silver, with each bid increasing by at least ten taels.”","The merchants sat in their chairs in silence. Their lips opened and closed, but not a single word came out."]},{"number":573,"title":"Chapter 573: Total Fifty-Three Thousand Taels","paragraphs":["“Five hundred and ten taels.”","A clear, gentle voice came from behind the crowd.","Everyone turned to look. The newcomer wore a narrow-cut lotus-colored dress with crisp, clean lines along the hem. The skirt fell just to the tops of her shoes, allowing her to plant her feet firmly and walk faster than ordinary women.","While the merchants from out of town were still wondering who she was, the local merchants immediately rose and knelt in greeting.","“Greetings to County Princess Linghui.”","When they turned and saw everyone around them kneeling, the visiting merchants’ pupils contracted. They hurriedly dropped to their knees as well, shouting along with the others, “Greetings to County Princess Linghui!” Their foreheads struck the floor, and they wished they could burrow straight into the ground and hide.","“There is no need for such ceremony. Today, this county princess is merely an ordinary merchant looking to buy some land.”","Though she said this, who would truly dare treat Song Jinzhao as an ordinary person?","Only after she had taken her seat did the others cautiously rise and sit down again, keeping their bodies rigid and barely daring to settle fully into their chairs.","Song Qiming held his breath and called out, “Five hundred and ten taels. Does anyone wish to bid higher?”","The room fell so silent that even the sound of breathing could be heard. It was as if everyone’s mouths had been glued shut.","No one had wanted the land, but now County Princess Linghui was buying it. She was clearly here to support Prefect Song.","If only they had known, they should have bought it earlier. Spending five hundred taels to make a good impression on Prefect Song and County Princess Linghui would have been well worth it!","Regret swept through them. They wished they could turn back time; they would certainly have been the first to raise their hands.","“Five hundred and ten taels, once. Five hundred and ten taels, twice. Five hundred and ten taels, three times.”","“Sold.”","As the wooden gavel fell, the plot known as Guanyin Miao successfully became Song Jinzhao’s.","The auction came to a smooth close. In the finance office, the clerks working out the accounts rattled their abacuses so loudly that, by the end, their eyes were nearly filled with tears.","A total of 223 plots had been auctioned for 53,000 taels. It was an outrageous profit.","Once the auction ended, the first thing every merchant who had won a plot did was seek out builders, carpenters, and tile workers to begin construction.","The cement shop received orders for more than seven thousand sacks that very day. There were not enough workers, so even seventy-year-old men from outside the city were found work carrying bricks.","Five days after the auction ended, the registration deadline for the storybook competition arrived.","Looking at the manuscripts piled throughout the room, Song Anhao felt the enormous workload weighing heavily on her.","Manager Lou held the registration list and reported, “We received 1,046 valid manuscripts in total. Of these, 562 are domestic-drama romances, 175 are mystery and courtroom stories, and the rest cover a wide range of subjects, including the supernatural, love stories, travel journals, and tales of people building their fortunes.”","After consulting Song Jinzhao, Song Anhao had decided that the storybook competition would place no restrictions on genre. Their goal was to make sure they did not overlook talented writers in any field.","Early the next morning, the judges they had recruited in advance arrived.","Twenty desks had been arranged in the spacious room. The proprietors of fifteen bookshops would carry out the first round of cross-screening. Each of them had more than ten years of experience reading books.","After three days, when the 1,046 manuscripts reached Song Jinzhao and the others, only 100 remained.","Liu Ruoxi randomly picked up a domestic-drama manuscript and began reading. Liu Ziyuan headed straight for the mystery and courtroom stories, while Song Jinzhao, Song Anhao, and Manager Lou started with the relatively few manuscripts in the other genres.","Compared with the first round, the second round of screening was much more thorough. They read every word and every sentence.","The writing, characterization, plot, originality, and even the outline for the later chapters all fell within the scope of their evaluation.","Selecting 100 manuscripts from 1,046 took fifteen people three days.","Selecting twenty from those 100 took five people a full four days. They scrutinized every word and were exacting about every detail.","In the end, Song Jinzhao personally chose the top three entries.","The first two were popular domestic-drama romances, while the third was a mystery and courtroom story.","Seeing his area of expertise lose once again to his younger sister, Liu Ziyuan was completely resigned. How were there so many people who liked all that lovey-dovey nonsense?","To promote the influence of the storybook competition, Song Anhao specially reserved the largest restaurant in Suining City and arranged a grand banquet.","Everyone who had entered the competition was welcome to attend.","The first and second floors were packed to overflowing, leaving barely enough room to walk."]},{"number":574,"title":"Chapter 574: Script Creation Contest Revealed","paragraphs":["Under the eyes of the entire crowd, the bright-red list of winners cascaded down from the railing on the third floor, its impact like a crashing waterfall of waves.","The golden names and book titles instantly seized everyone’s attention, especially the three written at the very top.","Moonlit Invitation—The General, You Look Incredibly Handsome After Battling on the Frontier","Pearl-Bearing Sparrow—The Noble Household’s Matriarch: Who Shall Kneel in the Ancestral Hall Today?","Bitter Pine—The Coroner’s Knife Became My Ladder to Success","The maid standing beside the railing on the second floor jumped up excitedly and threw her arms around the young woman next to her.","“Miss, you won first place!”","Zou Wudie, wearing a long veil hat, had tears and laughter mingling on her face.","She had hoped for it, but she never imagined she would actually come in first—not with more than a thousand people taking part.","Wearing a jade crown, Song Anhao straightened his back and walked toward the railing on the third floor with measured steps.","Looking down, he saw a sea of densely packed heads below.","He swallowed nervously, then drew a deep breath and slowly let it out.","“Good day, everyone. I am Song Anhao, proprietor of the Song Bookshop. We will now invite those ranked eleventh through twentieth to come up and receive their prizes.”","Brilliant red petals exploded into the air. As one name and book title after another was called, people gradually rose from among the crowd.","After looking around and spotting others standing, they instinctively made their way over.","Under normal circumstances, the three flights of stairs could be climbed in the blink of an eye. But now, every step felt as though it were landing directly on their hearts.","Thump! Thump! Thump!","Their chests trembled, their hearts seemingly ready to burst through their ribs.","Ten workers came out carrying trays. The gleaming silver ingots made everyone’s eyes burn with envy.","The young girl who worked at the silk shop stood there, flustered, with her arms full of money.","It wasn’t that she had never seen so much money before. It was simply that this time, all of it belonged to her.","When the awards reached the top three, Zou Wudie lowered her head and quietly signaled to her maid.","“You go up and collect it.”","The maid pressed her lips together. After a moment’s hesitation, she nodded and headed toward the stairs.","Before they came, the two of them had already discussed what to do: if they won, the maid would collect the prize money in person. But neither of them had expected to take first place.","At the corner of the third floor, as the three people who had stood rose into view, Song Jinzhao’s gaze drifted over the woman wearing the long veil hat.","The wording was elegant and graceful, and every line carried the effortless poise of flowing clouds and running water.","Moonlit Invitation had clearly read a great many books and had grown up surrounded by the fragrance of ink and literature.","She had a personal maidservant, and people were protecting her nearby. It would be inconvenient for her to show her face. She was probably the pampered daughter of some noble household.","Three thousand taels in silver ingots would have been too heavy. Yet the prize also needed to make an impact, so Song Anhao had simply had the money exchanged for one-hundred-tael banknotes. Thirty of them still made for a reasonably thick stack.","Even a maidservant who had seen the world could not help trembling as she held the bundle of banknotes.","The combined value of all her young mistress’s gold and silver jewelry was probably about the same. But holding the money in her hands, somehow it felt like an enormous fortune.","When they saw that the first two winners were both women, quite a few scholars in the audience who had received nothing began to feel indignant.","“Thirteen of the top twenty are women. I say the judges for this Song Bookshop competition have no real talent at all. They probably don’t even hold scholarly degrees.”","The people at the same table turned to look at him. After thinking it over, they too began to feel unsettled.","That was right, wasn’t it? They had traveled hundreds of miles only to receive not a single tael of silver, while the hundred thousand words they had written had all gone to waste.","Just as the murmuring grew louder and louder, a scholar seated on the second floor suddenly rose and shouted,","“Boss Song, may I ask what scholarly qualifications the judges of this story competition possess? What were the judging criteria?”","“I dare say my story is no worse than theirs. If you have the courage, bring out the top twenty stories and let everyone take a look. Then we can at least lose with conviction.”","The three winners, who had not yet returned to their seats, stopped in their tracks and turned toward the scholar in unison.","Song Anhao leaned forward and got a clear look at the speaker. Seeing that many people around him wore the same expression, he could not help slowly knitting his brows.","He had chosen every judge only after careful consideration, and the fairness of the competition was not something he would allow others to casually question.","As the commotion below grew louder and louder, Song Anhao still did not speak. Song Shixue began to worry. She was afraid he would be unable to control the situation and would lose his nerve.","She turned to Song Jinzhao.","“Elder Sister, what should we do now?”","Song Jinzhao leisurely set down her teacup, the corners of her lips curving in calm confidence.","“Let Anhao handle it himself. I believe he can resolve this.”"]},{"number":575,"title":"Chapter 575: All Twenty Contracts Signed","paragraphs":["The uproar buzzed like a swarm of flies, impossible to ignore any longer.","Realizing that her elder sister was encouraging her, Song Anhao thought for a moment before summoning her courage and shouting down at the crowd below.","“There were fifteen judges in the first round. Every one of them is a shopkeeper who has run a bookshop for more than ten years. They may not hold any scholarly titles, but they have read more popular storybooks than you have read the sages’ classics. From over a thousand manuscripts, they selected the best hundred, and it took them three full days.”","“There were five judges in the second round. They were the authors of The Story of Qin Niang and The Record of Redress, myself, the oldest manager of the Song Family Bookshop, and my elder sister, County Princess Linghui. The Story of Qin Niang, widely regarded as the pioneering work of inner-house intrigue fiction, was discovered by her.”","Seeing the people below gradually quiet down, Song Anhao raised her voice and enunciated each word clearly. “This is a popular-story writing competition, not the imperial examination. Being well-versed in the sages’ classics does not mean that what you write will be something ordinary people enjoy reading or can understand.”","“If you want to see the manuscripts ranked in the top twenty, you can wait until they are printed and buy them at a bookshop yourselves. It won’t take very long.”","As soon as she finished speaking, Song Jinzhao appeared beside the railing. She silently looked down at the crowd below until every one of them fell quiet.","The scholar who had raised the objection met Song Jinzhao’s calm, indifferent gaze. He silently sat down and buried his head between his knees.","If he had known that County Princess Linghui was one of the judges, he would never have spoken up. He had certainly offended her now.","After the unveiling ceremony ended, the twenty finalists were taken to three separate rooms.","Zou Wudie stared at the young man sitting before her. Only after he had finished explaining all the terms did she hurriedly speak.","“You said just now that Peach Blossom Hermit is also one of the judges. Could I meet her?”","The Story of Qin Niang was Zou Wudie’s favorite popular storybook. The reason she had wanted to write one herself was that she had been inspired by that very book.","After talking until her mouth was dry, Song Anhao felt even more exhausted when she realized that the other woman’s attention was elsewhere. She had been working hard all day, yet all Zou Wudie cared about was meeting Liu Ruoxi.","With so much money on the table, was meeting Liu Ruoxi really more appealing?","“Just as you had your maid accept the award onstage, Peach Blossom Hermit doesn’t want to reveal her identity either.”","Disappointment appeared on Zou Wudie’s face, and she sat back down in her chair.","“All right. How much money did you say just now?”","Song Anhao pushed the contract across the table. “Please read it carefully.”","Zou Wudie lowered her head and read it word by word. A moment later, her eyes suddenly widened.","“That much money?”","“Miss!” Her maid hurriedly nudged Zou Wudie’s shoulder, then looked up to observe Song Anhao’s expression.","When she saw that his expression remained perfectly normal, the maid’s anxious heart eased slightly.","Hopefully he wouldn’t regret offering such a high price.","Song Anhao smiled calmly.","“This is only the guaranteed minimum payment for printing the book. If it sells well, you’ll also receive a share of any profits exceeding the guaranteed amount.”","The delight in Zou Wudie’s eyes grew brighter and brighter, almost spilling over.","“Agreed.”","As she spoke, she uncontrollably signed her name at the end of the contract. Before Song Anhao could even begin explaining everything, a red thumbprint had already been pressed over the signature. Her decisiveness was astonishing.","“According to the outline you submitted, the book is expected to reach three hundred thousand words. The remaining two hundred thousand words must be submitted within two months.”","Zou Wudie nodded without hesitation.","“No problem. I can finish it in half a month.”","She had already completed most of the story on her way to Suining City. If she hadn’t been too distracted to write during the several days she spent waiting for the rankings, she would have finished it long ago.","At the thought of receiving the remaining two hundred thousand words in barely half a month, Song Anhao nearly failed to suppress the smile tugging at the corners of his mouth.","He liked writers like this—those who submitted their manuscripts ahead of schedule. There was no need to chase them, and their efficiency was excellent.","“May I ask where your family lives, Miss Yue? Is it far from Suining City?”","Zou Wudie opened her mouth, then froze halfway through. She swallowed the words she was about to say and replied, “I’ll be spending a few days sightseeing in Suining City. When I leave, I’ll hand over the complete manuscript to you.”","Song Anhao was clever enough to understand her concern instantly. She was afraid he would investigate where she lived.","“Then which inn are you staying at? Would you like the bookshop to arrange a quiet place for you?”","Zou Wudie shook her head.","“I’m staying at Mingyuan Inn. It’s very quiet there, so there’s no need to make other arrangements.”","Song Anhao gave a slight nod and courteously escorted her to the door.","After all twenty people had signed their contracts, Song Anhao stared at the delivery dates recorded in his hand and sighed.","“It’s a pity that only three of them live in Suining City. Keeping in touch with the others will be troublesome. Not only will it be difficult to urge them along, we won’t be able to keep an eye on them and make sure they start new books either.”","Song Jinzhao stepped over the threshold and entered.","“We have shops in every county of the southwestern province. Have them go directly to those shops. Communication will be just as convenient.”","Song Anhao abruptly lifted his chin.","“What about places outside the southwestern province? I think twenty people are still a little too few.”","Song Jinzhao merely smiled and said nothing.","There were indeed shops elsewhere—nearby, as far as Panzhou in the southwest, and farther still, all the way to Yandu, the capital of the Northern Shu Kingdom. But those were all covert shops used to relay messages. They could not attract too much attention."]},{"number":576,"title":"Chapter 576: The Cement News Reaches the Capital","paragraphs":["Three months after the Storybook Competition ended, the printing presses at the Song Family Bookshop had not stopped for a moment. Two hundred people worked from sunrise to sunset every day without even a single day off.","The printed storybooks were transported to Songzhou City in batches, then sold by various booksellers throughout Jiangnan, the capital, and other regions. Every half month, when Song Anhao received the sales orders and money, her face crinkled with smiles.","The four members of the Song family were working feverishly in Suining. As cement came into widespread use throughout the Southwest Province, merchants from other regions began purchasing it as well, and word of it gradually reached the capital.","On the first day of the eighth month, after the morning court session, Emperor Xiao Chengjing kept Prince Ying and several others behind and summoned them to the Imperial Study to question them.","“I’ve heard that something called cement has appeared in the southwest. Not only can it be used to build roads, but it can also be used to construct houses. It is sturdy and smooth, and costs several times less than bricks and stone. Was it created by County Princess Linghui?”","Dongfang Shaoting, standing below the dais, showed a slight change in expression. After more than half a year, the news had finally reached the capital.","“Gu Qishan, have you heard about this?”","Gu Qishan’s brows drew together into a deep frown, and his heartbeat began to quicken.","“Your Majesty, I have not heard of it.”","He had never paid attention to a place like Suining unless there was a war there.","As for the Southwest Province, Gu Zhongxun had not reported anything either.","“What about you, Prince Ying?”","Xiao Rongyan shook his head. “I have not heard of it either, Father.”","Ever since Song Jinzhao had left the capital, Prince Ying had been acting obedient and filial before the Emperor. Gradually, he had regained the favor he once enjoyed.","However, with seven more princes in the palace and the previous incident as a warning, the court officials had chosen not to take sides again. One by one, they had withdrawn and were lying low, waiting for the other princes to grow up.","At the Emperor’s signal, Eunuch Zhao, who had been waiting nearby, immediately picked up the memorial from the imperial desk and walked down to them.","Xiao Rongyan accepted the memorial and opened it. It was a memorial of greetings sent by Huang Wenlong, the Provincial Administration Commissioner of Jiangnan.","It mentioned that he wished to replace all the official roads in Jiangnan Province with cement roads. The project would require five hundred thousand taels of silver, and he was asking whether the Emperor would approve it.","“Five hundred thousand taels to build roads? Huang Wenlong has gone mad!”","His eyes blazed as he looked at Emperor Xiao, and his voice nearly rose to a roar.","“Father, you absolutely cannot approve this. The official roads are perfectly good and do not need repairs. This is nothing but a waste of money.”","Xiao Chengjing’s expression remained impassive. He had never intended to approve the proposal; he was merely curious about cement.","“None of you know what cement is?”","The answer was silence.","“Since the cement was created by County Princess Linghui, send someone to Suining Prefecture to take a look.”","Whether they would use it was one matter, but they had to find out whether the cement was truly as good as Huang Wenlong claimed.","Once the discussion ended, Xiao Chengjing casually ordered someone to set out for Suining Prefecture.","After returning to his residence, Dongfang Shaoting told Dongfang Yuanbin that the Emperor had sent someone to Suining Prefecture to investigate the cement.","“Last year, the production of smokeless coal was limited. The supply in the Southwest Province alone could barely meet demand. Besides, once winter passed, the common people bought less of it, which was why the news spread so slowly.”","“But once they reach Suining City, neither the cement plant nor the coal plant will be able to remain hidden. Whom is the Emperor planning to send?”","Dongfang Shaoting replied, “Attendant Wu from the palace.”","“Then there’s nothing we can do.” Dongfang Yuanbin shook his head with a bitter smile. “Attendant Wu is one of the Emperor’s trusted men. There is no room to turn this matter around. Once he returns from Suining City, His Majesty will certainly learn about the cement plant and the coal plant. He may even bring cement and smokeless coal back with him.”","Dongfang Shaoting lowered his eyes, his heart filled with indecision.","“The coal plant and cement plant are County Princess Linghui’s private property. The Emperor shouldn’t seize them by force, should he?”","Dongfang Yuanbin stroked his snow-white beard. He opened his mouth, then hesitated.","“Spread word in half a month that we have partnered with County Princess Linghui in the smokeless-coal business. You should also make some arrangements at court.”","Dongfang Shaoting took a deep breath and slowly nodded. “I understand, Father.”"]},{"number":577,"title":"Chapter 577: The Startled Palace Eunuch","paragraphs":["Three months later, Attendant Wu stood outside the city walls, one hand pressed to his aching lower back.","He stared up at the wall towering before him. It was three zhang high and so tightly built that not even a crack showed between the bricks. It looked even sturdier than the walls of the capital.","The soles of his shoes rasped against the paved road with a steady shushing sound. He stamped his feet twice more, then lowered his head to look. Aside from a few scratches, the soles were covered only in a thin layer of dust.","Since entering the southwestern province, he had seen two or three county towns laying cement roads. But they were all so narrow that only a single carriage could pass at a time. Even Songzhou City had roads barely wide enough for two carriages.","The road beneath his feet, however, was more than two zhang wide. Four carriages could pass side by side with room to spare.","As the carriage passed through the outer wall, a broad avenue stretching beyond sight came into view.","The farther they went, the more cement roads they saw—even the narrow country lanes on either side had been paved. Songzhou City had only managed to pave two main roads within its walls.","Attendant Wu leaned against the carriage as though waking from a dream, his gaze fixed straight outside the window.","The rice in the fields had already been harvested, leaving behind nothing but a layer of charred black ash.","In the distance, ditches ran alongside the cement road, water flowing through them.","After half an hour, they were still passing fields and farmhouses. Attendant Wu could not help frowning as he began to question Song Qiming’s abilities.","“There are plenty of commoners and merchants along the road. How is it that there isn’t a proper market anywhere?”","Without shops, where were the people supposed to buy things? Surely they couldn’t produce everything themselves.","And then there were the commercial taxes.","The Song family had once run a small business. Song Qiming couldn’t possibly be ignorant of such basic principles.","“Master, there’s another city wall up ahead!” the eunuch driving the carriage suddenly cried out.","Attendant Wu stuck his head out of the window. Sure enough, another wall stood ahead, though it was somewhat shorter than the first.","“Keep going.”","The young eunuch flicked the reins and urged the carriage onward. Only when they drew near did they finally see rows of shops stretching across the road.","Standing beneath the two-zhang-high wall, Attendant Wu raised his brows in confusion.","“How does Suining City have two walls? And this one is made of bricks.”","A passerby happened to overhear him and looked him up and down.","His voice was soft, and his skin was so pale it seemed translucent. He looked a little effeminate.","“You’re visiting Suining City for the first time?” the man asked.","The young eunuch was just about to step forward and stop him when Attendant Wu held him back.","Attendant Wu took a step forward and nodded at the man. “Yes, it’s our first time here. I never imagined it would be so—” He paused, then said, “It’s truly opened my eyes.”","The passerby grinned, his face glowing with pride as he puffed out his chest.","“Of course. Suining City is even livelier than Songzhou City now.”","He gestured toward the wall. “This is the inner wall. The one outside is the outer wall. It used to be nothing more than a ramshackle earthen wall, but it was rebuilt a few months ago.”","Attendant Wu blinked. “So the area outside used to be a village?”","“That explains why we didn’t see many shops, and why there were so many rice fields.”","The passerby continued walking. “The inner city is livelier than the outer city. Merchants and travelers all stay inside the inner walls.”","“There are plenty of places to eat and plenty of places to have fun. Go in and see for yourselves.”","Attendant Wu and the young eunuch exchanged a glance before climbing back into the carriage and entering the inner city.","Above the southern gate of the inner city, a covert guard stationed in the local government office kept his eyes fixed on the carriage. Only after it entered the inner city did he hurry down from the wall, mount a horse, and gallop to the prefectural office to deliver the news.","“My lord, Attendant Wu, sent by His Majesty, has just entered the inner city. He’s heading toward the prefectural office.”","Song Qiming set down the grain ledger in his hand. This year, the prefectural office had collected ten thousand dan more grain during the autumn harvest than it had the previous year. The grain taxes from the various counties had yet to arrive, and he had no idea how much more they would collect than last year.","“How many people are there in total?”","The covert guard replied, “Four in all. The carriage is being driven by a young eunuch who appears to be close to Attendant Wu. There are also two guards on horseback.”","Ripples spread across the water in the teacup as the table trembled. Song Qiming stopped tapping his index finger against the tabletop and looked toward Yao Ye, who was waiting nearby.","“Are our people at the post station in place?”","Yao Ye nodded. “They arrived yesterday. One woman and three men—two inside and two outside.”"]},{"number":578,"title":"Chapter 578: Is it Capable or Truly Lazy","paragraphs":["Before long, a yamen runner hurried in to report.","“My lord, a eunuch calling himself Attendant Wu has arrived outside. He says he has come bearing His Majesty’s orders.”","Aside from retired eunuchs who had left the palace, only the imperial palace was home to young eunuchs.","Song Qiming rose, gathered his sleeves, and strode outside with measured steps.","When he saw the visitor’s appearance, he couldn’t help marveling inwardly at the Dongfang family’s superb painter. Even the strands of hair were identical.","Pretending not to know anything, he confirmed with the man, “Are you Eunuch Wu from the palace?”","Attendant Wu’s shifty eyes swept over him from head to toe. He had seen Song Qiming once in the palace the year before last.","He took an identity token from his robes and showed it to Song Qiming.","“His Majesty heard that County Princess Linghui has developed something called cement, and that even the governor of Jiangnan wants to purchase it for road construction. His Majesty was quite curious, so he sent this servant to take a look. This journey is not an official assignment, so Lord Song may simply consider this servant to be out sightseeing.”","Song Qiming bent slightly at the waist, his smile never reaching his eyes.","“If you say you’re here to sightsee, then you’re here to sightsee.”","“After such a long journey by land and water, you should first go to the courier station and rest. Tomorrow, this subordinate will entertain you properly and take you to see the cement His Majesty is curious about.”","Attendant Wu stamped his feet. “What’s there to see? One look at the ground is enough to tell that it’s good stuff.”","“If Prefect Song had informed His Majesty sooner, a heaven-defying reward would surely have been delivered long ago.”","Song Qiming sighed. “There are things you don’t know, my lord. The initial investment in building the cement factory was enormous. If we hadn’t partnered with the Dongfang family, we wouldn’t have been able to get the business off the ground.”","“The factory has been open for half a year, and we still haven’t recovered our costs. How could we dare trouble His Majesty?”","Attendant Wu raised an eyebrow. “How come this servant heard that cement is made from nothing more than stones?”","Song Qiming gave a bitter smile and shook his head. “To help this subordinate and give the people of Suining Prefecture another way to make a living, my elder sister set the workers’ wages quite high.”","“We only make a few coins on each sack of cement sold to the common people, while cement sold to the government is priced at cost. If we want to recover our expenses and turn a profit, it will probably take three to five years.”","“Ha—” Attendant Wu cried out in disbelief.","Three to five years just to recover the costs? That was far too long.","“Where is the cement factory?”","Song Qiming quickly glanced at him, as if he had heard something strange.","“Did you not see it before coming here? It’s where the smoke is rising outside the city.”","Attendant Wu said, “I thought that place was on fire.”","People were burning the remaining rice straw in the fields everywhere, so it was perfectly normal for there to be smoke.","The corner of Song Qiming’s mouth twitched. He extended a hand in invitation. “You should go to the courier station and rest first, my lord. This subordinate will take you there tomorrow.”","After spending so many days in a carriage, every bone in Attendant Wu’s body ached. He wished he could sleep for three days and three nights without getting up.","“No rush. We’ll go the day after tomorrow.” It was rare to get out for once; he might as well enjoy himself. There was no need to hurry back.","After escorting him to the courier station, Yao Ye arranged for two undercover guards to attend to him personally.","When Song Qiming came to the courier station the day after next, he asked, “The cement factory is ready for inspection. When will Attendant Wu be departing?”","The guard turned and entered the courtyard. Before long, a little eunuch came out with quick, mincing steps, accompanied by the same guard from earlier.","“Prefect Song, my master has been utterly exhausted these past few days. Now that he has suddenly relaxed, he’s feeling somewhat unwell. We’ll go to the cement factory tomorrow.”","After returning to the rear courtyard of the government office, Song Qiming held the letter and portrait Fushun had sent over.","“Yukun’s letter said Attendant Wu was highly capable. Why doesn’t the reality seem to match?”","According to the information sent out by the undercover guards attending to him at the courier station, Attendant Wu had spent the past two days doing nothing but eating and sleeping. Every meal consisted of such an abundance of fine food and wine that a single table couldn’t hold it all.","When he had nothing else to do, he would sit in the courtyard admiring the bamboo grove and flowers, listening to the wind and birdsong. He wasn’t anxious in the slightest. He truly seemed to have come out for a leisurely trip.","Song Jinzhao lifted her chin and twisted her stiff, aching neck.","“It can take three months to travel from the capital to Suining City. I’d say he really isn’t in any hurry.”","The emperor had issued an order, but even if they hadn’t ridden horses and traveled day and night, that was one thing.","They had little luggage, and with a carriage drawn by fine horses, they could have reached Suining City in just two and a half months by traveling during the day. Yet they had taken three months and seven days.","It wasn’t winter yet, nor was it the rainy season. The roads should have been at their best.","Song Qiming sighed and sat down.","“If he refuses to leave, we’ll have to stay tense the entire time. I wonder what His Majesty’s attitude will be now that the Dongfang family has announced the partnership.”"]},{"number":579,"title":"Chapter 579: The Northern Kingdom Built Ocean-Going Sailing Ships Exactly Like Ours","paragraphs":["In the capital, thousands of miles away, at the Dongfang residence.","“The Emperor hasn’t mentioned the matter for two months. I thought he must have forgotten about it.” Dongfang Shaoting had just returned from the palace.","Two and a half months earlier, word had first spread through the teahouses that the Dongfang family and Song Jinzhao had gone into business together, selling smokeless coal.","As the rumor passed from mouth to mouth, it had transformed into claims that they were partners in both the smokeless coal and cement businesses. Some even said that the Dongfang family was the principal partner, with the Song family playing a secondary role.","Dongfang Yuanbin let out a mocking laugh. “Forgotten? How could he possibly have forgotten?”","“After all, everyone in the world knows that these are the private businesses of County Princess Linghui. With our Dongfang family involved as well, it’s only natural that people would start talking.”","Dongfang Shaoting lowered his voice as he took a deep breath.","“After court ended today, His Majesty summoned me to the Imperial Study to discuss another matter. Shuobei’s potato harvest has risen compared with last year.”","“The oceangoing sailboats manufactured by the Ministry of Works have been replicated exactly by Shuobei.”","The smoke from the incense burner rose slowly in the shape of a snake before vanishing. Seated upright in his grand armchair, Dongfang Yuanbin clenched his fists, his face growing increasingly grim.","“What did His Majesty say?”","“His Majesty ordered Minister of Works Ou Shinian to investigate himself for three days. If he can’t uncover the truth, he is to present his head.”","The Ministry of Works’ confidential blueprints were not something an ordinary person could obtain. There had to be a mole.","After a moment’s thought, Dongfang Yuanbin said, “Send someone to ask Ou Shinian whether Prince Ying has ever looked at the blueprints for the oceangoing sailboats.”","Dongfang Shaoting’s eyes widened. “Father suspects Prince Ying?”","Dongzhao had only two adult princes. The elder prince had stolen potatoes and sent them to Shuobei for his own personal gain. If the second prince did the same, the imperial family’s authority would be utterly destroyed.","Dongfang Yuanbin rose and rolled up his sleeves. “Prince Ying married the Princess of Shuobei. Who knows what might happen between them behind closed doors? We would do well to keep our guard up.”","“Back when Prince Qi was still around, Prince Ying had people in the Ministry of Works. You only need to mention Prince Ying in passing, and Ou Shinian will naturally investigate.”","The Ministry of Works remained tense until the end of the working day, with no one daring to leave.","From morning until night, Ou Shinian summoned more than a dozen people into his office. Each one emerged with legs so weak they could barely walk.","“We work at the Ministry of Works. How could we commit treason and sell out our country? That would be suicide.”","Everyone was deeply worried. If they couldn’t find the person who had leaked the information, the entire Ministry of Works might suffer the consequences. Then they would all be finished.","The officials sat on tenterhooks, glancing anxiously in every direction. Seeing the same urgency in everyone else’s eyes made them feel slightly better.","But once they had calmed down, they began to suspect one another.","The blueprints had been in the Ministry of Works. If one of their colleagues had leaked them, who could it be?","Could the culprit be sitting right beside them?","Ou Shinian leaned back in his chair, shifting several times, but he couldn’t get comfortable.","Misfortune had fallen from the heavens. Who had done this?","With no mind to return home, Ou Shinian spent the night tossing and turning on the narrow couch in the office’s temporary quarters.","Unable to sleep, he got up and paced around. When he reached his desk and saw the stacks of blueprints covering it, his frustration only grew.","“Bastard. Once I find out who did this, I’ll tear him limb from limb.” He slammed his fist onto the blueprints, leaving a dent.","The eunuch standing guard outside heard the noise. After thinking for a few seconds, he simply lowered his head and pretended he had heard nothing.","Ou Shinian spent the entire night awake. He didn’t even eat breakfast the next morning before heading to court.","As his shoes struck the tiled floor, he felt as though half his soul had drifted away from his body.","When he entered the main hall, the civil and military officials all turned to look at him.","Noticing the dark circles beneath Ou Shinian’s eyes, many officials lowered their heads and stared at the ground, their spirits sinking.","If the traitor wasn’t caught, today it would be the Ministry of Works suffering the consequences. Tomorrow, it could be any of them.","They stole a glance at the man seated upon the Dragon Throne. There was no pity on the Emperor’s face, only sternness. Their hearts sank even further.","When Prince Qi and Prince Ying had once stood in opposition to each other, the Emperor had still been relatively lenient. Now, he had grown increasingly ruthless, showing not the slightest regard for past ties.","Under the oppressive weight of the Emperor’s gaze, Ou Shinian endured the entire morning court session in trembling fear.","He had just prepared to return home and rest when a Ministry of Works official bumped into his arm.","“Lord Dongfang wants me to ask whether Prince Ying has ever seen the Ministry of Works’ blueprints for the sailboats.” The words vanished as quickly as they had appeared, like a breeze brushing past Ou Shinian’s ear.","His reaction had been dulled by exhaustion. By the time he looked up, the speaker had already walked three paces away.","From his back alone, Ou Shinian recognized him as one of his subordinates, an assistant director in the Ministry of Works who had risen through the ranks with the Dongfang family’s support.","Had Prince Ying seen the blueprints?","Ou Shinian knitted his brows as he walked, pondering the meaning behind the question.","After five steps, a flash of insight crossed his mind.","The Princess of Shuobei was now Prince Ying’s secondary consort. Could it be...?","The instant he realized that this was possible, a cold sweat broke out across Ou Shinian’s back.","He returned to the Ministry and began reconstructing which of his subordinates had once been connected to Prince Ying. Then he went back over the statements from the previous day. Before long, he had identified his target.","Qin Guo, a vice director of the Ministry of Works’ Waterways Bureau. He had once pledged allegiance to Prince Ying."]},{"number":580,"title":"Chapter 580: Oshinian: Heaven Wants to Destroy My Eastern Shining Kingdom","paragraphs":["Ou Shinian glared at his subordinate approaching from the opposite direction and said coldly, “Close the door.”","Qin Guo took a deep breath, then slowly turned around and shut the door.","So many people in the Ministry of Works had seen the blueprints for the oceangoing vessel. Without evidence, there was no way to pin the blame on him.","“I recall that you used to be quite close to His Highness Prince Ying.”","Qin Guo’s face instantly turned deathly pale. He looked up at Ou Shinian in disbelief.","Their eyes met: one filled with ferocity, the other with fear.","Qin Guo’s lips moved, but his throat was so tight that he could not get a word out.","“I’m asking you: did you show the blueprints for the oceangoing vessel to His Highness Prince Ying?”","Realizing that the matter had been exposed, Qin Guo dropped to his knees with a thud and hurriedly begged Ou Shinian for mercy.","“His Highness Prince Ying did ask this subordinate for the blueprints. He only looked at them for a few moments. I have no idea how the Kingdom of Shuobei obtained them. Please spare me, my lord. I am truly innocent.”","Ou Shinian walked around the desk and stopped in front of Qin Guo. His furious gaze bored into him, as though he wished he could flay him alive and tear him limb from limb.","“Did he really only look at them for a few moments?”","There were seven sheets in the complete set of blueprints for the oceangoing vessel, including the overall design and detailed drawings of every part. No one could possibly memorize them after only a few glances.","Trembling, Qin Guo pressed his forehead to the floor.","“That day, I developed a stomachache after drinking tea and had to leave for a while.”","“Bang!”","The desk shook. Outside, the officials from the Ministry of Works, who had been listening with their ears pressed close, all flinched.","Good heavens! Could it really be His Highness Prince Ying who had leaked the blueprints to the Kingdom of Shuobei?","“By imperial decree, Ou Shinian, Minister of Works, and Qin Guo, Director of the Waterways Bureau, are summoned to appear before His Majesty.”","Cui Zhengyang abruptly turned around in his seat. When he saw that the person delivering the decree was Eunuch Zhao, he felt that the dust was finally about to settle.","His Majesty must have learned what had happened in the Ministry of Works. He was summoning Minister Ou and Qin Guo to question them.","Watching the two men leave with hunched backs, Cui Zhengyang pressed his lips tightly together, his expression growing increasingly grave.","Even if it really was Prince Ying, would His Majesty punish him severely?","Or would someone else be made to take the blame?","In the imperial study, everyone was kneeling.","Prince Ying stood with his robes open at the shoulders, his face filled with indignation.","“This son of yours has seen the blueprints for the oceangoing vessel at the Ministry of Works, but I’m not the only one who has seen them. Why claim that I was the one who leaked them?”","The emperor sat wearily upon the throne. For some reason, his health had been deteriorating over the past two years. He became exhausted after sitting for even a short while, yet he still had so many troublesome matters weighing on him.","“Qin Guo, did you personally see Prince Ying reproduce the blueprints?”","Qin Guo knelt on the floor, cold sweat covering his forehead.","“This subject did not see it with his own eyes.”","Prince Ying puffed out his chest and faced Minister Ou indignantly.","“The Ministry of Works bears undeniable responsibility for the leak. Is Minister Ou trying to make me take the fall?”","Ou Shinian’s voice rose, his face flushed with anger.","“His Majesty never permitted Your Highness to interfere in the affairs of the Ministry of Works. Why did Your Highness examine the blueprints? And why did you take them back to the Prince Ying’s residence?","“If Secondary Consort He saw them, it would hardly be surprising if she leaked them to the Kingdom of Shuobei. Otherwise, how could they have built an oceangoing vessel so quickly, one that is identical to ours?”","Prince Ying pressed his lips together, his eyes turning slightly red.","“Father, I never wanted to marry the princess of the Kingdom of Shuobei. I accepted this marriage only because I was forced to do so for the sake of the Dongzhao Kingdom.”","“Everyone under Heaven knows who He Shuwan is. Even now, people mock me behind my back for taking a brothel woman whom countless men have ridden as my secondary consort. And now, because of this matter, you suspect me of colluding with the enemy and betraying our country. I have truly been wronged.”","With tears hanging from his eyes, he knocked his head against the floor, stirring a feeling of guilt in the emperor’s heart.","The emperor was not unaware of the cruel taunts, but for the sake of diplomatic relations between the two countries, he had been forced to turn a blind eye.","When Ou Shinian saw the guilt spreading across the emperor’s face, his heart sank.","If this continued, he would be the one to suffer.","In the space of a heartbeat, Ou Shinian quickly made a decision. He raised his head toward the emperor.","“This subject also does not believe that His Highness Prince Ying would secretly collude with the Kingdom of Shuobei. It must have been Secondary Consort He acting behind His Highness’s back. She must have secretly examined the blueprints, copied them, and then sent someone to deliver them to the Kingdom of Shuobei.”","The emperor’s exquisitely translucent jade thumb ring struck the imperial desk and shattered. He was just about to order Secondary Consort He’s punishment when he suddenly remembered her identity. He hesitated once more.","He said in a low voice, “Without evidence, we may give others grounds to accuse us and provide the Kingdom of Shuobei with an excuse to wage war.”","From the corner of his eye, Ou Shinian caught the smug smile tugging at the corners of Prince Ying’s lips. His suspended heart sank straight to the bottom of a cliff.","Prince Ying definitely knew what had happened. Otherwise, he would never have allowed Qin Guo to take the blueprints to his residence.","Heaven clearly does not favor our Dongzhao Kingdom. Two princes have secretly colluded with the Kingdom of Shuobei for their own selfish ends. Are they trying to bring about the downfall of our country?","After pondering for a moment, the emperor ordered Prince Ying, “Eliminate all the maids who accompanied Secondary Consort He from Shuobei. Leave her isolated and without anyone useful at her side.”","Prince Ying cupped his hands and promised, “This son will take care of it the moment I return to the residence.”","Outside the imperial study, Ou Shinian watched Prince Ying walk away with light, carefree steps. He sighed and glanced back at the imperial study.","From now on, he would have to guard against Prince Ying.","But as a prince who had already begun interfering in court affairs, Prince Ying would be almost impossible to guard against completely."]},{"number":581,"title":"Chapter 581: He's simply a lustful ghost, a perverted lecher","paragraphs":["The night was dim and hazy, darker even than the faces of the three generations gathered inside the house.","“Is the Emperor pretending to be a fool? Prince Ying has nothing to do with the Ministry of Works, yet he went out of his way to ask Qin Guo for the blueprints and even secretly took them to Prince Ying’s residence. If that isn’t a hidden scheme, then what is?” Dongfang Yukun was furious, utterly unable to make sense of it.","Dongfang Shaoting’s brows drew together as he snapped, “Enough! How dare you discuss the Emperor like that? If word gets out, the entire Dongfang family will suffer.”","Dongfang Yukun dropped heavily into a chair, his chest rising and falling violently.","Dongfang Yuanbin shook his head helplessly. “Prince Qi’s death dealt the Emperor a tremendous blow. How could he be willing to lose another son?”","“It’s a pity that the seven princes in the palace are still so young. Otherwise, the situation would surely be very different.” Dongfang Yukun slammed a fist onto the table. When he thought of how Song Qiming had also left the capital to avoid disaster because of the Emperor’s lack of virtue, his heart felt unbearably stifled.","As a young official, he had been full of ambition. He had thought he could accomplish great things and bring peace and prosperity to the world. Now, however, he was growing increasingly disappointed.","......","Attendant Wu had rested for four whole days at the post station before finally going out. On the very day he went to the cement factory, he even stopped at a restaurant for an extravagant Manchu-Han feast.","Picking his teeth with a toothpick, he praised the food. “I never imagined that a remote backwater like Suining could have such delicious dishes. The flavor truly isn’t inferior to that of Wangyue Restaurant.”","On the surface, Song Qiming wore a smile so stiff it nearly cramped his face. Beneath the table, however, the veins on his hand bulged one after another.","“If my lord likes it, this subordinate can have the restaurant prepare these dishes and deliver them to the post station every day.”","Ordering so many dishes and not even finishing them—of course you don’t mind when you aren’t the one paying.","He spent his days sleeping at the post station and even summoned courtesans to wait on him. He was already a eunuch, yet he was still so lustful. It was truly unbearable to watch.","Song Qiming concealed his thoughts well. Attendant Wu failed to notice and instead thought him quite accommodating, his expression becoming even more cheerful.","“How could I eat like this every meal? A dozen or so dishes are enough for one meal.”","Song Qiming forced out two fake laughs, nearly grinding his front teeth to pieces.","They took a carriage to the cement factory. Seeing the place in the distance where thick black smoke rose into the air, Attendant Wu asked, “Is that the cement factory too?”","Song Qiming shook his head. “That’s the coal plant. The cement factory gets its fuel from there.”","Attendant Wu did not think much of it.","Coal mines were troublesome to operate and offered little profit. He looked down on them.","As soon as they entered the factory grounds, dust swept toward them, making it difficult to keep their eyes open.","Attendant Wu covered his mouth, his voice carrying a hint of disdain. “With so much dust, can’t you keep the place cleaner?”","Song Qiming expressionlessly handed him a mask. “Wear this. It will help keep the dust out.”","If he himself and the others didn’t need to wear one, he truly wouldn’t have wanted to give it to him.","“Why are there women working here too?” Attendant Wu asked, pointing at a woman pushing a cart.","The woman pushing the cart tensed from head to toe when she heard that.","The women looked at Song Qiming in fear. This man looked like an important official. What if Prefect Song listened to him and dismissed them?","Song Qiming lowered his eyes and replied indifferently, “Elder Sister does not discriminate between men and women when hiring. If life weren’t so difficult for them, they wouldn’t want to do this kind of hard labor either.”","Attendant Wu delicately raised his little finger, more graceful than anyone else.","“It is improper for women to show their faces in public. And with so many men here, it will inevitably invite gossip if word gets out.”","Song Qiming said, “The families of the women working at the cement and coal plants work here as well. No one will have anything to say.”","Mud and sand blackened the soles of Attendant Wu’s pristine white shoes, while bits of gravel dug into the soft leather and made his feet ache.","On top of that, the temperature inside was more than ten degrees higher than outside. Before long, Attendant Wu was sweating all over, his clothes clinging to his body and making him feel hot and uncomfortable.","He stopped to catch his breath and asked, “Lord Song, how large is this factory?”","Song Qiming smiled, though the amusement never reached his eyes. “It takes two hours to walk around it.”","“That big?” Attendant Wu’s mouth fell open, and the urge to retreat in his eyes grew even stronger.","Song Qiming gave a slight nod.","Attendant Wu laboriously lifted his feet and continued forward.","He seemed to be going through the motions. Before long, he stopped and said, “Everything looks the same after going around in circles. We can stop here.”","He had arrived in a hurry and left just as quickly. Song Qiming had not even had time to take out the account books to show him.","After watching the carriage disappear completely from sight, Lanxi turned around and walked back inside with a look of speechless exasperation.","If they had known he was this sort of person, they wouldn’t have needed to make preparations over the past few days. He would probably try to pocket a tidy sum before leaving, too.","After returning to the post station, Attendant Wu summoned courtesans again that night.","The maid who had been sent to the adjoining room gazed at her plain, unremarkable face in the mirror and felt grateful for the first time that she was only average-looking.","Who could have imagined that a eunuch without a manhood could still indulge in pleasure night after night without tiring? Not to mention the bruises and injuries on the bodies of those courtesans.","He was a depraved lecher, a perverted fiend!"]},{"number":582,"title":"Chapter 582: Attendant-in-Common Wu's Eyes Went Wide: Only Three Coins per Catty","paragraphs":["The following day, Attendant Wu did not leave until nearly lunchtime. This time, Song Qiming used the excuse of being busy with official business to send Shi Simian over to entertain him. If he had to keep accompanying the man, he would have poked his fingertips raw.","“Lord Shi has served as an official in Suining City for many years and knows every blade of grass and tree here like the back of his hand. There’s no one better suited to show Your Excellency around Suining City.”","Yao Ye stood beside Shi Simian dressed as an ordinary guard, though his gaze kept furtively darting toward Attendant Wu and his three companions.","Someone had to keep watch while Shi Simian handled the eating and sightseeing.","“Is this the cement shop opened by County Princess Linghui?” From the south gate of the inner city, the cement shop at the left-hand corner of the street was clearly visible. It was bustling with customers coming and going.","Shi Simian tilted his head to glance at it, then nodded. “Yes. It’s the only one in all of Suining City.”","It looked much cleaner than the cement factory. Attendant Wu clasped his hands behind his back and swaggered inside.","Several dozen bags of cement were stacked against the wall. The shopkeeper, Xie Zhi, exchanged a glance with Yao Ye, then immediately lowered his eyes and came forward with a welcoming smile.","“What can Your Excellencies do for you?”","Attendant Wu turned his head and stared at the smokeless coal piled in the corner. “This coal has a rather unusual shape.”","Xie Zhi took a step back, picked up the iron tongs leaning against the wall, and used them to lift out a honeycomb briquette for the man to examine.","“Your Excellency may not know this, but this is smokeless coal. Because the holes inside it resemble a honeycomb, it’s also called a honeycomb briquette.”","Thinking of the coal factory Song Qiming had mentioned the day before, Attendant Wu asked, “Was this made by County Princess Linghui’s coal factory?”","“Smokeless coal—does that mean it gives off no smoke when burned?”","Xie Zhi smiled and nodded. “Not only does it produce no smoke, but it also has hardly any smell.”","“The County Princess spent eighty-one days perfecting this product. In order to help the people of Suining City survive the winter, she’s selling it at practically cost price. Last winter, nearly every household used this coal.”","“Take one out and let me have a look.” Attendant Wu clearly did not believe what Xie Zhi was saying.","It was not as though he had never seen anyone burn coal before. The smoke had been thick enough to make one unable to open one’s eyes, and the smell had been even more pungent.","Xie Zhi first lit the honeycomb briquette with a flame, then placed it inside the stove used for boiling water.","In moments, the entire briquette glowed red. Attendant Wu bent down to inspect it, repeatedly inching his nose closer.","Heat washed over his face, yet there was truly no smoke, and the smell was extremely faint—almost comparable to the golden-thread charcoal used by the emperor.","“How many coppers do you sell this smokeless coal for per jin?”","“Three coppers,” Xie Zhi replied. “One jin is one briquette.”","“Only three coppers? That’s cheaper than charcoal!” Attendant Wu stared in disbelief, his eyes widening so far they nearly popped out of their sockets.","Xie Zhi gave a bitter smile and shook his head.","“That’s why I said it’s being sold at cost. If the Dongfang family hadn’t invested in the business, we wouldn’t have been able to get it off the ground last year.”","Attendant Wu’s mouth fell slightly open as he looked at Xie Zhi and the shop assistants as though they were idiots.","When he thought of Song Jinzhao, who had gone to so much trouble to create these things yet made no money from them, he became even more convinced that she was an idiot.","Her medical skills were superb, and her martial arts were formidable. How could she be so foolish when it came to something as important as money?","Could it be that she thought being a County Princess meant she would never lack food or clothing, so she simply did not care?","How could anyone ever have too much silver? The more, the better.","At the thought of all that enormous wealth being thrown away for nothing, Attendant Wu’s heart ached. If only it were his.","The prices of both cement and smokeless coal had to be raised.","“I have been in Suining City for several days now, yet I have not paid my respects to County Princess Linghui. May I ask where she is at the moment?”","Shi Simian smiled and shook his head. “This subordinate isn’t certain. She may be in the rear courtyard of the prefectural office.”","Attendant Wu said, “Since I have to return to the post station anyway, I may as well stop by the prefectural office on the way.”","He absolutely had to persuade her. If she refused to make money, how would she have any money to give him?"]},{"number":583,"title":"Chapter 583: Old Tea for Entertaining Guests","paragraphs":["The sedan chair stopped at the side entrance of the county office. When the guards saw that the visitor was Attendant Wu, their expressions remained perfectly calm.","The County Princess had warned them long ago that he would certainly come calling.","Shi Simian instructed someone to step forward and make inquiries.","“Attendant Wu has come from the palace and wishes to see County Princess Linghui. May I ask whether the County Princess is currently in residence?”","The guard bowed and replied, “Please wait a moment, honored sirs. I’ll go in and inform her at once.”","After the time it took to finish half a cup of tea, the guard came out with a smile and opened the door. “The County Princess invites you in.”","The group crossed the threshold. When Attendant Wu saw that Shi Simian was about to follow, he stopped in his tracks.","“The county office is busy with official matters. Lord Shi, you should go attend to your duties.”","Shi Simian studied the look on Attendant Wu’s face and realized that the eunuch did not want him coming along. He could only smile, nod, and fall back.","“This subordinate does indeed still have official business to finish. The rear courtyard is directly behind the offices. If anything happens after I leave, Lord Wu may send someone to summon me at any time.”","Attendant Wu lifted his eyelids, satisfied that he had left everyone else behind.","“This servant pays his respects to the County Princess. May Your Highness enjoy boundless blessings and good fortune.”","Seeing Song Jinzhao seated upright in the main hall, Attendant Wu walked over and leisurely bent at the waist in greeting.","“There is no need for such ceremony, Attendant Wu. Someone, bring tea.”","A maid entered carrying a tea tray.","When the lid of the teacup was lifted, the tea was at just the right temperature to drink.","Attendant Wu picked up the cup and took a small sip. A trace of disdain flashed through his eyes.","Though it was Longjing of middling quality, it was stale tea. No household of an official ranked fifth grade or higher would serve such a thing to guests.","Despite being a county princess, her clothing and adornments were rather plain, and she had only a few maids attending her.","She must have come from a peasant household. Even after rising among the branches to become a phoenix, she could not rid herself of that narrow, provincial air.","She had money yet did not know how to make it—what a waste of the clever mind Heaven had given her.","“This servant was strolling through the city today and discovered that Suining City has more than just cement. It also possesses such a fine thing as smokeless coal.”","He wore a solemn expression, pretending to have Song Jinzhao’s best interests at heart.","“This servant feels that smokeless coal at three copper coins a jin is truly being sold far too cheaply. It ought to be thirty copper coins a jin.”","Song Jinzhao nearly choked on the tea she had just swallowed.","At thirty copper coins a jin, who besides wealthy households could afford it?","She put on an awkward expression and said, “As long as the common people can use it, it cannot be considered too cheap. The County Princess has no worries about food or clothing and has never intended to make money from this.”","Her words left Attendant Wu momentarily speechless.","Was she really the sort of person who thought that as long as she had enough to eat and drink, she had no need to pursue wealth or status?","With tea like this, clothing and jewelry like those, and a courtyard such as this one, would it not be better to earn more silver and buy herself a grand residence outside?","She lived in the rear courtyard of the county office, a place with neither attractive scenery nor favorable feng shui. It had probably been built countless years ago; even the paint on the rafters was different from one section to the next. It had clearly been patched up several times.","“If the County Princess sold it at a higher price, the county office could collect more commercial taxes as well. For the sake of Lord Song’s future, the County Princess ought to give this matter serious consideration.”","He raised his brows at Song Jinzhao, hoping she would understand his hint and agree.","To serve as an official, ability alone was not enough. One also had to be clever, tactful, and know how to conduct oneself. The silver that needed to be spent had to be spent.","Song Jinzhao sighed and shook her head, her face filled with helplessness.","“Attendant Wu, you do not know what Suining City was like when we first arrived. Every household was struggling to get enough to eat. They had to boil coarse grain mixed with dirt just to fill their stomachs, and bandits and thieves would come to plunder them from time to time. If I had not been worried about my younger brother, I would have wanted to return to the capital myself.”","“Left with no other choice, I had to lead people into the mountains to suppress the bandits. Everything we are doing now is also meant to help my younger brother build up enough merit to be transferred back to the capital sooner. Only when the people live well can an official’s reputation flourish. I must ask Attendant Wu to say a few favorable words for us before His Majesty.”","Thinking of the Emperor’s ruthless treatment of Ye Liangyu, Attendant Wu could not help feeling sorry for Song Qiming.","If only he had never taken that man as his master in the first place.","“The County Princess need not worry. Lord Song is Lord Song. As long as he keeps his distance from Lord Ye in the future, His Majesty will transfer Lord Song back to the capital for your sake. It will only be a few days later than expected.”","His eyes roamed over Song Jinzhao, as well as the maids and servants beside her. Seeing that some were sitting and others standing, yet not one of them made the slightest move, Attendant Wu’s narrow-minded nature surfaced once more.","They had asked him for help but had not offered the slightest token of appreciation. No wonder they had been exiled to Suining City.","Watching him leave with a cold expression, Song Jinzhao stood silently at the doorway and saw him off.","“County Princess, Attendant Wu seems to be angry,” said a maid.","Song Jinzhao sneered coldly. “It is not just ‘seems.’ He is angry. That is precisely the effect I wanted.”","The tea in the cups on the table had already gone cold. Its cloying fragrance made it undrinkable. Song Jinzhao had deliberately ordered them to serve stale tea.","Only when there was no profit to be made would people stop coveting it. If the Emperor suddenly decided to seize it and sell it at a high price, the common people’s spit alone would be enough to drown him."]},{"number":584,"title":"Chapter 584: The Emperor Who Thought He Had the Upper Hand","paragraphs":["Attendant Wu returned to the capital and immediately hurried to the Imperial Study to report to the emperor. Behind him, four guards carried a sack of cement and a basket of smokeless coal.","He dropped to his knees with a thud. “Your Majesty, the governor of Jiangnan was telling the truth. Cement truly does exist.”","“No—this time, I discovered another treasure in Suining City.”","He took a piece of smokeless coal from the basket and held it up for the emperor to see.","“This is smokeless coal. It is inexpensive, costing only three copper coins per jin. It burns without smoke or odor and is every bit as good as golden-thread charcoal.”","“...”","When no reply came for some time, Attendant Wu raised his head and looked at the emperor.","Xiao Chengjing’s face was calm, as though he had known about it all along.","“Your Majesty?”","Xiao Chengjing lifted his eyes and slowly swept them over Attendant Wu’s cautious face. He did not look angry so much as disdainful.","“Half a month after you left the capital, I already knew that the Dongfang family and County Princess Linghui were doing business in smokeless coal. You took far too long to return.”","Half a month earlier, the Dongfang family’s representative, Song Jinzhao, had presented a batch of smokeless coal to the court, along with a small amount of cement.","After using them, Xiao Chengjing had not been without covetous thoughts. But by now, everyone under heaven knew that Song Jinzhao had opened shops to sell the products and make money, with the Dongfang family involved as well. He could neither openly seize them nor afford to do so.","Cold sweat trickled down from Attendant Wu’s temples. He hurriedly knocked his head against the floor and begged forgiveness.","“This servant wanted to investigate the matter thoroughly, so I stayed in Suining City for several more days. I beg Your Majesty’s pardon.”","Xiao Chengjing withdrew his gaze, too lazy to look at him, and asked languidly, “How is the situation in Suining City?”","“Is County Princess Linghui’s shop profitable?”","At the mention of this, Attendant Wu immediately brightened.","“Cement roads have been built all over Suining City. The city walls are taller and sturdier than those in the capital, though they look rather ugly and lack the capital’s majesty.”","“As for County Princess Linghui’s shop, it can be said to be operating at a loss. Smokeless coal sells for three copper coins per jin, and the profit is less than twenty percent.”","“Cement is even being used to subsidize the government offices everywhere. The yamen in neighboring counties and prefectures also purchase it at extremely low prices. Only sales to ordinary people bring in any real profit.”","“In this servant’s opinion, County Princess Linghui is using her own money and reputation to help Prefect Song build his record of achievement, hoping that he can be transferred back to the capital soon.”","Xiao Chengjing lowered his head in thought. Gu Zhongxun and Dongfang Shaoting had also said that cement and smokeless coal brought very little profit, and that Song Jinzhao had set the prices only after gritting her teeth and bearing the loss.","“To spend her own money subsidizing public works... It seems I truly did appoint the right prefect.”","The court had no money to subsidize the southwest, while Suining Prefecture was the first line of defense bordering the lands of the southwestern tribes. If its defenses were solid, he would have less to worry about.","At most, she was a woman with some talent who cared deeply for her family. That was still safer than a general in command of a powerful army.","Knowing that Attendant Wu had returned to the capital, the County Princess’s residence and the Dongfang family had kept people watching. When several days passed without the emperor taking any action, they knew the matter had blown over.","In the rear courtyard of the Ye residence, the cold wind was not as frigid as Ye Liangyu’s heart.","He drained the last of the aged Huadiao wine in his cup.","“If I had known this would happen, I never should have accepted Qiming as my disciple. Instead, I’ve only ended up dragging him down.”","The wine cup slipped onto the table. A faint smile touched the corners of Ye Liangyu’s eyes, but his gaze was filled with desolation.","In the two years since Song Qiming had left the capital, Ye Liangyu had been demoted again and again. He was now merely a seventh-rank Investigating Censor of the Palace.","Sitting across from him, Fei Yanzhang lifted his cup and tapped it against the plate piled with braised snacks.","“What do you mean, dragging him down? Without you, he couldn’t have advanced so quickly.”","“Suining is better than the capital. And now he has the protection of the Dongfang family. You can rest easy.”","After draining his cup, Fei Yanzhang ran his fingers around its rim. After a long silence, he said, “Why don’t you leave the capital and go to Suining as well? The longer you remain here, the more uneasy I feel.”","Ye Liangyu gave a bitter laugh. “I can’t go to Suining, no matter where else I might go. If I did, I’d only cause trouble for Qiming.”","He leaned back against the pillar and raised his head toward the sky.","The night was as dark as ink, without a single star.","“I’ll stay here in the capital and watch to see what kind of future awaits the kingdom of Dongzhao.”","The empty wine cups cast no reflection of the two men’s faces."]},{"number":585,"title":"Chapter 585: Earned More Than Six Million Taels in a Year","paragraphs":["Inside Prince Ying’s residence, Xiao Rongyan swept his hand across the table, knocking more than a dozen dishes to the floor.","Soup and vegetable leaves splattered everywhere. Shards of porcelain flew against his hand, staining He Shuwan’s white handkerchief red.","“Although Father has not punished me, he must still have his doubts. Otherwise, he would not have left me without a single assignment for three whole months.”","He Shuwan stepped forward and slipped her arms around Xiao Rongyan, deliberately turning the bloodstained side of the handkerchief outward.","“My prince, don’t be angry. Things are different now. There are still seven other princes in the palace. Naturally, His Majesty no longer holds you in his heart.”","Her voice was soft and melodious, yet her words struck precisely at Xiao Rongyan’s most sensitive wound.","Sure enough, his fury intensified in the next instant. He shot to his feet, his eyes wide with rage.","“It’s all that damn Song Jinzhao’s fault! If it weren’t for her, Father would never have been able to father any children. She can forget about returning to the capital in this lifetime!”","Her slender, soft arms remained looped around the back of Xiao Rongyan’s neck. She pressed her upper body against him in consolation, a smile in her eyes despite the viciousness of her words.","“The Song family is merely a minor official’s household and poses no threat. No matter how capable County Princess Linghui is, anything she creates will eventually belong to you, my prince. The most important thing now is figuring out how to eliminate the seven princes in the palace.”","Xiao Rongyan frowned, his gaze cold.","“With Father protecting them, I have no chance to make a move. The slightest mistake would make me the first person suspected. This matter will be difficult to handle.”","He Shuwan bent down and leaned close to Xiao Rongyan’s ear, whispering softly.","“If disaster caused by man won’t work, then we can use a natural disaster. I have a plan—it just depends on whether my prince is willing to try it~”","Xiao Rongyan abruptly lifted his head. “What plan?”","He Shuwan let out a light laugh, a dark glint flashing through her eyes.","...","The main doors were tightly shut. Inside the spacious front hall, which was filled with tables, abacuses clicked and clacked without pause.","One completed form after another was handed to Song Jinzhao’s desk. This was the second winter since smokeless coal had been made available for sale.","Compared with last year, the factory had doubled in size, and the number of workers had increased to nine thousand. Sales were no longer limited to the southwestern provinces. Merchants from Jiangnan, the capital, and other regions had also sent people to purchase the coal, causing sales to rise steadily.","On top of that, there was the cement business, as well as the restaurants, inns, hot pot establishments, tea shops, braised-food stores, and various other food shops opened throughout the country. Verifying the accounts was an extremely complicated task.","Twenty carefully trained accountants had spent seven days and seven nights checking the books, yet they still had not finished.","Sitting beside them, Song Anhao stared at the three account books on his own desk, then looked toward the neighboring table.","The account books there were piled as high as a mountain, almost burying his elder sister beneath them.","He clenched his teeth and made up his mind. Tomorrow, I must open several more shops. I have to catch up with Elder Sister as soon as possible.","Song Anhao propped his chin on his hand and furrowed his brows, deep in thought. What kind of business should he start? It had to be something that could bring in money quickly.","The sun began to sink in the west. Everyone hurried to finish the work in their hands before the last rays of sunlight disappeared.","The clicking of the abacuses finally stopped, and their ears could at last enjoy some peace.","“County Princess, all the accounts have been checked. There are no problems.”","Everyone withdrew, leaving only Qing Shuang and Lan Xi behind.","Song Anhao moved his chair over beside Song Jinzhao’s. Just as he leaned his face toward her, a thick stack of statistical reports blocked his view.","“You’re not allowed to use an abacus. Use the method I taught you before and calculate the total profit from these accounts within fifteen minutes.”","Song Anhao lowered his head and stared at the large figures at the bottom of the forms, each amount totaling several thousand taels. Many of the entries below were over ten thousand.","He tapped his knuckles against the desk, then silently picked up his brush and began calculating.","Song Jinzhao raised her eyes slightly. Lan Xi and Qing Shuang sat down at the same time.","When Song Anhao saw that they were going to calculate as well, he unconsciously slowed down. After finishing each step, he checked the calculation once in his head.","After the time it took to drink a cup of tea, the hands of the three people trembled as they stopped writing. Taking a deep breath, they handed their results to Song Jinzhao.","“Not bad.”","Song Jinzhao smiled faintly. The total calculated by all three of them was exactly the same: six million six hundred seventy-nine thousand four hundred twenty-six taels and three wen.","Song Anhao stared at the profit written on the paper and swallowed hard.","He murmured, “I knew it was a lot, but I never imagined it would be this much.”","He had thought his publishing house was already profitable enough. He had never expected his elder sister to own so many businesses, all of them making such enormous profits.","He did not even have a fraction of what she earned."]},{"number":586,"title":"Chapter 586: Gu Gaoyuan Was Transferred and Promoted to Vice Director of the Ministry of Works, and Song Qiming Was Promoted to Daotai","paragraphs":["\"By the mandate of Heaven, the Emperor proclaims: Gu Gaoyuan, Prefect of Songzhou, has served in this post for six full years. He has upheld integrity and prudence in his conduct, and discharged his duties with diligence and acuity, which has earned my great favor.\"","\"I hereby specially promote you to the post of Director of the Waterways Bureau under the Ministry of Works, a rank of the fifth degree, with immediate effect to proceed to the capital to take up your new office. So says the Edict!\"","The Gu family members kneeling below the stone steps lifted their heads one after another, their eyes wide with utter astonishment.","How could the Emperor transfer someone to the capital all of a sudden, without the slightest prior rumor?","Gu Huaiyuan held both hands high to receive the imperial edict.","\"Your subject bows to thank His Majesty's immense grace. Long live the Emperor, long live, long live for ten thousand years.\"","Gu Zhongxun got to his feet and quickly stopped the imperial eunuch who was about to depart, while the senior maid beside Madam Gu discreetly slipped a pouch of silver into the eunuch's hand.","\"Eunuch, why has His Majesty suddenly transferred my son to the capital?\"","The imperial eunuch smiled and tucked the silver pouch into his sleeve.","\"His Majesty takes pity on Lord Gu, the Administrative Commissioner, who has devoted decades of his life to serving the country in this harsh, remote southwestern region. That is why he has made this exceptional promotion for Director Gu, so that you may move to the capital in two years' time to retire in peace and enjoy your well-earned twilight years.\"","Gu Zhongxun maintained a stiff smile to make a few perfunctory responses, but the moment the eunuch left, his expression fell completely somber.","He turned to look at his family: the man the edict concerned, Gu Huaiyuan, wore a face that hovered between a bitter smile and sorrow; Gu Huaiyuan said not a word; Gu Baozhu bit her lip tightly; and Madam Gu's eyes were filled with undisguised worry.","As Gu Zhongxun looked over them, they all turned their gazes back to him.","When they returned to the main hall and sat down, the servants, knowing full well to keep out of private family matters, quietly closed the doors and withdrew.","\"Father is not due to retire for another two years, and now Eldest Brother is being called to the capital. Does that mean our whole family will have to split apart?\"","Gu Zhongxun, who had long since let go of any lingering ambition to become a capital official, let out a long, weary sigh.","\"Your Second Brother is the Garrison Commander of Songzhou. Military officers are notoriously difficult to transfer out of their posts. Once he leaves his current assignment, it could be three to five years before we even get a chance to see each other again.\"","Madam Gu clutched her handkerchief tightly. \"Our Gu family has no connections or standing at all in the capital. The thought of Huaiyuan going there fills me with unease.\"","Gu Huaiyuan scowled and thumped the table hard with his palm.","\"Everything was arranged perfectly. Lord Jiang was set to be transferred away, and Eldest Brother was to be promoted to Circuit Intendant. Once Father retired, we would take over the administration of the entire southwest, and our whole family could stay together. How could everything change all at once for no reason?\"","Everyone in the room turned their eyes to Gu Zhongxun. He had said earlier that he had already submitted the memorial to the throne for that appointment, so how had the official position been changed?","Madam Gu shot to her feet and swatted at Gu Zhongxun with her handkerchief, her gaze as sharp as a blade dipped in ice.","\"Was this your doing? You never managed to become a capital official yourself, so you tried to live out that ambition through your sons? How could you not see that the capital is no easy place to make a living? To serve the Emperor is to live beside a tiger!\"","Gu Zhongxun hastily ducked his head and cried out in his own defense.","\"You wrong me, my dear! The memorial I submitted was for the Circuit Intendant post. I would never have dared to even dream of having Huaiyuan transferred to the capital.\"","He had struggled for decades without ever securing a capital posting, and he had long since stopped holding out high hopes for his two sons, who had always relied on his protection for their positions.","Gu Congwen, who had rushed back from the academy specially to be present for the edict ceremony, wore a confused frown.","\"But if Eldest Father cannot become Circuit Intendant, then who will take that post instead? Or does that mean Lord Jiang is staying on in his current position?\"","Those words plunged the whole room into silence. Gu Zhongxun knitted his brows in utter bewilderment.","\"I have no idea either.\"","The situation had strayed so far beyond his expectations that Gu Zhongxun even began to wonder if his title as the Administrative Commissioner of the southwest was nothing but an empty honor. Otherwise, how could he not have known that his own son, the Prefect of Songzhou, was about to be transferred away?","Half an hour later, at the Jiang Manor.","Jiang Roulan blinked, her eyebrows lifting in surprise.","\"Everyone said that after Lord Jiang was transferred away, Prefect Gu would be promoted to Circuit Intendant. How has he ended up being transferred to the capital instead?\"","While the post of Capital Director held the same official rank as a prefect, moving from a regional post to a capital appointment was strictly speaking, considered a form of special promotion.","Jiang Roulan's father sat in his chair, frowning in deep thought.","Gu Zhongxun was due to retire in two years. If the Emperor was moving Gu Huaiyuan to the capital now, did that mean His Majesty did not want the Gu family to hold the position of Administrative Commissioner of the southwest for another term?","Meanwhile, at the Ning Sui city yamen.","Song Qiming was still holding the imperial edict in his hands, too stunned to collect his thoughts.","He had only served as the Prefect of Sui Ning for two years, and now he was being promoted?","\"The Yukun family must have been working nonstop behind the scenes to pull strings. The Emperor even went out of his way to praise Eldest Sister in the text of the edict.\"","Song Jinzhao took the edict and unfolded it, a look of sharp irony curling at the corners of his mouth, along with open disdain for the Emperor's self-serving scheming.","\" 'Using personal wealth to support his brother, crafting tools and innovations to build up the city.' The Emperor clearly intends for the two of us to take charge of running the entire provincial administration of the southwest.\""]},{"number":587,"title":"Chapter 587: Building a House and Creating a Secret Passage","paragraphs":["When he received the news, Gu Zhongxun shook his head with a bitter smile, his eyes full of mockery.","“Two imperial edicts issued at the same time, without even notifying me. I’m truly a failure as their superior.”","Gu Huaiyuan rested his chin on one hand, his face filled with curiosity.","“I originally thought Song Qiming would be transferred back to the capital after serving as prefect for three years. Who could have expected him to become a circuit intendant after only two? Will he still return to the capital next year?”","Gu Huaiyuan shot him a look that clearly said, “Are you an idiot?”","“He definitely won’t be able to return within a year or two. Why do I feel that His Majesty intends for him to remain in the southwest for a long time?”","Gu Zhongxun’s heart felt as though it had been pricked by a needle.","“His Majesty truly favors and trusts Song Qiming.”","He had never seen a young official promoted so quickly. Song Qiming had only just come of age, yet he was already a fourth-rank circuit intendant—a position most officials could never reach in their entire lives.","Even Gu Zhongxun himself had not become a circuit intendant until he was in his early forties. He had served in that post for three years before being promoted to Provincial Administration Commissioner of the Southwest.","Gu Zhongxun let out a long sigh.","“Two years from now, I’ll retire. There’s an eighty percent chance that Song Qiming will take over as Provincial Administration Commissioner of the Southwest.”","The thought of the southwest province he had governed for so many years falling into the hands of an outsider left Gu Zhongxun deeply unsettled.","The oppressive atmosphere in the residence made Gu Baozhu completely forget how much she had once looked forward to the Song family moving to Songzhou City.","She stood in the courtyard of the main branch, watching the servants pack their belongings, her heart heavy with sorrow.","Gu Congwen came out of the study. Seeing the melancholy on her face, he forced a smile and walked over.","“Don’t be sad, Auntie. Even though the capital is over a thousand miles from Songzhou, you can still come back whenever you want.”","Gu Baozhu lowered her eyes, hiding the moisture gathering at their corners.","“I just feel a little reluctant to see you all leave so suddenly.”","Gu Congwen bent down and stared at her face.","“If you really can’t bear it, urge Second Uncle to have himself transferred to the capital too. Or he could give up the military and take up civil office.”","Gu Baozhu pressed her lips together, unable to suppress a smile.","“Give up the military for civil office? You might as well say he should resign.” The court had never transferred military officers stationed in the southwest. The only exception was when they died in battle and their bodies were carried home.","While the Gu residence was busy packing, the Song family was doing the same.","Shi Simian followed along, unable to keep the corners of his mouth from lifting.","He had never imagined that he would still be promoted at his age. Suining Prefecture truly was a blessed place.","“County Princess, this residence is close to the outer city, so it’s convenient to come and go. The only problem is that it’s a little expensive.”","All the vacant plots in the inner city had been sold at the previous auction. The larger residences were already privately owned, and their prices had risen by a full hundred percent compared with two years earlier.","After walking around the residence once, Song Jinzhao shook her head.","“It’s too small. Is there anything larger?”","Qing Shuang looked troubled.","“This is already the largest one.”","Although the family of four would be moving to Songzhou City, the coal and cement factories were still here. They would inevitably need to return often, so they had to maintain a place to stay.","As she surveyed the surroundings, an idea suddenly occurred to Song Jinzhao.","“Then let’s look outside the inner city. Are there any suitable properties in the outer city?”","Qing Shuang thought for a moment before replying, “The outer city consists entirely of households with one residence and one plot of land. I’ll have someone make inquiries and see whether anyone is willing to sell.”","“It would be best if the properties were near the outer city wall. If seven or eight houses next to one another are willing to sell, we can offer a higher price.”","Qing Shuang nodded and immediately sent someone to make inquiries.","Less than three days later, Qing Shuang arrived with the land deeds.","“Eight households in total, with twelve mu of land altogether. All the paperwork has been completed, and they can all move out within three days.”","Song Jinzhao took the deeds and drew a large circle on the map of Suining City.","The area was close to the outer city wall, with the only river channel nearby. A secret underground passage out of the city could be built there.","“Have our own people arrange the craftsmen. Don’t let outsiders get involved.”"]},{"number":588,"title":"Chapter 588: Cui Zhengyang Arrives in Songzhou City","paragraphs":["The sun was shining brightly on the day the Song family arrived in Songzhou City. After half a month of adjustment, Gu Baozhu’s spirits had more or less recovered.","As the familiar carriage gradually drew near, the corners of her lips lifted into a faint smile.","The residence Song Jinzhao had purchased in Songzhou City stood behind the government offices, barely half an hour’s walk from the Gu residence.","Song Shixue lifted the carriage curtain. When she saw Gu Baozhu standing at the entrance, she broke into a delighted smile.","“Baozhu.”","Gu Baozhu descended the steps and gave Song Jinzhao a slight curtsy.","“Greetings, County Princess.”","“There’s no need for formalities. Spring hasn’t even begun, yet you’re dressed so lightly. Aren’t you cold?”","Gu Baozhu smiled and shook her head. “I was practicing martial arts at home just now, so I’m still warm.”","After they entered through the main gate, Gu Baozhu and Song Shixue, who were walking behind the others, held hands and whispered to each other.","“I was planning to go to Suining City to see you after spring began. I didn’t expect you to arrive in Songzhou City before I could.”","Song Shixue looped her arm through hers.","“The imperial edict came far too suddenly. Even my brother was caught off guard.”","A trace of surprise flashed through Gu Baozhu’s eyes.","“Neither the County Princess nor Lord Song knew beforehand that he was being promoted to circuit intendant?”","Song Shixue gently shook her head. “There’s supposed to be a transfer every three years, but my brother has only served for two.”","After glancing around, she covered her mouth with one hand. Her voice was so soft that only Gu Baozhu could hear her.","“The edict said, ‘Provide financial support to aid your younger brother and manufacture equipment to develop the city.’ When my sister heard it, her face turned black with fury. She said the emperor had no shame—subsidizing one Suining Prefecture wasn’t enough for him, and now he wanted her to use her private fortune to support the entire southwestern province.”","Gu Baozhu’s eyes went blank. Once she understood, she looked up at Song Jinzhao, who was walking at the very front, then shifted her gaze to Song Qiming’s face and fell silent.","So this was what the emperor meant by “provide financial support to aid your younger brother and manufacture equipment to develop the city”—he had transferred Song Qiming to Songzhou City for precisely this purpose?","That was shameless beyond belief.","Half a month later.","“Brother Cui, how did it end up being you?”","Song Qiming stared at Cui Zhengyang in disbelief. He never would have imagined that the new magistrate of Songzhou City would be him.","With the Cui family’s reputation in Jiangnan and its connections at court, there was no reason for him to come all the way to the southwest.","Cui Zhengyang gave a low laugh, bitterness filling his eyes.","“That’s a long story.”","After entering, Gu Zhongxun noticed how familiar the two men were, and his mood soured even further.","They were already starting to build connections, and he hadn’t even left yet.","“The emperor’s transfer order came suddenly. The former magistrate of Songzhou City entered the capital more than a month ago. Lord Min will hand over all official matters to you.”","One newcomer had a more impressive background than the next. When had the southwest, once shunned by everyone, become such a coveted destination for the sons of wealthy and powerful families?","Cui Zhengyang stood before Gu Zhongxun, the sunlight streaming in through the doorway stretching his shadow long across the floor.","“On my way here, I happened to run into Lord Gu. We also discussed some matters concerning Songzhou City.”","Before setting out, Cui Zhengyang had already made inquiries about the situation in the southwest, especially the latest news regarding the Gu family’s father and sons.","At the mention of his eldest son, Gu Zhongxun’s expression finally softened a little.","“It was fate that you crossed paths with Gaoyuan.”","“Qiming, take him around the government offices and show him the ropes.”","Song Qiming cupped his hands and nodded. “I obey, Lord Gu.”","Watching Gu Zhongxun’s dejected back as he walked away, Cui Zhengyang turned to Song Qiming in confusion.","“His son has just been promoted, yet why do I feel that Lord Gu isn’t happy? His attitude toward me is rather cold as well, as if he’s harboring some resentment.”","After half a month in office, Song Qiming had already grasped nine-tenths of Gu Zhongxun’s temperament.","“Gu Zhongxun wants Gu Huaiyuan to take over as the provincial administration commissioner of the southwest. As for you, you were probably dragged into this because of me.”","Cui Zhengyang immediately understood. He tilted his head back, his face filled with disapproval.","“The position of provincial administration commissioner isn’t hereditary. Where did he get that confidence?”","Song Qiming shrugged. “Perhaps because no one holding a high-ranking office is willing to come to the southwest.”","He caught hold of Cui Zhengyang’s arm and led him into his office.","“Now hurry up and tell me what really happened.”"]},{"number":589,"title":"Chapter 589: Madam Gu Took a Fancy to Cui Zhengyang","paragraphs":["In a room occupied by only the two of them, Cui Zhengyang could not stop sighing after explaining the whole story.","“When all is said and done, His Majesty still harbors reservations about my Cui family. Otherwise, he would not have singled me out.”","Song Qiming’s face darkened, and he slammed his fist against the armrest of the chair.","“Who would have thought that the ocean-going sailboat my elder sister devised would ultimately benefit the Kingdom of Shuobei?”","The preliminary development of the sailboat had been complicated and costly, yet the Kingdom of Shuobei had simply taken advantage of the finished product. How could that not make one angry?","Cui Zhengyang lowered his gaze to the floor. “And it’s not just the ocean-going sailboats. The potatoes are the same. The Kingdom of Shuobei’s yield this year is considerably higher than last year’s.”","“One thing after another. Even Minister Ou had lost all heart by the time I left the capital.”","As he spoke, a smile tugged at his lips. “Still, knowing that you’re here in Songzhou makes me feel somewhat better.”","“I heard that the southwest has changed tremendously over the past two years. I was astonished myself when I entered the city.”","Song Qiming grinned. “If you ever go to Suining, then you’ll know what it really means for a place to undergo a complete transformation.”","Gu Zhongxun returned to his residence with a deeply troubled expression, only to find his wife looking rather pleased.","The moment she saw him, Madam Gu hurried over.","“Is Cui Zhengyang truly as handsome as the rumors say?”","Gu Zhongxun’s brows drooped. Not only did his expression turn sour, but his chest began to feel tight as well.","“He’s nothing special.”","Seeing his perfunctory attitude, Madam Gu pouted and sat down.","“What’s done is done. Stop dwelling on it and start thinking about Baozhu’s marriage.”","“Before, we thought there were very few promising young men in the Southwest worthy of our daughter. But now that Gaoyuan has been transferred to the capital, our choices aren’t limited to the Southwest anymore.”","“I think Cui Zhengyang and Song Qiming would both be excellent choices. Whether they remain in the Southwest or are later transferred to the capital, Baozhu will always have a home to return to.”","At that, Gu Zhongxun’s eyes widened until they looked like a bull’s.","“Song Qiming? How did you come up with him?”","The smile at the corners of Madam Gu’s mouth faded.","“Song Qiming is about the same age as Baozhu, and he’s accomplished. Baozhu is also close friends with Second Miss Song. Why can’t I consider him?”","“I didn’t think of him before because I knew they would eventually return to the capital, and I didn’t want Baozhu marrying too far away. But things are different now.”","The thought of Song Qiming becoming his son-in-law filled Gu Zhongxun with resistance.","He immediately shook his head and objected, hastily coming up with an excuse.","“No. If County Princess Linghui doesn’t marry out, wouldn’t she spend the rest of her life lording it over our Baozhu? Absolutely not.”","Madam Gu said, “Then there’s Lord Cui. I’ll go take a look at him tomorrow.”","Gu Zhongxun was so furious that he could neither vent nor swallow his anger. His cheeks puffed out like a pufferfish.","Just outside the door, Gu Baozhu had returned home. Her eyes were lowered, and her arms were folded across her chest.","It had only been six peaceful months, and they were already pressuring her to marry again. How annoying.","She returned to her room and sat down. Seeing that she was unhappy, her maid tried to console her.","“I’ve heard that Lord Cui comes from a prestigious family. He placed second in the palace examination at a very young age, and he’s said to be one of the most handsome men in all of Dongzhao. Why not give him some consideration, Miss?”","Her personal maid knew her mistress’s thoughts better than anyone, but she also did not want her to miss out on such a fine match.","Gu Baozhu sprawled across the couch and stared blankly at the red-lacquered beams overhead.","“Prestigious families have the most rules. The Cui family has been a scholarly clan for generations, so if I married into it, I probably wouldn’t even be allowed to go out often. What difference would that be from being in prison?”","The maid fell silent, unable to argue. The Cui family was a renowned family of scholars, and their ancestors had all been officials. They certainly had plenty of tedious rituals and formalities, and their temperament truly did not suit Miss Gu.","Gu Baozhu rolled over and buried her head in the bedding. Before long, she fell asleep while thinking about it.","The next time she encountered Song Qiming, she remembered what Madam Gu had said. Her gaze shifted from that of a friend looking at her older brother to that of a woman looking at a man.","From his hair crown down to his shoes, everything about him was first-rate: his looks, his character, and his family background. His younger sister was her closest friend, and the only elder in his household was County Princess Linghui. No one would restrict her or forbid her from going out. In every respect, he was an excellent choice.","There was just one problem—he seemed to have no romantic feelings for her whatsoever.","Song Qiming, dressed in his official robes, felt his scalp prickle under Gu Baozhu’s scrutiny.","He spread his arms and looked himself over. “Is there something wrong with my clothes today?”","Gu Baozhu glanced away, looking slightly embarrassed. “Nothing’s wrong. I just suddenly realized that this official robe suits you particularly well, Lord Song. You look much more spirited than usual.”","Song Qiming blinked, and two blushes appeared on his cheeks.","“I have something to do, so I’ll be going first.”","His footsteps were more hurried than usual."]},{"number":590,"title":"Chapter 590: Gu Baozhu Has Her Eyes on Song Qiming","paragraphs":["Song Shixue stood beside her, staring at Gu Baozhu in astonishment. She waited until Song Qiming had disappeared from sight before speaking.","“Baozhu, why do I feel like you’re acting a little strange today?”","In the past, Gu Baozhu had never said more than a few words to her brother, much less praised his clothes and appearance.","Besides, he wore this official robe every day. It wasn’t as though this was the first time Baozhu had seen him in it.","Gu Baozhu bit her lip, struggling with herself for a long while before slipping her arm through Song Shixue’s and whispering, “My mother wants me to meet another prospective husband. She has her eye on Cui Zhengyang, the prefect of Songzhou. The Cui family has so many rules. After thinking it over, I feel that your brother might not be so bad.”","Song Shixue’s almond-shaped eyes widened, and she blurted out, “You’ve taken a fancy to my—”","Gu Baozhu swiftly covered her mouth, preventing her from finishing the sentence.","“Keep your voice down. This is just something I’m considering.”","Once her mouth was uncovered, Song Shixue still hadn’t recovered from the shock.","She had never imagined that her best friend would take an interest in her brother. The two of them were hardly close at all; they could barely exchange a few words whenever they stood together.","“Are you sure? Do you actually like him, or are you just choosing him because you have no other option?”","Gu Baozhu pondered for a moment. “I simply feel that we’d be a good match. After taking a careful look at him just now, I suddenly realized that your brother really is quite outstanding.”","Song Shixue’s lips opened and closed, but for a moment she had no idea how to respond.","Seeing her friend fall silent, Gu Baozhu smiled and linked arms with her as they walked forward.","“Let’s not rush this. Weren’t we supposed to look at some storefronts today? Come on.”","They went from one shop to another, and once they became busy, Song Shixue gradually put the matter out of her mind. But after returning home and settling into the quiet, she couldn’t help thinking about it again.","“Lotus Leaf, do you think Baozhu and my brother would make a good match?”","After thinking it over, the maid, Lotus Leaf, counted off her points on her fingers. “Their family backgrounds are well matched, and they’re a handsome man and a beautiful woman. Miss Gu is close with the family, so there shouldn’t be any conflict between her and her sisters-in-law in the future. The Eldest Young Master doesn’t seem to dislike her either. This servant thinks they’re fairly well suited.”","Song Shixue drew her brows together.","“Not disliking someone doesn’t mean he likes her. They’ve known each other for so long, and I’ve never seen any sign that my brother feels that way.”","Lotus Leaf said, “This servant thinks the Eldest Young Master simply hasn’t realized his own feelings yet.”","Most ordinary men were already engaged and preparing for marriage by the time they came of age. The three young masters of the household were the exceptions.","After learning that Gu Baozhu had feelings for her brother, Song Shixue began observing him carefully whenever they happened to cross paths.","Their conversations grew from a few words to more than a dozen, and his expressions became far more animated. He always wore a smile.","After this happened several times, even Song Qiming noticed something was off. That evening, after Song Shixue returned from the newly opened medical clinic, he sought her out to ask about it.","“Has Miss Gu taken a fancy to me?”","“Clatter.”","The cup slipped from Song Shixue’s hand and fell onto the table, splashing water all over her.","Seeing her reaction, Song Qiming became even more certain of his guess. He simply couldn’t understand why.","If it was love, then she should have fallen for him at first sight. And if it was affection that had grown over time, he and Gu Baozhu had hardly spent any time together.","Song Shixue handed the tea-soaked handkerchief to Lotus Leaf, her lashes lifting slightly.","Lotus Leaf took the handkerchief and turned to leave, closing the door behind her.","Only after they were alone did Song Shixue explain.","“Madam Gu believes Baozhu has reached the age to marry. She’s been urging her to meet prospective husbands for the past two years, and this time she set her sights on Lord Cui.”","“Baozhu thinks Lord Cui comes from a scholarly family, so there are bound to be many rules in his household. She wouldn’t have as much freedom there as she does at home.”","Song Qiming pointed at himself. “So she chose me?”","Song Shixue nodded firmly.","“At first, she only thought you were suitable. But the more she observed you, the more she felt that you were a good choice. She wanted to get closer to you first, so she wouldn’t risk bringing it up abruptly and being rejected.”","Recalling how Gu Baozhu had tried to find any excuse she could to strike up a conversation whenever they met, Song Qiming couldn’t help finding it amusing.","But when Song Shixue saw that his smile didn’t look particularly pleased, she asked softly, “Brother, do you have feelings for Baozhu?”","Song Qiming lowered his eyes to look at her. After a moment, he shook his head helplessly.","“Marriage between a man and a woman isn’t something we can decide entirely on our own. We’ll still have to see what our older sister thinks.”","Song Shixue’s eyes widened. “So if our sister agrees, you’ll marry her?”","“...”","Song Qiming turned his head away and left. The moment he stepped outside, every trace of expression vanished from his face."]},{"number":591,"title":"Chapter 591: I Want to Marry Miss Gu as My Wife","paragraphs":["“Elder Sister.” Song Qiming slowly pushed open the door to Song Jinzhao’s study.","After ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​​​‍purchasing all the coal mines in the southwest—in fact, throughout the entire Dongzhao Kingdom—Song Jinzhao had been busy setting up branch factories ever since moving to Songzhou City.","“What is it?” Song Jinzhao lifted her head from the mountain of pressing affairs before her.","Song Qiming raised a hand, signaling the maid in the room to leave. He then walked over and sat down in the chair opposite Song Jinzhao.","“Elder Sister, I want to marry Gu Baozhu.”","A drop of ink fell onto the account book, blurring the number Song Jinzhao had just written into a black blot.","“You like her?”","Song Qiming was silent for a moment. Then he shook his head, only to nod a moment later.","“I can’t really say whether I like her or not. The Gu family is eager to arrange Miss Gu’s marriage. Madam Gu has taken a fancy to Brother Cui, but Miss Gu isn’t willing. She, on the other hand, has taken a liking to me. She thinks marrying into the Song family would give her more freedom, without too many rules to follow.”","Song Jinzhao set her writing brush aside, her expression turning solemn.","“And you? Why do you want to marry her?”","Song Qiming clenched his teeth. After hesitating briefly, he straightened his chest.","He said with utmost seriousness, “Since being transferred to Songzhou City, I’ve increasingly come to realize that Gu Zhongxun’s influence runs deep throughout the southwest. Whether it’s me or Brother Cui, nothing we try to do goes smoothly without Gu Zhongxun’s approval. Gu Baozhu is the Gu family’s only daughter and the apple of Gu Zhongxun’s eye. As long as I marry her, Gu Zhongxun won’t deliberately make things difficult for me, and I’ll also gain the Gu family’s support.”","His resounding words left Song Jinzhao feeling faintly stifled.","“Marriage is a lifelong matter for both man and woman. Getting married isn’t simply a matter of bringing a wife home and leaving her there. You’ll need to support each other through the decades ahead, until your hair turns white and death finally parts you, never abandoning one another.”","“My next words must be understood clearly. The Song family has no practice of taking a second wife or keeping concubines. Even if your future wife cannot bear children, you may not take a concubine or keep a mistress. If you wish to divorce, both parties must agree willingly. If you marry Gu Baozhu with nothing but the intention of gaining the Gu family’s support, and the two of you end up unable to get along, then unless she is the one to ask for a divorce, you’ll have to put on the appearance of a good husband—even if you have to pretend—and treat her well for the rest of her life.”","Song Qiming froze. He had never imagined that his unmarried elder sister, whom he had been raised by, would speak so sternly about marriage.","It sounded as though she were speaking of herself, and yet also warning him.","Beneath the table, the hands resting on his thighs tightened into fists, his palms growing hot.","After meeting Song Jinzhao’s eyes for a moment, his expression became solemn.","“Once I marry Miss Gu, I will respect and protect her for the rest of our lives. We will share both prosperity and hardship, and I will never abandon her.”","As he spoke, he raised three fingers toward the heavens.","“I swear to Elder Sister that after marrying Miss Gu, even if we never have children, I will never take a concubine. Even if she should sadly pass away before me, I will never marry another woman. I am willing to mourn her for the rest of my life.”","Song Jinzhao’s pupils widened slightly. Although she had raised Song Qiming herself, she had never expected him to agree so readily—much less promise never to marry again should his wife die.","A suspicion arose in her heart, and she could not help asking, “Are you truly without the slightest fondness for Miss Gu?”","Song Qiming blinked.","“I just think Miss Gu has a cheerful personality and suits our family well. Shixue is close to her too, so bringing her into the family would surely make everyone happy.”","Song Jinzhao drew a deep breath.","“A marriage between two people without affection is unlikely to last. Most such couples eventually grow sick of the sight of each other. You and Miss Gu never had any thoughts in that regard before, but now that you’re both considering it, spend more time talking and see whether your temperaments and interests are compatible. And remember, whenever you go out, you must bring Shixue and the Gu family’s second son with you. Don’t damage the young lady’s reputation.”","“There’s one more thing. You just said Lord Gu has objections to you.”","“Marriage is arranged by the parents and sanctioned by the matchmaker. If Lord Gu is unwilling to marry his daughter to you, then even if you and Miss Gu are both in agreement, the matter cannot be settled.”","Song Qiming rose and cupped his hands seriously toward Song Jinzhao. “If I truly intend to marry her, I will naturally obtain Lord Gu and Madam Gu’s consent. When the time comes, I’ll have to trouble Elder Sister to personally go to their residence and propose the match.”","Gu Zhongxun held the rank of Senior Second Grade. Only Song Jinzhao, a County Princess, was noble enough to personally visit the Gu residence and make the proposal.","Song Jinzhao waved her hand, signaling that he could leave.","“This matter isn’t urgent. Do as I’ve instructed first. Don’t wait until after the wedding to regret it. Come back and tell me your final decision in two months.”"]},{"number":592,"title":"Chapter 592: The Answer","paragraphs":["After Song Qiming left the room, Song Jinzhao stood by the window, gazing at the moon in thought. He did not return to his room to rest until the candle had burned out.","Gu Zhongxun was pressed repeatedly by Madam Gu, and in the end, he had no choice but to seek Cui Zhengyang out for information.","At the drinking table, he casually asked, “I hear that Lord Cui is already of such an age and still unmarried. May I ask whether you have someone in mind?”","His question immediately drew the attention of every official at the table. They all stared at Cui Zhengyang, eager to know whether he had someone he loved—and even more eager to see what Gu Zhongxun was trying to do.","Song Qiming, seated beside Cui Zhengyang, lowered his eyes and said nothing. A smile curved his lips, but his eyes remained indifferent.","The Gu family had indeed taken a liking to Cui Zhengyang. Unfortunately, they had come too late.","Cui Zhengyang set down his wine cup and laughed heartily.","Without avoiding the question, he said, “Before I came to Songzhou City, my father had already arranged a marriage for me. I need only return to Jiangnan during the New Year to be wed.”","The smile at the corners of Gu Zhongxun’s mouth stiffened, and he lowered his eyes in disappointment.","“I see. It seems I won’t be able to attend the wedding feast after all.”","Cui Zhengyang rose with a cup full of wine and toasted Gu Zhongxun.","“Once I return from Jiangnan, I will certainly host a feast at Ruyi House and invite all the gentlemen to celebrate with me.”","“He’s already betrothed...” The son-in-law she had set her sights on was taken, and Madam Gu frowned unhappily.","Gu Zhongxun removed his outer robe and placed it on the coat rack. “His fiancée comes from a prominent family in Jiangnan. Her family and the Cui family have been friends for generations.”","Madam Gu sank down onto the couch and sighed. “There are so many fine young men, and all of them are fighting to marry someone. I wonder where my Baozhu’s destined husband is~”","On their day off, they once again visited the sea of flowers in the Stone Forest. This time, no tactless people came over to curry favor, and Gu Baozhu was in an excellent mood as she strolled about.","She secretly stole a glance at Song Qiming, who was walking beside her. Gu Baozhu bit her lip, her pearly teeth staining a faint crimson.","She raised her eyes, wanting to get a clear look at his face, but their gazes unexpectedly met. Startled, she hurriedly looked away.","Gu Baozhu covered her heart. She had never felt it beat so quickly before. In the past, meeting Song Qiming had never made her feel this way.","“Here.”","Song Qiming held out the roasted chicken wing she liked.","Gu Baozhu’s fingertips trembled. Her ears flushed red as she accepted it and murmured her thanks.","“Thank you.”","Her soft voice fell upon Song Qiming’s heart like a feather brushing against it, stirring a sweet restlessness.","The exchange of glances and every small movement between them did not escape the notice of Song Shixue and Gu Jinghong.","One of them felt guilty, as though he were trying to coax someone else’s precious daughter into coming home with him, and shifted his gaze away.","The other watched with keen interest, sizing Song Qiming up from head to toe several times before finally admitting to himself that his little aunt’s choice was not bad at all.","They were a young man and a young woman in the first flush of love. Once they began spending time together with the idea that the other might become their future spouse, their feelings took wing after only three meetings and warmed rapidly.","On the way home after their fourth meeting, Gu Jinghong said with a smile, “Shouldn’t the Song family be coming to ask for her hand soon?”","Their mutual interest was obvious after several meetings. It was indeed time for the Song family to formally propose marriage.","Gu Baozhu pressed her lips together, a shy smile blooming across her face.","She quickened her pace and left Gu Jinghong behind. “How would I know?”","That afternoon, just after Song Jinzhao returned from outside, Song Qiming blocked his path.","“Have you made up your mind?” Song Shixue had reported every detail of their four outings over the past two months to Song Jinzhao each time she returned.","Seeing the barely concealed eagerness on Song Qiming’s face now, Song Jinzhao already agreed with the match in his heart.","Song Qiming nodded firmly, his gaze resolute.","“I’ve decided. I want to marry her.”","Song ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​​​‍Jinzhao lowered his eyes and agreed. “Tomorrow, I’ll go to the Gu residence first and sound out Madam Gu.”","“Good,” said Song Qiming."]},{"number":593,"title":"Chapter 593: Song Jinzhao Visits to Discuss Marriage","paragraphs":["At dawn, just as the sun peeked over the eastern horizon, the Song residence sprang into action.","At Song Jinzhao’s request, Steward Chunxing prepared the gifts for their visit. Half an hour after breakfast, Song Jinzhao set out. Her carriage stopped outside the Gu residence.","When ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​​​‍the gatekeeper saw Song Jinzhao step down from the carriage, he hurried inside and told a maid to deliver the news.","Before Song Jinzhao had even taken her seat in the front hall, Madam Gu arrived with her second daughter-in-law.","“County Princess Linghui, I apologize for keeping you waiting. This humble wife begs your forgiveness.”","Song Jinzhao smiled graciously. “I came without notice, Madam Gu. How could you possibly be at fault?”","The two women sat facing each other in the seats of honor, while tea and pastries were promptly placed within Song Jinzhao’s reach.","Under the watchful eyes of Madam Gu and Second Mistress Gu, Song Jinzhao lifted her teacup and took a leisurely sip.","Second Mistress Gu cast a puzzled glance at Madam Gu: What could the County Princess possibly want by coming here?","Madam Gu returned the look: How should I know?","Catching the mother-in-law and daughter-in-law exchanging meaningful glances from the corner of her eye, Song Jinzhao curved her lips and put on an aggrieved expression.","“To be honest, Madam Gu, I’ve come today to ask you for a favor.”","Second Mistress Gu’s heart, which had been lodged in her throat, finally settled back into place.","So the County Princess needed their help. Her expression immediately relaxed.","Madam Gu asked, “What is it?”","Song Jinzhao pressed a hand to her brow, looking troubled. “My younger brother has reached twenty this year, and I’ve begun to worry about his marriage.”","“As you know, our family has only recently arrived in Songzhou City, so we know very little about the unmarried young ladies of the various households. We thought we might come and ask you about them.”","Madam Gu raised her brows in surprise. “The County Princess wishes to arrange a marriage for Lord Song?”","County Princess Linghui and Second Miss Song were both of marriageable age and still unmarried. She had assumed Song Qiming would follow the same path.","Song Jinzhao gave a slight nod. “Our parents passed away when we were young, so I have no choice but to concern myself with Qiming’s marriage as his elder sister.”","As she spoke, her eyes shifted, as though she had suddenly thought of something.","“Come to think of it, Baozhu hasn’t been betrothed yet either. Madam Gu, aren’t you worried?”","Madam Gu’s expression stiffened. Staring at Song Jinzhao’s face, she grumbled inwardly.","Wasn’t it all because of the Song family? None of their children had married despite reaching the proper age. They had even claimed that having children in one’s teens was bad for the body and could easily lead to a difficult delivery. Otherwise, her own Baozhu would never have become so resistant to marriage.","“Our family has only one daughter, and her father and I are reluctant to marry her off too soon. We’d like to keep her with us for a few more years.”","Song Jinzhao’s voice rose slightly as she spoke almost casually.","“Speaking of which, Baozhu and Qiming aren’t far apart in age. If you’re willing, perhaps we could let them meet and see whether they might suit each other?”","“...”","Second Mistress Gu, who had been sitting below and enjoying the spectacle, instantly tensed.","How had the conversation suddenly turned to her sister-in-law?","An alliance with the Song family? Surely they couldn’t be serious.","Her father-in-law had never liked Song Qiming and would absolutely never agree to marry his daughter to him.","Madam Gu had once entertained the same thought, only to have Gu Zhongxun put a stop to it. Hearing Song Jinzhao make the suggestion now, however, brought the idea rushing back.","Seeing that the smile in Song Jinzhao’s eyes never faded, as though she were eagerly awaiting her reply, Madam Gu understood at once.","This was no visit to ask about eligible young ladies in Songzhou City. The County Princess had come specifically for her daughter.","Thinking of Song Qiming’s excellence, Baozhu’s close friendship with Second Miss Song, and the fact that Song Jinzhao had personally come to persuade her, Madam Gu desperately wanted to agree at once and let the two young people meet. But when she remembered her husband’s dislike of Song Qiming, she hesitated.","After pondering for a moment, she smiled and replied, “My husband treasures Baozhu above all else. I’ll have to discuss this with him first.”","Song Jinzhao had anticipated that answer. She curved her lips into a smile. “Then I’ll await Madam Gu’s news.”","After seeing her guests out of the residence, Madam Gu returned to the front hall. Looking at the chest of carefully selected gifts, she felt both delighted and conflicted.","“Second Mistress, what do you think I should say to persuade your father-in-law?”","Seeing the radiant smile on her mother-in-law’s face, Second Mistress Gu knew that Madam Gu was very pleased with Song Qiming.","“Mother, perhaps you should ask Baozhu first.”","“If she has no interest in Lord Song, then there’s no need to ask Father at all. But if she does like him, persuading Father will be twice as easy.”","Madam Gu’s eyes curved into happy crescents. She slapped her thigh excitedly.","“You’re right. I’ll go ask her now.”"]},{"number":594,"title":"Chapter 594: Mrs. Gu Shocked: It Was Her Daughter Who Was Interested in Song Qiming First","paragraphs":["Gu Baozhu had known for some time that Song Jinzhao had arrived, and she had remained in her room waiting while the maid relayed everything happening in the front hall.","“Miss, Madam is here.” The maid hurried into the room, supporting herself with one hand against the table as she panted for breath.","Gu Baozhu hurriedly sat down on the couch and picked up a storybook, pretending to read while actually straining her ears to listen to the sounds outside.","A shadow fell into the room. Gu Baozhu raised her head and called out as usual, “Mother.”","Madam Gu had not even sat down when curiosity arose in her heart.","“Usually, whenever County Princess Linghui visits, you’re the first one to run out and welcome her. Why didn’t you go out today?”","Gu Baozhu’s eyes darted about. She lifted her chin and pretended that her neck was sore from reading for too long.","“I went out with Shixue yesterday and saw County Princess Linghui then, so I didn’t feel the need to see her today.”","Madam Gu let out a heavy breath and sat down opposite her daughter.","“You’re quite close to the Second Miss Song. You must have seen Song Qiming many times. What do you think of him?”","Gu Baozhu clenched her teeth, forcing down the corners of her mouth that wanted to turn upward.","“Song Qiming is handsome and refined, with a gentle and warm manner. He doesn’t put on the airs of an official and is very easy to get along with.”","“He has an excellent memory, is learned in every field, and possesses beautiful calligraphy.”","Madam Gu’s brows lifted as she quietly stared at Gu Baozhu.","“He also cares for his younger siblings and respects his elder sister. In all my interactions with him, I’ve found him considerate, proper, and well-mannered. He has excellent character.”","The ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌‍handkerchief in Madam Gu’s hand tightened and tightened until she suddenly interrupted her daughter.","“I never realized you knew Song Qiming so well!”","The smile on Gu Baozhu’s face froze. Realizing that she had said too much, she hurriedly came up with an excuse.","“Shixue told me all of that.”","A mother knew her daughter best. Studying the expression on Gu Baozhu’s face, Madam Gu’s mind filled with a bold conjecture.","She held her breath and asked sternly, “Did you already know that County Princess Linghui would be visiting today?”","Gu Baozhu clenched her teeth, unable to suppress the unease rising in her heart.","After a long silence, she raised her head and met Madam Gu’s eyes. Stray strands of hair fell across her forehead, partially veiling her gaze.","“I knew.”","Madam Gu shot to her feet. “Then did you also know that she wanted you to meet Song Qiming with marriage in mind?”","Gu Baozhu gave a small nod. “I knew that too. I was the one who had my eye on Song Qiming first.”","Madam Gu’s eyes widened. “What did you say?”","Gu Baozhu gritted her teeth and told her mother everything she had done.","“When I heard you say that you wanted me to meet Cui Zhengyang, I didn’t want to marry into the Cui family and live under so many rules, so I thought of Song Qiming.”","“The Song family does things in their own free-spirited way, and I like spending time with them. After meeting Song Qiming several times, I realized that he was a good man. I was willing to consider the proposal, so I suppose you could say I had already given my tacit approval.”","Madam Gu felt dizzy, as if the sky itself had collapsed.","“Do you know that your father doesn’t like Song Qiming?”","This time, Gu Baozhu did not avoid her mother’s gaze.","She declared firmly, “His dislike is only temporary. Once Song Qiming becomes our Gu family’s son-in-law, Father will like him.”","Her father was merely jealous that an outsider had risen faster than he had and felt that the man had taken his son’s place. But once Song Qiming became part of their family, her elder brother could be considered to have risen in rank as well. Everything would be different then.","Madam Gu was so thoroughly stumped that she could barely speak. In the end, all she could say was, “You certainly are bold. Your father spoiled you rotten.”","Gu Baozhu tilted her head and smiled ingratiatingly. “Mother spoiled me too.”","“Shixue said County Princess Linghui had set a rule that the men of the Song family are not allowed to take concubines—not even if they remain without children.”","Madam Gu’s eyes flashed with surprise and delight. “Really?”","Gu Baozhu nodded emphatically. “County Princess Linghui told Song Qiming that herself, and he swore that he agreed.”","The slight displeasure Madam Gu had felt moments earlier vanished without a trace.","The Gu family’s rule against concubines was unusual. She had always worried that other families might not share it. Even if her daughter married beneath her station, she could not openly stop her husband from taking concubines. But now the Song family had the same rule—not even allowing concubines if there were no children. A family with such values was harder to find than one illuminated by a lantern.","“When your father comes home tonight, I’ll speak with him. Don’t worry. This marriage will definitely happen.”","Compared with her daughter’s happiness for the rest of her life, her husband’s petty misgivings were hardly worth mentioning. At worst, they would argue and give each other the cold shoulder for two days."]},{"number":595,"title":"Chapter 595: Mid-Month Persuasion Valley","paragraphs":["That night, after washing up, Gu Zhongxun lay in bed preparing to sleep. In his mind, he simulated Madam Gu slowly crawling up behind him and kneading his shoulders.","Gu Zhongxun turned toward his wife in surprise, his shoulders instinctively hunching.","“Madam, I haven’t done anything to anger you these past few days, have I?”","Madam Gu’s expression stiffened, and she immediately increased the force of her hands.","She gritted her teeth and said with a smile, “Of course not. I just saw how hard you’ve been working lately, so I thought I’d give you a massage.”","Gu Zhongxun relaxed. He closed his eyes and began to enjoy it.","“It has been somewhat tiring. That Song Qiming comes up with new ideas every day, and each one is more elaborate than the last. If the others weren’t all willing to listen to me, it really wouldn’t be easy to keep him in check.”","Madam ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‍Gu’s hands came to a stop. She asked quietly, “Are none of those ideas any good?”","Gu Zhongxun’s lips parted, then closed, then parted again. In the end, he managed to say, “The ideas are all good. It’s just that the person who came up with them is in the wrong.”","Madam Gu asked, “Since they’re good ideas, are you really willing not to use them?”","Gu Zhongxun took a deep breath, suppressing the tightness in his chest.","“We’ll use them eventually, but not yet. First, I need to break that brat’s spirit.”","Madam Gu’s patience gradually wore away with every word of disdain he uttered.","She released her hands and dropped herself down hard beside him. The bedding gave a loud thump.","“County Princess Linghui came to visit today. She wants to arrange a marriage for Song Qiming, and she has taken a liking to our Baozhu.”","Gu Zhongxun turned his stiff neck toward her, his eyes widening until they were almost as big as a bull’s.","“What did you say?”","Madam Gu rolled her eyes at him. “County Princess Linghui wants Baozhu and Song Qiming to meet and see if they suit each other.”","As if firecrackers had gone off beneath his feet, Gu Zhongxun sprang up from the bed. His head struck the canopy, and his vision blurred.","“No! I absolutely refuse to agree.”","Madam Gu said, “Baozhu was the one who took a liking to Song Qiming first. They had already discussed this arrangement, which is why County Princess Linghui came here today.”","The world before his eyes went black. Gu Zhongxun collapsed back onto the bed, his head buzzing.","Seeing how deeply her husband had been shaken, Madam Gu pressed on.","“Setting aside the fact that Song Qiming has risen through the ranks faster than you, among men his age, he can certainly be considered one of the most outstanding young talents.”","“Baozhu says the men of the Song family are not permitted to take concubines—not even if they have no children.”","“In my opinion, once he becomes your son-in-law, the southwest you’ve worked so hard to build won’t fall into the hands of outsiders. Our daughter will also have found herself a fine husband. It’s a win-win situation.”","Gu Zhongxun stared straight at Madam Gu. “Are you certain Song Qiming will never take a concubine?”","Madam Gu nodded. “That was County Princess Linghui’s condition, and Song Qiming swore that he would honor it.”","Gu Zhongxun turned away and fell silent again.","The anger on his face gradually faded, replaced by a calm, blank expression that was somehow even more unsettling.","Madam Gu slowly edged closer to him. “The Song family is small and uncomplicated. I think it’s a good match.”","With his heart still hanging in the balance, Gu Zhongxun pulled the bedding over himself.","“Give me some time to think.”","Knowing her husband’s temperament well, Madam Gu’s eyes flashed with surprise as she stared at Gu Zhongxun, who had buried his head beneath the covers.","He was actually considering whether the marriage was feasible. He hadn’t continued to reject it outright.","That night, Madam Gu slept soundly, while Gu Zhongxun remained awake almost until dawn. The next morning, he left for the government office without even eating breakfast.","Gu Baozhu, who had come to find out what was happening, noticed that Gu Zhongxun was absent from the breakfast table and asked Madam Gu, “Where’s Father?”","Madam Gu smiled warmly as she held her chopsticks. “Your mother thinks this matter may be much easier than we imagined.”","Gu Baozhu furrowed her brows in confusion.","What did that mean?","Had he agreed or not?"]},{"number":596,"title":"Chapter 596: One-on-One Conversation","paragraphs":["Gu Zhongxun waited at the government office for half an hour before Song Qiming finally arrived.","The moment their eyes met, Song Qiming knew he was in for a difficult time.","For the entire morning, whenever Song Qiming looked up, he would find Gu Zhongxun watching him through the half-open window of the adjoining room.","After two hours of fidgeting uneasily, just before noon recess, Gu Zhongxun silently came to a stop behind Song Qiming.","“I’ve reserved a private room at Ruyi House for lunch. Lord Song, you’ll join me.”","The heavy tone of his voice weighed on Song Qiming’s heart like a thousand catties.","He closed the memorial he had only read halfway and rose, pretending to be calm as he followed Gu Zhongxun out.","When Feng Yi, the proprietor of Ruyi House, saw the two men entering one after the other, curiosity stirred in him.","It appeared that Gu Zhongxun had reserved a private room to dine with the eldest young master, but why did the atmosphere between them feel so much like a cold war?","By the time the waiter led them into the private room, two plates of cold dishes had already been set out. A quarter of an hour after they took their seats, the waiter brought in two small stoves.","“Go out and keep your distance. We don’t need anyone waiting on us here.”","The waiter hurriedly nodded, bent at the waist, and lowered his head as he left, closing the door behind him.","The broth began to bubble and simmer. Gu Zhongxun fixed Song Qiming with a deep, piercing stare, like a wild wolf watching its prey.","“Why do you want to marry my daughter?”","Song Qiming clenched his fists and met the other man’s sharp gaze head-on.","“A graceful lady is a gentleman’s desire. I love Baozhu and wish to take her as my wife.”","“Liar.”","The ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​​‌‍two icy words struck Song Qiming in the face, more painful than hailstones and more nerve-racking than an imperial edict.","“I know exactly what you want. What I want to tell you is that Baozhu is the treasured jewel of the Gu family. Everyone dotes on her. She has never suffered the slightest grievance in her entire life. If, after marrying her, you ever make her suffer even a little, I will make you divorce her and drive you into the dirt, whether you have children or not. I will pursue you until one of us is dead.”","A little light returned to Song Qiming’s eyes.","Did Gu Zhongxun mean that he was willing to marry Baozhu to him?","Gu Zhongxun asked, “Even knowing that, are you still willing to marry her?”","Song Qiming composed himself, rose, and cupped his hands toward him in solemn assurance.","“If I am fortunate enough to marry your daughter, I swear that I will respect and cherish her for the rest of my life. I will never waver, and I will stand by her through life and death.”","Gu Zhongxun continued, “I’ve heard that even if the Song family has no sons, the men of your family are not permitted to take concubines or keep women outside the marriage. Can you put that guarantee in writing?”","Without the slightest hesitation, Song Qiming nodded. “I can. If I take another woman after we are married, the written agreement may state that you are permitted to kill me.”","After spending time with Baozhu on several occasions, he had already developed feelings for her. Whether it was for the sake of the Gu family or for Baozhu herself, he had resolved to treat her well for the rest of his life. Whatever agreement Gu Zhongxun wanted from him, he did not care.","Even Gu Zhongxun was momentarily stunned when he heard Song Qiming say that killing him would be acceptable.","He picked up his chopsticks and began eating in silence, mentally going over the pros and cons once more.","Setting aside the fact that he personally disliked Song Qiming, the man’s talent and appearance were indeed impeccable, and his family background was a good match as well. If Baozhu married him, then after Gu Zhongxun retired, should Song Qiming succeed in becoming the Southwest Provincial Administration Commissioner, he would be unable to leave the southwest for at least three to five years. Even if he were later transferred back to the capital, Gu Zhongxun could take his entire family there to live with his eldest son. No matter how things turned out, they would not have to be separated.","While Gu Zhongxun considered Song Qiming’s prospects, Song Qiming could only wait quietly, occasionally lowering himself to pour wine for the older man.","It was not until every dish on the table had been cleared away that Gu Zhongxun finally looked up at him.","“In a few days, have your eldest sister choose an auspicious date and come formally to ask for Baozhu’s hand.”","Watching Gu Zhongxun walk away without even turning his head, Song Qiming hurriedly rose and bowed deeply.","“Thank you, my lord, for granting your consent.”","He had never expected Gu Zhongxun to agree so readily. He had assumed the man would firmly oppose the match, or at the very least make things difficult for him several more times.","When Gu Zhongxun returned from the government office that evening, Madam Gu learned only then that he had agreed to the marriage and had even instructed the Song family to come formally with a proposal in a few days.","“I thought you would refuse.”","Gu Zhongxun removed his boots and placed his feet in the hot water. “As you said, Song Qiming is indeed an excellent candidate.”","“Gaoyuan has been transferred to the capital. The court will not appoint Huaiyuan, a military commander, as Southwest Provincial Administration Commissioner. I would rather have Baozhu’s future husband take that position than let it fall to an outsider.”","“To be perfectly honest, it will be easier to promote Song Qiming than Gaoyuan. His Majesty has clearly already made up his mind. Even if I wanted to stop it, I couldn’t.”","When he finished speaking, he let out a sigh, his heart filled mostly with a sense of defeat."]},{"number":597,"title":"Chapter 597: Formal Proposal Visit","paragraphs":["The day the Song family came to formally ask for Gu Baozhu’s hand in marriage, the sky was cloudless and clear, as though it had just been washed.","Ten heavy, redwood chests decorated with gold were carried in. Gold and silver ingots wrapped in red paper were piled on top of the first chest.","The second chest held two sets of solid-gold hair ornaments. One of them was inlaid with flawless rubies that shimmered with dazzling color, bright enough to make people squint in the sunlight.","The third chest was filled with dozens of bolts of cloud brocade, all prepared according to Gu Baozhu’s tastes.","Fine wine and tea, assorted candied fruits, wedding sweets, nourishing herbs—the ten chests were packed to the brim.","Song Qiming personally led the marriage procession, carrying a pair of wild geese he had just hunted. All four siblings were present, not one missing.","When the gatekeeper spotted the Song family approaching from afar, he immediately turned and hurried inside to report.","“Master, Madam, the Song family has arrived.”","By the time Song Jinzhao had reached the top of the steps, the couple from the Gu family’s second branch had just come out to welcome them.","“Greetings, County Princess Linghui.”","Both their eyes settled on the refined and graceful Song Qiming, and their satisfaction was impossible to conceal.","Everyone took their seats in the Gu residence’s front hall. Gu Baozhu, hiding behind the screen, desperately wanted to come out, but a matron from Madam Gu’s household staff stopped her. With no choice, she sat back down.","Song Shixue glanced toward the screen, and her eyes met Gu Baozhu’s for a fleeting moment.","The contents of the chests were displayed before everyone one item at a time. Finally, Song Jinzhao took out the betrothal letter and handed it to Madam Gu.","Madam Gu had intended to give it only a cursory glance, but when she unfolded it, she found a sheet of paper folded inside.","The contents left her stunned.","It was a written pledge, saying exactly what Gu Baozhu had asked for: that Song Qiming would never take a concubine.","Madam Gu had not expected Song Qiming to write it out with his own hand. Words spoken aloud and words committed to paper carried entirely different weight.","She handed the pledge to Gu Zhongxun. After reading it, he gave a slight nod.","The two families set the wedding for three months later, and the news soon spread throughout Songzhou City.","The following day, when Song Qiming reported for duty at the government office, Cui Zhengyang walked over to him with an unmistakably relieved expression.","He lowered his voice and whispered, “I never thought Gu Zhongxun would actually agree to marry his daughter to you. Now I don’t have to worry about what’s going to happen to me.”","Because he was close to Song Qiming, Cui Zhengyang had not enjoyed a single peaceful day since taking office.","Every major and minor matter was rejected, delayed, or picked apart. Not only did his work fail to proceed smoothly, but he felt stifled inside as well.","While the two men were speaking, a subordinate carried over a large stack of official documents.","“Lord Song, the Provincial Administration Commissioner has already approved all of these. He wants you to put them into practice as soon as possible.”","Song Qiming casually picked up the memorial on top. It contained his recent proposal to rebuild the irrigation channels, and the words “Approved” had been written at the end.","He then pulled out the one at the very bottom. It was his proposal from two months earlier concerning the use of compost to enrich the soil. It, too, bore the words “Approved.” The ink was still glossy and fresh, clearly written only recently.","Cui Zhengyang could not help curling his lips in a mocking smile.","“Should I say he’s slow or efficient? He approved two months’ worth of memorials in a single night.”","Song ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‍Qiming casually picked up one of the documents and waved it.","“All I know is that we’re going to be busy from now on.”","Over the next three months, apart from taking Gu Baozhu out on his days off, Song Qiming spent nearly all his time handling official business.","He rose earlier than the chickens and went to bed later than the dogs. After three months, he had lost several pounds, much to Gu Baozhu’s distress. She went home and complained to her father.","“Father, why did you give him so much work? Qiming has grown so thin.”","The teacup in Gu Zhongxun’s hand was neither easy to set down nor to drink from.","“I never urged him. He chose to keep himself busy.”","Gu Baozhu puffed out her cheeks. “What if he’s this busy even after I marry him?”","Madam Gu, sitting nearby, raised her head and admonished her daughter.","“Even when he’s busy, he still sends you gifts every few days. Whenever he has a day off, he spends several hours accompanying you without the slightest hint of impatience. Your father never treated me that well.”","Gu Zhongxun hurriedly defended himself.","“How did I not? When we were young, I often sent you gifts and took you out for good food.”","Madam Gu rolled her eyes at him.","“And what about now? Aside from my birthday, when else do you give me anything?”","Seeing the two of them argue more and more fiercely—and even start dredging up old grievances—Gu Baozhu quietly rose onto her toes and slipped out of the room.","They would make up by tonight at the latest.","But if she stayed, once they finished arguing and wanted to reconcile, she would become the convenient excuse that allowed them to climb down from the tree."]},{"number":598,"title":"Chapter 598: Song Qiming's Wedding","paragraphs":["The beginning of autumn in the thirtieth year of Yongyuan.","The Southwest Provincial Administration Commissioner was marrying off his daughter, while the younger brother of County Princess Linghui—and the youngest Circuit Intendant in the entire Southwest—was taking a wife. It was a marriage of mutual benefit, and the wedding was grander than any before it.","The wedding procession wound from the gates of the Gu residence around nearly half of Songzhou City before finally arriving at the Song residence.","Every official, great or small, as well as all the city’s prominent merchants, had been invited.","This was more than a wedding. It was a public declaration to everyone in the city: from this day forward, the Gu and Song families would stand closely allied. Anyone who wished to move against one family would first have to weigh the strength of the other.","A crimson carpet stretched from the manor gates all the way into the wedding hall. Song Jinzhao sat at the head of the hall. On the wedding altar before her, surrounded by red dates and longans, stood the memorial tablets of the Song family’s parents.","“First bow—to Heaven and Earth!”","Song Qiming and Gu Baozhu stood side by side and bowed deeply to the heavens.","“Second bow—to the elders!”","Looking at Song Qiming in his wedding robes, his face glowing with happiness, Song Jinzhao was overwhelmed by mixed emotions.","When she had first arrived in this world, he had been only ten years old. Unable to wait for her to return home, he would cry in fear.","Now he was old enough to start a family of his own. Time truly flew.","“Third bow—to each other!”","Watching her closest friend marry her own brother, Song Shixue sat to the side with a smile of blessing on her face.","She believed that the two of them would enjoy a wonderfully happy life together, just like the couples in the storybooks written by Liu Ruoxi.","“The ceremony is complete! Escort the newlyweds to the bridal chamber!”","The matchmakers crowded around the newlyweds and led them toward their new room. Gu Baozhu’s palm, clenched around the red silk, was already slick with sweat.","This was clearly what she had wanted, yet now that the moment had arrived, she still felt nervous.","Expectation and anxiety mingled together, leaving her restless and uncertain.","The next morning, she awoke in unfamiliar surroundings. A maid hurried happily to the bedside.","Gu Baozhu rubbed her eyes and asked, “What time is it?”","The maid answered with a smile, “It’s just past the hour of Chen. The young master went to the training grounds an hour ago.”","Gu Baozhu’s eyes flew open. “Then why didn’t you wake me?”","“The young master said there was no need to wake you. He said that at the Song residence, you could rise whenever you wished. There aren’t so many rules here.”","The instructions Madam Gu had whispered in her ear on the night before the wedding still echoed in her mind.","No matter how wonderful the Song family’s promises had sounded before the marriage, County Princess Linghui was still the head of the household. She absolutely could not neglect the proper respect and decorum.","“Quick, help me wash up. I’m going to pay my respects to County Princess—no, to Big Sister.”","For the first three days, she needed to get a feel for the household. After all, marrying into a family was different from visiting as a guest.","Just as she was washing her face, Song Qiming walked in from outside.","Their eyes met, and Gu Baozhu’s face immediately flushed.","“There’s no need to hurry. Once morning exercises are over, Big Sister and the others will still be washing up.”","When the newlyweds arrived in the front hall, breakfast had already been laid out. The two of them bowed and offered tea to Song Jinzhao.","“I heard that you also helped manage the shops at your family home. This is the deed to a grain store in the northern part of the city. Consider it a gift to welcome you into the family.”","Song Shixue picked up a box from the table and opened it. Inside, wrapped in red silk, was a hundred-year-old ginseng root.","“I’m not as wealthy as my elder sister, so I’ll give Sister-in-law a ginseng root.”","The two close friends exchanged a glance and could not help laughing.","Song Anhao eagerly pulled a red envelope from inside his robe and held it out to Gu Baozhu.","“This is my welcoming gift for Sister-in-law.”","Gu Baozhu hesitated before accepting it. The envelope felt rather thick.","Wasn’t the bride supposed to prepare gifts for her younger brothers and sisters? Why had things been reversed in the Song family?","After collecting herself, she hurriedly presented gifts to the three members of the Song family.","Jade ornaments and paintings were the customary welcoming gifts among wealthy families, but Gu Baozhu’s presents were quite different.","For Song Jinzhao, she had brought a dagger forged from refined iron.","For Song Shixue, a set of twenty-eight needles made of black iron for acupuncture.","For Song Anhao, a piece of chicken-blood stone the size of a fist. The moment she took it out, his eyes lit up.","“Thank you, Sister-in-law. I like it very much.”","Song Anhao accepted it with both hands. After sitting down, he continued stroking it.","After breakfast, Gu Baozhu returned to her room and, out of habit, opened the red envelope.","Once she had counted all the banknotes inside, she froze and looked up in disbelief.","“Anhao gave me ten thousand taels as a welcoming gift!”","Song Qiming’s hand paused over the book he was holding. In the end, he could only give a wry smile and shake his head.","“He’s certainly generous.”","Seeing his reaction, Gu Baozhu found it even more unbelievable.","“How could Anhao have so much silver? He’s only ten.”","Back at the Gu residence, not even she and Jinghong or Congwen had ten thousand taels to their names before marriage, let alone when they were ten years old.","For Song Anhao to give away ten thousand taels meant that he must have far more than that in his possession.","Song ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌​‍Qiming walked over to the couch and sat beside Gu Baozhu, leaning against it.","“It was all earned by Anhao himself.”","He pointed at his own nose and said, “In the entire Song family, your husband is the poorest one.”","Gu Baozhu remained speechless for a long time.","She knew that Song Anhao made money by selling storybooks, but she had never imagined that he could earn so much.","More importantly, Song Jinzhao had not taken the money from him. Instead, she trusted a ten-year-old child to manage his own fortune—while her own husband was the poorest member of the family."]},{"number":599,"title":"Chapter 599: Omen","paragraphs":["For ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​‍the first three days of their marriage, Song Qiming was on leave at home. Worried that he would not have time to keep his wife company once he returned to duty, he decided to spend all three days with Gu Baozhu. Even when he read or handled official business, he stayed on the couch in their bridal chamber.","The first day went well enough, but by the second day, Gu Baozhu could no longer sit still.","“I’m going out for some fresh air and to stretch my legs.” She ran out the door without sparing Song Qiming so much as a backward glance.","After making a circuit of the residence, Gu Baozhu discovered that Song Jinzhao, Song Shixue, and Song Anhao were all out.","“The county lady went to the newly opened cement factory, the second young miss went to the clinic, and the young master has to attend the academy in the morning and visit his newly purchased bookshop in the afternoon. He probably won’t make it back for lunch.”","Of the family’s five members, only she and Song Qiming were at home.","No. Once Song Qiming’s three-day leave ended, she would be the only one in the household with nothing to do.","Gu Baozhu returned to the room with a thoughtful look on her face, arousing Song Qiming’s curiosity.","Before he could ask what was wrong, Gu Baozhu instructed her personal maid to bring over the inventory of her dowry.","“Two small estates, three hundred mu of paddy fields, and twelve shops. I’ll have to find time to go and take a look.”","Gu Baozhu muttered to herself as she examined the dowry inventory and land deeds, making Song Qiming’s brows twitch uncontrollably.","Sure enough, he was the poorest person in the household!","On the day of their return visit to her family, the gifts had been prepared by Song Jinzhao. Seeing the two carts piled high with presents, Gu Baozhu could not stop grinning.","While Songzhou City remained peaceful, a catastrophe was quietly unfolding in the military camp of Yunzhong City, a thousand li away.","On the training grounds, Qin Yunqian stared unhappily at the battalion commander in charge of the troops.","“It isn’t winter yet. How have so many men come down with chills? Has the military physician examined them?”","“The physician already has,” the battalion commander replied. “He said they caught cold from exposure and has prescribed medicine. They should recover in a couple of days.”","Qin Yunqian’s chest tightened with anger. “When the seasons change in autumn, tell everyone to stop bathing in the river so no one else catches cold.”","The battalion commander hurriedly nodded his agreement.","Back in the main tent, Qin Guo, commander of the Jinglei Army, was writing a memorial requesting this year’s winter military supplies.","“Father, when will the court’s quilts and winter clothing arrive? Some of the men in camp have already come down with chills these past few days. There will certainly be more once winter arrives.”","Qin Guo stopped writing and let out a heavy sigh.","“I have already submitted a request, but the court has yet to respond. I was just about to send another reminder.”","Qin Yunqian’s expression darkened. “The court isn’t going to refuse us, is it?”","Qin Guo gritted his teeth. “It shouldn’t. They may simply send less than we requested.”","The moment Qin Yunqian heard that the winter supplies might be reduced, he exploded.","“Less? They cut them by a third last year. If they reduce them again this year, people will freeze to death!”","Qin Guo had now lost what little patience he had left for writing another urgent memorial.","“The two countries have arranged a marriage alliance, and His Majesty believes Shubei Kingdom will not go to war for the next three to five years. That is why he intends to reduce supplies for the border garrisons.”","Qin Yunqian turned toward the capital and cursed the emperor as a pigheaded fool countless times.","“Why reduce them now? What are we supposed to do if war breaks out? I think His Majesty has lost his mind.”","“Enough!” Qin Guo shouted sternly. “Do not say such treasonous things. Be careful someone overhears you.”","The camp was full of people, and there was no guarantee that someone would not hear him and report it.","Qin Yunqian’s face remained grim. He did not want to say another word, because he knew it would change nothing.","Three days later.","“How have they still not recovered after taking medicine for three days?” Qin Yunqian demanded as he pushed open the tent where the sick soldiers were staying.","Inside, the three men lay on their beds, their faces ashen and bitter-looking. Their foreheads were alarmingly hot to the touch.","The battalion commander who had brought him there felt a heavy weight settle in his heart.","“The military physician comes every day. The day before yesterday, he even gave them a stronger medicine, but instead of improving, their condition has worsened.”","“Their fevers keep rising. They could still open their eyes and say a few words before, but none of them has regained consciousness since yesterday afternoon.”","Qin Yunqian frowned. “Go and fetch the military physician.”","One of the soldiers he had just singled out suddenly staggered, then collapsed to the ground without warning.","“Long Er!”","The cry made everyone turn around at once.","Qin Yunqian crossed the distance in two strides and crouched beside him.","The soldier’s face was flushed. When Qin Yunqian reached out and touched him, he found that he was burning with fever too.","“Quick! Go call the military physician!”"]}]);
